2 CONC s, "Key to References ...," version 1.1 (2011). Notes: NEHGS summary includes comment, "The work is so huge and so comprehensive (it is estimated that 99% of all marriages are included), that it has become one of the principal res
2 CONC ources for seventeenth-century New England genealogy." William Swetland and Agnes ____; date as "by 1676," with reference to Salem and Salem CT.
