1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Pvt. Luke Swetland=
2 CONT * BIRTH 26 Jul 1729 New London, New London County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 30 Jun 1823 (aged 93) Forty Fort, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Forty Fort Cemetery, Forty Fort, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania, USA  Show Map GPS-Latitude: 41.2849839, Longitude: -75.8725520
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 26691749 Photos by Cyndy Pugh
2 CONT
2 CONT Luke Swetland was the son of John Oliver and Sarah (Davis) Treadway Swetland. He was the husband of Hannah (Tiffany) Swetland. They were married April 1, 1762. Hannah died January 8, 1809. Luke died at the home of his grandson, Wi
2 CONC lliam Swetland. Luke served during the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inscription''' on Gravestone
2 CONT  Luke Swetland
2 CONT  Pvt I INDPT Co
2 CONT Revolutionary War
2 CONT    Jul 26, 1729
2 CONT   Jan 30, 1823
2 CONT Ae 94 Yrs 14 Dys
2 CONT
2 CONT                     '''Inscription''' on Celophate
2 CONT                           LUKE SWETLAND
2 CONT                                     THE 
2 CONT            GRANDFATHER OF WILLIAM SWETLAND
2 CONT    Settling in Wyoming (PA) in 1769 was taken prisoner after 
2 CONT the Wyoming Massacre (3 July 1778) and after a years captivity 
2 CONT        and endured hardships among the Indians escaped to 
2 CONT            Sullivan's Army and thence rejoined his family 
2 CONT           who had fled to their former home in Connecticut.  
2 CONT               BELDING SWETLAND, father of WILLIAM 
2 CONT            leaving the fort near this spot after its surrender 
2 CONT             though but a lad yet the eldest of the children 
2 CONT                heroically piloted the family in their flight 
2 CONT                through the forests to their eastern home.  
2 CONT               WILLIAM SWETLAND was born in Sharon, 
2 CONT              Connecticut.  His grandfather and father with 
2 CONT               their families returned to Wyoming in 1794 
2 CONT and located where William Swetland thereafter
2 CONT lived and where he died in Christian triumph.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT John Oliver Swetland 1681–1750
2 CONT Sarah Davis Treadway Swetland 1686–1773
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Hannah Tiffany Swetland 1738–1809
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT John Swetland 1708–1783
2 CONT Joseph Swetland 1710–1783
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Belding Swetland 1763–1816
2 CONT Artemas Swetland 1769–1855
2 CONT Eli Swetland 1771–1777
2 CONT John Swetland 1777–1777
2 CONT
