1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===William Brattle===
2 CONT * Born: 22 Nov 1662, Boston MA
2 CONT * Died: 15 Feb 1717, Cambridge MA
2 CONT * Buried: Cambridge MA
2 CONT * son of Thomas William Brattle and Elizabeth Tyng
2 CONT * Marriage: Elizabeth Hayman on 3 Nov 1697 in Boston MA
2 CONT
2 CONT William married Elizabeth Hayman on 3 Nov 1697 in Boston MA. (Elizabeth Hayman was born in 1676 in Charlestown MA and died on 28 Jul 1715 in Cambridge MA.)
2 CONT * Reference: [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/4:1:KP3V-HHV FamilySearch Family Tree] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 12 2017, 20:33:57 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Fellow of the Royal Society. Member, Harvard College Class of 1680.
2 CONT
2 CONT See Biographical Sketches of Graduates of Harvard, by John Sibley & Clifford Shipton, Vol. 3, page 200.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.geocities.ws/bostonancestors/brattle.htm Cambridge deaths: BRATTLE, William, Rev., Feb. 15, 1716-17 (in his 55th y. GR1). 
2 CONT
2 CONT WILLIAM BRATTLE, S.T.B, F.R.S., b. Boston, Nov. 22, 1662, son of Thomas and Elizabeth (Tyng) Brattle; H.C., 1680, A.B., A.M.; S.T.B., 1692, being the first time this degree was conferred; F.R.S., London, 1713; membr. Corp., 1703; 
2 CONC Tutor, Fellow, H.C., 1703-1717; Treas., H.C., 1713-1715; Ord. Cambridge, Nov. 25, 1696; sett. Cambridge, 1696-1717; published a book of logic used as a text-book at H.C.; d. Cambridge, Feb. 15, 1716/17, a. 55. (Weis, F.L., The Col
2 CONC onial Clergy and Colonial Churches in New England)
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=50177300 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 12 2017, 20:37:52 UTC''
