1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT From Harris's Descendants of Thomas  Brattle [https://archive.org/stream/accountofsomeofd1867harr#page/4/mode/2up page 5] , [https://archive.org/stream/accountofsomeofd1867harr#page/26/mode/2up page 27],  [https://archive.org/stre
2 CONC am/accountofsomeofd1867harr#page/28/mode/2up page 28]
2 CONT
2 CONT His [Thomas Brattle's] children, all born at Boston, were, 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Bethiah, b. Dec. 13, 1666.
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) 7. Bethiah Brattle, third daughter of Thomas and Elizabeth (Tyng), married Joseph Parsons of Boston, merchant.  He was an advocate for the overthrow of Andross in 16S9, made freeman in March, 1690. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died at Boston, July 4, 1690, of small pox, their last child having died of the same disease ten days 
2 CONT before. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her issue were : 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 33. Joseph, bapt. July 27, 1684, d. young.  
2 CONT * 34. William, b. Dec. 29, 1685, bapt. Jan. 2  1685-6 d. young. The second son, William, then being the "only child," d. June 24, 1690.  
2 CONT * 35- Bethiah, b. Jan. i, 1686-J, bapt. next day, d. young.  
2 CONT * 36. Thomas, b. Aug. 11, 1689, bapt. same day, d. young. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Of Joseph Parsons, the father, after the death of the last of his family, we know nothing further except that he was living in 1720, and was held in esteem and affection by the brothers of his wife, each of whom bequeathed propert
2 CONC y to him in their wills. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From History of the Military Company of the Massachusetts, Now Called ..., Volume 1 By Oliver Ayer Roberts [https://books.google.com/books?id=VycMAQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA256&ots=htdJylPoKZ&dq=Bethiah%20(Brattle)%20Parsons&pg=PA256#v=onepag
2 CONC e&q=Bethiah%20(Brattle)%20Parsons&f=false Page 256]
2 CONT
2 CONT >Joseph Parsons (1679), of Boston, merchant, married Bethia Brattle, daughter of Capt. Thomas (1675). They had four children, all of whom died young; the mother herself dying July 4, 1690, ten days after her last child died.
2 CONT >Mr. Parsons (1679) was a member of the patriotic council for the overthrow of Andros in 1689, and was made a freeman in March, 1690.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Of Joseph Parsons (1679), the father, after the death of the last of his family, nothing has been learned, except that he was alive in 1720.
2 CONT
2 CONT Authorities: Savage's Gen. Diet.; Harris's Descendants of Thomas  Brattle [https://archivhttps://archive.org/stream/accountofsomeofd1867harr#page/26/mode/2up page 27], Harris's Descendants of Thomas  Brattle [https://archive.org/s
2 CONC tream/accountofsomeofd1867harr#page/28/mode/2up page 28]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
