1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Captain William Tyng, a merchant of distinction in Boston,  came to America in the "Nicholas," chartered by himself at London. He arrived in Boston, July 3, 1638. He was representative, 1639-44, and 1647; treasurer
2 CONC  of the colony, 164044; captain of the militia company of Braintree, Massachusetts, where he removed in his latter days, and which he represented in the federal court, 1649-51. His widow (Jane, his third wife) survived him. His fi
2 CONC rst wife was Ann Brown; his second, '''Elizabeth, daughter of Rowland Coytmore.''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Elizabeth Cotymore and William Tyng:
2 CONT # Eliz. b. I doubt not in Eng. 6 Feb. 1638, bapt. here, 10 Mar. 1639; m. a. 1656, Thomas Brattle;
2 CONT # Ann, 6, bapt. 12 Jan. 1640; m. 3 Nov. 1656, Thomas Shepard, afterwards min. of Charlestown;
2 CONT # Bethia, 17, bapt. 23 May 1641; m. Richard Wharton
2 CONT # Mercy, 13 Jan. bapt 5 Feb. 1643.  m. 1662, Samuel Bradstreet. Six of this name had been gr. in 1832 at Harv.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT * http://capecodhistory.us/genealogy/Nauset/i4056.htm#i17114
