1 NAME Capt. William Tyng
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE BEF 16 JAN 1603
2 ADDR
3 CITY Stanford Rivers
3 CTRY England
1 OCCU unknown
2 DATE 1640
2 PLAC Treasurer Of The MA Bay Colony
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 JAN 1653
2 ADDR
3 CITY Braintree
3 STAE Massachusetts Bay Colony
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 OCCU Merchant, captain, treasurer of the Massachusetts Bay Colony
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Capt. William Tyng''' was (probably) the William baptized 16 January 1602/3 at Stanford Rivers, Essex, England, son of Edward; he died on 18 January 1653 at Braintree, Norfolk, MA.1,2,3. At his death he was the 
2 CONC wealthiest man of his day. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His brother was Edward Tyng. "The name Dunstable derived from a town in England where both [Edward] Tyng and his wife were born. You may also see the rectangle of land referenced as 'The Ancient Town of Dunstable'." [SIC: probably
2 CONC  not] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===brief biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT From Hudson-Mohawk Genealogical and Family Memoirs: A Record of ..., Volume 1 edited by Cuyler Reynolds
2 CONT
2 CONT >Captain William Tyng, a merchant of distinction in Boston, who came to America in the "Nicholas," chartered by himself at London. He arrived in Boston, July 3, 1638. He was representative, 1639, 44, and 1647; treasurer of the col
2 CONC ony, 1640-44; captain of the militia company of Braintree, Massachusetts, where he removed in his latter days, and which he represented in the federal court, 1649-51. His widow (Jane, his third wife) survived him. [sic: died 1652]
2 CONC . His first wife was Ann Brown; his second, Elizabeth, daughter of Rowland Coytmore.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family===
2 CONT
2 CONT married 
2 CONT #  Ann Dersley (but Savage says Ann Brown), m Jun 1634 in England
2 CONT # Elizabeth Coytemore, daughter of Rowland Coytemore and Katharine Myles, m 1638 in England or Braintree
2 CONT # Jane, perhaps the widow of Richard Hunt,   m 10 Jan 1649 in Boston.  Died 3 Oct. 1652 according to Savage 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Tyng and Elizabeth Coytemore had 4 daughters
2 CONT # Elizabeth, wife of Thomas Brattle;
2 CONT # Anna, wife of Rev. Thomas Shepard, Gent; 
2 CONT # Bethia, wife of Richard Wharton, Esq; &
2 CONT #  Mercy, wife of Samuel Bradstreet 4,2,3 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://our-royal-titled-noble-and-commoner-ancestors.com/p3975.htm#i119384
2 CONT **1.  [S61] Unknown author, Family Group Sheets, Family History Archives, SLC.
2 CONT **2. [S16] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, 2nd Edition, Vol. I, p. 562.
2 CONT **3.[S4] Douglas Richardson, Royal Ancestry, Vol. II, p. 347.
2 CONT **4. [S15] Douglas Richardson, Magna Carta Ancestry, p. 243
2 CONT
2 CONT ===supporting data===
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From Savage, James. A Genealogical Dictionary of the First Settlers of New England Showing Three Generations of Those Who Came Before May, 1692, - Vol. I-IV (4). Boston, 1860-1862. Volume 4: 358
2 CONT
2 CONT >WILLIAM, Boston, elder br. of Edward the first, a merch. of distinct. came prob. in the Nicholas, of 300 tons, charter. by hims. at London, arr. at Boston, 3 July 1638, as Josselyn, wh. was a passeng.---tells in his curious vol. 
2 CONC of Voyages. He join. our ch. 3 Mar. foll. and was adm. freem. 10 days aft. was of ar. co. 1638, rep. 1639, 40, 1, 2, 3, 4 and 7, treasr. of the Col. 1640-4; capt. of the Braintree milit. comp. and in latter days liv. in that town,
2 CONC  was its rep. 1649, 50, and 1; his w. Jane, being his third, wh. may have been wid. of the first Enoch Hunt, d. 3 Oct. 1652, and he d. 18 Jan. foll. leav. larger est. than any in the country of that day. It is by his descend. Rev.
2 CONC  William Brattle, said, that " his first w. was Ann Brown, by wh. he had two ch. wh. d. bef. he m. our gr. mo. Eliz. d. of Rowland Coytemore, whose maiden name was Myles, and had a former h. named Gray, by wh. she had my aunts Now
2 CONC ell and Graves." By Eliz. he had Eliz. b. I doubt not in Eng. 6 Feb. 1638, bapt. here, 10 Mar. 1639; Ann, 6, bapt. 12 Jan. 1640; Bethia, 17, bapt. 23 May 1641; and Mercy, 13 Jan. bapt 5 Feb. 1643.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://capecodhistory.us/genealogy/Nauset/i4056.htm#i17114
2 CONT
2 CONT Wives:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Ann Dersley (but Savage says Ann Brown), m Jun 1634 in England.  
2 CONT * Ellizabeth Coytemore, m 1638 in England or Braintree
2 CONT **Her mother's 1st husband was Gray, at least 2 daughters, who m Nowell and Graves
2 CONT * Jane Hunt, m 10 Jan 1649 in Boston (widow of Enoch Hunt)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Member, Ancient & Honorable Artillery Company of Boston.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
