2 CONT *'''Genealogical Notes of Barnstable Families     By Amos Otis
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=0FX9Dptikw4C&pg=PA471&lpg=PA471&dq=benjamin+hatch+1686&source=bl&ots=B3Swe3Q05v&sig=CxGG8UOKeVem9hZ9EJ2zC4ZmetM&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjZhqub2pHLAhVD8mMKHQCJC244ChDoAQg8MAg#v=onepage&q=benjamin%20
2 CONC hatch%201686&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.467
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *   Children of Jonathan Hatch and Sarah Rowley, his wife. Born in Barnstable. (The discrepancies between the Barnstable and Falmouth records are noted.)
2 CONT *4. I. .... etc.
2 CONT *'''8. V. Benjamin''', Sept. 7, 1655, June 6, 1656.
2 CONT *9. VI.  .... etc.
2 CONT *Pg.469
2 CONT *'''   8-7. Benjamin Hatch''' was a farmer. In 1729 he removed to Mansfield, Conn., and died there or in Tolland before the year 1736. '''He married three wives:''' 1st Mary Hamblin, Jan. 17, 1678, a daughter of James, Jr., of Bar
2 CONC nstable. At the time of her marriage she had not completed her sixteenth year. She died early, and he married March 16, 1682, Elizabeth Eddy, who was born at Martha's Vineyard May 3, 1659. In another record her name is written Eli
2 CONC za. She was admitted to the Barnstable church July 14, 1710, and was dismissed to the church in Falmouth the following October, and died soon after. '''For his third wife he married Feb. 13, 1711-12, Experience, widow of Jabez Dav
2 CONC is, of Barnstable. She was a daughter of''' David Linnell, '''and died a widow Dec. 1736, aged about 72.
2 CONT *   Children of '''Benjamin Hatch''' born in Falmouth:
2 CONT *40. I. Abigail, Aug. 4, 1679.
2 CONT *Pg.470 is not part of this book preview. _____________________
2 CONT *'''The descendants of Moses and Sarah Kilham Porter of Pawlet, Vermont : with some notice of their ancestors and those of Timothy Hatch, Amy and Lucy Seymour Hatch, Mary Lawrence Porter and Lucretia Bushnell Porter     by Lawrenc
2 CONC e, John Strachan
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=cHEtAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA143&lpg=PA143&dq=benjamin+hatch+1686&source=bl&ots=7eJ-EvoZzs&sig=ECHakTwT_lstn8Aaw0lo0T0uc0E&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjZhqub2pHLAhVD8mMKHQCJC244ChDoAQhBMAo#v=onepage&q=benjamin%20
2 CONC hatch%201686&f=false
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/descendantsofmos00lawr
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/descendantsofmos00lawr#page/n302/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.141
2 CONT *   Thomas Hatch, the true ancestor of our branch of the Hatch family, emigrated to Boston, Mass. in 1630, or early in 1634. The name of his wife was ''Grace,'' She was of Welsh descent. I think it probable her family name was Lew
2 CONC is, though that is uncertain. He was probably born about the year 1603, somewhere in the county of Kent, and probably in the town of Biddenden, near Cranbrook; but possibly at or near Sandwich on the sea coast. 
2 CONT *   They had two children, one son and a daughter. They were probably married about 1624, perhaps 1627. 
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/descendantsofmos00lawr#page/n304/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.142
2 CONT **JONATHAN HATCH of Falmouth. 
2 CONT *   Jonathan Hatch of Falmouth, son of Thomas and Grace Hatch of Barnstable, was born in England about 1625, and emigrated to America with his parents and resided with them at Boston, Yarmouth and Barnstable. He was of very robust
2 CONC  constitution and lived to a great age, it is said near 100 years. He married Sarah Rowley at Barnstable, April 11, 1646. 
2 CONT *   They had the following children: 
2 CONT **	1. .... etc.
2 CONT **'''	5. BENJAMIN'''. b. at Barnstable, June 6, 1655. 
2 CONT **	6. .... etc.
2 CONT *   He was one of the fourteen original purchasers of the township of Falmouth, removed there in 1660, and died there. His son, Moses, was the first child born in that town. He and his sons were large landholders in that town. He 
2 CONC died in 1711. 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/descendantsofmos00lawr#page/n306/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.143
2 CONT **'''BENJAMIN HATCH of Falmouth.
2 CONT *'''   Benjamin Hatch''' married Mary Hamblin, Jan. 17, 1678. 
2 CONT *   They had: 
2 CONT **	Abigail, born Aug. 4, 1679. 
2 CONT **	Mary, born March 3, 1681. 
2 CONT *   The first wife died and he married Elizabeth Eddy of Tisbury, March 31, 1682. 
2 CONT *   They had: 
2 CONT **	Nathaniel, born Feb. 7, 1684. 
2 CONT **	Benjamin, born Oct. 17, 1686. 
2 CONT **	John, born Feb. 16, 1689. 
2 CONT **	Elizabeth, born March 25, 1691. 
2 CONT **	Malatiah, born Oct. 4, 1693. 
2 CONT **	TIMOTHY, born Oct. 19, 1695. 
2 CONT **	Hannah, born May 7, 1698. 
2 CONT **	Eddy, born Aug. 2, 1700. 
2 CONT **	Solomon, born May 7, 1704. 
2 CONT *   All were born at Falmouth. 
2 CONT *'''   Benjamin Hatch''' was a cordwainer. He was of Harwich in 1729, and bought land in Mansfield, Tolland county, Connecticut, in October of that year and removed to Tolland or Mansfield. His sons, Benjamin lived in Brewster, Jo
2 CONC hn in Mansfield, TIMOTHY in Tolland, Eddy in Willington, Solomon in Falmouth and all died in those places, except TIMOTHY, who removed to Kent, Litchfield county, in 1739. I have no information as to the daughter. Benjamin Hatch. 
2 CONC Jr., married Sarah Bangs of Brewster, and died there, Feb. 14, 1769, aged eighty-three. Malatiah was lost at sea, probably unmarried. 
2 CONT *   The following is taken from minutes kindly furnished me by Mr. Mark B. Hatch (AAEAC), of Ponce, Porto Rico : 
2 CONT *'''   BENJAMIN HATCH''', born September 7, 1655 in Falmouth, Mass. (Barnstable record makes birth June 6, 1656;) died before 1736, either at Mansfield, or Tolland, Conn. '''He married three times'''; first to Mary Hamblin, who di
2 CONC ed early; second, to Elizabeth Eddy, March 16, 1682, who was born at Martha's Vineyard, May 3, 1659. She was admitted to the Barnstable church, July 14, 1710, and was dismissed to the church in Falmouth in 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/descendantsofmos00lawr#page/n308/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.144 
2 CONT *October, and died soon after. '''His third wife was Experience, widow of Jabez Davis of Barnstable, whom he married Feb. 13, 1711/12. 
2 CONT **FOURTH GENERATION.
2 CONT *   TIMOTHY HATCH, born at Falmouth, October 19, .1695, .... etc.
2 CONT
