2 CONT =Additional Data=
2 CONT Jabez Davis
2 CONT Born about 1663 in Barnstable, Barnstable, Massachusetts Son of John Davis and Hannah (Linnell) Davis
2 CONT Brother of John Davis Jr, Samuel Davis, Mary (Davis) Hinckley, Hanna (Davis) Jones, Benjamin Davis, Joseph Davis, Simon Davis, Dollar Davis, Mercy Davis, Timothy Davis and Ruth (Davis) Linnell
2 CONT Husband of Experience (Linnell) Hatch — married 20 Aug 1689 in Barnstable, Barnstable, Plymouth Colonymap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Father of Sarah (Davis) Sweetland, Nathan Davis, Bashaway Davis, Abigail (Davis) Barlow, Jacob Davis and Mercy Davis
2 CONT Died before 3 Oct 1710 before about age 47 in Barnstable, Massachusetts Baymap
2 CONT
2 CONT Jabez Davis born ___, was the son of John and Hannah (Linnell) Davis. [1] He married on August 20, 1689, Experience, daughter of David and Hannah (Shelley) Linnell. [1] [2] [3]  Experience's mother, the widow Hannah Linnell, wrote
2 CONC  her will February 2, 1708/9 and it was proved the following April 5th. In it she mentions Experience, wife of Jabez Davis. [2]  He died between September 29, 1710 (the writing of his will) [4] and October 3, 1710, (the inventory 
2 CONC of his estate.) His estate was valued L538 16s 8d with debts due at L38 15s and L3 8s. [5] His will was written on September 29. 1710 and on January 3, 1710/11, his witnesses gave oath to his signing. In it he names: [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT sons Nathan, Isaac, Jacob, Samuel and Solomon
2 CONT daughters Bathshena, Abigail and Mary
2 CONT wife Experience sole executrix [4]
2 CONT In the will of his brother Samuel, dated June 25, 1711, he mentions Samuel, son of my brother Jabez, deceased. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT After his death, his widow Experience married Benjamin Hatch on February 13, 1711/12, as his third wife. [6]
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1719 distribution of his brother Benjamin Davis' estate, their were nine lots divided among his siblings, including one lot to the heirs of Jabez Davis. [7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Barnstable Births
