1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Lieut. Nathan Davis=
2 CONT * BIRTH 2 Mar 1690 Barnstable, Barnstable County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 17 Dec 1785 (aged 95) Harwinton, Litchfield County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Old Cemetery, Harwinton, Litchfield County, Connecticut, USA 
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID  78194676  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT Lieut. Nathan Davis was born on 2 March 1690 in Barnstable, Barnstable, Province of Massachusetts Bay, the son of Jabez and Experience (Linnell) Davis.  He married Elizabeth Phinney, daughter of John and Sarah (Lumbart) Phinney on
2 CONC  25 November 1714 in Barnstable, MA.  Their first four children were recorded in Barnstable by 1720.  Nathan died 17 September 1785 aged 96 years and was buried in the Old Cemetery in Harwinton, Litchfield, Connecticut.  Elizabeth
2 CONC  died on 30 June [or July] 1786, in her 97th year, and was buried next to Nathan. They were married 73 years. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Obituary==  
2 CONT Lieut. Nathan Davis "Died, at Harwinton, on the 17th of September ... in the 97th year of his age; leaving his wife a widow, and in the 97th year of her age, with whom he had lived 73 years in a married state. He was a man tempera
2 CONC te in his diet—laborious in his calling—a lover of his country and friends—and lived and died a good moral Christian; has left behind a numerous offspring, &c.
2 CONT ''Who then to vain mortality shall trust,
2 CONT But limns in water, or but writes in dust!''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Jabez Davis 1664–1710
2 CONT Experience Linnell Davis 1664–1736
2 CONT
