2 CONC , > on 25 November 1714. [2] Their first four children were recorded in Barnstable by 1720.[2]  Nathan died 17 September 1785 aged 96 years and was buried in the Old Cemetery in Harwinton, Litchfield, Connecticut.[3][4][5] Elizabe
