1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Hannah Woodward Lyman Swetland=
2 CONT * BIRTH 13 Sep 1708 Lebanon, New London County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 12 Feb 1781 (aged 72) Lebanon, New London County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL East Cemetery, Manchester, Hartford County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 248623002
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT When Hannah Lyman was born on 13 September 1708, in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut, United States, her father, Richard Lyman IV, was 30 and her mother, Mary Woodward, was 30. She married Joseph Swetland on 9 November 1732, in Le
2 CONC banon, New London, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America. They were the parents of at least 3 sons and 3 daughters. She died on 12 February 1781, in her hometown, at the age of 72, and was buried in Lebanon, New London, Con
2 CONC necticut, United States.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT Not to be confused with Hannah Lyman Vassar College's first Lady Principal, was born January 29, 1816 in Northampton, Massachusetts
2 CONT
