1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for CONNECTICUT with the rank of PRIVATE.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A111954  DAR Ancestor # A111954]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Pvt. Israel Swetland=
2 CONT
2 CONT When Israel Swetland was born on 12 January 1736, in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America, his father, Joseph Swetland, was 25 and his mother, Hannah Lyman, was 27. He married Dorcas Dewey on 6 May 175
2 CONC 6, in Coventry, Windham, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America. They were the parents of at least 4 sons and 2 daughters. He died on 8 February 1803, in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut, United States, at the age of 67.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT "We will pass by these old records and come down to later dates I  have the name of Israel Swetland. I failed to find the date of his birth or  his death, but the records state that he was the father of my grandfather.  His first 
2 CONC wife was Dorcas Dewey, their children were Theophilus and  Jacob and Mercy. His second wife was Mary Miner, their children were  Lurana, Israel and Hannah. Israel gave to his son Theophilus a portion  of his estate, the considerat
2 CONC ion was his good will and affection for him." [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Israel Swetland was a soldier in the Revolutionary War serving under Colonel Canfield's regiment of militia at West Point in September, 1781. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT This is the ancestor used by Martha Hall Butler to justify her membership in the Daughters of the American Revolution (DAR). She spells his name Israel Sweatland. Her application, dated Sept. 19, 1912, states that her 
2 CONT
