1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Pvt. Rufus Rood=
2 CONT * BIRTH 5 Jul 1719 Lebanon[1] Norwich[2], New London County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 12 Apr 1779 (aged 59) Royalton, Windsor County, Vermont, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL South Royalton Village Cemetery, South Royalton, Windsor County, Vermont, USA 
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 35313691  
2 CONT
2 CONT Revolutionary War Veteran; http://www.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~vtcroyal/Cemeteries.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Pvt. Rufus Rood, son of Jabez Rood and Mehitable Standish Rood, b. July 5, 1719, Lebanon, CT d. Apr. 12, 1779, Roy. ; m. Dec. 29, 1743, Lebanon, Conn., Abigail Standish, whose line of descent was Samuel [3], Josiah [2], Myles [1] 
2 CONC ; d. Aug. 31, 1747; m. (2) Feb. 14, 1750-51, Sarah Swetland of Norwich, Conn., b. 1719; d. June 3, 1803, Roy.; both bur. S. Roy. Cem, It is not known whether Mr. Rude took up land in Royalton or not, but his widow was at first giv
2 CONC en a right when the charter was granted in 1781, She probably had a home with her daughter, Mrs. Elias Stevens, after the death of her husband. Mr. Rude was the moderator at the first meeting that is on record relating to the town
2 CONC  of Royalton. In the 10th Co., 8th Conn. Cont. Regt., 1775, a Rufus Rude was private. The Rufus Rude named in Capt. Joseph Parkhurst's Co. in 1780, was probably his son, Rufus. 
2 CONT There may have been still other children than those that follow. i. Asa, b. Oct. 13, 1744, Lebanon, Conn.; d. Aug. 28, 1762. ii. Abigail, b. Oct. 28, 1746; m. Simeon, son Simeon and Sarah (Hutchinson) Curtis; ch.: (a) Asa, b. Oct.
2 CONC  13, 1770; d. Mar. 15, 1771, Tunbridge, Vt.; (b) Asahel, b. Apr. 22, 1772; (c) Amzi, b. Jan. 25, 1775; d. Apr. 28, 1777; (d) Amzi, b. May 18, 1777; (e) Abigail, b. Mar. 14, 1779; (f) Simeon, b. May 27, 1781; (g) Abel, b. Feb. 20, 
2 CONC 1785; m. Mar. 13, 1810, Sarah Brigham of Tunbridge. Ch. all b. in Tunbridge. iii. Rufus, b. Dec. 4, 1751, Lebanon, Conn. * iv. Sarah, b. Oct. 9, 1753; m. Gen. Elias Stevens. If Rufus Rude was the son of Jabez, his line of descent 
2 CONC through his mother was Mehitable (Josiah [3], Josiah [2], Capt. Myles [1]) Standish.
2 CONT
