1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Hannah Tiffany Swetland=
2 CONT * BIRTH 12 Apr 1738 Lebanon, New London County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 8 Jan 1809 (aged 70) Kingston, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Forty Fort Cemetery, Forty Fort, Luzerne County, Pennsylvania, USA
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 26691766 Add Photos by Kurt D. Moser
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah (Tiffany) Swetland was the daughter of Thomas and Mercy (Reed) Tiffany, Jr. She was the wife of Luke Swetland. They were married Warren Township, Litchfield Co., Pennsylvania April 1, 1762. Luke died June 30, 1823.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Obituary==
2 CONT SWETLAND.--Died in Kingston on the 8th of January, 18O9, Hannah Swetland, the wife of Luke Swetland, aged 7O years, 9 months, 6 days, having for several years past been feeble and on the decline. A few months before she died, she 
2 CONC was obliged to quit all desires and was attended by a physician; she was but a few days confined to her bed. She often spoke of her departure with a longing desire to be conformed to God's holy will and pleasure. She was singular 
2 CONC in her moral virtues, faithful, and modest in deportment; a faithful, prudent, discreet and loving wife, a kind and tender mother; she much delighted in Christian conversation, and public and private worship of God. She was remark
2 CONC edly friendly and charitable to her neighbors. Her death is much lamented by a large circle of friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inscription'''
2 CONT In Memory Of
2 CONT Hannah Swetland
2 CONT who departed this life
2 CONT January 8, 1809
2 CONT Aged 70 y'rs
2 CONT & 9 mos 6 dys
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Thomas Tiffany 1692–1768 
2 CONT Mercy Reed Tiffany
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Luke Swetland 1729–1823
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Bethia Tiffany Eaton 1721–1748
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Belding Swetland 1763–1816
2 CONT Artemas Swetland 1769–1855
2 CONT Eli Swetland 1771–1777
2 CONT John Swetland 1777–1777
2 CONT
2 CONT ==References==
2 CONT 1. https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/26691766/hannah-swetland
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. The Luzerne Federalist and Susquehanna Intelligencer Friday Evening, January 20, 18O9
