1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Mary Babcock===
2 CONT * Birth:  Jan 28 1681, New London Co, CT, USA 
2 CONT * Death:  Mar 10 1721, New London Co, CT, USA 
2 CONT * Inscription: Wife of John Sprague & daughter of Jonathan Babcock of Windham
2 CONT * Burial: Old Cem, Lebanon, New London Co, CT, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternate death dates: March 10, 1721 vs. January 5, 1720
2 CONT -------
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr08/rr08_305.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Family of Mary Curtis (6819) & Jonathan Babcock
2 CONT
2 CONT Iii.  Mary Babcock. Born on 28 Jan 1680/1 in Milton, MA. Mary was baptized in the Second Church of Scituate, on 21 Jun 1681.105,43 Mary died in Lebanon, CT, on 5 Jan 1721/2; she was 40.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 22 Feb 1710/1 when Mary was 29, she married John Sprague, son of Lieut. John Sprague (ca 1656-6 Mar 1727/8) & Lydia (-18 Jul 1725), in Lebanon, CT. Born ca 1690 in Duxbury, MA. John died ca 1763 in Canaan, CT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include:
2 CONT *. Jonathan Sprague (30 Apr 1716-17 Jan 1807)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 43. George Lincoln, et al., History of the Town of Hingham, Massachusetts, published by the Town of Hingham, 1893, Online edition at USGenWeb Hingham, http://plymouthcolony.net/hingham/history/contents.html. 105. “Scituate Births,
2 CONC  marriages, and deaths,” transcribed by George Ernest Bowman, Mayflower Descendant, various volumes, Vol. 1 (1899) 42-47, 106-110, 164-168, 233-238, http://archive.org/details/mayflowerdescend00mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. New England Families Genealogical and Memorial, New York: n.p., 1915 (William Richard Cutter).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
