2 CONT John  3. Son of Daniel 2, and grandson (jf Thomas 1; Mnlden; m.  Rcth Basset;  she and her sister Lydia, who m. his brother Daniel, were daughters of Joseph Basset, son of the fiist comer, William, who came over in ihe Fortune in 
2 CONC 1621, lived at Dnxbury, Mass., in 1637, and was representative from 1640 to 1644 inclusive; in 1652, with Gov. Bradford and others, he joined in the purchase of Dartmouth, and removed to Bridge water, and d. there in 1667.  Issue,
2 CONC   i.  John,  of Leicester; b. Sept. 12, 1694; ii.  Jeremiah.*  [See III.] iii.  Benjamin  ; m. Sarah Kendall, 1723 ; iv. Patience, m. Timothy Lamsou; v.  David.  April 6, 1706: m. Alice Kendall, of Bedford, Mass., March 11th, 1730
2 CONC -1; he was then of Boston; vi. Deborah, March 1, 1707-8;  Pelatiah,  Oct. 30, 1710; of Dunstable.
