1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Nathaniel OLIVER
2 CONT * Birth:	8 Mar 1651/2, Boston Suffok MA
2 CONT * Father: Peter OLIVER (1616-1670)
2 CONT * Mother: Sarah NEWGATE (1621-1692)
2 CONT * Spouse: Elizabeth BRATTLE
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Member of the Massachusetts legislature, circa 1696.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Gerald Warren's book, BOSTON 1689-1776 (pages 51-54):
2 CONT
2 CONT After 1692 he had been deeply involved in Phips's fraudulent use of the Vice-Admiralty Court for personal gain.  Whenever the Customs Office had seized a vessel for violation of England's Navigation Acts, Phips as Judge of the Vic
2 CONC e-Admiralty Court would dutifully condemn the ship and its cargo.  But instead of auctioning the ship and cargo publicly, Phips privately sold the condemned property for a pittance to Oliver. Oliver would then sell the vessel and 
2 CONC cargo as a private individual and give eleven-sixteenths of the proceeds to Phips. thus cheating the Crown.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
