2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethia Eyre was born on July 24, 1695 and baptized on July 28, 1695 in Boston, Suffolk County, Massachusetts Bay.[1]
2 CONT Bethiah, daughter of John Eyre & Katherine, was born on 24 July 1695 in Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethia Eyre married John Walley on March 18, 1713 in Boston, Suffolk County, Massachusetts Bay.[1][3]
2 CONT Bethia married John Walley on 18 March 1713 in Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Religion
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethia Walley was a member of Old South Church on March 17, 1713 in Boston, Suffolk County, Massachusetts Bay.[5][6]
2 CONT Issues
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Bethia Eyre and John Walley:
2 CONT Rev. John Walley (1716)
2 CONT Katharine Walley (1719)
2 CONT Sarah Walley (1722)
2 CONT Bethia Walley (1724)
2 CONT Thomas Walley (1725 - 1806)
2 CONT Elizabeth Walley (1731)
2 CONT Mary Walley (1733)
2 CONT Died
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Bethia Walley died on January 21, 1747 in Boston, Suffolk County, Massachusetts Bay.[7]
