1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT From History of the Military Company of the Massachusetts, Now Called ..., Volume 1 By Oliver Ayer Roberts [https://books.google.com/books?id=VycMAQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA256&ots=htdJylPoKZ&dq=Bethiah%20(Brattle)%20Parsons&pg=PA256#v=onepag
2 CONC e&q=Bethiah%20(Brattle)%20Parsons&f=false Page 256]
2 CONT
2 CONT >Joseph Parsons (1679), of Boston, merchant, married Bethia Brattle, daughter of Capt. Thomas (1675). They had four children, all of whom died young; the mother herself dying July 4, 1690, ten days after her last child died.
2 CONT >Mr. Parsons (1679) was a member of the patriotic council for the overthrow of Andros in 1689, and was made a freeman in March, 1690.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Of Joseph Parsons (1679), the father, after the death of the last of his family, nothing has been learned, except that he was alive in 1720.
2 CONT
2 CONT Authorities: Savage's Gen. Diet.; Harris's Descendants of Thomas  Brattle [https://archivhttps://archive.org/stream/accountofsomeofd1867harr#page/26/mode/2up page 27], Harris's Descendants of Thomas  Brattle [https://archive.org/s
2 CONC tream/accountofsomeofd1867harr#page/28/mode/2up page 28]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From Harris's Descendants of Thomas  Brattle 
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Thomas was appointed administrator of his estate April 
2 CONT 12, 16S3. The first division was made March 13, 16S3-4, "wherein  two eighths of the whole were set off to son Thomas, while Nat.  Oliver, John Eyre and Joseph Parsons, in right of their wives,  receive for their portion the iron 
2 CONC works at Concord, a farm of three  hundred acres at Rumney Marsh (Chelsea), eight acres of pasture  land near Sentry Hill, Boston, a house and land occupied by John  Marion, Jr. near the common or training field, £549.4.7 in debts
2 CONC ,  and an interest in lands at Narraganset, Queboug and Kennebec.  All of his real estate, comprising what was known as "Brattle  Close," except a small portion se-t off to his son William, passed  into the possession of his son T
2 CONC homas. The estate was appraised  at £7827.16.10, and, says Savage, was probably the largest inNew  England. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-661559141/joseph-parsons-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 13 2017, 3:59:50 UTC''
