1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Mary Legg''', daughter of Col. John Legg, Jr. and Elizabeth Peach was born January 06, 1676/77 in Salem, Essex Co, Massachusetts and died after 1740.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 
2 CONT *1) 23 March 1692-3 to Edward Brattle (d 1719), son of Thomas Brattle & Elizabeth Tyng; 2 children.
2 CONT *2) on  20 Sept., 1722 to Nathaniel Norden (d betw 1724-1728), son of Samuel Norden and Joanna Copp; his 2nd wife; he was Jane Latimer's widower.  No children.
2 CONT *3) on  24 June 1728 to Edmund Goffe (d 1740), son of Samuel and Hannah Bernard; his 2nd wife; he was Hannah Lynde's widower.  No children; Mary, his widow, survived.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with 1st husband:
2 CONT * 37. Mary, who married, March 20, 1712, James Smith, merchant of Boston, and probably died without issue before her father, as he does not name her or any child of hers in his will.
2 CONT * 38. Thomas, b. Sept. 17, 1695, bapt. at Old South Sept. 20, 1696, died young
2 CONT
2 CONT {{//s3.amazonaws.com/photos.geni.com/p13/71/69/82/46/5344484292b1fd43/edward_brattle_large.jpg|frame|center}}
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From Lieutenant Joshua Hewes: A New England Pioneer, and Some of His ..., Volume 1 By Eben Putnam [https://books.google.com/books?id=8W4-AQAAMAAJ&lpg=PA555&ots=2v4qzpZqek&dq=Samuel%20Norden%20joanna%20copp&pg=PA555#v=onepage&q=Sam
2 CONC uel%20Norden%20joanna%20copp&f=false page 555] "He [Capt. Nathaniel Norden] was married to JANE LATTIMER, a daughter of Christopher Lattimer of Marblehead, prior to 1686. She died 20-2-1722, and he married again 20 Sept., 1722, ''
2 CONC 'MARY LEGG''', then widow of Capt. Edward Brattle, and who after his death married, 24 July, 1728, Col. Edmund Goffe of Cambridge."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From Biography – GOFFE, EDMUND – Volume II (1701-1740) – Dictionary of Canadian Biography. (2017). Biographi.ca. Retrieved 13 February 2017 [http://www.biographi.ca/en/bio/goffe_edmund_2E.html link]
2 CONT
2 CONT GOFFE, EDMUND, soldier and politician; b. c. 1670 at Cambridge, Mass., son of Samuel and Hannah (Bernard) Goffe; married Hannah Lynde, daughter of Samuel Lynde, in May 1696; was married, a second time, 24 June 1728, to Mrs. Mary N
2 CONC orden, widow of Colonel Nathaniel Norden of Marblehead, Mass.; d. 16 Oct. 1740, at Cambridge, without issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
