2 CONT
2 CONT [https://books.google.com/books?id=_P1v1mqnsOYC&lpg=PA160&ots=pnyrYMvscc&dq=Thomas%20gray%20of%20Wapping%201625&pg=PA160#v=onepage&q=Thomas%20gray%20of%20Wapping%201625&f=false "Will of William Cottemore of Wapping"], written 5 Ju
2 CONC ne 1626.  Genealogical Gleanings in England, NEHGR, page 160
2 CONT
2 CONT >Rowland Coytemore of Wapping in the County of Middlesex, mariner, 5 June, 1626, proved 24 November 1626 by Katherine Coytemore, relict and executrix. To son Thomas Coytemore and his heirs, &c. the messuage or tenement, lands, her
2 CONC editaments and appurtenances in the manor of Milton in the parish of Prittlewell als. Pricklewell, in the County of Essex, now in the tenure and occupation of John Greene, &c. and my farm and copyhold land of forty four acres or t
2 CONC hereabouts, in the parish of Great Bursted in the County of Essex; wife Katheriue to have the use and rents until my son Thomas shall accomplish his age of one and twenty years. To my daughter Elizabeth Coytemore three score pound
2 CONC s at her age of one and twenty years or day of marriage, also the tenement or messuage known by the sign of the Blewboare in the town or parish of Retchford, in the County of Essex, now in the tenure of William Ashwell als. Hare. 
2 CONC To my son in law Thomas Gray* and his heirs my two copyhold tenements, &c. in Rederith ah. Rederiff, in the County of Surrey, now in the several occupations of Francis Welby and John Moore. If my children and children's children d
2 CONC ie before they accomplish their several ages of one and twenty or be married, then my aforesaid lauds shall remain, come and be unto my kinsman Hugh Hughs ah. Gwyn, my sister Elizabeth's son. To my grandson William Ball, son of Wi
2 CONC lliam Ball, forty shillings. To my daughter in law daughter Dorothy Lamberton forty shillings. To the poor of Wapping three pounds and to the poor of the Upper Hamlet of Whitechapel forty shillings. To the masters of Trinity House
2 CONC , for their poor, ten pounds within one year, &c.
2 CONT
2 CONT >My wife Katherine to be executrix and sons in law Thomas Gray and William Raiusborough of Wapping aforesaid, mariners, to be overseers. The witnesses were Raphe Bower pub. scr. and John Wheatley serve to the said scr. Hele, 125.
