2 CONT Notes for Thomas GREY
2 CONT
2 CONT Will names wife Katherine, daughter of Robert Myles, brother-in-law Thomas Wyseman, son Thomas, daughters Susan, Parnell, Katherine (all u18). He gave his wife a life estate, remainder in fee tail to Thomas, to be divided among hi
2 CONC s daughters if Thomas had no lawful heirs. If they had no heirs either, it went to Katherine’s heirs.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~amorrow/fg06/fg06_274.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Amelia Morrow, amorrow@post.harvard.edu at Rootsweb: 
2 CONT
2 CONT "She came to New England in 1636 or 1637 and settled in Charlestown, MA.  She came to America with her son, Thomas, and his wife, and her daughter, Elizabeth.  She was admitted to the church in 1638. Her will, dated Apr. 28 or 30,
2 CONC  1658, named 14 grandchildren, including the 5 children of her daughter, Katherine. She probably had 6 children.  Her son-in-law, Thomas Graves, and family probably came at the same time."
2 CONT
2 CONT NEHGS Register Vol. 138, p. 40-41 Genealogical Notes, MYLES
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine Myles, bap. Sutton, Suffolk, 17 Mar 1576; s. at Charlestown, MA, 29 Nov 1659. She m. (1) at Sutton, Suffolk, 30 Apr 1593 Thomas Gray, bap. Harwich, Essex, 18 Aug 1572, and bur. there 7 May 1607, ... She m. (2) ... at Har
2 CONC wich, Essex, 27 Dec 1610, Rowland Coytmore, who d. at Wappingbet 4 Jun 1626 (will) and 24 Nov 1626 (probate) Children by first marriage, surname GRAY: ... vii. Catheryn, bp. at Sutton, 30 Jun 1605; d. at Charlestown, MA, 21 Feb168
2 CONC 2/3; m. Thomas Graves, ...
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Has Children Joseph Graves b: 13 APR 1645 in Charlestown, Suffolk Co., MA
2 CONT
