1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=109570004
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Coytemore- Memorial
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	1612 Prittlewell Essex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Dec. 27, 1644, Spain
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Rowland Coytemore and Katherine Myles. Grandson of William Coytemore of Coetmore in Llechwedd, Uchav, Caenarvonshire, Wales and Jane Williams of Cochwillan, Wales, Robert Myles of Sutton, Suffolk and Parnel Reve. 
2 CONT
2 CONT After his father's death, his mother immigrated to New England in about 1636 with Thomas and his wife, followed by his sister, Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas was a sea captain, educated at Charlwood School, matriculated Christ's College, Cambridge, 1628. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Martha Rainsborough, daughter of Captain William Rainsborough and Judith Hoxton. They married at Wapping, Stepney, Middlesex on 14 June 1635, and had two sons and one daughter; Thomas, William and Katherine. All three c
2 CONC hildren died in infancy. They immigrated to New England in 1636 and settled at Charlestown, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas was lost at sea off the Spanish coast 27 Dec 1644. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT   Katherine Myles Coytemore (1576 - 1659)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sibling:
2 CONT   Katherine Gray Graves (1605 - 1683)*
2 CONT   Thomas Coytemore (1612 - 1644)
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Body lost at sea Specifically: Lost at sea off the Spanish coast
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Anne Shurtleff Stevens Record added: Apr 26, 2013  Find A Grave Memorial# 109570004
