1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sweetland aka Swetland Sweatland: 
2 CONT
2 CONT The first of the family in America was William Swetland who came over in 1676 and settled at Salem, MA. From him and his wife Agnes, the line of descent is traced through their son Joseph, who married Mercy Babcock. He served as d
2 CONC eputy for the town of Hebron and was also an officer in the training band of the village.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married twice.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Sweetland-9
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 2 Feb 2020 | Created 14 Apr 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT William Sweetland (1646 - 1703)
2 CONT
2 CONT William Sweetland aka Swetland, Sweatland
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1646 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John Sweetland and Susanna (Unknown) Sweetland
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of William Swetland [half], Susanna Sweetland [half], Temperance Sweetland [half] and John Sweetland [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Agnes (Unknown) Sweetland — married 1 Aug 1676 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Agnes (Swetland) Lovett, Benjamin Sweetland, Peeter Swetland, Grace Swetland, John Oliver Swetland and Joseph E Sweetland
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1703 in Salem, New London, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Variants of surname: Sweetland, Sweatland, Swetland.
2 CONT
2 CONT William was born and died in Salem Village (known today as Danvers), Essex, Massachusetts.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Agnes (surname unknown) on 8 March 1675 in Salem.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Agnes 8 March 1675 in Salem, and they had 5 children (of whom we are more or less certain.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Below are some data and relevant sources from "Family with Sources" at 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LCF4-93F
2 CONT
2 CONT Title: William Swetland (and family), Ancestry and Descendants of Sylvanus Eaton (1900) Web page: http://archive.org/stream/ancestrydescenda00wigh#page/34/mode/2up Citation: Jane A Wight, _Ancestry and Descendants of Sylvanus Eato
2 CONC n, Jacob Swetland and Christopher Reynolds (1900) The Eddy Family Reunion at Providence (Two Hundred & Fiftieth Anniversary . . . _, 2d ed. (Boston: [J. S. Cushing], 1884); digital images _Internet Archive_ (accessed 2013), pp. 34
2 CONC -51, "Swetland or Sweatland Genealogy." Notes: Bibliographic note: This source was cited by Torrey for the William Swetland-Agnes marriage entry.
2 CONT
2 CONT This authored work generally does not provide references. Introduction to the article cites "record furnished by Eli Swetland of Springfield, Mass."
2 CONT
2 CONT The first generation of the article reports that William and Agnes Swetland "were probably born prior to 1650 and came from England or Sweden." Reports "they resided in Salem, Mass., in 1676 and in Salem, New London County, Conn. 
2 CONC in 1703. Child list reports four children as (quoting below):
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Peter^2 born July 1, 1676 No Family. [GJ note: July is struck through and Sept. Entered] 2. Grace^2 born March 8, 1679 [annotated to read 1679-80] 3. John^2 born July 1, 1681 [GJ note: July is struck through and Sept. entered] 
2 CONC 4. Joseph^2 born November 5, 1683 [GJ note: November is struck through and Jan. is entered; year annotated to read 1683-4.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sidney Perley (1858-1928), _The History of Salem Massachusetts, 1626-[1716], 3 vols, 3 (1928): 102; digital images, _FamilySearch_ (accessed 2013 via the FamilySearch catalog), entry for William Swetland. Notes: Bibliographic note
2 CONC : This source is referenced Torrey for the marriage of Simon Lovitt and Agnes. Torrey treated this wife as though she was the widow of William Swetland. If William Swetland and Agnes were living at New London County, Conn. in 1703
2 CONC , as B. S. Swetland claimed, then his widow could not have been Simon's wife as children were reported born to this couple before that date. See _Partial Genealogy of the Swetland Family_ (1908)
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnote entry about William Swetland, without further reference. Transcript follows.
2 CONT
2 CONT “William Swetland, born about 1646, married Agnes ----; she married, secondly, Simon Lovitt of Beverly, Oct 10, 1676: children 1. Peter, born Sept. 1, 1676, 2. Grace, born March 8, 1679-80, John, born Sept. 1, 1681; fisherman, liv
2 CONC ed in Marblehead in 1705; 34. Joseph, born Jan. 5, 1683-4. "
2 CONT
2 CONT Douglas Patrick Sweetland, _A partial genealogy of the Swetland / Sweetland / Sweatland family in America, 1560-2003_ (2003); digital images, FamilySearch (accessed 2013 via the FamilySearch Catalog), pp. 1-3 for "William [(3a)] S
2 CONC wetland," xix-xxi, "Preface to the 2003 revision" and xxv-xxvii, "Preface, 1998." Notes: Bibliographic note: This is one of several descendant genealogies that have been prepared. In this version, the author and his collaborator a
2 CONC cknowledge conflicts about the family of William Swetland and his ancestry. The basis for the "first section" (to p. 443) is said to be "Partial Genealogy" by B. S. Swetland (no date given), but new information is added to that ma
2 CONC terial.
2 CONT
2 CONT In this 2003 version, the wife of Simon Lovett is shown as the eldest child of William and Agnes (____) Swetland--Agnes, b. 1672 at Beverly, based on "…[convincing] data from Judith Leone Young-Thayer" (see para 4 p. xix").
2 CONT
2 CONT Name
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: William /Sweetland/[3][4][5] Name: William /Sweetland/ Found multiple versions of NAME. Using William /Sweetland/.
2 CONT
