2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT SWETLAND: The first of the family in America was William Swetland who came over in 1676 and settled at Salem, MA. From him and his wife Agnes, the line of descent is traced through their son Joseph, who married Mercy Babcock. He s
2 CONC erved as deputy for the town of Hebron and was also an officer in the training band of the village.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: William, m. Johanna Pummery. Aaron. m. Lois Allen, 
2 CONT
2 CONT served in the revolutionary war. Harmon, m. Rosamond Watrous. (p. 464)[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mercy Badcock, b March 15,1679, dau. of Jonathan and Mary (Curtis) Badcock; 
2 CONT
2 CONT m. February 13,1705, Joseph Sweetland of Milton, afterwards of Hebron, CT. (p. 4)[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Salem Births
2 CONT
2 CONT SWETLAND, Joseph, s. William and Agnes, 5: 11m: 1683. CTR (p. 333) [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Milton Births:
2 CONT
2 CONT BADCOCK, Marcy, dau. of Jonathan, March 15, 1679. (p. 2)
2 CONT
2 CONT Milton Marriages
2 CONT
2 CONT BADCOCK, Marcy and Joseph Swetland, both of Milton, Feb. 13, 1705. (p. 85)[4]
2 CONT
