1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Rootes, son of Josiah of Beverly, Mass. (See No. 4), b. a. 1646, in Beverly, Mass. He removed, probably in com pany with his uncle Richard, to Fairfield, Ct., where he had lands granted to him March 2, 1676, b
2 CONC y his kinsman Michael Try, who married the widow of his uncle Richard Rootes. From that place he went to Woodbury, about 1681 or '2. He purchased a house and lot of Samuel Hull, Feb. 22, 1686. He also purchased lands of Nicholas C
2 CONC amp, town attorney, Nov. 8, 1687, and various other parcels of land at later periods, till he became possessed of a large real estate.* He has been sup posed by some to have been the son of John Roote, Sr., of Farmington, but this
2 CONC  could not be, as John of Farmington deeded land to his son John of Westfield. [See note appended to No. 2801.] That the Woodbury branch descended from Jo siah of Beverly there is no room to doubt after the examination of the vari
2 CONC ous facts on record. In September, 1739, a power of attorney was given to Joseph Roots, son of John of Wood bury, by the brothers and sisters of the former, " to inquire into the rights belonging to John Root, Senior, lying within
2 CONC  the province of Mass. bay whether real or personal." This in quiry no doubt related to the remaining property belonging to the family there. The family names bestowed by John Roots upon his children are also strongly conclusive, 
2 CONC in connection with the other facts, as to the relationship. The spelling of the name with s final in the records of Woodbury, and in other old documents that have been examined by the compiler, is another evidence of the same. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Roots was m. to Dorcas . He d. May 25, 1723. She d. May 15, 1720.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: (Born mostly in Woodbury.) 
2 CONT * 11. I. John, bap. April, 1685, in Woodbury ; d. young. 
2 CONT * 12. II. Susanna, bap. April, 1685, in Woodbury, f. ; d. April 26, 1738. 
2 CONT * 13. III. Mary, bap. April, 168; ; m. Robert Warner. 
2 CONT * 14. IV. Josiah, bap. Mar. 1688, f. ; d. 1727. 
2 CONT * 15. V. Bethia, b. Dec. 1691 ; d. July 23, 1700. 
2 CONT * 16. VI. John, b. June 9, 1693, f. ; d. Aug. 3, 1757. 
2 CONT * 17. VII. Joseph, b. June, 1698, f. ; d. 1761. 
2 CONT * 1 8. VIII. Bethia, b. Feb. 7, 1703. 19. IX. Thomas, date of birth unknown, f. ; d. June 3, 1727 .
2 CONT
2 CONT https://books.google.com/books/reader?id=X6VPAAAAMAAJ&printsec=frontcover&output=reader&pg=GBS.PA52
2 CONT
