2 CONT "History And Genealogy Of The Families of Old Fairfield:" John Root b. about 1645, d. at Woodbury 25 May 1723 in 78th year...without much doubt is son of Josiah of Salem. Will of father Josiah Rootes dated 15 May 1683: "I give unt
2 CONC o my son John Roots Twenty shillings";
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 1. Woodbury Church Records; Childrens births are documented in Woodbury   Church Records.  John Rootes was admitted to Church at Woodbury  Sep. 1702; The name is also spelled Root;
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 2. "History Of Ancient Woodbury"-pg:675; Also pg: 77: "In 1702, a division of the meadow on Shepaug River was made to the landholders of Woodbury;" John Roots name is on the list.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 3. Will of father, Josiah Rootes, dated: 15 May 1683;  "Item I give unto  My son John Roots twenty shillings;"
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 4.Book: 974.69/F D2J:  "History And Genealogy Of The Families of Old Fairfield" by Donald Lines Jacobus: pg: 505; "Born about 1645, d. at Woodbury, 25 may 1723 in 78yr. He was nephew of Richard Root of Salem and Fairfield, 
2 CONC and without much doubt was son of Josiah of Salem, who came in the Hercules 1635. Josiah had son Josiah, and daus. Bethia and Susanna, names that were repeated among John's children; John married Dorcas Abbot, dau. of George Abbot
2 CONC  of Norwalk  (later of Woodbury); Her father's will named his dau. Dorcas Roots. Mrs Dorcas Root d. at Woodbury, 15 may 1720." On 16 Jan 1673 John Roots had land at Fairfield by gift from his uncle Michael Try.  (Michael Try being
2 CONC  (2) husband of Margaret (Margery) who M: (1) Richard Root, brother to Josiah Root;  Josiah being father of John.His uncle Michael's name is also given as Fry in New England marriages;
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 5; Woodbury (Conn.) church Records, 1702-1713: As found in The American Genealogist,  Volunw 21: copied by Donald Lines Jacobus:
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 6; Microfilm: 00016171: Probate records, 1719-1916: Connecticuit Probate Court (woodbury District) (main author): "The children & heirs of Mr John Roots, late of Woodbury, deceased, came to the court and presented an agreem
2 CONC ent representing the Estate of their honored father---under their hands & seals and acknowledged the same before the court, all of them being leagally capable of acting and was ordered to be recorded & is as followeth: We, the und
2 CONC ersigned names heretowith agree for a quiet & peacable agreement and settlement of the movable Estate of our Honored Father, John roots, late of Woodbury, deceased, and do agree as followeth: Viz: First: That Thomas & Joseph Roots
2 CONC  shall have the 2 oxen & Hurds that Joseph hath in present custody;  Two cows, one heffer, three young calfs, 2 two year old calfs, & one heffer, 2 2 year old calfs & one Steer, 1 year old---& eight sheep. upon the record thereof,
2 CONC  Thomas & Joseph do quist themselves from any further demands or claims to any one of our father's movable Estate; Next: We agree that Susanna Minor shall have 10 pounds out of the movable Estate, added to what her father formerly
2 CONC  gave her and that Mary Warner shall have 10 pounds added to what her father formerly gave her and also that Bethia Root shall have 10 pounds out of movable Estate of our honored father as foresaid and when the above summs are div
2 CONC ided to the above daughters, Susanna, Mary, & Bethia, that movable Estate that yet remains if any be, shall be equally divided between Josiah Roots, John Roots, Susanna Minor, wife of Joseph Minor, mary Warner, wife of Robert Warn
2 CONC er & Bethia Roots, and for the confirmation hereof to all-This ends the proceedings and is witnessed by us hereto & affix our hands & seals this 5th October, 1723; Signed by; Josiah Roots, John Roots, Thomas Roots, Joseph Roots, J
2 CONC oseph Minor, susanna Minor, Robert Warner, Bethia Warner. October 31, 1723: Each of ye persons hereunto signing and sealing, acknowledge their hands & seals before the court excepting Susanna Minor, who was not present.  Athony St
2 CONC oddard, Clerk:"
