1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lovett-1412
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail Lovett, probably born Mackerel Cove, then Salem, Essex County, Massachusetts Bay Colony, after 27 May 1659 (date sister of the same name died), the daughter of John Lovett and his wife, Mary ____.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail married (1) perhaps at Beverly, Essex County, Isaac Randall, probably born England. Isaac died before 23 April 1684.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She probably married (2) after 8 November 1686,[2] Thomas Woodbury, baptized Salem, 3 July 1667 (3 : 5m : 1667).[3] Thomas Woodbury was a joiner. He died before 22 August 1698, the date administration of his estate was granted to 
2 CONC his widow, Abigail.[4] Abigail submitted several inventories to the court. The inventory dated 23 December 1698 included "six acres of land adjoyning robert Bradfords and land of john louitts."
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail was pregnant with a child by John Ford of Beverly "gotten last October," when, as the widow of Thomas Woodbury, she married (3) "by an old man in Ipswich below the meeting house," before 26 March [1699/1700], Thomas Larcum
2 CONC , as his second wife.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Larcum was born Ipswich, Essex County, about 1651, the son of Modicai Larcum and his wife, Elizabeth _____, the widow of William Clarke.[6] Thomas' sister, Rebecca Larcum was married at Beverly, before 25 August 1695 to Joh
2 CONC n Standley, son of Bethiah (Lovett) Standley,[7] Abigail's older sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lovett-1412
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail Lovett married twice, 1st to the 2nd Thomas Woodbury, 4 children; 2nd to Thomas Larcom, son of Mordecai, as 2nd wife; 3 children. Abigail, widow of Thomas Larkum died between June 5 and August, 1740 (Robert Hale's record).
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://uneeke1.tripod.com/d5.html#i23969
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Woodbury (son of Thomas Woodbury & Hannah Dodge) married Abigail Lovett. He was christened on 5 May 1667 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts, USA and died on 22 Aug 1698 in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts, USA at age 31. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes: First Church Records of Beverly list Abigail as LOVETT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children from this marriage were:
2 CONT # 394 M   Simon Woodbury was born on 16 Jan 1688 in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts, USA and died in Feb 1688 in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts, USA. Notes: Simon, s. Thomas and Abigaile (Lovett), b. Jan. 16 1687-8. Beverly V.R. (Pg.
2 CONC  #391). Simon, s. Thomas and Abygaile, d. Feb. 26, 1687-8, a. abt. 6 w. Beverly V.R. (Pg. #618).
2 CONT #395 M  Samuel Woodbury was born on 7 May 1689 in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts, USA, was christened on 27 Sep 1691 in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts, USA, and died from Mar 1761 to 1762 in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts, USA at age
2 CONC  71. Notes: Samuell, s. Thomas [jr. C.RI] and Abigaile (Lovett), May 7, 1689. Beverly V.R. (Pg. #391). Samuel, bp. Sept. 27, 1691, 1st Church Records, Beverly, MA Essex Historical Collection Vol. #37; Pg. #200.Sam[ue]l, ____, 1762
2 CONC , a. 74 y. P.R.1. Beverly V.R. (Pg. #613).
2 CONT #392 F  Jemima Woodbury <twin> was christened on 27 Sep 1691 in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts, USA and died on 29 Mar 1704 in Wenham, Essex, Massachusetts, USA at age 12. Notes: Jemima, d. Thomas, jr., bp. 27 : 7m : 1691. C.RI Bev
2 CONC erly V.R. (Pg. #393). Jemina, d. Mar 29, 1704, Wenham V.R. (Pg. #225).
2 CONT #393 F Kezia Woodbury <twin> was christened on 27 Sep 1691 in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts, USA. 
2 CONT # 396 F Mary Woodbury was born on 26 Jan 1698 in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts, USA and was christened on 26 Jun 1698 in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT From Essex Institute Historical Collections, Volume 58 “Larcum.” Page 132-133 [https://books.google.com/books?id=nRkRAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA42&ots=aR6E1Nt619&dq=Mordecai%20Larcum&pg=PA133#v=onepage&q&f=true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Thomas2 Larcom (Mordecai1), was probably third son and born about 1661. He was a fisherman. He was
2 CONT married, first, to Hannah , by whom he had a son Thomas, recorded on the Manchester, Mass., records as born Feb. 16, 1694/5. He married, second, Abigail, widow of Thomas Woodbery, about 1699-1700. On March 24, 1714, he was appoint
2 CONC ed fence viewer, and on March 15, 1715/6, he was appointed to enforce the law relating to swine. He died March 30, 1718.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Aug. 19, 1718, Abigail Larcom, widow of Thomas Larkum, late of Beverly, husbandman, sells four and a half acres of land to her son-in-law, John Masury, who had married her daughter by her first husband, Keziah Woodbery. On July
2 CONC  18, 1727, widow Abigail Larcom sells land in Mackerel Cove to John Thorndike, cordwinder. Dec. 25, 1739, Abigail Larcum is pronounced non compos mentis by the Beverly selectmen, and Brackenbury Patch (son-in-law), Mark Morse (son
2 CONC -in-law), and John Standley (husband of Thomas Larcom's sister, Rebecca), sign bond given by Brackenbury Patch, who is appointed guardian. Widow of Thomas Larkum died between June 5 and August, 1740 (Robert Hale's record).
2 CONT
2 CONT Child by first wife: 
2 CONT *Thomas, b. Feb. 16, 1694/5; probably died young. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by second wife: 
2 CONT # Phebe, b. 1702/3; m. Nov. 11, 1729, Brackenbury Patch, who was b. May 17, 1705. They had five children. Two d. young; the others were Hannah, Sarah and Benjamin. Brackenbury Patch d. May or June, 1743. Phebe, bar. March 18, 1787
2 CONC , aged 84. Widow Phebe Patch was bapt. Aug. 2, 1772.
2 CONT # Jemima, b. 1704; int. of m. Nov. 5, 1727, to Mark Morse. On March 3, 1728, Jemima, wife of Mark Morse, bapt. He was bur. May 5, 1783. She d. May 20, 1797, aged 93. They had seven children, Mark, Thomas, Samuel, Christian, Hannah
2 CONC , David, Jemima.
2 CONT # Hannah, birth and death or burial not found; m. John Bradford (second wife), March 31, 1741. They had one child, Robert. John Bradford was b. Feb. 26, 1689/90. and d. March 29, 1751. She was bapt. July 15, 1753
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *"Massachusetts, Town Clerk, Vital and Town Records, 1626-2001," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:Q29L-8V4B : 10 February 2018), Thomas Woodburie in entry for Simon Woodburie, 26 Feb 1687
