1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Reynold Bush===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Birth: 1587 in Messing, Essex, England
2 CONT * Death: 1686 in Cambridge, Middlesex, Massachusetts
2 CONT * Father: Reynold Bush (1568 – )
2 CONT * Mother: Isabella Hall (1571 – 1612)
2 CONT * Siblings:
2 CONT * Samuel Bush (1590 - )
2 CONT * John W. Bush ( 1593 – 1662)
2 CONT * Jonathan Bush (1593 – 1670)
2 CONT * Spouse (1): Elizabeth Clench[1] m. Date unknown
2 CONT * Spouse (2): Susannah Lovett
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT BUSH,  Randolph, or Reynold, Cambridge,  propr. 1641. Mortg. land in 1644 and redeemed It in 1657. 
2 CONT
2 CONT - Pope's "Pioneers of Massachusetts"
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bush-386
2 CONT
2 CONT Reynold Bush was married twice. First to Elizabeth,[4] and secondly to Susannah Lovett.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Renold and Elizabeth had at least one known child:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Bush
2 CONT
2 CONT a fine was issued to "Jno." Bush and his father Renold dated 14th day 11th month 1655[11]
2 CONT
2 CONT it is suggested that this John Bush was the father of Joseph Bush from Newton Massachusetts[2] and of Samuel and Jonathan from Springfield/Westfield Massachusetts[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Renold Bush married Susannah Lovett on 2 September 1678 in Cambridge, Middlesex, Massachusetts.[14]
2 CONT
2 CONT Renold and Susannah had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Hannah Bush b 1682 [4]. Married George Rood.
2 CONT # Unknown Bush b abt. 1684 [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Disputed Children
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son Reynold: It is sometimes proposed that Reynold had a son named Reynold who married Susannah Lovett, but the sources cited above accept that Reynold was "old" when he married Susannah.
2 CONT * Jonathan Bush (abt.1650-1739) may be a son or grandson of Reynold. A misreading of the 1655 fine to Reynold Bush and his son "Jno. Bush"[11] as "Jonathan Bush" had been interpreted that he had a son of this name.
2 CONT * John Bush (1633-1663) of Cambridge, may also be a son of Reynold[2]
2 CONT * Samuel Bush (abt.1642-abt.1733) Suggested by DeForest and Deforest[4]
2 CONT * Deborah Bush, wife of John MacCoone, suggested by DeForest and Deforest as a daughter or granddaughter[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===DNA testing===
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www.personal.psu.edu/users/g/a/gah4/BushDNA/EAnc.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Reynold Bush, baptized 1600 in Fering Parish, Essex Co, England, emigrated about 1640 to Cambridge, MA, d 1686 in Cambridge, MA, m 1625 in Essex Co, England to Elizabeth Clench. Son John Bush, b abt 1626, d 1663 in MA, m abt 1646 
2 CONC Elizabeth, d 1705 in Sudbury, MA. Abiel Bush (son of John and Elizabeth), b 1661 in Cambridge, MA, m 1688 in Marlborough, MA to Grace Barrett, b 1669 in Marlborough, MA, d 1739 in Marlborough, MA. B-007 is a 6g grandson of Abiel B
2 CONC ush.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bush-1785
2 CONT
2 CONT Reynold was the son of a yeoman farmer in Messing, Essex, a village that nowadays has one pub, one restaurant, no shops and 350 inhabitants. It's a place where the houses have names instead of numbers, and where streets are so few
2 CONC  that the main one through the village is officially called The Street.
2 CONT
2 CONT Essex is the county immediately east of London and Messing is set among gently undulating open fields of wheat, barley and rapeseed.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bush-2927
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-596116947/reynold-bush-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 16 2017, 6:36:37 UTC''
2 CONT * Note: Deborah Bush was probably the daughter of Randall (Reynold?) Bush (who d. 1 Nov 1662 Cambridge) and who came to Cambridge in 1641.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
