1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Mary Lovett
2 CONT * FamilySearch Family Tree
2 CONT * Birth:	Nov 29 1695 - Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts Bay, British Colonial America
2 CONT * Death:	1766 - Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts Bay, British Colonial America
2 CONT * Parents:	John Lovett III, Mary Lovett (born Pride)
2 CONT * Spouses:	John Cressey, Rev John Conant II
2 CONT
2 CONT John Conant (1) 30 Jan., 1713-4, Martha, dr. of Richard and Mary (Eaton) Dodge, of Wenham. She was admitted to First Church 8 Aug., 1714, and d. 5 Oct., 1721. Richard Dodge was son of Richard the immigrant.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. (2) 2 June, 1722, Mary (Lovett) Cressy, widow of John Cressy; she d 1766.
2 CONT
2 CONT His will is dated 28 May, 1754, proved 26 May, 1755; re- corded in Essex Co. Probate Records, Vol. 333, p. 44. He left a legacy to the second parish of Beverly, to which other suras were added in 1760, and a silver tankard for com
2 CONC munion service purchased. His will mentions: wife, Mary; sons, John, Samuel and Lot; daughters, Martha Friend, Bithiah Dodge, Sarah Waldron, Mary Baker and Elizabeth Conant. His cousin, Jonathan Conant, and son, Samuel, are appoin
2 CONC ted executors. The inventory of the estate was returned 8 July, 1755, and amounted to £628 15s. 8d.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Mary Lovett and John Cressey:
2 CONT #John Cressy
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Mary Lovett and John Conant:
2 CONT #Elizabeth, b. 6 May, bapt. 9 June, 1723.
2 CONT # Sarah, b. 20 July, 1725 (bapt. 18 July, 1725V); ni. Waldron.
2 CONT #Mary, b. 31 Aug., bapt. 3 Sep., 1727; m. Baker.
2 CONT # 85. Samuel Conant, b. 14 Apr., bapt. 19 Apr., 1730
2 CONT #Benjamin Conant, b. 9 Apr., 1732 (bapt. 2 Apr., 1732?); d. 16 May, 1736
2 CONT #  86. Lot Conant, b 2 Oct., bp 9 Nov 1735 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
