2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter was born, perhaps at Spurwink, Cumberland County, then Massachusetts Bay, about 1681. He is presumed the son of Peter Shaw and his wife, Jane (Allison) (Shaw) (Bradford) Leach[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married at Beverly, Essex County, 14 October 1705 (intention), Bethia Lovett. [2][3] She was baptized at Beverly 4 June 1682,[4][5] the daughter of John^2 Lovett and his wife, Bethia Rootes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter died 28 August 1709,[6] and Bethia married again, at Beverly, 6 September 1711, Nehemiah Hayward.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Shaw, baptized 1708.[7]
2 CONT Bethiah Shaw, christened in 1709.[8]
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT One Peter was christened at England, 29 Jun 1681 to a father William [9]
2 CONT
