1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Nehemiah Hayward 
2 CONT * AKA Haward 
2 CONT * Born 10 Jul 1670 in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT * Died 1756 at about age 85 in Reading, Middlesex, Province of Massachusetts bay
2 CONT * Son of Nathaniel Hayward and Elizabeth Corning
2 CONT * Husband of Ruth (Clarke) Hayward — married 12 Jan 1693 in Marblehead, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT * Husband of Bethiah (Lovett) Hayward — married 6 Sep 1711 in Beverly, Essex, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hayward-371
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth (Clarke) Hayward was born about 10 May 1674 in Marblehead, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colony, and baptized on 10 May 1674 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colony at the First Church of Salem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth was mentioned in her father Matthew Clark's will of 24 Sep 1684.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth married Nehemiah Hayward (1670 - 1756) on 12 Jan 1693 in Marblehead, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colony.[2] They were then residing in Beverly, Essex, Massachusetts Bay Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Abigail (Hayward) Dodge (1 Sep 1695 - )[3]
2 CONT # Dr James Hayward (1698 - 1738)[4]
2 CONT # Ruth Hayward (1705 - )[5]
2 CONT # Nehemiah Hayward (1709 - ).[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth died in 1710 in Beverly aged ~36.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethia was born about 1682. She was christened in 4 Jun 1682. Her parents were John Lovett and Bethia (Rootes) Lovett. [1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethia was married to (2) Peter Shaw on 14 October 1705 in Beverly, Essex County, Massachusetts. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Bethia Lovett and Peter Shaw: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Peter b 1706/7 [4] He was christened in 1708. [5]
2 CONT # Bethiah b 1709. [6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her first husband died about 1709.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married (2) Nehemiah Howard/Haward in 1711. [7] Vital Records of Beverly, Massachusetts, to the end of the year 1849, 2 vols. (1906-1907) 2:273 (Shaw); digital images, Trust ; she is Bethiah Shaw; he is "Nehemiah Haward of Sal
2 CONC em.";
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Bethiah Lovett and Nehemiah Hayward, all 6 born or christened in Beverly Massachusetts: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Josiah b 1712. [8]
2 CONT # Jabez c 1714. [9]
2 CONT # Elmira c 1717. [10]
2 CONT # Eunice b 1717. [11]
2 CONT # Andrew b 1719. [12]
2 CONT # Rose b 1722. [13]
2 CONT
2 CONT In Bethia's father's will from 1723 John Lovit refers twice to the surname "Howard." First to "my Daughter Bethia Howard" and second, to "my [son] in Law Nehemiah Howard."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
