2 CONT Profile last modified 7 Jun 2022 | Created 21 Jul 2017
2 CONT This page has been accessed 1,379 times.
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [hide]
2 CONT 1 Biography
2 CONT 1.1 Children
2 CONT 2 Research Notes
2 CONT 3 Sources
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT William Bradford, brother of Robert Bradford,[1] was born about 1639; he died at Beverly, Essex County, Massachusetts, 15 June 1717, aged about 78.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT William married at Beverly, 14 Nov 1676, Rachel Raymont. She was born Salem, 14 : 12 m : 1659 [14 February 1659],[3] baptized Beverly, 13 November 1670,[4] the daughter of John Rayment and his first wife, Rachel Scruggs.
2 CONT
2 CONT William and Rachel Bradford, and Rachel's cousin, William Rayment, Jr., testified in the Salem Witch Trials, regarding accuser, Mercy Lewis. Key parts of the court record are unreadable. From the record,[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT [--damaged--] william Bradford & Rachell his wife [--damaged--] [t]hat a bout two years and half since Mercy [--damaged--] listed persons did Live with us about [--damaged--] quartes of ayear: & we did then Judg that [--damaged--]
2 CONC  [m]atter of consione of speaking the truth [--damaged--] and untruth she would stand stifly to [--damaged--] William Rayment Junior testifieth [--damaged--] the above s'd Marcy Leuis I Knew her when [--damaged--] of my neighbours
2 CONC  and I all wayes took her to [--damaged--] as the above writen evidences hath decribed
2 CONT Rachel (Rayment) Bradford died, probably Beverly, before 1 February 1696/7, for on that date, her father John Rayment senr, yeoman, deeded "for & in consideration of mine own love & affection unto my son in law william Bradford of
2 CONC  Beverly, husbandman, "& ye love I bear unto the chilldren of his by his former wife my Daughter Ratchell," a twenty acre parcel of "Upland & swamp Ground situate ... in ye Township of Beverly" and "one Mare & two Cows & some othe
2 CONC r moveable goods of mine," which are already in his possession.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 30 December 1706, William Bradford was named administrator of his brother's estate. The inventory of Robert's estate, including 17-3/4 acres of upland and swamp ground, totalled £203 2s 8d. After the satisfaction of debts, the 
2 CONC estate was conferred upon "William Bradford of Beverly only surviving bro. of Robert Bradford ..."[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT William Bradford and his wife Rachel, were the parents of seven children, all recorded Beverly,
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachell Bradford, died 21 February 1677[/8][8]
2 CONT Abigaile Bradford, born 5 September 1682.[9]
2 CONT Rachell Bradford, born 13 July 1684[10]
2 CONT William Bradford, baptized 3 October 1686.[11]
2 CONT John Bradford, born 26 February 1689/90.[12]
2 CONT Bathia Bradford, born 20 June 1692.[13]
2 CONT Rebecca Bradford, baptized 11 March 1693/4.[14]
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother, not son, of Robert Bradford. By subscription, see AmericanAncestors for page 7 of the estate file, "William Bradford of Beverly only surviving bro. of Robert Bradford ..."
2 CONT
2 CONT A prior version of this profile treated Robert as William's father, "Proposed father may have been baptized 1621, although a recorded deposition implies 1626 (no primary source). Father's probate is Dec 1706, spouse at death is Ha
2 CONC nnah, m. abt 1672, no source provided for later deaths. A marriage of Robert and Hannah in Boston occurred early 1640's but is implied to be a different Robert."
2 CONT
2 CONT Age/date of birth. His estimated date of birth is based on the age reported in his Beverly death record, William [sr., June 16. C. R. ; 17, C. R. I.], June 15, 1717, a. abt 78 y."
2 CONT
2 CONT A William Bradford testified in 1694/5 that he was [about] age 70 (thus born about 1627).[15] The underlying record has not been reviewed to determine the identity of this William.
2 CONT
2 CONT Possible parentage. Of Robert and William Bradford's parentage, Scott Andrew Bartley (2006) wrote,[16] "It seems possibe the two brothers ... are the oldest children of Robert Bradford of Boston." And also, "This theory seems to f
2 CONC all apart when Robert deeds [in 1673] "out of my ffatherly affection I beare to my onely sone Moses Bradford." Further, "The only other possibility is that these are the unidentified chidren of John^1 Bradford of Dorechester as me
2 CONC ntioned only in the will of his brother Alexander^1 Bradford of Dorechester."
2 CONT
2 CONT Second wife? Walter Goodwin Davis reported William Bradford married a second time, to Jane (Allison) Shaw, daughter of Ralph Allison and his wife, Anne Dixon. Jane would have been the widow of Peter Shaw. See Ancestry of Bethia Ha
2 CONC rris ... (Portland, Me., The Southworth Press, 1934), 122; digital images, Hathi Trust.
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogical Dictionary of Maine and New Hampshire (part 5, p. 626), also refers to this Jane Allison, daughter of Ralph, writing that she married (2) William Bradford of Beverly, and (3) Robert Leach.
2 CONT
