2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT John Linnell
2 CONT
2 CONT John Linnell, son of David (b. 1627), married Ruth Davis, daughter of John Davis. He was a prudent industrious and respectable man. He resided a part of his life on his farm in the easterly part of Chequaquet now called Hyannis Po
2 CONC rt, and a part on the John Davis estate. He was one of the earliest who removed to South Sea, as the south part of the town was then called. He died Feb 7th (town record)1747-8 in the 78th year of his age, and his wife Ruth May 8,
2 CONC  1748 in the 75th year of her age.(p. 159). Both have monuments to their memory in the old graveyard.
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT John Linnell was born ca. 1670|1671, based on his age at death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: David Linnell, b. 1627
2 CONT Mother: Hannah Shelley on March 9, 1752-3[1].
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT John Linnel, son of David Linnell and Hannah Shelly, married Ruth Davis, daughter of John Davis (d. May 8, 1748 aged 75[2].)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children[3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thankful Linnell Bearse, b. Nov. 12, 1696, d. Jun. 7, 1759 ; m1 James Bearse ca. Nov 12, 1726 ;
2 CONT Samuel Linnell, b. Nov. 16, 1699; m. ca. 1725, to widow Hannah Scudder and had 6 children; d. Sept. 12, 1770[5]
2 CONT John Linnell, b. June 15, 1702; m. Mary Phinney on Oct 24, 1734.
2 CONT Bethia Linnell Bearse, b. May 14, 1704; m. Augustine Bearse (son of Benjamin) on 3rd June, 1728; d. Oct 7, 1743 (bef. July 5, 1748...father's will codicil)). He m2. Sept. 7, 1744, Thankful, widow of Nathaniel Bacon.
2 CONT Joseph Linnell, b. June 12, 1707; m. Dorcas Smith on Nov 26, 1747; removed to Yarmouth in 1755; had eight children.
2 CONT Hannah Linnell, b. July 10, 1709; spinster ca. July 5, 1748.
2 CONT Jabez Linnell, b. July 31, 1711; m1. Sarah Bacon on Nov 11, 1736; m2. Mrs. Sarah Sturgis on Sep 26, 1751. She died Jan 31. 1768 aged 54; He ahd eight children. (p. 160)[6]
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT John Linnell died Feb 7th (town record)1747-8 in the 78th year of his age [7]; his wife Ruth May 8, 1748 in the 75th year of her age.(p. 159)
2 CONT
2 CONT Wills
2 CONT
2 CONT In his will dated Oct. 1, 1717, proved 7th July 1748; he names his wife Ruth, and his daughters Thankful, Hearse, Bethia Bearse, and Hannah Linnel. In a codicil dated, July 5, 1748 he says his daughter Bethia is dead. To his daugh
2 CONC ter Hannah he gave his great chamber and privileges in the house so long as she remained single. To his son Samuel, the southwest part of his farm or homestead at South Sea; ; to his son John, 19 acres of upland marsh, to his son 
2 CONC Joseph, the remaining or easterly part, to his son Jabez, all his homesteded farm lands meadows and house wherein he then dwelt.(p. 159)[8][9]
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife Ruth owned real estate in her own right. In her will proved July 5, 1748; Ruth refers to her sister Mercy Davis, deceased, and to her unmarried daughter Hannah. She owned land on the east side of the Hyannis road adjoinin
2 CONC g Nathaniel Baker's formerly the property of her father. (p. 160)[10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
