2 CONT Note: John Davis lived in Barnstable, and died there in 1703; Was a Farmer and House -Carpenter. His name appears frequently in Barnstable town records in connection with transfers of real estate, negotiations with Indians, and in
2 CONC  other capacities. He took the oath of fidelity at Barnstable, 1657; was surveyor of highways in 1656,1671,1672,1675, and 1677; sole executor of his father's will 1673; on grand inquest, 1682: He owned considerable real estate at 
2 CONC  various places and settled portions of it on his sons during his own life. His will is dated May 10, 1701, and speaks of his wife as living, also of sons John, Benjamin, Samuel, Dollar, Timothy, and Jabez, of daughters Mercy, Rut
2 CONC h Lynnell, and Mary Hincley; also of Hannah Jones's  five children son John's four eldest sons, granddaughter Mary Goodspeed, and grandson Joseph Davis. Will proved April 9, 1703. Amount of inventory, 268 pounds 12 sixpence 4d. 
2 CONT
