2 CONT The Winthrop Society has documented Passengers of the Elizabeth Master: William Stagg Voyage of 1635:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Davies Age:  9 Date of Record 17 April 1635 Roll # 75  
2 CONT
2 CONT This table details the roll of passengers of the Elizabeth, which sailed from London in the latter half of April, 1635, bound for New England. The ship arrived safe at Massachusetts Bay. The rolls represent persons who were ready 
2 CONC to embark at the date of record, which often preceded the actual sailing by several weeks. This information was transcribed in the 19th century by James Savage, and later by Michael Tepper from records found in the Public Rolls Of
2 CONC fice, London.  Mary John's Sister was age 4 was a companion during the trip with John because they have consecutive roll numbers. http://www.winthropsociety.com/ships/elizabeth2.htm
