2 CONT *'''DAVIS, Bashaway 
2 CONT *b. 16 JAN 1693/4 
2 CONT *Family:
2 CONT *'''Marriage: 5 FEB 1712/3
2 CONT *'''Spouse: HATCH, Nathaniel 
2 CONT *'''b. 7 FEB 1683/4 Falmouth, Barnstable, Mass.
2 CONT *'''Parents:
2 CONT *Father: HATCH, Benjamin 
2 CONT *Mother: EDDY, Alice 
2 CONT *'''Children:
2 CONT **HATCH, Elizabeth 
2 CONT *From: http://www.genealogyofnewengland.com/f_2fa.htm#80 ___________
2 CONT *'''The descendants of Moses and Sarah Kilham Porter of Pawlet, Vermont : with some notice of their ancestors and those of Timothy Hatch, Amy and Lucy Seymour Hatch, Mary Lawrence Porter and Lucretia Bushnell Porter     by Lawrenc
2 CONC e, John Strachan
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=cHEtAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA143&lpg=PA143&dq=benjamin+hatch+1686&source=bl&ots=7eJ-EvoZzs&sig=ECHakTwT_lstn8Aaw0lo0T0uc0E&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjZhqub2pHLAhVD8mMKHQCJC244ChDoAQhBMAo#v=onepage&q=benjamin%20
2 CONC hatch%201686&f=false
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/descendantsofmos00lawr
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/descendantsofmos00lawr#page/n302/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.141
2 CONT *   Thomas Hatch, the true ancestor of our branch of the Hatch family, emigrated to Boston, Mass. in 1630, or early in 1634. The name of his wife was ''Grace,'' She was of Welsh descent. I think it probable her family name was Lew
2 CONC is, though that is uncertain. He was probably born about the year 1603, somewhere in the county of Kent, and probably in the town of Biddenden, near Cranbrook; but possibly at or near Sandwich on the sea coast. 
2 CONT *   They had two children, one son and a daughter. They were probably married about 1624, perhaps 1627. 
2 CONT *   JONATHAN, the son, was born in England, probably in 1625. Lydia, the daughter, was probably born about 1628. This implies that his wife, Grace, was born about 1604. It is said he was a tailor by trade. They probably lived in s
2 CONC ome village, possibly Cranbrook, or Sandwich. His wife, it is said, was the daughter of a farmer, and born and brought up on a farm and accustomed to the usual female labor of a farm at that period of time; among other things to a
2 CONC ssist in the harvesting or field labor in harvest time and was expert at it. Some anecdotes of them are preserved which show this. He was small, slender, and of feeble strength; she was robust strong and healthy. 
2 CONT *   Thomas Hatch was admitted a freeman of the colony of Massacliusetts Bay at Boston, May 14, 1634. 
2 CONT *   January 17, 1639, he became one of the nine original purchasers of Yarmouth township, Plymouth colony, on Cape Cod; and was admitted a freeman of that colony and removed to that place from Boston. 
2 CONT *   The nine proprietors were Anthony Thatcher, John Crome, Marmaduke Matthews, Thomas Hower, Philip Tabor, William Palmer, Samuel Rider, William Lump- 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/descendantsofmos00lawr#page/n304/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.142
2 CONT *kin and Thomas Hatch. See records of Plymouth colony, General Conrt, January 7, 1639, O. S. for the record of the grant. Part of these persons probably emigrated in the same ship with him, as they were made freemen at Boston with
2 CONC  him. 
2 CONT *   In 1640, he became an equal, or joint, proprietor of the township of Barnstable with about twenty-five other men. In June, 1641, he is described as "of Barnstable" in deeds and public records of the colony, and therefore had b
2 CONC ecome a resident of that town. He died there in the year 1661, a respected citizen. He was a member of the Congregational church of that town and probably was a member of that church before leaving England. 
2 CONT *   He was a man of considerable pecuniary means. He was a resident freeholder in Dorchester, Mass., May 14, 1634. 
2 CONT **JONATHAN HATCH of Falmouth. 
2 CONT *   Jonathan Hatch of Falmouth, son of Thomas and Grace Hatch of Barnstable, was born in England about 1625, and emigrated to America with his parents and resided with them at Boston, Yarmouth and Barnstable. He was of very robust
2 CONC  constitution and lived to a great age, it is said near 100 years. He married Sarah Rowley at Barnstable, April 11, 1646. 
2 CONT *   They had the following children: 
2 CONT **	1. Mary. (m. Weeks.) b. at Barnstable July 16, 1647. 
2 CONT **	2. Thomas. b. at Barnstable, Jan 1. 1649. 
2 CONT **	3. Jonathan. b. at Barnstable, May 16, 1652. 
2 CONT **	4. Joseph. b. at Barnstable, June 10, 1654. 
2 CONT **	5. BENJAMIN. b. at Barnstable, June 6, 1655. 
2 CONT **	6. Nathaniel. b. at Barnstable, Sept. 3, 1657. 
2 CONT **	7. Samuel. b. at Barnstable, Oct. 4, 1659. 
2 CONT **	8. Moses. b. at Falmouth, March 4, 1663. 
2 CONT **	9. Sarah. (m. Wing.) b. at Falmouth, March 23, 1665. 
2 CONT **	10. Mercy. (m. Rowley. b. at Falmouth, April 27, 1667. 
2 CONT **	11. Lydia. b. at Falmouth, May 16, 1669. 
2 CONT *   He was one of the fourteen original purchasers of the township of Falmouth, removed there in 1660, and died there. His son, Moses, was the first child born in that town. He and his sons were large landholders in that town. He 
2 CONC died in 1711. 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/descendantsofmos00lawr#page/n306/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.143
2 CONT **BENJAMIN HATCH of Falmouth.
2 CONT *   Benjamin Hatch married Mary Hamblin, Jan. 17, 1678. 
2 CONT *   They had: 
2 CONT **	Abigail, born Aug. 4, 1679. 
2 CONT **	Mary, born March 3, 1681. 
2 CONT *   The first wife died and he married Elizabeth Eddy of Tisbury, March 31, 1682. 
2 CONT *   They had: 
2 CONT **'''	Nathaniel, born Feb. 7, 1684. 
2 CONT **	Benjamin, born Oct. 17, 1686. 
2 CONT **	John, born Feb. 16, 1689. 
2 CONT **	Elizabeth, born March 25, 1691. 
2 CONT **	Malatiah, born Oct. 4, 1693. 
2 CONT **	TIMOTHY, born Oct. 19, 1695. 
2 CONT **	Hannah, born May 7, 1698. 
2 CONT **	Eddy, born Aug. 2, 1700. 
2 CONT **	Solomon, born May 7, 1704. 
2 CONT *   All were born at Falmouth. 
2 CONT *   Benjamin Hatch was a cordwainer. He was of Harwich in 1729, and bought land in Mansfield, Tolland county, Connecticut, in October of that year and removed to Tolland or Mansfield. His sons, Benjamin lived in Brewster, John in 
2 CONC Mansfield, TIMOTHY in Tolland, Eddy in Willington, Solomon in Falmouth and all died in those places, except TIMOTHY, who removed to Kent, Litchfield county, in 1739. I have no information as to the daughter. Benjamin Hatch. Jr., m
2 CONC arried Sarah Bangs of Brewster, and died there, Feb. 14, 1769, aged eighty-three. Malatiah was lost at sea, probably unmarried. 
2 CONT *   The following is taken from minutes kindly furnished me by Mr. Mark B. Hatch (AAEAC), of Ponce, Porto Rico : 
2 CONT *   BENJAMIN HATCH, born September 7, 1655 in Falmouth, Mass. (Barnstable record makes birth June 6, 1656;) died before 1736, either at Mansfield, or Tolland, Conn. He married three times; first to Mary Hamblin, who died early; se
2 CONC cond, to Elizabeth Eddy, March 16, 1682, who was born at Martha's Vineyard, May 3, 1659. She was admitted to the Barnstable church, July 14, 1710, and was dismissed to the church in Falmouth in 
2 CONT *https://archive.org/stream/descendantsofmos00lawr#page/n308/mode/1up
2 CONT *Pg.144 
2 CONT *October, and died soon after. His third wife was Experience, widow of Jabez Davis of Barnstable, whom he married Feb. 13, 1711/12. 
2 CONT **FOURTH GENERATION.
2 CONT *   TIMOTHY HATCH, born at Falmouth, October 19, .1695, .... etc. _______________________
2 CONT *'''The New England Historical & Genealogical Register and ..., Volume 14
2 CONT *https://books.google.com/books?id=ZAPVAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA198&lpg=PA198&dq=benjamin+hatch+1686&source=bl&ots=Gzzt6qGrA9&sig=p4eMH4-oybz2U8mRfpTGlClbCNw&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjZhqub2pHLAhVD8mMKHQCJC244ChDoAQhKMA0#v=onepage&q=benjamin%20
2 CONC hatch%201686&f=false
2 CONT *Pg.197
2 CONT *   THIS family, descended from Thomas Hatch, who was an immigrant as early as 1633-4; and was made a freeman .... died in 1661. His only son, Jonathan Hatch, was one of the purchasers .... etc.
2 CONT *   .... Mr Jonathan Hatch resided there until his death. He married Sarah Rowley, at Barnstable, April 11, 1646. His only sister Lydia, married Henry Taylor, .... etc.
2 CONT *   He had 11 children; 7 born in Barnstable, and 4 in Suckannessett;
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *Pg.198
2 CONT * 8 sons, and 3 daughters, viz.: (2) Mary,2 b. July 16, 1647;—(3) Thomas,2[†] b. Jan. 1, 1649; m. Abigail Codman, at Barnstable, Jan. or Feb. 22, 1679;—(4) Jonathan,2[†] b. May 16-17, 1652; m. at Barnstable, Abigail —— , per Fal. 
2 CONC rec. Sept. 4, 1676; or Eliza Walker, per Bar. rec. Dec. 4, 1676;—(5) Joseph,2[†] b. March 7, or June 10, 1654; m. per Fal. rec. Amy Allen, Dec. 7, 1683, per Bar. rec. Mary Allin, Dec. 7, 1689; had 4 sons and 6 daughters; and d. Fe
2 CONC b. 16, 1738, ae. 84 at Fal.;—(6) Benjamin,2[†] b. per Bar. rec. Sept. 7, 1655; m. Mary Hamblin, Jan. 17, 1678; or, per Fal. rec. b. June 6, 1656; m. Mary Lumber, [Lombard,] June 17, 1678; who d. and he m. a 2d wife in 1682, name u
2 CONC nrecorded; and had 6 sons and 4 daus.;—(7) Nathaniel,2[†] b. per Bar. rec. June 5, 1657; per Fal. rec. Sept. 3, 1658; m. ——.;—(8) Samuel,2[†] b. per Bar. rec. Oct. 11, 1659; per Fal. rec. Oct. 4, 1660; m. —— . All the pre. b. at B
2 CONC ar.;—(9) Moses,2 b. per Bar. rec. March 4, 1662; per Fal. rec. March 7, 1663; 1st white child b. in Fal.;—(10) Sarah,2 per Bar. rec. b. March 21, 1664; per Fal. rec. March 23, 1665;—(10) Mark,2 b. April 27, 1667;—(10a) Lydia,2 b. 
2 CONC May 16, 1669; all the last 4 in Suckannesset.
2 CONT * .... etc.
2 CONT *   6. BENJAMIN2 HATCH had (28) Abigail,3 b. Aug. 4, 1679;—(29) Mary,3 b. March 3, 1681;—'''(30) Nathaniel,3[†] b. Feb. 3, 1684''';—(31) Benjamin,3 b. Oct. 17, 1686;—(32) John,3 b. Feb. 16, 1689;—(33) Elisabeth,3 b. March 25, 1692
2 CONC ;—(34) Maltiah, Melatiah, or Malatiah,3[†] b. Oct. 4, 1693;—(35) Timothy,3[†] b. Oct. 19, 1695;—(36) Hannah, or Harmah,3 b. May 7, 1698;—(37) Solomon,3 b. 1704.
2 CONT *   8. SAMUEL2 .... etc. _______________________
