2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Rogers [1]
2 CONT *F, 
2 CONT *b. 12 November 1698, 
2 CONT *d. before November 1767
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Rogers was born on 12 November 1698 at Eastham. She was the daughter of James Rogers and Susanna Tracy. Mary Rogers married Jacob Davis, son of Jabez Davis and Experience Linnell, on 14 June 1733 at Eastham. Her married name 
2 CONC was Davis. Mary Rogers died before November 1767; (not among heirs of her brother Isaac). All of her children were baptized 22 Nov 1741 (probably Harwich).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Mary Rogers and Jacob Davis
2 CONT *1. Mary Davis b. 13 Jun 1736
2 CONT *2. Susanna Davis b. 12 Dec 1738
2 CONT *3. Isaac Davis b. 16 Nov 1741
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S1] Ann T. [Revised by], (Originally compiled by Alice W. A. Westgate) Reeves, Mayflower Families Through Five Generations: Descendants of the Pilgrims who landed at Plymouth, Mass. December 1620: Family of Thomas Rogers (Ply
2 CONC mouth, MA: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 2000), p. 126. Hereinafter cited as Rogers-Silver.
