1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Genealogy of the Lyman Family in Great Britian and America, by Lyman Coleman,D.D., Published by: J. Munsell, State Street, Albany, N.Y., 1872. p. 88.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married early in life Mary Guile, a woman of estimable character, and consistent, uniform and religious life, who died July 4, 1797, in the 90th year of her age.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dea. Thomas Lyman sustained for many years this office in the church in Lebanon Crank, the 2d in Lebanon, and by an eminently religious life honored his office in the church, manifesting the power of divine grace and the fruits of
2 CONC  a holy life, by uniform communion with God. His epitaph is as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sacred to the memory of Dea. Thomas Lyman, who died Aug. 13, 1783, in the 80th year of his age. Few have enjoyed more constant communion with heaven; or, at intervals, had greater discoveries of divine things. His life was zealou
2 CONC s and exemplary; his death peaceful and triumphant. "Behold, my friends, what grace cna do for men, When, by it, they, like babes, are born again."
2 CONT
2 CONT He died from injuries received by a fall in the bark mill of his tannery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogy of the Lyman Family in Great Britian and America, by Lyman Coleman,D.D., Published by: J. Munsell, State Street, Albany, N.Y., 1872. p 88.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription on the tombstone.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Stop passenger! see where I lie,
2 CONT
2 CONT As you now are so once was I,
2 CONT
2 CONT As I am now so you must be
2 CONT
2 CONT Prepare for death and follow me."
