1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Theophilus Swetland==
2 CONT * BIRTH 17 January 1757
2 CONT * DEATH 17 May 1822
2 CONT
2 CONT When Theophilus Swetland was born on 17 January 1757, in Coventry, Windham, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America, his father, Israel Swetland, was 21 and his mother, Dorcas Dewey, was 18. He married Zilpha Sprague on 8 May
2 CONC  1779. They were the parents of at least 5 sons and 5 daughters. He died on 17 May 1822, in East Longmeadow, Hampden, Massachusetts, United States, at the age of 65, and was buried in Billings Hill Cemetery, East Longmeadow, Hampd
2 CONC en, Massachusetts, United States.[1]  ...Theophilus father israel gave him a portion of his estate, the consideration was his good will and affection for him.  Theophilus, my grandfather, lived in Longmeadow, Mass. He was a farmer
2 CONC . Many a time I visited the old homestead but it has changed greatly since my boyhood. Theophilus was married twice, had nine  children by each wife. He lived to be 65 years old."[3]
