1 NAME Richard /Curtis/
2 GIVN Richard
2 SURN Curtis
2 _MARNM Curtis
1 NAME Richard Curtis, of Scituate
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1621
2 ADDR
3 CITY Ash-Juxta-Sandwich
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 OCT 1693
2 ADDR
3 CITY Scituate
3 STAE Massachusetts
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Date and place of birth have also been (erroneously?) reported to be 1620 in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Curtis, son of Thomas Curtis of Kent & Richardene, was born ca 1620. Richard died on 15 Oct 1693 in Scituate, MA.48
2 CONT
2 CONT ==family==
2 CONT
2 CONT Ca 1648 Richard married Ann Hallet (2604) , daughter of John Hallet (1162) (-ca 1674), in Scituate, MA. Born ca 1628. Ann died bef 1692 in Scituate, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Anna Curtis (12 May 1649-)
2 CONT # Elizabeth Curtis (12 Jan 1651-)
2 CONT # John Curtis (9 Dec 1653-)
2 CONT # Mary Curtis (9 Jan 1655-28 Mar 1719)
2 CONT # Martha Curtis (15 Mar 1657-)
2 CONT # Thomas Curtis (16 Mar 1659-3 Jan 1738)
2 CONT # Deborah Curtis (16 Apr 1661-bef 1693)
2 CONT # Sarah Curtis (20 Jul 1663-ca 1739)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr02/rr02_258.html#P11649
2 CONT
2 CONT “Four brothers, Richard, William, John and Thomas Curtis, settled in Scituate. Thomas went to York, Maine; John appears to have left no descendants, while those of Richard and William are numerous in Scituate, Hanover and vicinity
2 CONC  in Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT “Richard Curtis, immigrant ancestor, was born in Kent, England. He settled in Scituate, Massachusetts, about 1643, and died there in 1693. Some writers have confused this RIchard with Richard Curtis, of Dorchester and Milton; and 
2 CONC with Richard Curtis, of Salem and Marblehead. Richard, of Scituate, was on the list of Plymouth colony men able to bear arms in that 1643, and was a town officer in 1650. His brother William as also on this list, and together they
2 CONC  took the oath of fidelity. He was one of the ‘allowed and approved inhabitants’ to whom portions of the common lands were assigned by the joint committee of the general court in 1673. Richard Curtis and Thomas Hyland were witness
2 CONC es to the will of General James Cudworth in 1682. His home was between that of Gowen White and the harbor below Millbrook.”44
2 CONT
2 CONT From Deane’s History of Scituate:49
2 CONT   Richard Curtis was one of four brothers who came early to New England, viz. Richard, Thomas, John and William. John left no family. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard had lands at Marblehead in 1648, and in the same year he purchased lands in Scituate, and built a house between Gowin White's and the Harbour.  
2 CONT His will, dated 1692, gives 'To oldest son John two thirds of my real estate, he providing for my wife Lydia during her life. To son Thomsas one third, &c. To daughters Hannah Curtis, Elizabeth Brooks, Mary Badcocke, and Martha Cl
2 CONC ark.'
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT * FamilySearch AFN: 1TGP-18
2 CONT
