1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Curtis-19387
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas was born on 18 March 1659 in Scituate. He is the son of Richard Curtis and Ann Hallett.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mary Cocke on 6 March 1695 in Scituate. (Researcher's Note: Beware: The transcription of her last name in many trees online is Cook/Cooke. Please view the original documents (this marriage, the children's document, the 
2 CONC will of William Cocke attached to his profile, and the guardianship record of Thomas Jr.) to analyze the handwriting.)[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children[3]:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Deborah Curtis, b. 17 February 1697
2 CONT # Ruth Curtis, b. 19 April 1699
2 CONT # Mary Curtis, b. 6 March 1701/02
2 CONT # Thomas Curtis, b. 5 March 1703/04
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married his second wife, Mary Gilford on 19 September 1711 in Scituate.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth Curtis, b. 24 February 1711/1712.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT On 1 May 1712, Thomas Curtice of Scituate is appointed guardian of the estate that his late wife, Mary’ received from herfather, William Cocke, who had passed down a legacy to his grandson son Thomas Jr., who is nine years old.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed away in 1738.[6]
2 CONT
