0 @I6000000001690621942@ INDI
1 NAME Robert /Babcock/
2 GIVN Robert
2 SURN Babcock
2 _MARNM Babcock
2 NICK Badcock
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1620
2 ADDR
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 NOV 1694
2 ADDR
3 CITY Milton
3 STAE Province of Massachusetts
1 OCCU rater, supervisor of highways, selectman for Milton
1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} appointed sergeant and later captain in the Indian Wars
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/136333419
2 CONT
2 CONT Comment February 2017
2 CONT
2 CONT >... all of the research and records I have says that Robert and the Badcocks were not from Wivenhoe, that a visit to Wivenhoe found no Badcocks or Babcocks in Parish Records and their original origins are unknown. It also states 
2 CONC that Robert was the was the son of David Badcock, who was in Dorchester Massachusetts in 1640 and his wife Mary. It also shows that Robert was also likely the father of George Badcock, James Badcock and Margaret Badcock Leland.”
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *The Pioneers of Massachusetts: A Descriptive List, Drawn from Records of the ...Charles Pope.  Page 27.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=k___uh7sQAkC&lpg=PP1&dq=%E2%80%A2%20Henry%20Pope%2C%20The%20Pioneers%20of%20Massachusetts
2 CONC &pg=PA27#v=onepage&q&f=true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT *Stephen Babcock, Babcock Genealogy (New York: Eaton & Mains, 1903), digitized by Archive.org.
2 CONT * Wm. S. Appleton, “Family of Badcock of Milton,” The New England Historical and Genealogical Register (1865), 19:215-218, digitized by Archive.org. [https://archive.org/stream/newenglandhisto74unkngoog#page/n220/mode/2up Archive.
2 CONC Org]
