1 TITL Capt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Capt. John Sprague
2 CONT * Gender:  Male
2 CONT * Born:  Abt 1690  Place:  Duxbury, Plymouth Co., MA, USA 2
2 CONT * Died:  6 Apr 1763  Place:  Canaan, Litchfield Co., CT, USA 2, 3
2 CONT * Buried: Place:  Mountain View Cemetery, North Canaan, Litchfield Co., CT, USA
2 CONT * Father: Lt. John Sprague (Abt 1656 - 6 Mar 1727/28) 5
2 CONT *Mother: Lydia [--?--] (Abt 18 Jul 1658 - 18 Jul 1725)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sprague.one-name.net/getperson.php?personID=I15138&tree=Sprague
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Mary Babcock (28 Jan 1680/81 - 10 Mar 1720/21) 4  Married: 22 Feb 1710/11  Place: Lebanon, New London Co., CT, USA 6, 7
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT *1  Ebenezer Sprague (12 Dec 1711 - 1771) 8, 9
2 CONT * 2 Hannah Sprague (30 Jun 1714 - Yes, date unknown)
2 CONT * 3  Jonathan Terwiliger Sprague (30 Apr 1716 - 17 Jan 1807) 4, 10
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Hannah Burt ( - Yes, date unknown)  Married: Abt 1722 11
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: 
2 CONT * 1 John Sprague (22 Jul 1723 - Bef 5 May 1779)
2 CONT *  2 Thomas Sprague (8 May 1725 - 13 Jan 1732/33)
2 CONT *  3 Huldah Sprague (15 Apr 1734 - 14 May 1804) 12, 13
2 CONT *  4  Rachel Sprague (19 Aug 1737 - Yes, date unknown)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT Capt. John Sprague was born about 1683 in Duxbury, Plymouth Co., MA.
2 CONT From Virginia Sprague Webster, correspondent. In response to W. V. Sprague's indicated dob of 1690 and another reported date in 1692: I have a problem with his d.o.b. When I was in Canaan, the Canaan/Falls Village Town Records had
2 CONC  the entry of his death: "died on April 6, 1760 at the age of 77." As you can see, for this to be possible he would have to have been born ca 1683. If this is accepted as fact, he would then be the first and not the fourth child o
2 CONC f Lt. John Sprague and Lydia Unknown. According to the Town Record of Old Headstones, he is buried in the Lower Cemetery off route 126, Canaan, CT and the headstone was last seen in 1934. When I was there in May 1994 the stone was
2 CONC  no longer there. He died on 6 Apr 1760 in Canaan, Litchfield Co., CT.(142) "Sprague Families in America", by W. V. Sprague, page 17. 1718-9, March 24. He deeded to Benjamin Sprague of Lebanon the farm given him by his honored fat
2 CONC her John Sprague. 1724. Capt. John Sprague with 22 sentinels marched from Simsbury, CT. 1739. Capt. Sprague removed from Lebanon to Sharon, CT. He drew the 37th home lot. He was Selectman for several years, and what is singular he
2 CONC  could not write his name. The words John X (his mark) Sprague are appended to many official documents on the Sharon records. He built the first frame house in town. In 1748, he exchanged farms with Cornelius Knickerbocker and rem
2 CONC oved to Furnace Village (now Lakeville) in Salisbury, CT. He afterwards removed to Canaan, CT. where he died.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: See John #AD Sprague as a possible illegitimate son of Capt. John Sprague and Abigail Calkin.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Mary Babcock (daughter of Jonathon Babcock and Mary Curtis) on 22 Feb 1710/ 11 in Lebanon, New London Co., CT.(143) (144) Mary Babcock was born on 28 Jan 1680/81. She died on 10 Mar 1721 in Lebanon, New London Co
2 CONC ., CT.(145) (146)(147
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
