1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Sprague Families in America", by Dr. Warren Vincent Sprague,  page 28.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Ebenezer Sprague moved to Sharon, CT. in 1739.  In the French and Indian War he served as follows: enlisted April 16, 1759; disc. Dec. 14, 1759, 1st Regt. with Co., of Capt. Brainard of Windsor.  In 1st Regt., 9th Co., of Capt. W
2 CONC alcott of Windsor, 1761.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Capt. John Sprague & Mary Babcock.  Married 1) Elizabeth Thatcher 2) Hannah St. John.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://sprague.one-name.net/getperson.php?personID=I38554&tree=Sprague
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT My fifth cousin six times removed, and my sixth cousin seven times removed through his great great great great grandfather's sister, Alice Doggett. [Harry Kenneth Doggett]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.New England Families Genealogical and Memorial, New York: n.p., 1915 (William Richard Cutter). 
