1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *''''''History and Genealogy of the Pomeroy Family: Collateral Lines in Family ... (1912)
2 CONT *http://archive.org/details/historyandgenea01pomegoog
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/historyandgenea01pomegoog#page/n221/mode/1up
2 CONT *   8 CALEB POMEROY, (Eltweed). bap. at Windsor, March 6, 1641; m. March 8, 1665, Hepzibah Baker, b. May 10, 1646, dau. of Jeffrey Baker and Joan Rockwell, of Windsor, Conn. He was one of the original settlers of Northampton, was 
2 CONC made freeman in 1663, had home lot in section 6, subscribed three pounds of flax to the Harvard College fund; took part n the Falls Fight, May 19, 1676. In 1686 he sold his place and moved to Southampton or Easthampton, Mass., and
2 CONC  is ancestor of all the Pomeroys of those places, except Captain Lemuel Pomeroy; he was identified with the town from the first and was still active in promoting the welfare of the place as a prominent and influential citizen up t
2 CONC o the time of his death. Nov. 18, 1691, a victim to the epidemic of fever and ague prevalent at the time.
2 CONT **	3d gen. Children, b. Northampton, except first and tenth:
2 CONT **   24 HEPZIBAH POMEROY, b. Windsor, July 27, 1666; d. young at Northampton.
2 CONT **''''''   25 SAMUEL POMEROY, b. May 29, 1669. +
2 CONT **   26 ABIGAIL POMEROY, b. Oct. 20, 1671. +
2 CONT **   27 HEPZIBAH POMEROY, b. Jan. 19, 1673; m. Jan. 25, 1705, Walter Lee of Westfield; his estate was settled in 1709.
2 CONT **   28 EBENEZER POMEROY, b. March 14, 1674; d. Sept. 12, 1699.
2 CONT **   29 CALEB POMEROY, b. May 3, 1677; d. April, 1690.
2 CONT **   30 ELDAD POMEROY, b. Dec. 6, 1679. +
2 CONT **   31 HANNAH POMEROY, b. July 4, 1682. +
2 CONT **   32 MERCY POMEROY, b. Sept. 20, 1684. +
2 CONT **   33 SARAH POMEROY, b. Southampton, Aug. 6, 1687; m. June 21, 1709, Deliverance Church; m. (2) Dec. 12, 1721, Noah Wright.
2 CONT *   An old document recites .....
2 CONT *http://archive.org/stream/historyandgenea01pomegoog#page/n237/mode/1up
2 CONT *''''''   25 SAMUEL POMEROY, (Caleb, Eltweed), b. May 29, 1669, at Northampton, Mass.: m. (1) about 1690, Elizabeth, dau. of John and Mary (Kingsley) French of Rohoboth, Mass.: m. (2) Dec. 7 1703, Johanna, dau. of Jacob and Mary (
2 CONC Frary) Root, b. Nov. 5, 1681, d. Jan. 20, 1713; m. (3) 1715, Elizabeth, dau. of Joseph* and Elizabeth^ (Chapman) Strickland, b. Jan. 29, 1685; living in 1746, when he made his will. He was a teacher and farmer, and settled in Sout
2 CONC hampton. He received five acres of meadow land of an additional grant in Northampton. He had a home lot in Easthampton on West Street, near the saw-mill with a lot intervening, which had been sequestered for school purposes. He d.
2 CONC  about 1748.
2 CONT **''''''	4th gen. Children by 1st wife:
2 CONT **   168 SAMUEL FRENCH POMEROY, b. 1691. +
2 CONT **   169 CALEB POMEROY, b. May 14, 1693; d. young.
2 CONT **   170 ELIZABETH POMEROYS, b. Sept. 30, 1694; d. Oct. 8, 1714; unm.
2 CONT **   171 CALEB POMEROY, b. Dec. 1, 1696; d. young.
2 CONT **   172 EBENEZER POMEROY, b. May 31, 1700; d. Aug. 9, 1709.
2 CONT **''''''	Children by 2d wife:
2 CONT **   173 JOHANNA POMEROY, b. about 1704; mentioned in her father's will in 1746; unm.
2 CONT **   174 HEPZIBAH POMEROY, b. in 1706; also mentioned in her father's will  1746; unm.
2 CONT **   175 CALEB POMEROY, b. Oct. 2, 1707, Northampton. +
2 CONT **''''''	Children by 3d wife:
2 CONT **   176 MARY POMEROY, b. July 1, 1716. +
2 CONT **   177 JOSHUA POMEROY, b. Sept. 9, 1717. +
2 CONT **   178 NOAH POMEROY, b. Oct. 13, 1719. +
2 CONT ***	* Joseph Strickland was son of Thwaite Strickland and Elizabeth, dau. of Edward Shepard of Cambridge. Will June 21, 1670.
2 CONT ***	^ Elizabeth Chapman was dau. of Edward Chapman and Elizabeth Fox.
2 CONT **http://archive.org/stream/historyandgenea01pomegoog#page/n238/mode/1up
2 CONT **   179 RICHARD POMEROY, b. Nov., 1721; went into Maine; descendants not yet traced.
2 CONT **   180 ELIZABETH POMEROY, b. Feb. 25, 1723. +
2 CONT **   181 SIMEON POMEROY, b. June 5, 1725, Northampton. +
