1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Bruce C. Johnson Jr., research notes 1985 - 1995, Port Bruce, Ontario
2 CONT
2 CONT Bible entry gives birth as 21 Sept. 1773.
2 CONT
2 CONT IGI extraction for a Jonathon Brown, born 21 Nov. 1741, Hebron Twp., Tolland Co., CT, son of Jonathan Brown. Is this the same person, and the query date is actually a baptism? Burton Library, Mansfield, CT, 1703-1850, Births, Bapt
2 CONC isms and Deaths, by Susan Dimock, 1898. ANF; GH2Z-MO gives Jonathan Brown bp. at Caterbury, W 3 Dec. 1738.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1790 at Chemung Twp., Montgomery Co., NY there is a Jonathan Brown living near the family of Benajah and Violetta Brown. Also nearby is Daniel Brown.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1800 census for Burlington Twp., Otsego Co., NY. Jonth Brown over 45 is living next to 3 of his sons, Abner, Charles and Erastus. In the History of Otsego Co., NY, pub. 1878 by Everts & Pariss, p. 103 he is given as one of 
2 CONC the founders and moderator of the Congregational Church founded in 1797.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1810 census for 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ref. query in the Brown Family News and Gen. Soc., Vol. 20, issue #2, Francis H. Brown, 1603 Maryland Ave., Woodbridge, VA 22191. Connecticut Bible and Family Records, Conn. State Library, Vo., 24, pp 129-132, 1951.
2 CONT
2 CONT See Michigan Heritage, Winter 1968 pp 87-89 for Brown - Jewett Bible transcriptions, Monroe Michigan, confirms will of William Swetland of 25 Nov. 1779 mentioning children of Hannah (Swetland) Brown, deceased includs Benajah Brown
2 CONC .
