1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (daughter of John and Sabra (Alger) Closson)wife of John ANNIS  Children of John and Sabra (Closson) Annis included:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sabra Annis. b. Mar. 22, 1784 Thetford, Vt. d. July 13, 1803 Thetford, Vt. md. Moses Howe of Thetford, Vt., Mar. 24, 1803.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. John Closson Annis. b. May 8, 1785 Thetford, Vt. md. June 16, 1806 Hannah Clifford at Thetford, Vt.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Ezra Annis. b. May 8, 1787 Thetford, Vt. d. 1872
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Asenath Annis. b. Feb. 24, 1789 Thetford, Vt. d. Sept. 14, 1872 Thetford, Vt. md. Elijah Green at Thetford, Vt.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. Sarah (Sally) Annis. b. Apr. 3, 1791 Thetford, Vt. d. About 1816 at Bethany, Genesse County, N.Y. md. 1806 - Jesse Torrey.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Harvey Annis. b. 1793 Thetford, Vt. d.1793 Thetford, Vt.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Harvey Annis 2nd. b. 1794 Thetford, Vt. d. 1794 Thetford, Vt.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Dorothy (Dolly) Annis. b. Oct. 13, 1796 Thetford, Vt. d. Nov. 3, 1843 Rome, Crawford County, Pa. md Daniel Bennett, Sept. 15, 1816 in the town of Ellery, Chautauqua County, N.Y.
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. Harvey Annis 3rd. b. June 5, 1799 Thetford, Vt. d. Aug. 1814. Was killed in battle during the American assault of Fort Erie, Niagara River (War of 1812).
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. Mary (Polly) Annis. b. Jan. 13, 1801 Thetford, Vt. d. Jan. 28, 1872 town of Carroll, Chautauqua County, N.Y. md. 1st. Zenus C. Hall. md. 2nd Job Tobey III on Oct. 2, 1827. Job a son of Job Tobey, Revolutionary War veteran who 
2 CONC came from Vermont to the town of Carroll in 1814.
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. Phineas Annis. b. Dec. 14, 1803 Thetford, Vt. d. Mar. 8, 1880 town of Carroll, Chautauqua County, N.Y. md. 1st Belvera Putnam Oct. 30, 1822 and they became the parents of nine children. md. 2nd Phoebe (Wilmarth) Putnam (widow 
2 CONC of Ephron Putnam) late in 1841. Phineas bd. Lewis Cemetery.
