1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Bassett Sr. migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1621-1640). (See ''Great Migration Begins'', by R. C. Anderson, Vol. 1, p. 127)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT He left no will.  Death caught William unawares; he wrote no will but Plymouth court testimony records the deathbed scene. On April 3, 1667, he found himself so weak and sick that he told Mary: Quoted to his Wife, I must leave the
2 CONC e but I shall leave thee with the Lord; if God had lengthened out my life it might have been that thou mightest have been more comfortably provided for.
2 CONT ===William Bassett===
2 CONT *Birth:	 between 1599 and October 24, 1600 in (possibly) Bethnal Green, Middlesex, England 
2 CONT * Death:	 before May 12, 1667 Bridgewater, Plymouth, Massachusetts  
2 CONT * Possibly the son of William Bassett of Bethnel Green, London: unproven. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT * 1) Elizabeth (unknown) 6 children. 
2 CONT * 2) Mary Tilden, widow of Thomas Lapham. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Do not confuse with  https://www.geni.com/people/William-Bassett/6000000032101135975
2 CONT
