2 CONT The Pilgrims,   
2 CONT Thinking they had the problem solved 6 Sep 1620 they departed again, only to have to return this time to Plymouth, England.  Here they abandoned the Speedwell and 20 people were left behind.  The Mayflower left alone to cross the 
2 CONC waters. William Bassett was one of the 20 people left to come as soon as a vessel transport could be found.  It was said that he decided to wait for his Bride.  This Bride most likely being Elizabeth Tilden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Tilden was born 17 May 1603 at Bridgewater, Worcester, England.  She was the daughter of Nathaniel Tilden and Lydia Hucksteppe.
2 CONT
2 CONT William and Elizabeth probably married sometime in 1620 in Holland.  They had children (1) William born ca 1624 who was married to Mary Rainsford. (2)  Elizabeth  born ca 1626, (3) Nathaniel born 2 Feb 1628 at Plymouth, Massachuse
2 CONC tts who married Dorcas Joyce, (4)  Sarah born ca 1630 who married Peregrine White and she died 22 Jan 1711 at Scituate, Mass, (5) Joseph Bassett born ca 1635 who married Martha Hobart and second Mary Lapham.  He settled his family
2 CONC  at Bridgewater and died there in 1712 (6) Jane b. ca 1639 at Duxbury, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT             William Bassett sailed to America the following year in 1621 on the âFortuneâ.[4]  The ship arrived on November 19. This was the second ship to reach Plymouth.âThe (shipâs) company included a few more from Leyd
2 CONC en â¦ William Bassett, the much married master mason, with his third wifeâ¦â[5]  In the William Bradford History 1621, Nov. 19, P 127 says: This is a memorable day of surprise and rejoicing for Plymouth for the Fortunes arrive
2 CONC s with 35 more Pilgrims, âmostly lustly young men but sadly lacking in provisionsâ. Our William was one of them and if he was lacking in eatables, etc., he did not forget his provisions of books, a large library for those days
2 CONC , which attests to his scholarly education. Perhaps he had his blacksmith tools also for this was his trade, as will appear.
2 CONT --------------------
