2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 0 FLOWERS 76 William Bassett was the husband of Elizabeth Unknown and Mary Tilden. Father of my 7th great-grandmother Sarah Bassett White, wife of the first pilgrim child, Peregrine White.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Bassett's origins are unknown at this time. He was among the very early arrivals in New England, arriving on the "Fortune" in 1621. His first wife Elizabeth may have also been among the passengers, either as a single woman
2 CONC  or recently married to him.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a freeman of Plymouth,MA, among those already admitted before Jan 1,1632/3. By 1639 he had removed to Duxbury. He was a blacksmith by trade. He wrote his will on April 3,1667, probaby dying very shortly thereafter. His esta
2 CONC te inventory was taken May 12,1667.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, first, Elizabeth ____, probably before 1623. Sometime after 1651, he married Mary (Tilden) Lapham, the widow of Thomas Lapham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children(all by first marriage): William Bassett Jr, Elizabeth Bassett Burgess, Sarah Bassett White, Nathaniel Bassett, Joseph Bassett, and Ruth Bassett Sprague.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Spouses Elizabeth Bassett 1603–1650 (m. 1623)
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Tilden 1603–1667
2 CONT
