2 CONT William Bassett the immigrant, who came over in the ship " Fortune"in 1621, lived in Duxbury in 1637, was deputy to the general court several years and joined Governor Bradford and others in the purchase of Dartmouth Massachusetts
2 CONC , and removed to Bridgewater where he died in 1667. Ruth Whittemore was appointed April 3  1730, administratrix of her husbands' estate, which was inventoried at five hundred and three pounds.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:https://www.books.google.com
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
