1 NOTE Was Deputy to the General Court, Sandwich, MA (1666-1673); Assistant to the Governor, 1666-1686; 1689-91. From a deed dated 29 Apr 1674: "Edmond ffreman Junr. of Sandwich in the Colony of New Plimouth in America for a fatherly aff
2 CONC ection unto my son Joseph Burge & my daughter Patience the w. of Joseph Burge afsd... doe give freely... one moyetee of upland... in Sandwich, being formerly in the poss. of Edmond ffreeman Senr... six acres... doe give unto my so
2 CONC n in law Joseph Burge... his heirs..." Signed Edmond ffreeman. Witnesses: Richard Bourne, the mark of Thomas Burge. The grantor personally appeared and acknowledged the instrument 2 Mar 1674/5, at which time "Margarett freeman his
2 CONC  wife appeared and gave up... all her right in the meadow herein specified." [Plymouth Colony Records 5, pt. 2:379]. ["Edmond Freeman of Sandwich," The American Genealogist 40:2, Apr 1964].
2 CONT
2 CONT Wm.E. WRIGHT: "GREENE & LEWIS"; [private]; Houston, TX; 1991; pp 87-88. [Crandall homepage http://pages.prodigy.com/NY/cranfamassoc/ne.html]
2 CONT
2 CONT Barnstable June ye 9th 1705. By Barnabas Lothrop Esq. Judge of Probate and Granting Letters of Administration for the County of Barnstable the Estate of Edmond ffreeman late of Sandwich who died intestate...pay
2 CONT Edmond ffreeman son of the deceased £ 15. 00. 00.
2 CONT To Isaac Pope and Alice his wife 09. 07. 00.
2 CONT To Richard Allen of Sandwich 00. 01. 10.
2 CONT To John ffish and Margaret his wife 01. 13. 08.
2 CONT To John Launders and Rachel his wife 01. 06. 00.
2 CONT To Patience Burg vid. 05. 08. 00.
2 CONT (Barnstable County Probate 2:190)
2 CONT The above distribution names all but the two youngest daughters of the deceased, namely, Sarah the wife of Richard Landers and Deborah the wife of Thomas Landers. [Maclean W. McLean, "Mr. Edmond Freeman of Sandwich, Mass., and His
2 CONC  Family," The American Genealogist 40:20:103-110, 1964]
2 CONT
2 CONT FREEMAN, EDMUND, s. of the preced. b. in Eng. m. 22 Apr. 1646, at Eastham, Rebecca, d. of Thomas Prence, the Gov. had only Rebecca, after b. of wh. his w. d. prob. in short time, and he m. 13 July 1651, Margaret Young, had Margare
2 CONC t, b. Oct. 1652; Edmund, 5 Oct. 1655; Alice, 29 Mar. 1658; Rachel, 7 Sept. 1659; Sarah, 6 Feb. 1662; and Deborah, 9 Aug. 1665; was rep. and the time of d. of hims. or of his w. is unkn. [Savage, Gen. Dictionary, 1965]
