1 NOTE William was of Sandwich, Kent, Eng. Cd 100 has Bridgewater, Plymouth, Mass. Cd 100 & Genealogical Register of Plymouth Families p 22 differ on these 2 Williams & their wives & children.
1 NOTE Gunsmith, worker in metals, master mason
2 CONT Arrived Plymouth, MA aboard the "Fortune" , the first ship after the Mayflower, 11/09/1621
1 NOTE William Bassett moved to Duxbury in 1638 and alternated with Myles Standish for several years in serving the town as Deputy to the General Court.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1645 the town of Duxbury was granted a plantation, incorporated as Bridgewater in 1656.  William Bassett was one of the fifty-four propriators who paid Massasoit seven coats containing a yard and one-half each, nine hatchets, e
2 CONC ight hoes, twenty knives, four moose skins and ten and one half yards of cotton cloth.  Each settler was granted a six acre house lot.
2 CONT
2 CONT He owned a great deal of land for the times and had the largest library of any of the Pilgrims, including "Wilson's Dictionary", two concordances and commentaries on books of the Bible.
