2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 0 FLOWERS 29 William Basset married Elizabeth _____ by 1623 (and probably by 1621). She came to Plymouth with him as a passenger on the Fortune in 1621. She appears in no record after 1627, and may have died soon a
2 CONC fter the birth of the last child about 1634, or she may have lived until just before William Bassett married his second wife.  She & William had six children: William Jr., Elizabeth Burgess, Sarah White, Nathaniel, Joseph & Ruth S
2 CONC prague Thomas. Source: Anderson's Great Migration Study Project
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth T died at Plymouth, Devonshire, Eng.
2 CONT *Anecdote*: She was a passenger on FORTUNE, arriving in North America in 1621.1,2
2 CONT *Married Name: Her married name was Bassett.
2 CONT *Birth*: She was born circa 1603 at Tenterden, Kent, Eng.
2 CONT *She was the daughter of Thomas Tilden and Elizabeth Focell. UNPROVEN 
2 CONT *Marriage*: Elizabeth Tilden married William Bassett, son of William Bassett and Cecelia Light,  UNPROVEN in 1621 at Plymouth, Plymouth Co, MA; 1st m. for William.1,2,3
2 CONT *Death: Elizabeth Tilden died before 1651.4
2 CONT *Family: William Bassett b. c 1595, d. 10 Apr 1667
2 CONT *Marriage*: She married William Bassett, son of William Bassett and Cecelia Light, in 1621 at Plymouth, Plymouth Co, MA; 1st m. for William.1,2,3
2 CONT
