1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''n.b. This is NOT the William Bassett of Lynn, MA, and is NOT the William Bassett who married Sarah Burt.  That William Bassett was born 1621 and his parents were Roger Bassett (1589) and Ann Holland (1602).  Plea
2 CONC se avoid merging those branches, as there is no evidence of their connection.''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Bassett''' was b abt 1624, Plymouth, MA, d 10 Jun 1670, Sandwich, Barnstable, MA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:  William Bassett "the Immigrant" (b. abt 1596-1667) and Elizabeth ??.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married:
2 CONT # abt 1652, Plymouth, MA to Mary Rainsford, daughter of Edward Rainsford by his first wife, identity undetermined. She was b 1 Jun 1632, Boston, Suffolk, MA, d 31 Aug 1689, Deerfield, Franklin, MA. Mary Rainsford was married secon
2 CONC dly (June 1671) to James Percival, with whom she had three children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Bassett and Mary Rainsford:
2 CONT # Mary Bassett b 21 Nov 1654, Sandwich, Barnstable, MA, d bef 1692; md John Redding 22 Oct 1676.
2 CONT # Hon. William Bassett b 1656.
2 CONT # Thomas Bassett b 1659, Sandwich, Barnstable, MA.
2 CONT # Sarah Bassett b 1662, Sandwich, Barnstable, MA, md Thomas Lewes.
2 CONT # Richard Bassett b 1665, Sandwich, Barnstable, MA.
2 CONT # Nathan Bassett b 25 Sep 1667, Sandwich, Barnstable, MA, d 16 Nov 1743, Chilmark, MA; md Mary Huckins 2 Oct 1690.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT William Bassett was one of the early settlers of Sandwich in Barnstable. He was licensed in 1659 to keep an ordinary. He served as Collector and Constable of Sandwich in 1657, as well as Deputy to the General Court at Plymouth in 
2 CONC 1662. He was one of the few individuals in the Colony accorded the title "Mr." At his death, all of his children were still minors. His widow, Mary (nee Rainsford) married Lieut. James Percival in Jun 1671, and with whom she had t
2 CONC hree children.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Links==
2 CONT * http://www.geneajourney.com/bassett.html
