2 CONT He was baptized in St. Martin's Church. He came on the Abigail in 1635 with
2 CONT his mother and stepfather. His date of baptism might also be 27 Apr 1623 in
2 CONT Dorking, co. Surrey, England.
2 CONT He is said to have married, about 1646, Sarah Burt, the daughter of his stepfather, Hugh. No mention of her thus far has been found in ship passenger lists, nor is her baptism recorded with other of Hugh's children in St. Martin's
2 CONC  Church. No marriage record has been found, but there seems to have been no one qualified to perform a marriage ceremony in Lynn before 1658. It may have taken place elsewhere. Sarah was not mentioned in Hugh Burt's will although 
2 CONC she was living at that time. However, since few women owned property, it is perhaps logical to believe that the legacy would be left to her husband rather than to her and in his will Hugh Burt bequeathed land "to my son will: Bass
2 CONC it", which could mean stepson, son-in-law, or both. Every history of early Massachusetts consulted, which mentioned the wife of William Bassett of Lynn, stated that she was Sarah Burt, daughter of his stepfather.
2 CONT He was an ensign in the ompany of Capt. Gardner, of Salem, in the Indian war, and was at the "swamp fight." For his services, the General Court made him a grant of land. He was a Militia Captain, Quartermaster, Member of Council o
2 CONC f War with Major Benjamin Church, at Scarborough, ME, 11 November 1689. His name often appears in the oldest records of Lynn, where in 1691, he is called Quartermaster Bassett.
2 CONT Will of William Bassett, proved and allowed 22 May 1703:
2 CONT "In the name of God Everlasting Amen: I William Bassett Senr. of Lyn in ye County of Esex in Newengland being of good & perfect memory & Rationally Disposed And having attained to ye years of a good old age & being very sensable o
2 CONC f ye decay of nature & ye many Distempers & Infirmities that do attend my outward (mein? man?) not knowing how soone my great & last change may come have therefore taken this opportunity to settle ye affaires of my family & so lea
2 CONC ve this as my last will and testament. Impr: as for my precious mortall soul I freely resign it to him that gave it & to my Redeemer Jesus Christ which by his precious blood hath ransome my soul from Death as for my body which is 
2 CONC fraile I comend it to ye dust willing a decent Interment thereof suitable to my Rank & quality. Although worms my skin destroy yet in my flesh I shal see God - Amen. As for the disposall of my outward Estate which God of his Goodn
2 CONC ess hath given mee - my will is that after my funerall charges & lawful debts bee paid I bequeathe to my deare & loving wife who hath bin carefull of me & industrious in her place for ye procurement of what outward Estate I have I
2 CONC  bequeath unto her the Improvement of my whole Estate during her naturall life and all the moveable estate in my house which is mine to be at her disposall - as shee shall see cause: Item: I give to my eldest son willm Bassett all
2 CONC  ye housing land meddowes marshes and movables within ye bounds of Lyn township or Elsewhere to bee at his absolut disposall: further it is to be under stood that my son willm Bassett is to pay out of such Estate all such Legasies
2 CONC  as I shall give to ye rest of my children as followeth: Item: i give to my son John Bassett five pounds in mony: Item: I give to my son Elisha Bassett fivetie shillings in mony: Item: I give to my son Samuel Bassett fivetie shill
2 CONC ings in mony: Item I give to my daughter Elizebeth Bassett allias Richards forty shillings in mony: Item: I give to my daughter Sarah Elwell fortie shillings in mony: Item: I give to my daughter Merriam Sandy fortie shillings in m
2 CONC ony: Ittem I give to my daughter Mary Ruck fortie shillings in mony: Ittem I ive to my daughter Rachel Silsbe fortie shillings in mony: Ittem I give to my daughter Rebeckah Bassett fortie shillings in mony: ittem I ive to my daugh
2 CONC ter Hannah Lille fortie shillings in mony -- and if any of ye above named Children Except my son Willm should dye then to be divided Equaly amongst them all. It is to be understood that these legasies are to be paid within a one y
2 CONC eare after my disease and my wives and my will is that neither str? nor waste be made But to the end foresaid. Ittom my will is that my son William Bassett bee sole Executtor to this my last will and testament. Heare unto I have s
2 CONC ett to my hand and seale this tenth day of february in the yeare of our 1701. Sighned William Bassett with a seale --- Witnessed by Before sighning it is to be understood that my son William Bassett is to have my whole Estate as i
2 CONC s above mentioned to him & his heirs for ever.
2 CONT Witnesses: Samuel Johnson, Lois Rogers, Ezekiel Rogers."
