1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ii Elizabeth Bassett,  b. Plymouth about 1626; m. Sandwich 8 November 1648 Thomas Burgess , from whom she was divorced on 10 June 1661 .
2 CONT
2 CONT >Elizabeth divorced Thomas Burgess after he was brought to court for an act of uncleanness with Lydia Gaunt. This was the first divorce in Plymouth Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT >>"1661, June 10- Sarah's older sister Elizabeth secured the first recorded divorce in the Colony. Her husband Thomas Burgess, Jr. had not been faithful having eloped with Lydia Gaunt to Newport, RI where they reared a family. Eli
2 CONC zabeth and Thomas had been married for 13 years and had lived in Sandwich, MA. She was awarded one third of his property and 40 shillings of bed and bedding "that are at William Bassetts (her father)." "
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.cyberancestors.com/cummins/ps31/ps31_232.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT The Descendants of Elder William Brewster, Part 1, Generations 1 through 4, Barbara Lambert Merrick, General Society of Mayflower Descendants, Plymouth MA, 2014, p. 146
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Proof of Patience the sister
2 CONT
2 CONT “Patience Freeman was born circa 1647 at Plymouth or Barnstable County, Massachusetts. She was the daughter of Edmond Freeman and Rebecca Prence. Patience Freeman married Joseph Burgess, son of Thomas Burgess and Dorothy (Unknown)
2 CONC , in September 1665 at Sandwich, Barnstable County, Massachusetts. Patience Freeman died after 1695. She died before 16 March 1715 at Perhaps, Rochester, Plymouth County, Massachusetts.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Burgess (M) b. circa 1633, d. August 1695, #73520 Pop-up Pedigree Relationship=8th great-granduncle of David Kipp Conover Jr..
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Burgess was born circa 1633 at Lynn, Essex County, Massachusetts. He was the son of Thomas Burgess and Dorothy (Unknown). Joseph Burgess was born circa 1636. Joseph Burgess was born in 1638 at Sandwich, Barnstable County, M
2 CONC assachusetts. Joseph2 Burgess, the 4th son of Thomas1, was a landholder in Sandwich in 1658. In 1659. He married Patience Freeman, daughter of Edmond Freeman and Rebecca Prence, in September 1665 at Sandwich, Barnstable County, Ma
2 CONC ssachusetts. Joseph Burgess died in August 1695 at Rochester, Plymouth County, Massachusetts. He died circa 5 August 1695 at Rochester, Plymouth County, Massachusetts. He left a will on 5 August 1695 at Rochester.  mentions daught
2 CONC ers Rebecca Ross and Dority Clifton.”
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
