1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bassett-176
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Bassett was born say 1628 in Plymouth Colony to parents Elizabeth and William Bassett, Sr.[1] William and Elizabeth were present and accounted for in the 1727 Plymouth cattle division, but Sarah was not on this list.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Bassett married before 6 March 1648/9 Peregrine White,[1] On 6 Mar 1648/9, "Peregrin White, and Sara, his wife, both of Marshfield" were presented to the court for fornication before marriage or contract. They were cleared b
2 CONC y paying a fine.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 3 June 1652, William Bassett of Duxbury deeded forty acres of upland with the meadow adjoining to his son-in-law Lt. Perigrine White, and 16 June 1656 William made a deed of gift of land in Marshfield to his two sons living in Mar
2 CONC shfield, Peregrine White and Nathaniel Bassett. [1][3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Peregrine White of Marshfield left to his wife Sarah everything that was not otherwise disposed of in his will.[5][6]
2 CONT
2 CONT "mrs Sarah White Deceased January ye 22 : 1711" [1711/2] in Marshfield, Plymouth, Massachusetts [7] [8][9][10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT # Daniel White b. c. 1649, based on age at death
2 CONT # (child) White b. c. 1650/1, Bradford said Peregrine had two children when he enumerated the Increasings and Decreasings of the Maryflower passengers. This may be Joseph killed in King Phillip's War.
2 CONT # Jonathan White b. Marshfield 4 Jun 1658
2 CONT # Peregrine White b. c 1661 (based on his age when he was bpt and his age at death
2 CONT # Sarah White b. Marshfield Oct 1663
2 CONT # Sylvanus White b. Marshfield before 1667
2 CONT # Mercy White b. c. 1670 based on age at death .
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 22 January 1710/11.
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings: William born 1624, Elizabeth born 1626, Nathaniel born 1628, Ruth born 1633, and Joseph born 1635.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1661, June 10- Sarah's older sister Elizabeth secured the first recorded divorce in the Colony. Her husband Thomas Burgess, Jr. had not been faithful having eloped with Lydia Gaunt to Newport, RI where they reared a family. Elizab
2 CONC eth and Thomas had been married for 13 years and had lived in Sandwich, MA. She was awarded one third of his property and 40 shillings of bed and bedding "that are at William Bassetts (her father)." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://www.cyberancestors.com/cummins/ps31/ps31_141.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Daughter of William and Elizabeth Bassett. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Captain Peregrine White. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Daniel White, Jonathan White, Peregrine White Jr., Sarah White, and Mercy (White) Sherman. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of William and Elizabeth Bassett.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Captain Peregrine White.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Daniel White, Jonathan White, Peregrine White Jr., Sarah White, and Mercy (White) Sherman.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandmother and great-grandmother.
