2 CONT
2 CONT '''Bethiah Eaton''' was born about 1668, daughter of Samuel and Martha (Billington) Eaton. She died before 12 Jan 1735/6 (husband's will).[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 5 Nov 1691 in Taunton, Massachusetts, Joseph Bassett,[2] s/o Joseph and Mary (Lapham) Bassett.[3][4][1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Bassett’s will names the three daughters: 
2 CONT #oldest, Bethia Bassett (named executor); married William Coddington 
2 CONT #2nd Mehetebell Holloway of Middleboro; married Nathaniel Holloway 
2 CONT #3rd Lydia Phillips of Norton; married Samuel Phillips 
