2 CONT ===Daniel Whittemore (1663 - 1756)===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Whittemore
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 27 Apr 1663 in Malden, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Daniel Whittemore and Mary (Mellins) Whittemore
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of John Whittemore Sr, Thomas Whittemore, Mary Whittemore, Nathaniel Whittemore, James Whittemore and Pelatiah Whittemore
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Lydia (Bassett) Whittemore — married 1688 in Chelsea, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Daniel Whittemore, Lydia (Whittemore) Richardson, Joseph Whittemore, Mary (Whittemore) Wait, Richard Whittemore, Elizabeth Whittemore, Jonathan Whittemore, Hannah (Whittemore) Woodcock, William Whittemore and Sarah (Whit
2 CONC temore) Clark
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 21 Sep 1756 in Malden, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Whittemore-72 created 6 Sep 2011 | Last modified 4 Oct 2020
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT 1688 taxed in Charlestown (REGISTER, vol. 34, p. 274).
2 CONT 1702-03-16 Representatives of Boston and Charlestown to renew the bound marks between these towns "are to meet at the House of Daniell Whittemore at ye Head of South River at Eight O'clock in the morning..." (Boston Record Commiss
2 CONC ioners, vol. 11, p. 18).
2 CONT 1704-10-20 contribution made to rebuilding Malden Meeting House (History of Malden, p. 214).
2 CONT 1724-06-21 sell estate of "Father Joseph Bassett" (Plymouth Deeds, vol. 19, p. 164).
2 CONT 1728-06-28 signed petition protesting location of new Meeting House (History of Malden, p. 504).
2 CONT 1756-10-04 will filed (Middlesex Probate #24781).
2 CONT Daniel bequethed to more than half of his children his longevity, since they lived more than 80 years, a long life in those early days.
2 CONT lived his 93 years on "the original family farm" he inherited from father, without much change.
