2 DATE BET 1724 AND 1742
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph, his wife Elizabeth, and son Edmund were all baptized at the same time 5 July 1719 Church of Rumney Marsh, Chelsea.  There is just the one child born and it presumed that Elizabeth died in 1721.  It is not k
2 CONC nown really when Joseph died, but he is not mentioned in the will of his father who died in 1743. There is some information in Documentary History of Chelsea, volume II, available on Google books.  Information also in 1952-1954 is
2 CONC sues of NEHGR. The parentage of his wife Elizabeth Chamberlain has not been determined.  A few possibilities have been proposed.  My favorite is that she was born 29 May 1699 (along with twin Mary), the daughter of Samuel Chamberl
2 CONC ain and Elizabeth Emerson of Chelmsford.  Another proposed set of parents in John and Hannah Chamberlain as it has been suggested that they had a daughter Elizabeth born in 1992, but that would make Elizabeth 26 at the time of her
2 CONC  marriage to Joseph which seems too old.  An old Whittemore genealogy book gave her father as Richard Chamberlain, but stated her birth date as 29 May 1699 and also said she was a twin.  But that Elizabeth is the daughter of Samue
2 CONC l.  But she would be the right age for marrying in 1718.
2 CONT
2 CONT It has been suggested that this is the Joseph Whittemore that relocated to Connecticut, but that appears to have been disproved.  It is not known what happened to this particular Joseph Whittemore who was the husband of Elizabeth 
2 CONC Chamberlain and the father of Edmund.  There were several Joseph Whittemores around at the same time, but a series on the Whittemore family in the 1952-1954 issues of the NEHGR states that this is not the one that went to Connecti
2 CONC cut.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other information that goes against the idea that this Joseph Whittemore had a second marriage and more children is the will of his father Daniel Whittemore probated in 1656.  In that will Daniel lists the following children as he
2 CONC irs:   Daniel, Lydia, Mary, Richard, Elizabeth, Jonathan, William, Hannah, and Sarah.  These are all his children except Joseph who has died.  The will also mentions just one grandchild, Edmund Whittemore, who was the son of Josep
2 CONC h and Elizabeth Chamberlain.  If this Joseph had a second wife and more children, it would seem that would have been listed as grandchildren of his deceased son Joseph in the will of Daniel Whittemore. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Whittemore-361
