1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DAVID, OF LITCHFIELD, N. H.
2 CONT        David  4.   Sou of John (3), Daniel (2), Thomas (1);   b.   April 16, 1706, at Maiden, Mass.;
2 CONT        married (1) Alice Kendall, March 11, 1730; (2)Sarah , who died
2 CONT        Dec. 3, 1825; he d. Sept. 1782, at Litchfield, N. H.  Issue,  i. David, 4. Nov. 1731, died Sept. 4, 1734.   ii, Alice, b. July 25,1733, d. Sept. 4,1733,
2 CONT        ae. 6 weeks,    iii. Alice, b. Dec. 24, 1734, d. young,   iv. Alice, b.  d.
2 CONT        young.    V. David, Jr., born 1737, d. young,    vi. Deborah, b.  , d.
2 CONT        young,   vii. Ruth, b. . married Thomas Hills, of Nottingham West,
2 CONT        (now   Hudson,  N. H.,) moved to Maine,    viii. Elizabeth, b. , in.
2 CONT        David Austin, moved to Maine,   ix. Persis, b. , m. Caleb Austin;
2 CONT        died in Bow, N. H., family extinct,  x. Jacob, b. Dec. 25,1748.  xi. Sarah,
2 CONT        b. , died young,   xii. Sarah, b. , died young.   David, the father,
2 CONT        came from Boston, where he was then a resident, to Dunstable, and from here, after a brief residence, to Litchfield. At Litchfield, he purchased the fann, which has been in the possession of the family down to this date, an
2 CONC d is now owned by his descendants, Jacob and Zachariah K. H. His name is attached to a petition for the incorporation of Litchfield, as a town, March 28, 1746. At the first annual town meeting of Litchfield, held in March, 1750, h
2 CONC e was chosen Treasurer and sealer of leather; also, in 1761-2
