2 CONT VIEW ALL
2 CONT Name Meaning
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Crossman
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel
2 CONT English (Somerset and Devon): topographic name for someone who lived by a cross, from Middle English cros, cros(s)e + man.
2 CONT Americanized form of German Crössmann or Krössmann: from Middle Low German krōs, krüs ‘pitcher’, and hence a metonymic occupational name for maker of these; alternatively, a metonymic occupational name for a butcher, from Middle H
2 CONC igh German kroese ‘tripe’.
2 CONT MORE
2 CONT Americanized form of German Grossmann .
2 CONT Dictionary of American Family Names © Patrick Hanks 2003, 2006.
