1 NOTE from History of Norton, Massachusetts
2 CONT "At the same chh.-meeting abovesd., the chh. did, by a vote, suspend James Briggs from
2 CONT communion with them at ye Lord's Supper, for his unjust seperation from communion with
2 CONT ym, & his setting up a seperate meeting at ye house in which he dwells, in opposition to
2 CONT ye meeting and worship of God in this chh. and precint. also, att ye same chh.-meeting
2 CONT abovesd., ye chh. did, by a vote, suspend Phinehas Briggs; aslo Joshuah Campbel, and
2 CONT abigal his wife; also Mary ffiney, ye wife of John ffiney, senior; also John ffiney, ye 2nd; also
2 CONT Lydia Campbel, ye wife of william Campbel, - for their unjust seperation from communion
2 CONT with ys chh., and their Joyning with yose yt have set up and held a seperate meeting,
2 CONT in opposition to ye meeting and worship of God in this chh. and precinct."
