2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cushman-1122
2 CONT
2 CONT Phebe Bassett formerly Cushman
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1737 in Taunton, Bristol, Province of Massachusetts Bay  [uncertain]
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Jabez Cushman and Sarah (Padelford) Cushman
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Hannah Cushman, Huldah Cushman, Sarah (Cushman) Bassett, Molly Cushman, Zebedee Cushman, Samuel Cushman and Jabez Cushman
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Joseph Bassett Jr. — married 2 Dec 1756 in Bridgewater, Plymouth, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Caleb Bassett, Phebe (Bassett) Leonard, Nathan Bassett, Abigail (Bassett) Lathrop, Joseph Bassett III, Hannah (Bassett) Alger, David Bassett and Cushman Bassett
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 25 Feb 1796 in Bridgewater, Plymouth, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 1 Jul 2019 | Created 7 Dec 2016
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Phebe Cushman. [1][2][3][4][5] Born 1737 Plymouth, Plymouth, Massachusetts, USA. [6][7][8]
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 25 Feb 1796. Bridgewater, Plymouth, Massachusetts, USA. [9][10][11]
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried Bridgewater, Plymouth, Massachusetts, USA. [12]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Husband @P187@. Wife @P188@. Child: @P152@. Marriage 02 Dec 1756. Bridgewater, Plymouth, Massachusetts, USA. [13]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband @P236@. Wife @P237@. Child: @P188@. Marriage 2 Dec 1736. Taunton, Bristol, Massachusetts, USA. [14]
2 CONT
2 CONT Plymouth Colony and Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT From John Maltby: Lt. Joseph Bassett (Jr.), son of Joseph and Elisabeth (Ames) Bassett, married as his 1st wife to Phebe Cushman, daughter of Jabez and Sarah (Paddleford) Cushman,[15] on 2 Dec. 1756 in Bridgewater.[16] She was bor
2 CONC n ca. 1737,[17] a granddaughter of Benjamin and Sarah (Eaton) Cushman,[18] and of Jonathan and Hannah (King) Paddleford.[19] She died on 25 Feb. 1796 in Bridgewater, aged 58 years,[20] and Joseph remarried. Lt. Joseph Bassett died
2 CONC  testate on 6 May 1803 in Bridgewater, aged 72 years,[21] his will dated 5 Apr. 1798, and probated on 2 June 1803, mentioned his wife Sarah, his five sons Caleb, Nathan, Joseph, David and Cushman Bassett, and his three daughters P
2 CONC hebe Leonard, Abiel Lathrop, and Hannah Alger, and he named his son Caleb Bassett as executor of his estate.[22] (See Appendix (A) for a full transcription of his will.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Bassett (Jr.) had had children by Phebe Cushman:[23] Caleb Bassett, born on 11 Nov. 1757 in Bridgewater, married Bethiah Keith, daughter of Benjamin and Abigail (Leach) Keith, of Bridgewater, on 18 Apr. 1782 in Bridgewater,
2 CONC  and they settled in New Gloucester, ME. Phebe Bassett, born on 19 Aug. 1759 in Bridgewater, married Barnabas “Barney” Leonard, of Taunton, MA, on 5 Feb. 1780 in Bridgewater. She died on 30 Oct. 1838 in Bridgewater, aged 79 years.
2 CONC  Nathan Bassett, born on 12 Aug. 1763 in Bridgewater, settled in Genesee, NY. Abigail Bassett, born on 12 Sept. 1765 in Bridgewater, married Seth Lathrop (Jr.), son of Seth and Mehitabel (Daily) Lathrop, on 25 Nov. 1784 in Bridgew
2 CONC ater. Joseph Bassett (3rd), born on 5 Jan. 1769 in Bridgewater, married Ruth Leach, daughter of James and Hasadiah (Keith) Leach, on 26 Jan. 1792 in Bridgewater. Hannah Bassett, born on 8 June 1771 in Bridgewater, married Deacon J
2 CONC ames Alger Jr., son of James and Martha (Kingman) Alger, of Bridgewater, on 29 May 1791 in Bridgewater. She died a widow on 16 Jan. 1845 in Bridgewater, aged 73 years, of old age. David Bassett, married Phebe Dean, daughter of Job
2 CONC  and Judith (Williams) Dean, of Raynham, MA, on 15 Dec. 1796 in Raynham, and they settled in Maine. Rev. Cushman Bassett, also settled in Maine. Sources
2 CONT
