1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Katherine Saltonstall===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Born: 19 Jun 1704, New London CT
2 CONT * Marriage: William Brattle on 23 Nov 1727 in Cambridge MA
2 CONT * Died: 28 Apr 1752, Cambridge MA
2 CONT
2 CONT Katherine married William Brattle, son of William Brattle and Elizabeth Hayman, on 23 Nov 1727 in Cambridge MA. (William Brattle was born on 18 Apr 1706 in Cambridge MA, christened on 21 Apr 1706 in Cambridge MA and died in Oct 17
2 CONC 76 in Halifax Nova Scotia Canada.)  He survived her and married again in 1755, Mrs. Martha, widow of James Allen, and daughter of Thomas Fitch.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William Brattle and Katherine Saltonstall, born at Cambridge:
2 CONT
2 CONT * William bp Jan 4 1729
2 CONT * Katherine b June 2 1730, bp June 7 1730. Married John Mico Wendell.
2 CONT * Mary bp Mar 8 1733
2 CONT * Elizabeth bp June 16 1734 died May 8 1743
2 CONT * Sarah bp June 6 1736
2 CONT * William (again) bp Oct 8 1738
2 CONT * Lucy bp Mar 30 1740
2 CONT * Thomas bp July 14 1742. Never married.
2 CONT * Elizabeth (again) bp May 8,1743, died 10 July 1754.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Of his nine children, only two lived to maturity, Katherine in whom the line but not the name was perpetuated, and Thomas."
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From New England Life in the Eighteenth Century: Representative Biographies from ... By Clifford Kenyon Shipton [https://books.google.com/books?id=lxOxa8LCrAYC&lpg=PA204&ots=JyPSSZ7iZ7&dq=Martha%20(Fitch)%20Brattle&pg=PA204#v=onep
2 CONC age&q=Martha%20(Fitch)%20Brattle&f=false page 204]
2 CONT
2 CONT "When he [William Brattle] was quarreling with George Whitfield, his wife and daughter lay sick of throat distemper (19), probably in this instance diphtheria which he had brought into his home from the bedside of some patient.  F
2 CONC ive small daughters and a son were carried from the mansion to the burial ground.  Katherine Saltonstall Brattle survived these blows only to succumb to the smallpox on April 28, 1752.  The Major was married again on November 2, 1
2 CONC 755, this time to Martha Fitch Allen, widow of James Allen (A.B. 1717).  She died on August 26, 1763."
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:  Sibley's Harvard Graduates, Class of 1722
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Genealogies of the Families  and Descendants of the Early Settlers of Watertown, Mass. by Henry Bond, M.D.  Boston, 1860."[http://files.usgwarchives.net/ma/middlesex/towns/watertown/watertown756-928.txt link]
2 CONT
2 CONT (children of Gov. Gurdon Saltonstall coninued from p. 924:
2 CONT
2 CONT By his 2nd wife, Elizabeth, he had:
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Katherine Saltonstall b. June 19, 1704; m. Thomas Brattle of Boston.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
