2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas WALLEY (Boston merchant and active revolutionary in the struggle for Independence), who was born 1725.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married firstly Mary KNEELAND (on 29 Dec 1748) by whom he had Mary 'Polly' WALLEY - see http://www.geocities.com/bostonancestors/langdon.htm .
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas WALLEY married secondly 13 December 1767 to Sarah HURD** (by whom Sarah 'Sally' WALLEY who was in turn the mother of fiery anti-slavery campaigner Wendell PHILLIPS).
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas died 1806 in Boston. Thomas was mentioned on a memorial in King's Chapel Burying Ground, Boston, Suffolk County, Massachusetts, United States with a death date of 5 September 1806.[1]
