2 CONT * AFNH0QC-DC
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=8FQMAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA174&ots=4pPpAEzUyG&dq=Richard%20gray%201602&pg=PA174#v=onepage&q=Richard%20gray%201602&f=false "Notes on the Ancestry of Thomas Graves"]  Essex Institute Historical Collec
2 CONC tions (Google eBook) Essex Institute Press, 1895 - Essex County (Mass.).  Page 173
2 CONT
2 CONT >Thomas Graye1 of Wapping, mariner. Will dated 15 Nov., 1625; prov. 6 April, 1627. Mentions ship Rainbow; sister Katherine Graye; brother Thomas Coytmore; cousin Mary Egglefleld; sister Parnell Parker, widow, and her daughters. P.
2 CONC  C. C. Skinner, 45.
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=_P1v1mqnsOYC&lpg=PA160&ots=pnyrYMvscc&dq=Thomas%20gray%20of%20Wapping%201625&pg=PA160#v=onepage&q=Thomas%20gray%20of%20Wapping%201625&f=false "Will of William Cottemore of Wapping"], written
2 CONC  5 June 1626.  Genealogical Gleanings in England, NEHGR, page 160
2 CONT
2 CONT >My wife Katherine to be executrix and sons in law Thomas Gray and William Raiusborough of Wapping aforesaid, mariners, to be overseers. The witnesses were Raphe Bower pub. scr. and John Wheatley serve to the said scr. Hele, 125.
2 CONT
