1 NAME Jonathan /Tyng/
2 GIVN Jonathan
2 SURN Tyng
2 _MARNM Tyng
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 DEC 1642
2 ADDR
3 CITY Boston
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 JAN 1723
2 ADDR
3 CITY Woburn
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 OCCU Merchant 
1 TITL Col.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Here lyes buried the body of Jonathan Tyng, Esqr., who deceased January 19th, 1723-1724, in ye 81st year of his age.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan Tyng, Esquire - Colonel - was born December 15, 1642, son of Colonel Edward Tyng, of Boston (died in Dunstable, 1681). He married Sarah, daughter of Hezekiah Usher; died 1713. Judith, his widow, died 1736. His father's fa
2 CONC mily was one of the most prominent families in Massachusetts. He was Colonel of the Second Regiment of foot and a justice of the court, was one of Sir Edmund Andros's Council, 1687, a magistrate, and a man of influence. 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. HON. JONATHAN TYNG, son of Hon. Edward, born December 15, 1642. He was one of the earliest settlers of the original township, and occupied a commanding position in civil and m.ilitary affairs. He was colonel of the north or upp
2 CONC er Middlesex regiment and was vested with unusual authority by the government of the province. In the successive wars with the Indians he was in command over a considerable territory and at all times secured the confidence of the 
2 CONC government.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1676 he was appointed superintendent over the friendly Indians colonized at Dunstable. In this mission, Robert Parris was his deputy or assistant.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In the commission of King James II. to Governor Joseph Dudley, 1686, he is named one of the councillors. The same council was continued through the administration of Governor Andros. Crowning the honors of of a serviceable career 
2 CONC he was a judge of the court of Middlesex county from 1702 to 1719.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In the superior qualities of his mind and character in the activities of his useful life and in the achievements of his descendants is found the inviting and substantial material for a volume of local history.  
2 CONT
2 CONT [p.84] Hon. Jonathan Tyng married Sarah Usher, daughter of Hezekiah and Frances Usher of Boston. A record of her death has not been discovered. She was the mother of his children. He married, second, in Boston, May 30, 1706, Sarah
2 CONC  (Gibbons-Richards) Davie. She was a daughter of William Gibbons, born in Hartford, August 17, 1645. She married James Richards of Hartford, who died July 29, 1680; she married, second, Humphrey Davie of Boston, his second wife. S
2 CONC he died at Woburn, February 28, 1712-3 "in the 69year of her age . Gravestone at Woburn. In Massachusetts Historical collections, sixth series, Vol II., page 298, is found an item by Samuel Sewall; "March 4, 1713-14 went to Woburn
2 CONC  to attend the funeral of Aunt Tyng being his second wife."  
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, third, Judith (Reyner) Fox, a daughter of Rev. John Reyner of Plymouth, Mass., and Dover, N.H., and widow of Rev. Jabez Fox of Woburn.  
2 CONT
2 CONT He removed from Dunstable to Woburn 1712 or 1713, and there died January 19, 1723-4. His widow died June 5, 1736, aged 98 years. Gravestones at Woburn.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Five children were born in Boston and seven in Dunstable.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Early Generations of the Founders of Old Dunstable: Thirty Families By Ezra S. Stearns.  Page 84. [https://books.google.com/books?id=UCduacZqPYcC&lpg=PA84&ots=NsCm3cpI1f&dq=Sarah%20(Gibbons)%20Richards&pg=PA84#v=onepage&q&f=true
2 CONC  GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * The New England Merchants In The Seventeenth Century By Bernard Bailyn.  Page [https://books.google.com/books?id=y-J8CgAAQBAJ&lpg=PT126&ots=QFz2DHOy2N&dq=Sarah%20(Gibbons)%20Tyng&pg=PT125#v=onepage&q=Sarah%20(Gibbons)%20Tyng&f=t
2 CONC rue GoogleBooks]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *ref: [http://records.ancestry.com/Jonathan_Tyng_records.ashx?pid=23985349 public Ancestry record]
2 CONT  Married 1st Sarah Usher; 11 children:
2 CONT *Francis Tyng
2 CONT *Elizabeth Tyng
2 CONT *Jonathan Tyng
2 CONT *John Tyng
2 CONT *Mary Tyng
2 CONT *William Tyng
2 CONT *Hezekiah Tyng
2 CONT *Edward Tyng
2 CONT *Joseph Tyng
2 CONT *Eleazer Tyng
2 CONT *Bersheba Tyng
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 2nd Judith Reyner.
