2 DATE AFT 1691
2 PLAC France
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *'''Sources:'''
2 CONT **https://www.biographi.ca/en/bio/tyng_edward_1680_91_1E.html
2 CONT **https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_governors_of_Acadia
2 CONT **https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_Tyng_(military_officer)
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~marshall/esmd90.htm Tyng Family]
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.  Col. Edward Tyng (Edward2, ___1); b. 26 Mar 1649 at Boston, MA; baptized 1 Apr 1649; m. Elizabeth Clarke, daughter of Lt. Thaddeus Clarke and Elizabeth Mitton, circa 1680 at Falmouth, ME; d. circa 1700 at France; as a prisoner
2 CONC  of the French.
2 CONT
2 CONT He resided at Portland, ME. He resided at Falmouth, ME. He was a member of the Ancient and Honorable Artillery Company in 1668. He was a councillor of New England, appointed by King James II on 6 Feb 1685. He was appointed Governo
2 CONC r of Annapolis after the reduction of Nova Scotia in 1690.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tyng was appointed Governor of Acadia until he was captured by Villebon and died in prison, at La Rochelle, some time after 1691.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Clarke was buried on 4 Jul 1690.      
2 CONT
2 CONT Known children of Col. Edward Tyng and Elizabeth Clarke were as follows:
2 CONT * i. Mary Tyng, m. Rev. John Fox.
2 CONT * ii. Comm. Edward Tyng; b. 1683 at Boston, MA; m. Elizabeth Southack, daughter of Cyprian Southack; m. Anna Waldo, daughter of Jonathan Waldo and Hanna Mason, 27 Jan 1731 at Boston, MA; d. 8 Sep 1755 at Boston, MA; apoplexy. He a
2 CONC nd Anna Waldo resided at Boston, MA. He was a merchant. He was a naval Commodore.
2 CONT * iii. Elizabeth Tyng; b. circa 1685; m. Samuel Franklin, son of Josiah Franklin and Ann Child, 16 May 1705 at Boston, MA.
2 CONT * iv. Jonathan Tyng; d. age 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=9TwvAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA102&ots=FcRZ3N4LHW&dq=elizabeth%20Clarke%20Edward%20Tyng&pg=PA102#v=onepage&q=elizabeth%20Clarke%20Edward%20Tyng&f=true Publication, Issue 5] By Society of Colonial Wars i
2 CONC n the Commonwealth of Massachusetts Page 102
2 CONT
2 CONT >Edward Tyng, b. 19 Feb., 1681/2 son of Edward and Elizabeth (Clarke) Tyng, of Boston. He married (1) Elizabeth, dau. of Capt. Cyprian Southack, and widow of Francis Parnel, and (2) Ann, dau. of Jonathan Waldo.
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''Edward the father''' was appointed by Sir Wm. Phips governor of Acadia. On returning from Port Royal in Oct., 1691, in a vessel commanded by Capt. John Alden, Tyng and John Nelson and Alden's son were taken prisoners by M. de 
2 CONC Bonaventure, sent to Quebec, and thence to France in Sept., 1692, where Tyng died in prison.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT *ref: [http://records.ancestry.com/Edward_Tyng_records.ashx?pid=23983344 public Ancestry record]
