1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born: 7 Feb 1651, Braintree MA Marriage: Anna Shepard on 8 Nov 1682 in Boston MA Died: 10 Aug 1690, Boston MA
2 CONT
2 CONT   General notes:
2 CONT
2 CONT Silversmith
2 CONT
2 CONT   Events in his life were:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Apprenticed about 1664 to John Hull in Boston MA 1
2 CONT * He worked from 1672 to 1774 as a silversmith in Boston MA continuing in the shop of his masters, Hull and Sanderson.
2 CONT * He worked from circa 1777 to 1790 as a silversmith in Boston MA having travelled for several years prior in England, establishing trade prospects for himself and for Hull and Sanderson. His work in the partnership was probably a
2 CONC dminastrative, though there are records of his working as a smith and watchmaker. 8
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel married Anna Shepard, daughter of Thomas Shepard and Anne Tyng, on 8 Nov 1682 in Boston MA. (Anna Shepard was born on 13 Sep 1663 in Charlestown MA, christened in Charlestown MA and died on 24 Jul 1708 in Quincy MA.)
2 CONT
2 CONT >DANIEL, Boston, goldsmith, eldest s. of Edmund the sec. ar. co. 1675, m. 9 Nov. 1682, Ann or Hannah, d. of Rev. Thomas Shepard of Charlestown, had Ann, b. 1 June 1685; and John, 21 July 1689, H. C. 1708; and d. 10 Aug. of the yr.
2 CONC  foll. his will of 4 Apr. 1690, being pro. 18 Sept. aft. His wid. m. 7 Jan. 1701, Rev. Moses Fiske as his sec. w and d. 24 July 1708. His d. Ann m. John HoIman, wh. may have been the gr. of H. C. 1700; and his only s. was speaker 
2 CONC of the ho. of Reps. 1729-39, many yrs. of his majesty's council, and d. 13 July 1767.
2 CONT
