1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nathaniel Williams, M.A. (Boston Latin School 1682, Harvard 1693). This Nathaniel Williams, 3rd, was a physician. In early life he removed to the West Indies, but soon returned to Boston, where he succeeded Ezekiel
2 CONC  Cheever as master of the Latin School (1703—1735). He married Ann, daughter of Dr. Samuel Bradstreet of Jamaica and granddaughter of Gov. Simon Bradstreet of Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Nathaniel_Williams_%2856%29_
2 CONT * Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts, United States. Births, Baptisms, Marriages, and Deaths, 1630-1699 (A Report of the Record Commissioners). (Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts, United States: Rockwell and Churchill, City Printers, 188
2 CONC 3), 136. 1675. Town. "Nathll.. of Nathll. & Mary Williams born Aug."
2 CONT *  Drake, Samuel G. (Samuel Gardner). The history and antiquities of Boston...from its settlement in 1630, to the year 1770: also, an introductory history of the discovery and settlement of New England, with notes critical and ill
2 CONC ustrative. (Boston, Massachusetts: Luther Stevens, 1856), 604. "1738. Jan. 10. Mr. Nathaniel Williams died on the tenth of January, in his sixty third year. He had been a Minister, Physician, and School-master. He was Master in th
2 CONC e Free Grammar School from 1703 to 1734; having succeeded Master Cheever, and was himself succeeded by the celebrated Master John Lovell. [Footnote: Mr. Williams was son of Nathaniel and Mary (Oliver) Williams, and was born Aug. 1
2 CONC 6th, 1675.]"
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=tchPAQAAIAAJ&pg=PA9&lpg=PA9&dq=anna+alcock+john+williams&source=bl&ots=pyqruU0VLy&sig=21aC93vimdiAG1kIK98saXCoD10&hl=en&sa=X&ei=WvGUVMXMEZfloASGsICAAw&ved=0CDAQ6AEwBg#v=twopage&q&f=true Putnam'
2 CONC s Monthly Historical Magazine and Magazine of New England History] (Google eBook).  Salem Press Publishing and Printing Company, 1915 - New England.  Page 7-9.  JOHN WILLIAMS OF NEWPORT, MERCHANT, AND HIS FAMILY. BY Gnonon ANDREWS
2 CONC  MORIARTY, JR., A.M.:
