1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Norrington-1
2 CONT
2 CONT On July 27, 1603 at Eastwell, Kent, Emma Norrington married Edmund Roots. He died and was buried at Ashford, Kent on September 13, 1613. The administration of his will was granted to "Eme Roots" his widow on January 17, 1613/14.
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1619 Emma had married John Mason. He died suddenly on July 18, 1621, "John Mason who died suddenly on the top of a load of hay was buried..." He was buried at Eastwell, Kent. The administration of his will was granted to "Emme 
2 CONC Mason," his widow on July 25, 1621.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emma originated at Eastwell, Kent "Emme Mason of the parish of Eastwell widow" and was enrolled at Sandwich in 1635 as a passenger on the Hercules. Upon her arrival to New England, she first resided at Salem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also on the Hercules with Emma, and listed immediately above her in the passenger list, was "Joseph Rootes of Great Charter." Without a doubt, this was her son, Josiah Roots. Great Charter was next to Ashford, (Josiah's baptism lo
2 CONC cation) and several Essex County records for Josiah Roots were misentered or misread as Joseph Roots.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Norrington-1
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with first husband, Edmund Roots
2 CONT # Edmund Roots was baptized on August 19, 164 at Eastwell, Kent. No further records.
2 CONT # Em Roots was baptized on February 2, 1605/6 at Eastwell, Kent. No further records.
2 CONT # Richard Roots was baptized on December 11, 1607 at Eastwell, Kent. He married Margery (_____) unknown surname.
2 CONT # Thomas Roots was baptized September 5, 1610 at Eastwell, Kent. By 1651 he married Katherine (_____) unknown surname. She was admitted into the Salem church on July 20, 1651; deposed on November 28, 1678 to being "aged about sixt
2 CONC y-two years. Thomas married (2nd) Sarah (_____) (Standish) Hutchinson after July 21, 1682 and before November 7, 1683. Sarah was the widow of James Standish and Richard Hutchinson.
2 CONT # Josiah Roots was baptized March 7, 1612/3 at Ashford, Kent. By about 1542 he had married Susanna (_____) unknown surname. On September 10, 1648 four children of Joseph (Josiah) Rootes were baptized at Salem.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with second husband, John Mason
2 CONT # Anne Mason was baptized on June 6, 1619 at Eastwell, Kent.
2 CONT # John Mason was baptized on October 1, 1620 at Eastwell, Kent.
2 CONT # Ruth Mason was baptized on January 21, 1621/2 at Eastwell, Kent. She was buried at Eastwell on March 15, 1625/6
2 CONT
