2 CONT '''Dorcas Abbott''' was born circa 1655 in Norwalk, Connecticut Colony, the daughter of George Abbott and Mary Weed.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married '''John Root''' (also recorded as Roots or Rootes) in 1678. The family relocated from Norwalk to Woodbury, where Dorcas was admitted to full communion at the First Congregational Church and baptized as an adult on 30 A
2 CONC ugust 1685.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorcas died on 15 May 1720 in Woodbury. Her husband, John Root, died three years later on 25 May 1723.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Identity Audit ==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Naming Conventions:''' While some secondary transcripts suggest "Dorothy," primary evidence confirms the name as '''Dorcas'''. Her father, George Abbott, explicitly refers to her as "Dorcas Roots" in his 1689 will. Woodbury c
2 CONC hurch records also consistently use Dorcas.
2 CONT * '''Adult Baptism:''' The Woodbury Church records (printed in TAG) document her adult baptism in 1685, a common practice for those joining the church after relocating from other parishes.
2 CONT * '''Parental Verification:''' Verified as a daughter of George Abbott of Norwalk through probate distribution and town records.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT The following children are recorded in Woodbury:
2 CONT
2 CONT # '''Susanna Root:''' bap. April 1685; d. 26 April 1738.
2 CONT # '''John Root (1st):''' bap. April 1685; d. young.
2 CONT # '''Mary Root:''' bap. April 1685; m. Robert Warner.
2 CONT # '''Josiah Root:''' bap. March 1688; d. 1727.
2 CONT # '''Bethia Root (1st):''' b. December 1691; d. 23 July 1700.
2 CONT # '''John Root (2nd):''' b. 9 June 1693; d. 3 August 1757.
2 CONT # '''Joseph Root:''' b. June 1698; d. 1761.
2 CONT # '''Bethia Root (2nd):''' b. 7 February 1703.
2 CONT # '''Thomas Root:''' d. 3 June 1727.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT * '''Probate:''' Fairfield Probate Records, Vol. 1689–1701. Will of George Abbott (1689).
2 CONT * '''Church Records:''' Woodbury, Litchfield County, CT. First Congregational Church Records, Vol. 1 (1670-1829).
2 CONT * '''The American Genealogist (TAG):''' Woodbury Church Records, baptism and membership of Dorcas Roots.
2 CONT * '''Cothren, William.''' ''History of Ancient Woodbury, Connecticut''. Waterbury, CT: 1854. (p. 675).
2 CONT * '''Hinman, Royal R.''' ''A Catalogue of the Names of the Early Puritan Settlers of the Colony of Connecticut''. Hartford: Case, Tiffany and Co., 1852.
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Abbott-166
