1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Larkum-3
2 CONT
2 CONT From Essex Institute Historical Collections, Volume 58 “Larcum.” Page 132-133 [https://books.google.com/books?id=nRkRAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA42&ots=aR6E1Nt619&dq=Mordecai%20Larcum&pg=PA133#v=onepage&q&f=true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Thomas2 Larcom (Mordecai1), was probably third son and born about 1661. He was a fisherman. He was married, first, to Hannah , by whom he had a son Thomas, recorded on the Manchester, Mass., records as born Feb. 16, 1694/5. He 
2 CONC married, second, Abigail, widow of Thomas Woodbery, about 1699-1700. On March 24, 1714, he was appointed fence viewer, and on March 15, 1715/6, he was appointed to enforce the law relating to swine. He died March 30, 1718.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Aug. 19, 1718, Abigail Larcom, widow of Thomas Larkum, late of Beverly, husbandman, sells four and a half acres of land to her son-in-law, John Masury, who had married her daughter by her first husband, Keziah Woodbery. On July
2 CONC  18, 1727, widow Abigail Larcom sells land in Mackerel Cove to John Thorndike, cordwinder. Dec. 25, 1739, Abigail Larcum is pronounced non compos mentis by the Beverly selectmen, and Brackenbury Patch (son-in-law), Mark Morse (son
2 CONC -in-law), and John Standley (husband of Thomas Larcom's sister, Rebecca), sign bond given by Brackenbury Patch, who is appointed guardian. Widow of Thomas Larkum died between June 5 and August, 1740 (Robert Hale's record).
2 CONT
2 CONT Child by first wife: 
2 CONT *Thomas, b. Feb. 16, 1694/5; probably died young. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by second wife: 
2 CONT # Phebe, b. 1702/3; m. Nov. 11, 1729, Brackenbury Patch, who was b. May 17, 1705. They had five children. Two d. young; the others were Hannah, Sarah and Benjamin. Brackenbury Patch d. May or June, 1743. Phebe, bar. March 18, 1787
2 CONC , aged 84. Widow Phebe Patch was bapt. Aug. 2, 1772.
2 CONT # Jemima, b. 1704; int. of m. Nov. 5, 1727, to Mark Morse. On March 3, 1728, Jemima, wife of Mark Morse, bapt. He was bur. May 5, 1783. She d. May 20, 1797, aged 93. They had seven children, Mark, Thomas, Samuel, Christian, Hannah
2 CONC , David, Jemima.
2 CONT # Hannah, birth and death or burial not found; m. John Bradford (second wife), March 31, 1741. They had one child, Robert. John Bradford was b. Feb. 26, 1689/90. and d. March 29, 1751. She was bapt. July 15, 1753 .
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
