1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Concerns
2 CONT #''' There is no known record of death.''' Wikitree's profile for Ebenezer (as of 28 Dec 2022) admittedly shows an insupportable death date. 
2 CONT ## Please do not re-enter 20 December 1785 for death unless a sourced is for it is first supplied to this Overview.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====WIKITREE; [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Rood-483 Ebenezer Rood (1704–abt. 1785)]
2 CONT * Ebenezer Rood was born February 21, 1704 in Norwich, New London, Connecticut. He was the son of George Rood and Hannah Bush. 
2 CONT * He married his wife Mary Green on May 9, 1726. Together they had the following children:
2 CONT ** Ebenezer Rood
2 CONT ** Mary Rood
2 CONT ** Sarah Rood
2 CONT ** Lowas Rood
2 CONT ** Lydia Rood 
2 CONT * '''Ebenezer passed away at some point.''' 
2 CONT ** (There's no viable family history book indicating that Ebenezer ever removed from Connecticut. The speculative death date, if it were true, would mean the American Revolution was well underway. Whether the war cause a change of
2 CONC  residence outside of Connecticut may never be known. – Ken Shelley, 3 September 2025._
2 CONT * '''Sources'''
2 CONT ** ''Vital Records of Norwich, 1659-184''8 (Society of Colonial Wars in the State of Connecticut, Hartford, 1913) Part 1.
2 CONT *** Page 41. Gives parents' names, birth date, birth place.
2 CONT *** Page 103. Gives his marriage date, wife's name, children, death date.
