1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Allison-7735
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Jane Allison''' was the daughter of Ralph Allison and Ann Dixon.  She died after 1 September 1728 (date of deed, Robert Leach and Jane Leach deeded property to Sarah Allen),[4] or 1734.[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogical Dictionary of Maine and New Hampshire (part 5, p. 626), refers to this Jane Allison, daughter of Ralph, writing that she married (1) Peter Shaw, (2) William Bradford of Beverly; his 2nd wife; he was Rachel Rayment’s w
2 CONC idower; and (3), at Manchester, 13 March 1717/8, to Robert Leach, Jr.[1][2][3]. His 3rd wife.  He married 1) Sarah 2) Hannah.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Peter Shaw and his wife, Jane Allison[5] (uncertain birth order),
2 CONT # Sarah Shaw, married 8 November 1694, John Tuck
2 CONT # Walter Shaw, married 4 December 1696, Anna Gale
2 CONT # Peter Shaw (probably), married (intention) 14 October 1705, Bethiah Lovett
2 CONT # Mary Shaw (probably), married (1) 29 November 1711, Cornelius Balch; married (2) 1 February 1753, Dr. Michael Dwinell of Topsfield, and died his widow.
2 CONT # Elizabeth Shaw, born about 1689, married (intention) 10 August 1712, Roger Haskins or Haskell.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
