1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William was born in 1715 in Beverly, Massachusetts, the son of William Bradford and Grace Elliot. He married, in 1737 at Boxford, Massachusetts, to Mary Lambert. It appears that they removed to Amherst, New Hampshi
2 CONC re between 1742 and 1745 (when William was appointed town surveyor). After Mary's death in 1770, he married (in Amherst?) to Rachel Small. He passed away in 1791, in Amherst, Hillsborough, New Hampshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT A Patriot of the American Revolution for NEW HAMPSHIRE.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A013436  DAR Ancestor # A013436]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT DAR ancestor ID A013436 for William Bradford Sr. on dar.org.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT William was born in 1715 in Beverly, Massachusetts, the son of William Bradford and Grace Elliot. He married, in 1737 at Boxford, Massachusetts, to Mary Lambert. It appears that they removed to Amherst, New Hampshire between 1742 
2 CONC and 1745 (when William was appointed town surveyor). After Mary's death in 1770, he married (in Amherst?) to Rachel Small. He passed away in 1791, in Amherst, Hillsborough, New Hampshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Bradford, Sr. is identified as a DAR Patriot. ID #A013436.[1]
2 CONT Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage records show various dates: 23 Oct 1737, 10 Jan 1737, and 18 Jan 1837. The Jan records appear to be from Middleton (Mary's home), and the Oct records are from Boxford (William's home town at the time). After reviewing all
2 CONC  of the available records, I believe they were married in Boxford, thus 23 Oct 1837. I'm open to persuasion otherwise. --Scott Prentice
2 CONT William Bradford was appointed surveyor for the year, 1745, along with, Deacon Hobbs, and James Cofrren. They were the first surveyors of highways appointed in the township (Amherst).[2]
2 CONT From History of the town of Amherst, Hillsborough County, New Hampshire, by Daniel F. Secomb, 1883. Pages 516-517.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT BRADFORD.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. William Bradford, from Middleton, Mass., settled in Souhegan West, at an early date. He m. (1) Mary Lambert 18 January, 1737. She was b. 11 March, 1718; d. 18 February, 1770 ; m. (2) Rachel Small, who d. in 1802. He d. 1791. Hi
2 CONC s will was presented for probate 7 September, 1791.
2 CONT Children (the two last by second wife) —
2 CONT 2. Samuel, b. about 1738; m. Anna Washer, of Amherst, 17 December, 1761 ; was a Revolutionary soldier; settled in Hillsborough ; d. in Antrim 5 February, 1813.
2 CONT 3. Patience, m. Joseph Lovejoy, of Amherst, 9 July, 1761 ; d. in Amherst, 3 March, 1826, aged 85.
2 CONT 4. Mary, m. John Averill, of Amherst ; d. in Mont Vernon 21 August, 1811 ; aged 73. She was baptized in Middleton, Mass., 1712.
2 CONT 5. Enos, b. 3 November, 1744 ; m. Sarah Chandler, of Bedford, 24 January, 1769 ; d. of starvation, from a disease of the throat which prevented him from swallowing food.
2 CONT 6. Joseph, a Revolutionary soldier ; d. at Medford, Mass., July, 1775.
2 CONT 7. William, a Revolutionary soldier and a soldier of the war of 1812.
2 CONT 8. Huldah, unmarried.
2 CONT 9. Olive, in. Reuben Boutell, Jr., 11 November, 1779; rem. to Antrim 1783.
2 CONT 10. Eunice, m. Moses Pettengill 4 February, 1779.
2 CONT 11. Hannah, b. 20 May, 1773 ; m. James Tuttle, 5 July, 1798.
2 CONT 12. Lambert, b. 18 March, 1775; d. in Merrimack 12 February, 1850
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bradford-4198
2 CONT
