1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daughters of American Revolution Ancestor #: [http://services.dar.org/public/dar_research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A013331 A013331] Patriotic service 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Capt Andrew Bradford'''
2 CONT * Birth:	Nov 1 1717 - Beverly, Essex County, Massachusetts
2 CONT * Death:	1798 - Milford, Hillsborough, NH, US
2 CONT * Parents:	William Bradford, Grace Elliott
2 CONT * Wives:	Rebecca Cole, Hannah Goffe
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT He rem. to Souhegan, N. H., November 27, 1743, previous to its incorporation as the town of Amherst. Rem. to Hillsborough, but he died in Milford, aged over 80 years. He was known as "Captain Andrew". (Browne, p. 2:77)
2 CONT
2 CONT He bought the right of John Bowtel of Reading, Mass., also right of John Farrington of Lynn, Mass., to lot No. 22 and to lot No. 110, respectively, in Souhegan West, being farm now [1901] owned by J. Fitch Crosby. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Rebecca Cole in 1743 and came to his home in the wilderness.
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Bradford, "housewright" in 1760 was listed in a document along with John Goffe and John Hall of Derryfield
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family==
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 34. Capt. Andrew Bradford, from Middleton, Mass., brother of William Bradford, settled in Souhegan West previous to its incorporation as a town. He d. in Milford in 1798, aged 80. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT #  Rebecca Cole in 1743 (born 1723)  She died before 1757.
2 CONT # Mrs. Hannah (Goffe) Chandler, widow of *Thomas Chandler, of Bedford, daughter of Col. John Goffe. She was b. 16 January, 1723; d. in Milford 14 December, 1819. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by first marriage
2 CONT # John  Born: 1744             at: Souhegan West, Hillsborough, New Hampshire  Married Sarah PUTNAM  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by second marriage—
2 CONT # Rebecca, b. 7 November. 1757.
2 CONT # Mary, b. 12 June, 1760; m. John Wallace, of Amherst.
2 CONT # Andrew, b. 11 June, 1763; m. Lucy Parker 19 December, 1785. .
2 CONT # Mehitable, b. 27 July, 1766.  Married 1) Elijah Averill 2) Henry Codman 3) Upton
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
