2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogical Summary
2 CONT
2 CONT Priscilla Randall was born, probably "Cape Porpus" (now part of Kennebunkport), York County, now Maine, about 1666.[1] She died (widow of William) in Beverly, Essex County, Province of Massachusetts Bay, 23 Apr 1752, aged 86 years
2 CONC .[2] Priscilla was the daughter of Richard Randall of Saco and Cape Porpoise, and his wife, whose name is not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Priscilla married, perhaps Saco, York County, before 26 May 1685 (fornication court record), William Presbury.[3][4][5] He was born, probably Saco, about 1663 (he came of age in 1684).[6] William died, perhaps Beverly, probably be
2 CONC tween November 1717 and 16 March 1717/8,[7] and before 31 March 1718 (administration granted).[8] William was the son of John Presbury and his wife, whose name and/or identity is unproven.
2 CONT
2 CONT At Maine and Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT According to her testimony, Priscilla lived at Cape Porpus, York County, now Maine, until she "went away" at age eighteen, when she married William Presbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hostilities and raids sent William and Priscilla, with their family, to Beverly, Massachusetts. The family lived in the Beverly Farms area.[citation needed]
2 CONT
2 CONT William died between November 1717 and March 1717/8. Afterward, Priscilla sold their Beverly homestead and dwelling to John Cleaves.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1726/7, widows and sisters, Priscilla Presbury and Sarah West, claimed their father Richard Randall's land in Cape Porpus, and sold it to Priscilla's son, Edward and Stephen Presbury, then both shipwrights of Newbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1730, her son Stephen claimed his grandfather's Saco Page Plantation and sold it to Nathan Whitney.
2 CONT
2 CONT Priscilla long survived as his widow, she died in Beverly, 23 April 1752, age 86.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family
2 CONT
2 CONT William and Priscilla (Randall) Presbury/Presson were the parents of ten (10) known children (birth order of the oldest two children is unknown),[9]
2 CONT
2 CONT David Presbury,[10] born, probably Saco, about 1688 (age at death),[11] died in Manchester, Essex County, June 1763, age 73;[12] married (1) in Beverly, 21 April 1707, by Robert Hale, Esq,[13] to Mary Pearce of Manchester.[14] the
2 CONC n of Marblehead, he married (2) in Beverly, 14 August 1719, Anne Hill of Beverly,[15][16] their intention having been earlier published at Beverly, 7 June 1719.[17] presumably the "Mrs. ------ [Presson]," who died in Manchester, 1
2 CONC 5 May 1769, aged 76 years.[18]
2 CONT Edward Presbury, born, probably Saco, before 1690 (guess),[19] died, perhaps Newburyport, Essex County, after 15 May 1765 (acknowledged a deed);[20] married (1) in Newbury, Essex County, 27 August 1713, Catherine Pierce,[21] born 
2 CONC in Newbury, 18 September 1690, and died before 1749 (he married again), the daughter of Daniel Pierce Jr. and his wife, Elizabeth Milward; married (2) in Newbury, 22 May 1749 Jane Stevens,[22] died, perhaps Newbury, after 24 Octob
2 CONC er 1764 (acknowledged a deed).[23]
2 CONT Nehemiah Presson, born in Beverly, 15 January 1691/2,[24] presumably died, perhaps Beverly, after 6 October 1765 (son is Nehemiah Jr in baptismal record);[25] married (1) in Beverly, 16 December 1714 by Rev. Thos Blowers, Abigail 
2 CONC Allen,[26] presumed the Abigail born in Manchester, 10 June 1690 (of Samuell, jr. and Abigall),[27] daughter of Samuel Allen, Jr. and Abigail Williams, Abigail Presson died in Beverly, 18 November 1743 (wife of Nehemiah);[28] marr
2 CONC ied (2) in Beverly, 11 October 1744, Abigail [(_____)] Allen,[29] presumed the widow Abigail Preston, buried in Beverly, 31 October 1783.[30]
2 CONT Mary Presson, born in Beverly, 5 March 1694/5;[31] married in Manchester, 16 December 1720, Samuel Williams,[32] the son of Daniel Williams and his wife, Abigail Allen.
2 CONT Stephen Presson, born in Beverly, 3 May 1697,[33] died, probably Newbury, before 12 March 1750 (guardianship granted);[34] married in Newbury, 3 June 1723, Abigail Sargent,[35] born in Newbury, 26 June 1704,[36] the daughter of Ed
2 CONC ward Sargent, and his wife Elizabeth Plaisted.[37]
2 CONT Benjamin Presson, born in Beverly, 1 January 1699/1700,[38] died, perhaps Manchester, before 12 December 1743 (administration granted);[39][40] married (1) in Manchester, 15 April 1723, Mary (Hilton) Woodbury, baptized 16 April 17
2 CONC 04 (dau. of Margaret) at First Congregational Church, Marblehead, the daughter of William and Margaret (Stilson) Hilton and widow of Samuel Woodbury; married (2) in Manchester, 6 May 1737, Lydia (Lee) Goodale,[41] born in Manchest
2 CONC er 19 April 1699,[42][43] died before 18 June 1744 (administration granted),[44][45][46] the daughter of Samuel and Rebecca (Masters) Lee and widow of Ezekiel Goodale;[47]
2 CONT Randall Presson, born in Beverly, 3 April 1702,[48] died in Beverly 27 March 1744, about age 42 years,[49] or aged 41 years, 11 months and 24 days;[50] married in Beverly, 2 July 1723, Susannah Stone,[51] born in Beverly, 20 Augus
2 CONC t 1702, died in Beverly, 1751,[52] the daughter of John Stone and his second wife, Sarah Gale.[53]
2 CONT William Presson, born in Beverly, 1 January 1704/5,[54] died, probably Chester, Rockingham County, New Hampshire, before 29 October 1766, the date administration of his estate was granted to the widow, Mary Presson;[55] married in
2 CONC  Beverly, 2 May 1728, Mary Raymond,[56] born in Beverly, 31 January 1709/10,[57] the daughter of Nathaniel2 Rayment (John1) and his wife, Rebecca3 Conant (Lot2, Roger1).
2 CONT Nathan Presson, born in Beverly, 18 May 1707;[58] married in Salisbury, Essex County, 13 December 1727, Martha Collins.[59]
2 CONT Ruth Presson, born in Beverly, 25 March 1710,[60] died in Ipswich, Essex County, 3 March 1787, aged about 77;[61] she is presumed[62] the woman who married, perhaps then Chebacco (now Essex), Essex County, or Ipswich, shortly afte
2 CONC r 19 August 1727 (date of Ipswich intention), William Goodhue,[63] the son of Nathaniel Goodhue and his wife, Mercy Hawkes.[64]
