2 CONT 1727. York Deeds, multiple vols., 12 (2):224; digital images, InternetArchive, "Priscilla Presburys test" (testimony of Priscilla Presberry of Beverly ad perpetuam Rei Memoriam in Salem, 6 Oct 1727); also as Priscilla Presberry te
2 CONC stimony in [York Couny (Maine)] Deeds, 1642-1904, 12:224; digital images, FamilySearch, FSL digital collection (DGS) 008297471, image 246 of 688.
2 CONT Priscilla Presberry of Beverly aged about sixty one Years testifieth that she lived with her Father Richard Randall at Capeporpus until she was about eighteen Years old & very well remembers one John Miller who lived about a Mile 
2 CONC from her Fathers House & that he the sd Miller did possess & improve a certain Farm butting Westerly on a Creek called Millers Creek where one Gilbert Endecot built a Saw Mill & Easterly on a Cove then called Long Cove Southerly o
2 CONC n a Place called the Opening That the sd Miller lived there ever since she could remember any Thing till she the sd Priscilla came away which was when she was about eighteen Years old.     Priscilla X Presbury's Mark.
2 CONT Essex Sc/Priscilla Presbury psonally appearing made Oath to the Truth of the above written Evidence signed under her Hand — Taken ad perpetuam Rei Memoriani in Salem Octobr 6, 1727.
2 CONT 1730. York Deeds, multiple vols., 14 (1906):275-76; digital images, HathiTrust, Stephen Presbury to Nathan Whittny 1730 deed; dated 5 August 1730, recorded 10 March 1730[/1], acknowledged 23 December 1730; William Presbury's name 
2 CONC is not mentioned in the deed. Grantor is "Stephen Presbury of Nubarry ... Massachusetts"; conveyance refers to "Fifty Acres of Upland .... formerly known & called by the name of Page." Grantor warrants against the "lawful Claims &
2 CONC  Demands of the Heirs of my Grandfather John Presbary Decd"; witnessed by Saml Sewall and Nathaniel Whitney.
2 CONT
