1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Page 4
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.  John 2  Stone  (John1)  was  born  about  the  year  1622.  He married  Abigail  Dixey,  daughter  of  Capt.  William  and  Anna Dixey,  about  1652,  and  lived  in  Beverly,  where  he  kept  an  inn from  1673  to  1682.  H
2 CONC e  is  called  a  seaman  in  1677,  and  it  is probable  that  the  business  of  the  inn  was  the  principal  care  of his  wife.  It  is  recorded  that  a  rally  of  the  militia,  under  Capt. Dixey,  took  place  at  the
2 CONC   Stone  inn  at  eight  o'clock  on  the  morning of  January  14,  1676. § 
2 CONT
2 CONT Stone  was  an  overseer  of  Robert  Morgan's  will  in  1672.  He took  the  oath  of  fidelity  in  1677.  He  died  before  September 25,  1691,  when  his  widow  and  administratrix  presented  an  inventory, taken  by  Paul
2 CONC   Thorndike,  Zachariah  Herrick  and Nehemiah  Grover,  amounting  to  £228:10.  Abigail  Stone,  whose bondsmen  were  Joseph  Morgan  and  Sergeant  Balch,  died  before completing  her  trust  and  administration  was  granted
2 CONC   to  Samuel Stone  "now  eldest  son,"  July  12, 1703.  He  presented  an  account 
2 CONT and  a  division  of  the  estate  on  March  13, 1703/4,  the  heirs  being sons  Samuel  (double  portion),  Jonathan  and  Nehemiah,  daughters Abigail  Briscoe  and  Anna  Stone,  and  grandchildren  Hannah,  Abigail  and  Wil
2 CONC liam  Stone,  children   of  William   Stone, deceased. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail  (Dixey)  Stone's  age  was  estimated  as  forty-three  in 1678  and  about  forty  in  1679,  in  legal  cases  in  which  she  testified, from  the  evidence  in  which  we  learn  that  she  employed  two maids,  Sarah
2 CONC   Riggs  and  Mary  Barrett,  and  that  included  in  her finery  were  "a  great  handkerchief  with  spots  in  it,  a  lace  cap with  running  strings,  and  a  long  neck-cloth  laced  at  both  ends."
2 CONT
2 CONT She  died  between  1691  and  1703. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children :  — 
2 CONT
2 CONT i.       '''John''',  b.  25:  9:  1654,  in  Salem;  d.  before  1703/4,  s.  p. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.  ii.      Samuel,  b.  15:  9:  1658,  in  Salem. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5.  iii.     William. 
2 CONT
2 CONT iv.  Jonathan,  bapt.  10:  3:  1668,  in  Beverly;  m.  Hannah  Herrick  June 21,  1706;  probably  d.  s.  p.;  she  d.  Feb.  9,  1746,  aged  seventy-nine, his  widow. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6.  v.      Nehemiah,  bapt.  May  29,  1670,  in  Beverly. 
2 CONT
2 CONT vi.  Abjgail,  b.  about  1672;  m.  Capt.  Robert  Briscoe  of  Beverly  before 1692  ;j  d.  June  1,  1724,  aged  fifty-two.  Capt.  Briscoe  was  a  man of  large  wealth  and  of  prominence  in  the  community,  serving  th
2 CONC e 
2 CONT town  as  selectman,  assessor,  treasurer  and  representative  to  the General  Court.  He  presented  the  town  with  a  bell  in  1712  and the  church  with  a  silver  communion  cup  in  1718,  and  the  elegance of  his  
2 CONC house  was  still  remembered  a  century  after  his  death. A  street  and  a  school  (Briscoe  Hall)  in  Beverly  bore  his  name in  the  middle  of  the  nineteenth  century.  His  second  wife  was Elizabeth  (Leavitt)  Du
2 CONC dley  of  Exeter,  to  which  town  Capt. Briscoe  moved  his  residence.  He  died  in  1729,  and  remembered by  will  Zachariah,  Samuel  and  Robert  Stone,  Abigail  Stevens  and Elizabeth  Ober,  nephews  and  nieces  of  h
2 CONC is  first  wife,  and  also left  £20  to  the  poor  of  Beverly.    His  widow  m.  Rev.  John  Odlin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT vii.    Israel,  bapt.  27:  4:  1675;  d.  before  1703/4,  s.  p. 
2 CONT
2 CONT viii.  Anna,  bapt.  Dec.  21,  1679;  living,  unmarried,  in  Beverly  in  1703/4. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Bibliographic information:
2 CONT
2 CONT * ''The ancestry of Sarah Stone, wife of James Patten of Arundel (Kennebunkport) Maine''
2 CONT * by    Davis, Walter Goodwin, 1885-1966
2 CONT * Publication date    1930 
2 CONT * Publisher    Portland, Me. : The Southworth Press 
2 CONT * Contributor    Boston Public Library 
2 CONT * Pages    172 
2 CONT * https://archive.org/details/ancestryofsarahs00davi/page/4/mode/1up
2 CONT
2 CONT
