1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT William Stone was baptized in 1665 in Salem. He was the son of John Stone and Abigail Dixey. He died by 1703/4 when his brother Samuel divided the estate of their father, in which distribution the children of William shared.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Stone moved to Bristol, Rhode Island, and had three children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Stone-3781
2 CONT
2 CONT William Stone (abt. 1665 - bef. 1704) 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===William Stone===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1665 in Salem, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John Stone and Abigail (Dixey) Stone
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of John Stone, Samuel Stone, Jonathan Stone, Nehemiah Stone, Abigail (Stone) Briscoe, Israel Stone and Anna Stone
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Hannah (Walley) Leonard — married 2 Jun 1686 in Bristol, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Hannah Stone, Abigail (Stone) Leonard and William Stone
2 CONT
2 CONT Died before 1704 before about age 39 in Bristol, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Stone-3781 created 14 May 2013 | Last modified 9 Mar 2020
2 CONT
