1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Patriot of the Revolutionary War service massachusetts, rank Lieutenant, Ancestor #A071610 Service Description:  1) CAPTS MORGAN LEWIS,JAMES LITTLEFIELD 2) COL EBENEZER SAYER
2 CONT
2 CONT Tobias Lord, born 1748, Arundel.In his youth, it was his daily task for a considerable length of time to drive the ox team loaded with lumber from one point of the woods to another, where wolves were exceedinglt numerous and troub
2 CONC lesome, and as he was fr equently obliged to beat them off with a club, his courage and strength were all that  prevented himself and hiss beats from being devoured.. June 26, 1776, he was commissioned second LT. of captain Morgan
2 CONC  Lewis'Twelfth Company, Col. Ebenezer Sayer's First Regiment and also 2nd LT of Captain James Littlefield's Company.  Lt Tobias Lord settled in Kennebunk, where he became a properous merchant, an enterprising ship builder and a pr
2 CONC ominent citizen. He died suddenly in 1808
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Lieutenant Tobias Lord, present at Bongoyers surrender, Kennebunkport and Alfred.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: https://archive.org/details/historyofdescend00lord Full text " A History of the Descendants of Nathan Lord of Ancient Kittery, Me." Compiled by C. C. Lord; Arranged for Publication by George E. Lord: The Rumford Press
2 CONC , Concord, N.H. 1913
2 CONT * Reference: https://archive.org/details/ancestorsdescend00lord Full text " Ancestors and Descendants of Lieutenant Tobias Lord", by Charles Edard Lord ; Privately Printed, 1913
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-109889316/lieut-tobias-lord-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 28 2021, 18:53:32 
2 CONC UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT A 2nd Lieutenant in the York County militia during the Revolutionary War.  He was part of the militia sent to reinforce the Northern Army in August 1777.  He was at the surrender of General Borgoyne at Saratoga, NY in October 1777
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Grave stone reads: Scared To The Memory Of Mr. TOBIAS LORD Obt. Jan. 16, 1808 Aet 59. A Distinguished merchant who rose to eminence by virtuous industry, the fruit of which he liberally distributed to assist the enterprising yeoma
2 CONC nry. Kennebunk, the scene of his activity, will long mourn the loss of a patron, and society regret the departure of one of god's noblest works - an honest man.
2 CONT
2 CONT The actual name of the cemetery is First Parish Unitarian Universalist Church which is adjacent to Hope Cemetery.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/18936244/tobias-lord Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 28 2021, 21:11:43 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===DESCENDANTS OF LIEUTENANT TOBIAS LORD AND MEHITABLE SCAMMON HIS FIRST WIFE 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lieut. Tobias /5 Lord [Capt. Tobias /4 John /3, Nathan /2, 
2 CONT Nathan /1).  Born February 22, 1749, at Arundel (Kennebunkport),*  Me.; died January 16, 1808, at Kennebunk; married  1st, December 3, 1772, at Biddeford, Me., '''Mehitable  Scammon''', daughter of Samuel and Mehitable (Hinckley) 
2 CONC Scammon of Saco, Me.; baptized June 10, 1753,  at Biddeford; died 1781, probably at Kennebunk.
2 CONT * Note; The town was called '''Arundel''' from its foundation in 1717, until February 19,  1821, when its name was changed to '''Kennebunkport'''. Kennebunk was set off  from Wells, June 24, 1820. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===CHILDREN. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===1.  Samuel /6 Lord, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born February 26, 1774, at Moulton's Mills (Whicher's Mills), Sanford, Me. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptized March 6, 1775, at Biddeford. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died November 8, 185 i, at Kennebunk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married February 26, 1799, at Wells, Me., Hannah 
2 CONT Jefferds, daughter of William and Olive (Gilpatrick)  Jefferds. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born October, 1775, at Wells. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died February 14, 18 16, at Kennebunk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===2.  Nathaniel/ 6 Lord, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born June r, 1776, at Moulton's Mills, now Whicher's 
2 CONT Mills, Sanford, Me. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptized July 20, 1776, at Biddeford, Me. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died February 24, 181 5, at Kennebunkport. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married July 2, 1797, at Kennebunkport, Phoebe  Walker, daughter of Capt. Daniel and Lois (Stone)  Walker. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born February 9, 1 781, at Arundel (Kennebunkport). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died October 16, 1864, at Kennebunkport. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===3.  Tobias /6 Lord (3d), 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born April 6, 1778, probably at Kennebunk.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died September 4, 1854, at Woodbridge, N. J.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married ist, January 3, 1799, at Kennebunkport, Hannah Perkins, daughter of Capt. Ephraim Perkins of 
2 CONT Arundel (Kennebunkport).
2 CONT
2 CONT Born October 19, 1780, at Arundel. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died July 31, 1846, at Boston. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 2d, 1847-8, at New York, Mrs. Sarah (Adams)  Perkins, daughter of Charles and Hannah Adams,  and widow of Perkins, said to be a brother of  Hannah Perkins, his first wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born April 5, 1796, at Bass River, now New  Gretna, N. J. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died January 3, 1864, at Lumberton, N. J. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Mehitable /6 Lord, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1781, at Kennebunkport. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1781, at Kennebunkport. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===DESCENDANTS OF LIEUTENANT TOBIAS LORD AND HEPHZIBAH CONANT HIS SECOND WIFE 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lieut. Tobias 5 Lord {CapL Tobias /4, Johm /3, Nathan /2, 
2 CONT Nathan  /1)  Born February 22, 1749, at Arundel (Kennebunkport),  Me.; died January 16, 1808, at Kennebunk, Me.;  married 2d, November 7, 1781, at Alfred, Me., Hephzibah Conant, daughter of Nathaniel and Abigail  (Dodge) Conant, b
2 CONC orn February 3, 1760, at Beverly,  Mass.; baptized March 16, 1760; died October 23, 1818, at Alfred. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===CHILDREN. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===1.  Mehitable /6 Lord, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born September 17, 1782, at Kennebunk. 
2 CONT Died September 12, 1 812, at Kennebunk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married November 11, 1802, at Kennebunk, Francis  Watts, son of Dr. Edward and Mary (Oxnard)  Watts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1780, at Portland, Me.  Died April 6, 1845, at Boston. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===2.  Abigail/6 Lord, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born October 3, 1784, at Kennebunk. 
2 CONT Died February 11, 1848, at Kennebunk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married December 25, 1S03, at Kennebunk, Charles  White Williams, son of William and Joyce (Shell-  cock) Williams. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born July 21, 1780, at Boston. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died October 21, i860, at Kennebunk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===3.  Hephzibah  /6 Lord, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born January 25, 1788, at Kennebunk. 
2 CONT Died October 6, 1862, at Boston. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married December 25, 1810, at Alfred, Robert Water-  ston, son of Robert and Helen (Cassie) Waterston.  Born February 12, 1778, at Edinburgh, Scot-  land.  Died August 30, 1869, at Boston. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Elizabeth Lord, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1790, at Kennebunk. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died January 10, 1846, at Boston. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married October 24, 18 13, at Alfred, as his second 
2 CONT wife, Francis Watts, son of Dr. Edward and Mary  (Oxnard) Watts ; he had previously married her  sister, Mehitable (i) Lord. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 17S0, at Portland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died April 6, 1745, at Boston. 
2 CONT
