1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Peninnah Howes Linnell=
2 CONT * BIRTH 11 Apr 1596 Egerton, Ashford Borough, Kent, England
2 CONT * DEATH 16 Feb 1679 (aged 82) Barnstable, Barnstable County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Lothrop Hill Cemetery, Barnstable, Barnstable County, Massachusetts, USA 
2 CONT * Latitude: 41.7028008, Longitude: -70.3174973 
2 CONT * PLOT GPS: 41.7028008; -71.3174973  
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID  166681028  
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT She was the daughter of John Howes. Her father was the parish clerk of Eastwell. Her sister, Hannah was the wife of Rev. Thomas Lothrop. She and her brother, Samuel belonged to Rev. Lothrop's Independent Church in London, England.
2 CONC  In 1632 she was questioned by the Ecclesiastical Division of the Court of High Commission regarding her connection with Rev. Lothrop's church.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Was sentenced to jail with brother Samuel for refusing to pledge honor to England religious rule---99f Eastwell. Her sister, Hannah was the wife of Rev. Thomas Lothrop. She and her brother, Samuel belonged to Rev. Lothrop's Indepe
2 CONC ndent Church in London, England. In 1632 she was questioned by the Ecclesiastical Division of the Court of High Commission regarding her connection with Rev. Lothrop's church.  hrop (1594 - 1633)**-sibling
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT Henry Howes. Bapt. Eastwell, 28 June, 1612. Note. There has been great confusion in the American record to the effect that Robert Linnell’s first wife was a Jemimah Howes, presumably another daughter to Rev. John Howes. '''This ha
2 CONC s been compounded by an LDS record of the supposed marriage of a Jemimah Howes to Robert Linnell in 1621 in Ashford, Kent. There are no records to support this.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father Rev. John Howse was born say 1565. He died 30 August 1630 (according to his probate) and was buried in Eastwell, Kent, 2 September 1630. A wife Alice was mentioned in his will and was buried in Eastwell 17 June 1640. Ho
2 CONC wever, his oldest three children may have been by an unknown first wife.
2 CONT
