1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Children: 	 1. Hannah Shelley married David Linnell on 9 Mar 1653
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. John Shelley
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Mary Shelley married William Harlow on 25 Jan 1665. Mary also married Hugh Cole and Ephraim Morton.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Robert Shelley married Susannah Dimmock abt 1664.
2 CONT
2 CONT  	 The Name Garnett is also called Gardner in various records; This makes research very difficult for our Gardner and this Garnett line;
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 1. New England Marriages Prior To 1700; . Judith Garnett of Boston, her name is spelled various ways, including: Gannett, Gannant, Garnett;
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 2. The Great Migration Begins pg: 1662: Judith Garnett, our brother John Coggershall's maidservant, was admitted to Boston church on 7 September 1634; 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 26 September 1636, Robert Shelly and his wife from Boston married here; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Our sister Judeth Garnett now the wife of one Robert Shelley a member of the Church of Barnestable dismissed to Barnstable church 14 July 1644;
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 3. New England Historical & Geographical Record vol 9:279; Book: 974. B2ne;
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 4. Barnstable Church Records 42;
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 5. New England Historical & Geographical Record vol: 9 286;
2 CONT
2 CONT Both records relating to Boston land Records BTR 1:20, 46, refer to events in the past. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Widow Shelley had earlier owned a house, which she had already given up by 1637, and her son had been granted land at Braintree by the end of 1639, at which time he was trying to defend his right. These two items probably belong t
2 CONC o Robert Shelly of Scituate and his mother, but this is not absolutely certain. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1632 passenger list entry may have been for the son Robert born about 1612, perhaps accompanied by his sister and widowed mother, and we have no mention of the father of Robert & Ann. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Pope (followed by others) proposes a third sibling in this family, Margaret, based on the admission of Margaret Sheeleone of our brothers of William Coddington's maidservants to Boston church on 19 June 1636;
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 6: Pioneers of Massachusetts: Book: 974.4 D2p; Judith, ae 26, came in the Francis of Ipswich April 30 1634; Judith, maid servant to John Coggeshall, admitted to the Church at Boston 7 July 1634; Now wife of Robert Shelly, d
2 CONC ismissed to Barnstable 14 May 1644 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Could Judith be a sister to John Gardner or Garnett as the name is sometimes spelled?)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 6: Plymouth Colony Marriages To 1650; Book: 974.482/P3 V25W: Robert Shelly and his wife from Boston married here 26 Sep, 1636. Judith Garnett came in the Francis of Ipswich on 30 April 1634, aged 26 and was in Sept. admitte
2 CONC d to Boston Church as our brother John Coggeshalls maid servant and either as maid or widow soon married Robert Shelley of Scituate and took letters of dismissal to the church there 14 July 1644.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 7: The Founders of New England: pg: 331; A note of the names and ages of all the Passrngers which tooke shipping in the Francis of Ipswich, Mr. John Cutting, bound for New England the last of Aprill, 1634: Judeth Garnett ag
2 CONC e 26 is listed;
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Garnett-46
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith Garnett came to Massachusetts on the ship Francis in 1634, at age 26.[1] She was admitted to the Boston church 7th Sept. 1634[2] "as our brother Coggeshall's maid servant.[1] Robert Shelley's sister Anne Shelley was also a 
2 CONC servant of John Coggeshall.[2]
2 CONT Mr. Hatherly married Judith Garnett to Robert Shelley in Scituate, Massachusetts, on 26 Sept. 1636, according to Scituate and Barnstable church records.[3] [2] Robert and Judith had three children: Hannah, Mary and John.[1] Judith
2 CONC  died (possibly about 1658) before 1663, when Robert married for his second wife Susanna Dimock.[1]
2 CONT Robert and Judith (Garnett) Shelley and their family were among the founders of Barnstable, on Cape Cod, in 1639.[4] [5]
2 CONT Judith (Garnett) Shelley had a lifelong feud with Rev. John Lathrop, who excommunicated her 4 June 1649.[6]
2 CONT Please read the entertaining blog about Judith Garnett by her descendant fenway49 In the Daily Kos, at the address below.
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith (Garnett) Shelley (abt. 1608 - abt. 1658)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Judith Shelley formerly Garnett aka Gardner===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1608 in England [uncertain]
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of [father unknown] and [mother unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT [sibling(s) unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Robert Shelley — married 26 Sep 1636 in Scituate, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Hannah (Shelley) Linnell, Mary (Shelley) Cole and John Shelley
2 CONT
2 CONT Died about 1658 at about age 50 in Barnstable, Barnstable County, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 12 Sep 2023 | Created 6 Jun 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith (Garnett) Shelley migrated to New England during the Puritan Great Migration (1621-1640). (See The Great Migration (Series 2), by R. C. Anderson, vol. 3, p. 26)
2 CONT
