2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Shelley immigrated to New England as a child during the Puritan Great Migration (1621-1640).
2 CONT Robert Shelley was born about 1612. He arrived in Boston in 1632 on the ship Lyon, and settled in Boston or Roxbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married first Judith Garnett, at Scituate 26 September, 1636.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She had been admitted to the Boston church on 7 September, 1634.
2 CONT Judith Garnet is thought to have come to America on the "Francis."[2]
2 CONT In 1644 Robert Shelley is described as a member of the church at Barnstable. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1668 Robert Shelley married second, Susanna (possibly Susanna Dimock, daughter of Thomas Dimock). [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Shelley signed his will 11 March 1688/89[4] in the presence of witnesses. He died 6 September 1692.[4] Inventory of his estate was taken 3 October 1692, and entered at Barnstable Court 22 October 1692.[4][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert was literate, and signed his name on his will. His inventory included books worth 10 shillings. It also included two beehives and a cow, his house, land, and other property. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah, bpt Scituate 2 Jul 1637;[6] she died between 2 Feb 1708/9 and 5 Apr 1709; she married in Barnstable 15 March 1652/3 David Linnell.
2 CONT Mary, bpt Barnstable, 2 Nov 1639;[7] she d. aft 30 Jan 1693/4; she married first at Plymouth 25 Jan 165[6], William Harlow; she married second at Plymouth 19 Oct 1692 Ephraim Morton
2 CONT John Shelley, bpt Barnstable 31 July 1642; d bef 29 Oct 1669. No issue.
2 CONT (possibly) Susanna, b abt 1662-64; d. Halifax, Mass., 6 feb 1735; m1 John Gardner; m2 Joshua Ransom
2 CONT Joseph, b Barnstable 21 Jan 1668[8]
2 CONT Shobel (aka Shubael), b Barnstable 25 Apr 1674;[8] m in Guilford, Connecticut 15 Feb 1703/4 Mary (____) Euarts/Evarts
2 CONT Benjamin, b Barnstable 12 Mar 1679/80;[8] d prob Raymham, Mass.; m. Barnstable 8 Aug 1705 Alice Goodspeed.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigration
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigration: on the ship Francis, 1634, Boston, Suffolk Co., Massachusetts
2 CONT List September, 1632 The Lyon, from London , England, arrived at Boston, Massachusetts
2 CONT Source: ...The Planters of the Commonwealth... , pages 99-102
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence: 1636, Scituate, Plymouth Co., Massachusetts
2 CONT "Robert Shelley and his wife Judith Garnett from Boston were married by Mr. Hatherly in Scituate, 26 Sep 1636. He built the 39th house between 1636 and 1637 and removed to Barnstable in 1639." [9]
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Scituate, , Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Susan P. Canney, author [title? when published?]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Robert Shelly came to New England on the ship Lion which sailed 21 June 1632 and landed in Boston on 12 September 1632. Judith Garnet came in the ship Frances which sailed from Ipswich, England, the last of April 1634. Her age is
2 CONC  given on the ship's list as twenty-six. In September 1634 she was admitted to the first church at Boston as "our brother John Coggeshall's maidservant." Robert and Judith were living in Scituate, Plymouth Colony, MA, soon after R
2 CONC ev. John Lothrop arrived. Lothrop kept careful church records, of which the following relate to the Shelleys: "The Houses in the plantation of Situate...since my coming...No. 39 was Robert Shellyes, 1636." "Goodman Shelley joyned 
2 CONC 14 May 1637." "Isaac Robinson & Margaret Handford contracted at Mr. Hatherlyes 27 June 1636, and by him Robert Shelly and his wife from Boston marryed here 26 September 1636." Robert had a farm in Scituate in 1636, on the Third Cl
2 CONC iff near Gillson's windmill. Plymouth Colony records show: Nov. 5, 1638m "Robert Shelly & John Winter desire to be admitted freeman at the next Genral Court." 1 Feb. 1639/40, Robert Shelly of Scituate took oath of allegiance and f
2 CONC idelity." In October 1639, he, with Mr. Lothrop and other members of the church, moved to Barnstable, where he was living in 1670. Another record shows that he was listed among those able to bear arms, in 1643. On 5 Jan. 1643/4, T
2 CONC homas Hinckley, Thomas Lothrop, Henry Cobb and Isaac Robinson drew up a list of those who were then inhabitants of Barnstable, and among the forty-five householders was "Robert Shelley, from Scituate 1639." Mr. Lothrop's Barnstabl
2 CONC e church records state: "Judith Shelly joyned by dismission from the church att Boston, 25 August 1644."
2 CONT
