1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Linnell-75
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Linnell
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 12 Oct 1703 in Eastham, Barnstable, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Jonathan Linnell and Elizabeth (Unknown) Linnell
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Jonathan Linnell
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Thankful (Hopkins) Paine — married 6 Oct 1726 in Harwich Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Elkanah Linnell, Jonathan Linnell and Thankful (Linnell) Freeman
2 CONT
2 CONT Died before 3 Oct 1737 in Eastham, Barnstable, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 18 Aug 2019 | Created 3 Oct 2012
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Linnell was born 12 October 1703 in Eastham, the son of Jonathan and Elizabeth (____) Linnell. He married Thankful Hopkins of Harwich on 6 October 1726, daughter of Stephen and Sarah (Howes) Hopkins.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas died Eastham between 01 July and 03 October 1737, the dates that he wrote his will and it was proved. His will names wife Thankful as executrix, and four "small children," Elkanah, Jonathan, Josiah and Thankful, as well as 
2 CONC borther Jonathan Linnell. On 3 October 1737, widow Thankful and brother Jonathan Linnell divided lands in Eastham and in Harwich inherited by them from their father, Jonathan Linel.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thankful married John Paine at Eastham on 08 Dec 1743.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, first two recorded Eastham; all from father's will:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elkanah, b. 24 Jun 1727; m. Mary Sparrow Jonathan, b. 23 Apr 1729; m. Priscilla Gould Josiah Thankful, m. Jonathan Freeman No more info is currently available for Thomas Linnell. Can you add to his biography?
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 John D. Austin, Mayflower Families Through 5 Generations, Stephen Hopkins, Vol. 6 (Plymouth, MA: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 2001 [3rd edition]), p. 337.
