2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer Phinney was born in Barnstable, Plymouth Colony on 18 February 1673, the son of John and Mary (Rogers) Finney/Phinney.[1][2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Susanna Linnell at Barnstable on 14 November 1695.[4][3] She was born ca. 1673, the daughter of David and Hannah (Shelley/Shelbey) Linnell.[3] Her father's 1688 will names her as Susanna Linnell.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was admitted as a townsman in Barnstable on 28 October 1696.[6] He was named in a division of meadow and marshland on 12 Jan 1696/7 in Barnstable, he received one share.[7] In a division of marshland in Barnstable on 6 May 1697
2 CONC , he was again named.[8] Eben Phinny received 15 1/4 shares in a division of the common lands in Barnstable on 19 February 1702.[9]
2 CONT
2 CONT Susanna died in Barnstable on 10 April 1752.[10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer wrote his will, dated 26 November 1754 and proved 10 January 1755, which named sons Samuel, Ebenezer and David Phinney, daughters Mehitable Higgins, Mary Davis, and Rebecca Davis, granddaughter Lydia Phiney. Sons Samuel a
2 CONC nd Ebenezer to be executors.[11] Ebenezer died in Barnstable on 28 November 1754, age 81 years.[12]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children born or baptized Barnstable:[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mehitable, b. 14 Aug 1696; m. Samuel Higgins 1718 Barnstable
2 CONT Mary, b. 23 Mar 1698; m. Job Davis 1724 Barnstable
2 CONT Martha, b. 22 Apr 1700; prob. d. young.
2 CONT Samuel, b. 1 Apr 1702; m. Hannah Ray 1729 Barnstable/Edgartown
2 CONT Rebecca, bp. 11 Jun 1703; m. Stephen Davis 1700 Barnstable
2 CONT poss. Lydia, bp. 17 Jul 1706; n.f.r.
2 CONT Ebenezer, b. 26 May 1708; m. Rebecca Barnes 1730 Plymouth
2 CONT David, b. 10 Jun 1710; m. Mary Pope 1733 Sandwich
2 CONT poss. Seth, b. 12 Sep 1714; n.f.r
2 CONT
