2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer Phinney was born on 26 May 1708 in Barnstable, the son of Ebenezer and Susanna (Linnell) Phinney. On 22 September 1730 in Plymouth, he married Rebecca Barnes. She was born Plymouth 14 March 1711, the daughter of Jonathan 
2 CONC and Sarah (Bradford) Barnes. She was a descendant of Pilgrim William Bradford of the Mayflower.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He and Rebecca were living on 21 January 1772 when they sold land to Jeremiah Howe of Plymouth. At the time of the deed he was of Barnstable and a seafaring man. The land they sold fell to them from their father Jonathan Barnes la
2 CONC te of Plymouth. There are no Barnstable County probate records for Ebenezer or Rebecca. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children born Barnstable:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah, b. 11 May 1732
2 CONT Jonathan, b. 14 Sep 1733
2 CONT Martha, b. 16 Jul 1735
2 CONT Lemuel, b. 24 Apr 1737
2 CONT Seth, b. 9 Jun 1743; d. 1744/5
2 CONT Rebecca, b. 16 Mar 1747
2 CONT
