1 NOTE Sister of Simon Willard, of Horsemonden, Kent county, who was one of the founders of Concord. Came to America in 1635.
2 CONT
2 CONT Major Paul Davis was a descendant in the fifth generation
2 CONT from Dolor Davis, who came from Kent, England, to this country
2 CONT in l634. He settled in Cambridge; afterwards removed.to
2 CONT Concord, and died at Barnstable, in June, i673. His first wife
2 CONT was Margery Willard, by whom he had three children, Ruth,
2 CONT Simon and Samuel. Samuel married Mary Meads,
2 CONT January nth, 1665, and they had six children, Mary, Samuel,
2 CONT David, Eleazcr, Stephen and Simon. Simon was born August
2 CONT 9th, 1683, and died in 1763. He married Dorothy Hale. [History of Holden]
