1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Dolor Davis''', of Cambridge, Duxbury & Barnstable, was born say 1593, traditionally said to be of Benefield, Northamptonshire, England, and died in   June of 1673 in Barnstable, Massachusetts Bay Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dolor Davis's name is pronounced dollar. Throughout his life, the variations of his name are spelt Dolor, Dolar, Dolard, Dolord, Dolore, Dollard, Dolerd, Dollerd, Dollar and Dollar.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first record we have of Dolor Davis, in New England, is on the Proprietor's Records in Cambridge of a grant of twenty-five acres (6) on Aug. 4, 1634; also a half rood house-lot (6), June 4, 1635. The wife Margery is supposed t
2 CONC o be the 'Margerett Davies, age 32, who with three children, John Davies (9 years old), Marie Davies (4), Elizabeth Davies (1), sailed on the Elizabeth, from the port of London, April 17, 1635, Wm. Stagg, master.'
2 CONT
2 CONT "By trade he was a house-builder, added to which was farming."
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family===
2 CONT
2 CONT His parents are not known as of January 2016. We have no actual proof of who Dolor's father is such as birth certificate or church records that definitively say who Dolor's father is. With out this definitive proof of any kind of 
2 CONC record available there was another member of the Geni staff that came in and disconnected the profile from Ichabod. I had originally had Dolor's profile connected to Ichabod's where I got this information from was the internet. Th
2 CONC e internet is just all kinds of people posting all kinds of stuff substantiated or not. In this case it was the not part. Ichabod's father is Reeze Davis who it is said to reside at Tickenham in this county of Somerset where there
2 CONC  are ruins of Reese Davis, date 1500 where there is a banquet hall is carved a coat of Arms which formed a seal on Ichabod Davis. So according to this information Dolor is suppose to have a coat of Arms. In my research I was unabl
2 CONC e to find any kind of coat of arms for Dolor. Reeze's information is in Somerset which is on the southern west coast of England. Ichabod and Dolor were born in Benefield , Northhampton which is located more like mid east part of t
2 CONC he England Island. Dolor's DNA is Scandinavian where his ancestors came from Scandinavian Viking raids on the east coast in the 800's. Over on the other side off the England Island in Somerset County which is an  Anglo-Saxon area 
2 CONC where Reeze is from. What my problem is here is that Dolor's Ancestry is Scandinavian not Anglo-Saxon so this discredits that line of the family. So that means we are back to not knowing who Dolor's Scandinavian father is. I am su
2 CONC re if Dolor Davis had a coat of Arms they would have held onto that information with dear life and had that information as an integral part of there life. From my research I can not find any kind of coat of arms for Dolor Davis. T
2 CONC his is the website that I got for Dolor Davis DNA information that I am basing his Scandinavian heritage for Dolor:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familytreedna.com/public/Davis/default.aspx?section=yresults
2 CONT
2 CONT Dolar Davis was twice married, first to 'Margerye Wilerd' on March 29, 1624. Margery Willard was born sometime around 1602.  She was the daughter of Richard Willard, who died 1617, leaving a large estate, mostly in lands, part of 
2 CONC which came to his daughter Margery Willard, and another part to the son, Simon Willard, who was later the founder of Concord, in New England -- and a close friend of Dolar Davis.  Margery died before 1666 of Concord.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 2nd, after his return to Barnstable in 1666, Mrs. Joanna Bursley, born in England, 1620, daughter of Rev. Joseph Hull and widow of Capt. John Bursley. She was living in 1683. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The six children of Margery Willard & Dolor Davis were:
2 CONT # John, born 1626,in East Farleigh, England, inherited homestead; Died April 9th 1703 in Banestable, MA.; married Hannah Linnell
2 CONT # Mary, born 1631, England
2 CONT # Elizabeth, born 1633, England, died young
2 CONT # Samuel, born July 11th 1639, Cambridge, Massachusetts; Died October 30, 1720 in Concord, Middlesex Co. MA.; married Mary Meadows
2 CONT # Simon, born 1640, Massachusetts
2 CONT # Ruth, born 1645, Barnstable, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT ===origins===
2 CONT
2 CONT Dolor was born in Bennefield, Northampton  as Stated above  this area was Danelaw originated from the Viking expansion of the ninth century AD. Danelaw can describe the set of legal terms and definitions created in the treaties be
2 CONC tween the West-Saxon king, Alfred the Great, and the Danish warlord, Guthrum, written following Guthrum's defeat at the Battle of Edington in 878. Bennefield Northampton is pretty much in the very middle of this area. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dolar shows  up  in the Family Tree DNA  results as Haplogroup I-M253  which is a Scandinavian DNA group. Dolor's Blood line there fore has 720 years  to grow and live in this Benefield Northhampton area. At some time in Dolor's y
2 CONC oung life time he must have moved from Bennefield Northhampton to East Farleigh, Kent where he is to marry his first wife Margery Willard on March 29, 1624, Dolor was 31 when he married to Margery. Before he got married to Margery
2 CONC  though Dolor got an inheritance at the age of 21 from James CLARKE, in the will it states " I give unto Dolor Davis my servant, my house and land lying in the parish of Marden, the which is in the occupation of one Terrye".  This
2 CONC   inheritance is the seed money that sets up Dolor for the rest of his life that gives him enough status to be able to marry his wife Margery because her family is very well to do. I am a little confused though about this will thi
2 CONC nking why would James give such a nice inheritance to a servant or apprentice who is not tied to James by blood relation. Only thing I can think of is maybe he is related to the Clark Family threw a female connection strictly a gu
2 CONC ess now or maybe he was just an indispensable Carpenter Apprentice or servant highly regarded. I have seen where websites say it was William's will that gave Dolar his inheritance. This I believe is false because William was James
2 CONC  son who died 4 years before James did and as far as I can tell didn't have a will because he died suddenly and young at age 38. It could be possible Dolor's  relationship was with William and maybe the land that Dolor got belonge
2 CONC d to William and James knew that William wanted to have Dolor inherit  it, not really sure of this story though because it is not explained in the will that way, the way it is stated is that James is giving it to Dolor him self th
2 CONC rew his will not William. 
