2 CONT MARY DAVIS [81] was descended from immigrant DOLOR (DOLLARD, DOLLAR) DAVIS
2 CONT [1296] who was b. in Bennefield, Northamptonshire, England c.1593.  He m. (1)
2 CONT on 29 Mar. 1624, in East Farleigh, Kent, MARGERY WILLARD [1297] (bp. 6 Nov.
2 CONT 1602 at Horsmonden, Kent; sister of Major Simon Willard, bp. there 7 Apr.
2 CONT 1605).  DOLOR and Simon both came to Cambridge in 1634, where they received
2 CONT grants of land.  MARGERY came to New England on the Elizabeth on 17 Apr. 1635
2 CONT with her children John 9, Marie 4, and Elizabeth 1.  A carpenter and master
2 CONT builder, DOLOR owned a house lot in 1635 in Cambridge, Mass. on the easterly
2 CONT side of Dunster St. between Winthrope and South Streets.  He moved to Duxbury
2 CONT in 1640, and was of that church when he removed to Barnstable in 1643.  At
2 CONT Barnstable, he was on the list of men eligible for military service, 1643; a
2 CONT freeman, 1646; a member of the church on 27 Aug. 1648; surveyor of the highways in 1652, and constable in 1654.  He moved to Concord, Mass. in 1655,
2 CONT petitioning for the grant of the Town of Groton in 1656, and was one of the
2 CONT twenty from the Plymouth Colony who had lands granted them there in 1658, the
2 CONT year MARGERY died.  He returned to Barnstable in 1666, m. (2) Mrs Joane (Hull) Bursley in 1671, and d. in 1673, " aged 80."
2 CONT
