1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Mary Davis
2 CONT '''Parents:''' Dolar Davis, Margery Davis (born Willard) 
2 CONT '''Siblings:''' John Davis, Samuel Davis, Elizabeth [1]. Elizabeth [2] Elizabeth [3] Davis, Ruth Davis, Nicholas Davis
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Davis, born 1631 in England; Married Thomas Lewis June 15, 1653 in Barnstable, Plymouth Colony; born January 05,1629/30 in Benchley, Kent, England; died May 18, 1710 in Falmouth, Barnstable Co., MA..
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 6/l5/1653 to Thomas, son of G & B Lewis. Had at least 4 children
2 CONT
2 CONT >'''MARRIAGE'''
2 CONT >"Massachusetts, Town Clerk, Vital and Town Records, 1626-2001", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:Q29G-PVY8 database with images, FamilySearch] (pub. Sun Mar 10, 2024)
2 CONT >Thomas Lewes and Mary Davis – Marriage: 15 Jun 1653 in Barnstable, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Children: Baptisms
2 CONT # '''James Lewes, March 1654.'''
2 CONT ## "Massachusetts Births and Christenings, 1639-1915", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FZD1-JDC FamilySearch] (16 Mar 2022).
2 CONT ## "Maryland, Church Records, 1668-1995", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QGJD-4Q1K (with image) FamilySearch] (pub. Fri Mar 8,2024), Entry for James Lewes and Thomas Lewes & Mary Davis.
2 CONT # '''Thomas Lewes, 15 July 1656.'''
2 CONT ## "Massachusetts Births and Christenings, 1639-1915", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FZD1-6FK database, FamilySearch] (16 March 2022).
2 CONT ## "Maryland, Church Records, 1668-1995", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSMZ-CSGG-Y?view=index&personArk=%2Fark%3A%2F61903%2F1%3A1%3AQGJD-47MK&action=vie(with image) FamilySearch] (pub. Fri Mar 8,2024), Entry f
2 CONC or '''Thomas''' Lewes and Thomas Lewes & Mary Davis.
2 CONT # '''Mary Lewes, 2 November 1659.'''
2 CONT ## *"Massachusetts Births and Christenings, 1639-1915", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FZDY-BHS database, FamilySearch] (16 March 2022).
2 CONT ## "Maryland, Church Records, 1668-1995", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QGJD-47MZ (with image) FamilySearch] (pub. Fri Mar 8, 2024), Entry for '''Mary''' Lewes and Thomas Lewes & Mary Davis.
2 CONT # '''Samuel Lewes, 2 November 1659'''
2 CONT ## "Massachusetts Births and Christenings, 1639-1915", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FZD1-PQB database, FamilySearch] (16 March 2022).
2 CONT ## "Maryland, Church Records, 1668-1995", (with imge) [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QGJD-47MK FamilySearch] (pub. Fri Mar 8, 2024), Entry for Samuel Lewes and Thomas Lewes & Mary Davis.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Wikitree: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Davis-192  Mary (Davis) Lewis (bef. 1633-1687)]
2 CONT * Sources and quoted matter in this profile align with records about her in Plymouth Colony. For these things, this Wikitree profile has much useful information. 
2 CONT * ''A sticking point'' might be making sense of Mary's birth place and date as appearing on Wikitree. One should weigh the merit of it for oneself:—
2 CONT ** '''Was this Mary was baptized in Catsfield, Sussex, England on before 2 Feb 1633?'''
2 CONT *** Catsfield is 21 miles south of Horsemonden, the birthplace of her mother, so it's not implausible.
2 CONT ** It's unknown where Dolor was born or where he lived before and after marriage. except ''maybe'' county Kent (the county of his wife's birth).
2 CONT ** There is no 1590s record in all of England in FamilySearch's repository for a baptism of a "Dolor" Davis or Davie.
2 CONT *** There are between 1,000 and 2,000 indexed baptism records for county Sussex on FS for "Davis" or "Davie" limited to the 1590s. The same it true for county Kent.
2 CONT *** Notably, FS has no marriage record for Dolor Davis and Margery Willard in its repository in all of England between 1620-1630.
2 CONT ** The name ''Dolor'' in only appears in England's church records (to date) linked to a baptism for Mary "Dav'''ie'''" ([https://ywww.familysearch.org/search/record/results?count=20&q.anyDate.from=1593&q.anyPlace=England&q.givenNa
2 CONC me=Dolor&q.givenName.1=Dolor&q.surname=Davis&q.surname.1=Davies FamilySearch Query Results]). But this Mary was baptized on 9 May 1631, which differs from the date Wikitree shows in the profile's 16 Jan 2024 update.
2 CONT *** It's rare to see a male's name be "Dolor" (''i.e''., melancholy). This easily leads AI hints to connect "Dolor Davie" to a baptism record for a "Mary Davie" in Catsfield, Sussex. 
2 CONT ** As of 7 May 2024, there is no original parish record available for this baptism. There's a transcribed document of the Sussex baptism provided by a typist who used an early-model typewriter. (See [https://www.ancestry.com/disco
2 CONC veryui-content/view/3035016:62049?tid=174604283&pid=132579594038&hid=1037332781762 Ancestry.com].) Therefore, one can't decipher if the transcription-reading is accurately Dav'''ie''' of it's possibly Dav'''is'''.
2 CONT ** Geographically, Catsfield Sussex is nearer the ocean than Horsemonden. Now, if one accepts what Packrat-pro shows as representing the family's ship to Colonial America, the "Elizabeth" sailed out to sea on the Thames from Londo
2 CONC n. London is 67 miles north of Catsfield. 
2 CONT **Passenger of the "Elizabeth", Master William Stagg, voyage of  April 1635 Elizabeth was four years old during this Voyage accompanied by Mother and 2 siblings.  This information comes from the Winthrop Society: http://www.winthr
2 CONC opsociety.com/ships/elizabeth2.htm Passengers of the Elizabeth Master: William Stagg Voyage of 1635. 
2 CONT **''See also'' [https://www.packrat-pro.com/ships/elizabeth2.htm Packrat-pro]'s list of persons aboard this ship. The abbreviation of her father's name there is spelled "Jo.", which may be a misreading and transcription for "Do." 
2 CONC from the original list.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Dolor Davis A Sketch of his life with a Record of his Earlier Descendants By Horace Davis Printed in 1881 Page 37 the Paragraph Starting as " Mary Davis, Daughter of Dolor and Margery, Born in England about 1631;married in Barnsta
2 CONC ble June 15, 1653, Thomas, son of George Lewis of B. (I assume this means Boston) He was born in England resided in Barnstable  till 1668; freeman June 1, 1658; Surveyor of Highways, 1668; moved to Falmouth, proprietors' clerk the
2 CONC re and a prominent citizen. Mary Lewis was living in 1672. Savage identifies this man with Thomas Lewis of Swansey; Amos Otis says Lewis of Swansey was a Different person, and he is undoubtedly right. See "Barnstable Patriot,"  Ja
2 CONC nuary 2, 1866."
