1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Obituary for LT Simon Davis:
2 CONT
2 CONT >Simon Davis, the eldest son of Dolor Davis and Margery Willard was born in "New Towne" Plymouth Colony (present day Cambridge, Middesex County, Massachusetts) in 1636.
2 CONT >
2 CONT >Mary Blood, the daughter of James and Eleanor (Harrison) Blood was born in Concord, Massachusetts on July 12, 1640. They were married on December 12, 1660 in Concord, and settled there on a farm given to him by his father, situat
2 CONC ed near his father's homestead.
2 CONT >
2 CONT >In 1675 he was appointed command of the troops defending the garrison at Brookfield, Massachusetts; Captain Wheeler having been wounded. Battle of Brookfield was a part of the King Phillips War 1675-1677. He received his commissi
2 CONC on as lieutenant, July 2, 1689. He was admitted a freeman, March 21, 1699.
2 CONT >
2 CONT >In the publication "A History of the Town of Concord, Middesex County, Massachusetts" he appears as Constable Simon Davis on March 31,1680. In 1689, 1690, 1692 and 1705 his name also appears under the heading of Deputies and Repr
2 CONC esentatives from the first Settlement of the Town.
2 CONT >
2 CONT >Simon and Mary had seven children, all born in Concord, Massachusetts as follows:
2 CONT ># Simon Jr, born 12 OCT 1661 settled in Concord and was one of the distinguished physicians of his day. Dr. Davis married Elizabeth Woodhouse on 14 FEB 1680. They had eight children.
2 CONT ># Mary, born 3 OCT 1663. Married Deliverance Wheeler of Stow on 28 MAY 1691 where they settled.
2 CONT ># Sarah, born 11 MAR 1665. Married Thomas Wheeler of Concord on 13 NOV 1695.
2 CONT ># James, born 19 JUN 1668. Married Ann Smedley in 1701. James and Ann had eight children. James died 16 September 1727. Ann JUN 1760.
2 CONT ># Elener, born 22 OCT 1672. Married Samuel Hunt in Concord on 14 MAY 1669. They had at least one child.
2 CONT ># Ebenesar (Ebenezer), born 1 JUN 1676. Married Dinnah Browne on 14 FEB 1700 in Chelmsford, MA. They had seven children. Ebenezer died 31 MAR 1753 in Harvard, MA.
2 CONT ># Hannah, born 1 APR 1679. Married Samuel Blood 1 APR 1701 in Concord, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT >sources: A History of the Town of Concord, MA, Massachusetts; Town Birth Records 1620-1850; North American Family Histories 1500-2000; U.S. and International Marriage Records 1560-1900; Concord, Massachusetts Births, Marriages an
2 CONC d Deaths 1635-1850; Dolor Davis A Sketch of His Life; Historic Homes and Institutions and Genealogical and Personal Memoirs of Worcester County, MA; Soldiers of King Phillips War; History of Holden, MA 1684-1894; Vital Records of 
2 CONC Concord, MA 1635-1849. New England Families Vol III by William Richard Cutter
2 CONT
