2 CONT Simon (Lt.) Davis
2 CONT Birth: 1636 - Concord, Middlesex, MA or Cambridge  Death: June 14 1713 - Concord, Middlesex, MA  Parents: Dolor Kent DAVIS, Margery DAVIS (born Willard)  Siblings: John Davis, Nicolas Davis, Elizabeth Owen (born Davies), Elizabeth
2 CONC  Grice (born DAVIS), Samuel Davis, Samuel Davis, Ruth Hall (born Davis), Mary Lewis (born davis)  Wife: Mary Davis (born Blood)  Simon (Lt.) Davis,born Bet.1636-1640 in Cambridge MA; died June14,1713 in Concord, Middlesex Co., MA;
2 CONC  Mary Blood; born July 12, 1648 in Concord, Middlesex Co., MA; died October 30, 1710. Notes for Simon Lt. Davis: Married 12/12/1660 to Mary Blood the daughter of James Blood, Concord Mass. Saved by Major Willard at Nfld., Mass. ra
2 CONC id. Had at least 7 Children. [information on Simon came from Probate Records ancestry.com ] Lt Davis settled in Concord, was Deputy 1689, 1690, 1705, and was in command of the troops after the wounding of Capt. Wheeler at Brookfie
2 CONC ld1675. Wife Mary and 7 children mentioned in will as still living, also grandson Samuel Hunt. Like his father and brother Samuel, he had divided most of his real estate among his sons before his death. {another source lists child
2 CONC ren as Hannah1659-1687 in Concord, MA. Hannah b. 1661 in Cambridge, Middlesex, MA, Simon [doctor] b. 12 Oct 1661 in Concord, Mary b 3 Oct 1663 in Concord Sarah b. 1l Mar 1664/65 in Concord, James b.19 Jan, 1667/68 in Concord, Elen
2 CONC er b. 2 Oct 1672 in Concord, Ebenezer b. I Jun 1667 in Concord, Hannah b. 1 Apr. 1679 in Concord, Hannah b. 1 Apr. 1687 in Concord) was Lieut. of militia; in command of Concord men at the Brookfield fight with Indians. ___________
2 CONC __________________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Concord marriages: Simon Davis, and Mary Blood were married 12 December 1660 Concord deaths: Lt Simon Davis ye Husband of Mary his wife Dyed June ye 14 day 1713 [in his 77th yr. G.S.]. _____________________________________________
2 CONC ________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon was the son of Dolor Davis and Margery Willard. Simon was a lieutenant, representative, and other wise distinguished, m. Mary, daughter of James Blood, 1660, d. June 14, 1713, a. 77; and had Simon, Mary, Sarah, James, Ellen,
2 CONC  Ebenezer, and Hannah. (History of Concord)  Parents: Dolar Davis was in Cambridge 1634, went to Concord about 1659, d. 1673. He m. Margery b. about 1602, sister of Maj. Simon Willard. (Littleton Records) _________________________
2 CONC _____________________________________________________________ Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   Dolor Davis (1593 - Between 1665-1667)
2 CONT   Margery Willard Davis
2 CONT   Children:
2 CONT   Mary Davis Wheeler (1663 - 1748)*
2 CONT   Siblings:
2 CONT   Simon Davis (1636 - 1713)
2 CONT   Samuel Davis (1639 - 1720)*
2 CONT   Ruth Davis Hall (1644 - 1715)*
2 CONT  Inscription on head stone: MEMENTO MORI FUGIT HORA HERE LYES THE BODY OF  SIMON DAVIS WHO DEPARTED THIS LIFE JUNE ye 14 DAY 1713 IN THE 77 YEAR OF HIS AGE Burial: South Burying Place, Concord, Middlesex County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONC  . Find A Grave Memorial# 24305220 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dolor Davis A Sketch of his life with a Record of his Descendants by Horace Davis Printed 1881 page 38 First Paragraph head of page " Simon Davis (Lieut.), son of Dolor and Margery, born in America about 1636; married December 12,
2 CONC  1660, Mary, daughter of James Blood of Concord, born July 12, 1640. Lieut. Davis settled in Concord; was Deputy 1689, 1690, 1692, and 1705, and held other responsible positions; was in command of the troops after the wounding of 
2 CONC Capt. Wheeler at Brookfield, 1675; freeman Mass. Col. March 21, 1689 or 90; died June 14, 1713 at the age of 77; grave-stone now standing in Concord; original will on file at East Cambridge, made June 24, 1710, proved July 3, 1713
2 CONC , and bearing his autograph; a better autograph maybe seen on the Concord records 1689 or 90 attesting election of town clerk. Wife Mary and 7 children mentioned in will as still living, also grandson Samuel Hunt. Like his father 
2 CONC and brother Samuel he had divided most of his real estate among his sons before his death."
2 CONT
2 CONT  I found this at this web site: http://miller-aanderson.blogspot.com/2011/07/dolor-davis-1593-1673.html copy paste below:
2 CONT
2 CONT Simon Davis, b. at Concord, Aug. 9, 1683; m. at Stow, Mass., 1719, Dorothy Heald, daughter of Israel Heald by wife Martha. He lived in Stow, and was a blacksmith; d. Sept. 7, 1738, aged 78. His will is on record at East Cambridge,
2 CONC  and mentions daughter Dorothy Davis and grandson Joseph Davis. Wid. Martha d. June 14, 1746. "Lieut." Simon Davis lived at Concord until about 1721, when he moved to Worcester County, and settled in Rutland; selectman 1721; innke
2 CONC eper 1723; waylaid and nearly killed by the Indians in the same year. Petitions with others to the General Court on May 13, 1740, to be set off in a separate township to be named Holden. This request was granted, and Mr. Davis was
2 CONC  made moderator of the first town meeting in Holden, May 4, 1745; chairman of board of selectmen for several years; also juryman. He was closely identified with the church. He d. Feb. 21, 1763; wid. Dorothy d. July 21, 1776. Eight
2 CONC  children. He was the ancestor of three Massachusetts governors: "Honest" John Davis, John Davis Long, and George D. Robinson. The ancestry of Hon. Horace Davis separates here from my own. 
2 CONT --------------------
