3 TEXT Dolor Davis A Sketch of his life with a Record of his Descendants by Horace Davis Printed 1881 page 38 First Paragraph head of page " Simon Davis (Lieut.), son of Dolor and Margery, born in America about 1636; married December 12,
4 CONC  1660, Mary, daughter of James Blood of Concord, born July 12, 1640. Lieut. Davis settled in Concord; was Deputy 1689, 1690, 1692, and 1705, and held other responsible positions; was in command of the troops after the wounding of 
4 CONC Capt. Wheeler at Brookfield, 1675; freeman Mass. Col. March 21, 1689 or 90; died June 14, 1713 at the age of 77; grave-stone now standing in Concord; original will on file at East Cambridge, made June 24, 1710, proved July 3, 1713
4 CONC , and bearing his autograph; a better autograph maybe seen on the Concord records 1689 or 90 attesting election of town clerk. Wife Mary and 7 children mentioned in will as still living, also grandson Samuel Hunt. Like his father 
4 CONC and brother Samuel he had divided most of his real estate among his sons before his death
