1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Samuel Davis,''' born July 11,1639 in Cambridge Ma; died October 30, 1720 in Concord, Middlesex Co., MA. He was the son of Dolar Kent Davis and Marjory Willard. He married Mary Meadows at Lynn, Mass., Jan. 11, 1
2 CONC 665. Settled in that part of Concord which afterwards was set off as Bedford. Mary Meadows, born Abt. 1639 in Lynn, Essex Co. MA; died October l7, 1710 in Concord Middlesex Co., MA. She was the daughter of Philip Meadows and Eliza
2 CONC beth lggleden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Davis was made freeman March 91, 1689-90. He was with Major Simon Willard at the Brookfield fight on Sept. 28, 167'5. (King Philip's War, p. 121.)
2 CONT
2 CONT His farm was on the back road from Concord to Bedford, about three miles from Concord town, on the edge of the river meadow.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Family==
2 CONT  * Parents: Dolor Davis (1599 - ____) & Margery Willard Davis
2 CONT
2 CONT Married 
2 CONT #  Mary Meadows Davis (1639 - 1710)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT * [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=69585788 Find A Grave Memorial# 69585788]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Samuel Davis:
2 CONT
2 CONT First married to Mary Meades [Meddowes] who died l0/17/l710 then married Ruth Taylor who dies in 1720. Had at least 7 children. Samuel Davis was a Freeman, March 21, 1689 to 1690.He was with Major Simon Willard at the Brookfield f
2 CONC ight on Sept. 28, 167'5. (King Philip's War, p. 121.)  He settled in that part of Concord which became Bedford, and his homestead is still owned by his descendants today. It is located on the back road from Concord to Bedford, abo
2 CONC ut 3 miles from Concord, on the edge of the river meadow. A well is there which he is said to have dug. He was still living March15,1714 and had already settled upon his sons most of his land during his life time. According to Sav
2 CONC age Report, Eleazer, Stephen and Simon were triplets b. 5/26/1680 in Concord. On June 20,1690, Samuel petitioned Concord authorities for 'a bridal path from his house to Billerica road'' In 1706 he conveys houses and lands to his 
2 CONC 'two well beloved sons.' On May 8,1713 he sells house, barn and 9 acres to Eleazer Davis for L50. It appears that he gave his property to his family while living'"
2 CONT ======
2 CONT
2 CONT Dolor Davis A Sketch of his Life With A Record of his Earlier Descendants by Horace Davis printed in 1881 page 40  the paragraph is a direct quote  it states: " Samuel Davis, son of Dolor and Margery, birth East Farleigh, Kent; ma
2 CONC rried at Lynn, January 11, 1665 or 66, Mary Meddowes. She died at Concord, October 3, 1710. Samuel married second wife October 18, 1711, Ruth Taylor. Ruth died August 6, 1720. Samuel was a freeman March 21, 1689 or 90. He settled 
2 CONC in that part of Concord which afterward became Bedford, and his homestead is owned by his descendants to-day. He is my lineal ancestor , (Mine too) and I visited his farm on the back road ( now this description is back in 1881 or 
2 CONC so)  from Concord to Bedford, about three miles from Concord,  on the edge of the river meadow. A well is there which  Samuel  is said to have dug. Mr. Benjamin J. Davis, the owner of the property, kindly loaned me some ancient de
2 CONC eds, dating from 1694 to1712, and containing signatures of Samuel Davis and some of his family. From these I learned that he was still living March 15, 1714, and had  already  settled upon his sons most of his land during  his own
2 CONC  lifetime. Samuel's name sometimes appears on the Concord records, but he took little part in public affairs. In his deeds he styles himself husbandman and yeoman. The date of his death and place of burial are unknown."
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Married at Lynn, Essex, Mass.
2 CONT --------------------
