1 NOTE From The Rufus Parks Pedigree.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 87:
2 CONT 1,296.6   Samuel  [=648] b. c.1639 Cambridge, m. Mary Medos 11 June 1665 in Concord.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 91:
2 CONT Dolor and Margery's son Samuel Davis [648] was b. c.1639 in Cambridge, Mass. to Dolor Davis and Margery Willard. He accompanied his father to Concord, Mass., where he m. (1) Mary Medos (Meadows) [649] on 11 Jan. 1665/6.  Mary's fa
2 CONC ther was possibly the Phillip Meadows of Roxbury whose dau. Hanna was bp. 1 Feb. 1642 and m. Alasdair MacDougal on 1 Mar. 1659 in Lynn.  Mary d. at Concord on 3 Oct. 1710, and Samuel m. (2) 18 Oct. 1711, Ruth Taylor.
1 NOTE Lancaster, Groton
1 NOTE first married to Mary Meades [Meddowes] who died 10/17/1710 the married
1 NOTE (II) Samuel Davis, son of Dolor Davis (l), was born probably in Concord ; married, at Lynn, January n, 1665-6, Mary Mead or Meddowes, who died at Concord, October 3, 1710. He married (second), October 18, 1711, Ruth Taylor, who di
2 CONC ed August 6, 1720. Samuel was admitted a freeman March 21, 1689-90. He settled in Concord, Massuchusetts, in that part which became Bedford, and his homestead is now or was lately still owned by his descendants. It was on the road
2 CONC  from Concord to Bedford, on the edge of the river meadow, and the old well which is still in use is believed to have been dug by Samuel. He was a farmer. He was living in 1714; the date of his death is not recorded. The children 
2 CONC of Samuel and Mary were : Mary, born October 27, 1666, died December 18, 1667 ; Samuel, June 21, 1669, married at Concord, March Law, resided at Bedford ; Daniel, March 16 or 26, 1673, resided at Bedford; Mary, August 12, 1677; 2,
2 CONC  1697-8, Abigail Read, married (second) Mary Eleazer, July 26, 1680, resided at Bedford; Simon, lieutenant, mentioned below; Stephen, March 30, 1686, resided at Bedford. [Historic Homes and Institutions and Genealogical and Person
2 CONC al Memoirs of Worcester County ...  By Ellery Bicknell Crane]
