1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Nicholas Davis=
2 CONT ===~• early Massachusetts Colony Quaker===
2 CONT
2 CONT * Parents: perhaps the brother of Dolar Davis who married  Margery Davis (born Willard)  Who had: John Davis, Ruth Hall (born Davis), Mary Lewis (born Davis), Samuel Davis, Simon Davis 
2 CONT ======
2 CONT * Seen as Born: 1627 in Horsemonden, Kent Co. England without supporting evidence.
2 CONT *  died 24 Jul 1672 in New Port, RI;
2 CONT * married Sarah; born May10,1629 in Stood, Kent, England.
2 CONT ======
2 CONT Genealogical Guide to the Early Settlers of America [https://books.google.com/books?id=cSrlHHj2AFcC&pg=PA136&lpg=PA136&dq=genealogical+guide+to+the+early+settlers+of+america+Nicholas+Davis&source=bl&ots=rHhgAuOjpn&sig=ba9b4Dem6wuw
2 CONC e3PfKsquT6NKbB8&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0CCsQ6AEwBWoVChMI_I2QseupyAIVB5UNCh07BAmq#v=onepage&q&f=true page 136]
2 CONT ======
2 CONT Nicholas Davis, of Barnstable, able to bear arms 1643, when he is last on the list, so that possibly it may be and error, as Hamblen put him into a list of inhabitants admitted after 1660. He may have been of Newport,1638, and the
2 CONC re learned the strange policy of toleration in religion. In Sewel, I, 388, it is said he favored the Quakers at their first meeting. He had wife Mary, and was banished from Mass. for his peaceful pravity.  At Newport he was drowne
2 CONC d before August 9, 1672, as Roger Williams in his  public conference, there, with the friends of George Fox, he made good use of the event. --------------------
2 CONT * http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Clarke_(Baptist_minister)_
2 CONT **[https://books.google.com/books?id=LA7ntaS11ocC&lpg=PA254&ots=ZtbrpzotPf&dq=Hannah%20(Davis)%20Brenton&pg=PA63#v=onepage&q&f=true Page 254] of The Genealogical Dictionary of Rhode Island: Comprising Three Generations of ... By J
2 CONC ohn Osborne Austin<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===also===
2 CONT Davis.. had been an early settler of Aquidneck Island in 1639, but became a merchant and moved to Hyannis in the Plymouth Colony. Davis had many business dealings in Massachusetts, but when he became a Quaker, he was imprisoned an
2 CONC d banished from there in 1659, and later lived in Newport. He transported Quaker founder George Fox from Long Island to Newport in 1672, during Fox's visit to the American colonies. Soon thereafter Davis drowned, and within a year
2 CONC  and a half his widow married Clarke.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Updated info
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/discussions/237966?msg=1505648
2 CONT
2 CONT Quaker Nicholas Davis, died by drowning in Newport, RI harbor on 24 Jul 1672.  
2 CONT
2 CONT If he was not the son of Dolor Davis, then his birthplace, birthdate, and his parentage are unknown. His first verifiable is in Barnstable in 1651.
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife was Sarah (Ewer) Blossom Davis Clarke Walley. Sarah married twice after Nicholas died to Dr. John Clarke of Newport, and then to Rev. Walley of Barnstable. She was first married to Thomas Blossom.
2 CONT
2 CONT His children were: Samuel, Hannah, Simon, Sarah, Thomas and Mercy.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===comment===
2 CONT A number of Davis men continued in the Quaker faith. It is suggested that [https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Davis-of-Middletown-Jersey-Province/6000000036421209251 '''Thomas Davis'''], born in Middletown, Monmouth, NJ in 1686 is
2 CONC  a relative.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===sources===
2 CONT *The Genealogical Dictionary of Rhode Island: Comprising Three Generations of Settlers who Came Before 1690, with Many Families Carried to the Fourth Generation by John Osborne Austin; Genealogical Publishing Com, 1969 - Reference
2 CONC  - 496 pages; see page 63
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT "First settler of Hyannis; forced to depart Massachusetts on "pain of death" because of Quakerism."
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Name:	Nicholas Davis
2 CONT Gender:	M (Male)
2 CONT Birth Date:	1627
2 CONT Birth Place:	Horsmonden, Kent, England, United Kingdom
2 CONT Death Date:	24 juin 1672 (24 Jun 1672)
2 CONT Death Place:	Drowned in the Newport Harbor, Rhode Island, USA
2 CONT Father:	
2 CONT Dolor Kent Davis
2 CONT Mother:	
2 CONT Margaret Margery Willard
2 CONT Spouse:	
2 CONT Sarah Ewer
2 CONT Child:	
2 CONT Hannah Maria Davis
2 CONT View on Geneanet:	
2 CONT [https://gw.geneanet.org/ealm7856?n=davis&oc=&p=nicholas]
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "Nicholas Davis; Davess; Davies
2 CONT 	ae. 40, Sarah, ae. 48, Joseph, ae. 13, with Wm. Lock, ae. 6, cert. from Stepney parish, came in the Planter March 22, 1634. Res. at Charlestown; rem. to Woburn, 1640. Wife Sarah d. 24 (3) 1643. He m. July 12, 1643, Elizabeth Isaa
2 CONC c. Rem. to York. Juryman Oct. 17, 1650. Took oath of allegiance to Mass. govt. 22 Nov. 1652, and was appointed constable.</P><P>Will dated 27 April, 1667, inventory rendered 12 March, 1669-70; beq. to wife Elizabeth; daughter Asti
2 CONC ne and her children, Mary and Sarah, cousins, Matthew Barnard, son of Matthew B. of Boston, and William Locke of &quot;Owborne&quot; [Woburn]; Mary, Elizabeth and Mehitable Dod: friends Capt. John Davis and Mr. Peter Weare oversee
2 CONC rs; wife executrix. Admin. of his est. in Plym. Col. given by Mass. Gen. Court to John Wales of Boston; inv. filed at Plym. 13 (5) 1673."
2 CONT [Source Information
2 CONT Ancestry.com. Maine Pioneers, 1623-60 [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 1999.
2 CONT Original data: Pope, Charles Henry. The Pioneers of Maine and New Hampshire, 1623-1660. n.p., 1908.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
