1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Noah Davis Birth: Sep 7 1707 - Barnstable, Barnstable, Massachusetts  Death: July 25 1787 - Falmouth, Barnstable, Massachusetts  Parents: John Jr Davis, Hannah Davis  Siblings: John1 Davis, Benjamin Davis, John Dav
2 CONC is, Jabez Davis, Shubael Davis, James Davis, Ebenezer Davis, Nicholas Davis, Jedediah Davis, Hannah Hatch (born Davis), Desire Davis  Wife: Mercy Davis (born Weeks) 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Davis-14991
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 18 Jun 2020 | Created 22 Mar 2013
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Noah Davis (1707 - 1787)==
2 CONT
2 CONT Noah Davis
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 7 Sep 1707 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John Davis Jr and Hannah (Lombard) Davis
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of John Davis [half], Benjamin Davis [half], John Davis [half], Jabez Davis [half], Ebenezer Davis [half] and Jedediah Davis
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mercy (Meigs) Davis — married 25 Jun 1733 in Falmouth, Barnstable, Massachusetts Bay Colonymap
2 CONT [children unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 25 Jul 1787 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Noah Davis was the son of John Davis Jr and Hannah widow of Nat. Bacon[1] According to his bio at find-a-grave "On June 25, 1733 at Falmouth, Noah m. as her 2nd husband, Mercy Meigs, dau. of Ebenezer Meigs and Mercy Weeks, and wid
2 CONC ow of John Weeks, Jr., b. Dec. 11, 1705 at Guilford, Conn. She d. at Falmouth Jan. 3, 1788, age 82. Five children of the marriage (surname Davis): Mercy, Hannah, Susanna (d.y.), Susanna, and son Francis."[2] The vital records show
2 CONC  his wife was Mercy, who he married June 5 (June 25. CR1), 1733 and support that they had the mentioned children. [3] However, there is no sourced information, just speculative, to support that his wife was Mercy Meigs. For severa
2 CONC l centuries, his wife has been speculated as the widow of John Weeks, Jr. However, there were other possible Mercy Weeks that he could have married. [4] Jabez's nephew Solomon married Mercy & John Weeks daughter Thankful.
2 CONT
2 CONT Noah Davis, h. Marcy and s. John and Hannah, July 25, 1787, a. 79 yr[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Genealogical Notes of Barnstable Families, by Amos Otis, ↑ https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/5865191/noah-davis ↑ Falmouth Vital Records ↑ Weeks, Robert D., Genealogy of the Family of George Weekes, of Dorchester, Mass., 1635-
2 CONC 1650 ↑ Falmouth Vital Records https://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Barnstable/Falmouth/aDeathsD.shtml Acknowledgments
2 CONT
