2 CONT
2 CONT HISTORY OF THE TOWN OF STONINGTON, County of New London, Connecticut, from its first settlement in 1649 to 1900, by Richard Anson Wheeler, New London, CT, 1900, p. 429
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/John-Hinckley/6000000091134977021
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hinckley-68
2 CONT
2 CONT Ensign John Hinckley was born before 26 May 1644 in Barnstable, Massachusetts to Samuel Hinckley Sr and Sarah (Soole) Hinckley. He is the brother of Thomas Hinckley, John Hinckley, Susannah (Hinckley) Smith, Marie Hinckley,  Sarah
2 CONC  (Hinckley) Cobb, Mary (Hinckley) Robbins, Elizabeth Hinckley, John Hinckley,  Elizabeth (Hinckley) Parker, Samuel Hinckley, Samuel Hinckley, Unknown Hinckley, Twin Son Hinckley, Twin Son Hinckley and	Samuel Hinckley. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John married  Bethia (Lathrop) Hinckley in July 1668 (to 10 Jul 1694) 
2 CONT
2 CONT in Barnstable, Massachusetts Bay Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Mary (Davis) Hinckley on 24 Nov 1697 in Barnstable, Province of Massachusetts Bay.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is the father of Sarah (Hinckley) Crocker, Samuel Hinckley Sr, Bethia Hinckley, Hannah (Hinckley) Lewis, Jonathan Hinckley, Ichabod Hinckley, Gershom Hinckley, Job Hinckley, Mary (Hinckley) Crocker, Mercy Hinckley and Abigail H
2 CONC inckley. John died 7 Dec 1709 in Barnstable, Barnstable, Plymouth [uncertain] Profile managers: Wiley Walters and Merry Ann Palmer  Profile last modified 18 Oct 2018 | Created 21 Sep 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT John Hinckley married (1) Bethiah Lothrop July 1688 Barnstable, Massachusetts. He married (2) Mary Goodspeed on 24 Nov 1697 in Barnstable, MA by J.T. Howes, daughter of Nathaniel Goodspeed and Elizabeth Bursley.
2 CONT
2 CONT [For Barnstable, pp28-31] "Samuel Hinkleys Children born at Barnstable his Son John Born ye 24. of May 1644" "John Hinkley & Bethiah Lothrop Married July 1668 (the births of seven children are recorded) Bethiah ye wife of ye above
2 CONC  sd John Hinkley Departed this Life July 10 day 1694 ye Above Sd Mr John Hinkley Deceas'd ye 7th of Decem'r 1709
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Pioneers of Massachusetts" Charles Henry Pope, Boston, MA, 1900 "Massachusetts Genealogical Records, 1600s-1800s" CD-ROM Genealogy.com, 2000 p231: "HINCKLEY, HINKLY, Samuel...they brought four children: Thomas, (who became go
2 CONC vernor of Plymouth Colony,) Susanna, (m. Rev. John Smith,) Sarah, (m. Henry Cobb,) and Mary; other ch. b. here were Elizabeth bapt. Sept. 6, 1635, (m. 15 July, 1657, Elisha Parker,) Samuel bapt. 24 July, 1642, John bapt. 26 May, 1
2 CONC 644."
2 CONT
2 CONT "John, bapt. at Barnstable 26 May 1644; m. (1) in July 1668, Bethia Lothrop; m. (2) 24 Nov. 1697, Mary Goodspeed; had issue." [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Hinckley Family" George W. Messinger NEHGR v13 p208 (Jul 1859) Lists 12 of the 16 children, citing Scituate and Barnstable church records.
2 CONT
2 CONT The text lists the 12 children, only 7 of which survived childhood. "John Hinckley, son of Samuel, resided at West Barnstable. He was a man of some note, often employed in town affairs, and ensign of the militia company, an office
2 CONC  of honor in his day. He married for his first wife July 1668, Bethia Lothrop. She was a member of the church, but does not appear to have been an exemplary sister. She died 10th July, 1697, and he married Nov. 24th, 1697, for his
2 CONC  second wife, Mary (Davis) Goodspeed." [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT "m. July 1668, Bethia, d. of Thomas Lothrop... He had sec. w. 24 Nov. 1697, Mary Goodspeed, perhaps wid. of Benjamin." (Not to be confused with his brother's wife of the same name, presumably.) [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT "New England Marriages Prior To 1700" Clarence A. Torrey, (as found on NEHGS CD-ROM, Boston, 2001) "HINKLEY, John (1644-1709) & 1/wf Bethiah LOTHROP (-1694?); Jul 1668; Barnstable"
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
