2 CONT
2 CONT Zebulon Young 
2 CONT *M, 
2 CONT *b. 1700, 
2 CONT *d. 29 December 1788
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Zebulon Young''' was born in 1700 at Eastham. He was the son of Nathaniel Young and Mercy Davis. Zebulon Young married Abigail Rogers, daughter of James Rogers and Susanna Tracy, on 23 February 1748 at Eastham. Zebulon Young di
2 CONC ed on 29 December 1788 at Eastham.
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S1] Ann T. [Revised by], (Originally compiled by Alice W. A. Westgate) Reeves, Mayflower Families Through Five Generations: Descendants of the Pilgrims who landed at Plymouth, Mass. December 1620: Family of Thomas Rogers (Ply
2 CONC mouth, MA: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 2000), p. 39. Hereinafter cited as Rogers-Silver.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ancestors.familysearch.org/en/9MQJ-58H/zebulon-young-1700-1788
2 CONT
2 CONT Zebulon Young
2 CONT Male
2 CONT 1700–29 December 1788
2 CONT •
2 CONT 9MQJ-58H
2 CONT
2 CONT Brief Life History of Zebulon
2 CONT
2 CONT When Zebulon Young was born in 1700, in Eastham, Barnstable, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America, his father, Nathaniel Young, was 44 and his mother, Mercy Davis, was 44. He married Mercy Sparrow on 23 February 1725
2 CONC , in Eastham, Barnstable, Massachusetts, United States. They were the parents of at least 4 sons and 3 daughters. He died on 29 December 1788, in Eastham, Barnstable, Massachusetts, United States, at the age of 88.
2 CONT
