1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Preston-1492
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Ebenezer was born in 1723.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Son of Joseph and Jane Cook Preston, born at Wallingford ... viii. Ebenezer Preston, b. 17 Sep 1723, m. 1st Martha (widow of Abel Hoadley and John Howd), m. 2nd at Winchester 20 Feb 1771 Martha Catlin, resided in Branford and Win
2 CONC chester"[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage to Martha Catling[3] Joined the church in 1772 with Martha his wife (from Harwinton church). This Martha must have been his second wife, whom he married in Feb 1771.[4] Taken from the Annals and Family Records of WInchest
2 CONC er, Conn., by John Boyd, published Hartford: Press of Case, Lockwood & Brainard, 1873.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also from the Annals and Family Records of Winchester, Conn.[5]Ebenezer (of Wallingford) married Martha who died May 16 1770, then married again Martha Catling on Feb 20 1771 and had Phebe and Rebecca. Phebe born July 20 1773 and 
2 CONC Rebecca born August 27 1774
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ "Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F746-2RL : 7 January 2020), Ebenezer Preston, 1723.
2 CONT ↑ https://mathcs.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr05/rr05_029.html
2 CONT ↑ "Connecticut, Vital Records, Prior to 1850," database, FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QPQC-9X6D : 15 April 2022), Ebenezer Preston in entry for Martha Catling, ; citing Marriage, Winchester, Litchfield
2 CONC , Connecticut, United States, Compiled by Lucius A. and Lucius B. Barbour, housed at State Library, Hartford, Connecticut; FHL microfilm 008272226.
2 CONT ↑ https://archive.org/details/annalsfamilyreco00boyd/page/88/mode/1up?view=theater&q=ebenezer+preston
2 CONT ↑ https://archive.org/details/annalsfamilyreco00boyd/page/34/mode/1up?view=theater&q=ebenezer+preston
