1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT 105 Pg 61
2 CONT
2 CONT JEREMIAH GUILD  (jeremiah, Samuel,' Samuel,' John') son of Jeremiah and Elinor (Evans) Guild, born in Middletown, Conn., Sept. 4, 1746, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Married first, Jan. 15, 1775, HANNAH HALE, daughter of Ebenezer
2 CONT and Mary (Turner) Hale, of Middlefield, Conn. She was born June 27, 1756, and died in Warren, May 9, i800. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married second, Sept. 2, 1800, LUCINDA FENTON who was born in Coventry, Nov. 13,
2 CONT 1768, and died Feb. 22, 1849. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When a young man he made several voyages to the West Indies, and having studied navigation, he purchased a sloop for the purpose of trading on his own account. During one of the voyages his vessel was seized and burned by the Brit
2 CONC ish, and with his brother Samuel, who was with him at the time, he was carried a prisoner to Halifax. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When released on parole, he returned to Middletown and engaged in farming on the land owned by his mother and some additional which he had purchased. In the spring of 1793 he bought one hundred and fifty acres of land at Warren, m
2 CONC oved his family to this place, and commenced manufacturing charcoal for several iron works in the vicinity. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was an honest, upright man, and a member of the Episcopal Church at Trinity Parish, Milton, which edifice he had taken an active part in building. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at Warren Jan. 31, 1822.
2 CONT
2 CONT Individual note:
2 CONT When a young man, Jeremiah Guild made several voyages to the Nest Indies. Having studied navigation, he purchased a sloop for the purpose of trading on his oun account. During one of the voyages, his vessel was seized and burned b
2 CONC y the British. He and his brother Sanuel were carried prisoner to Halifax. When released on parole, he returned to Middletown CT and engaged in farning. He noved later to Harren. He vas a member of the Episcopal Church at Trinity 
2 CONC Parish, Milton, which ediface he had taken an active part in building.
