1 NAME Isaac /Searl/
2 GIVN Isaac
2 SURN Searl
2 _MARNM Searl
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Cadiz Cemetery, Cadiz, Cattaraugus County, New York, USA
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 OCT 1789
2 PLAC Whitehall, Washington County, New York, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 11 APR 1860
2 PLAC Franklinville, Cattaraugus County, New York, USA
2 ADDR
1 TITL Sgt.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of Gideon SEARL, Jr. (1762–1830) and Hannah Woodward SEARL (1768–1811).  Hannah is Gideon's 1st wife and daughter of Elias WOODWARD (1741–1825) and Bethiah Clift WOODWARD (1744–1795).
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings include:
2 CONT Abigail SEARL (1784–1854)
2 CONT Abraham SEARL (1787–1846)
2 CONT Jeriah SEARL (1788–1863)
2 CONT Phoebe SEARL (1791–1869)
2 CONT Jacob SEARL (1793–1876)
2 CONT Samuel SEARL (1796–1874)
2 CONT Pamela SEARL (1798–)
2 CONT Sally SEARL (1800–1810)
2 CONT Arza SEARL (1802–1884)
2 CONT Marilla SEARL (1805–1835)
2 CONT Cynthia SEARL (1807–1882)
2 CONT Gideon SEARL (1810–1882)
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Martha HOTCHKISS in Jul 1811.  They had the following children:
2 CONT Phoebe SEARL (1812-)
2 CONT Samuel SEARL (1812–1865)
2 CONT David SEARL (1814–1844)
2 CONT Orange SEARL (1816–1896)
2 CONT Lyman SEARL (1818–1892)
2 CONT Isaac SEARL (1820–1895)
2 CONT Lucy L. B. SEARL (1822-1854)
2 CONT Arvilla SEARL (1825–1903)
2 CONT Hannah SEARL (1828-1907)
2 CONT Andrew Jackson SEARL (1832-1874)
2 CONT ▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬
2 CONT He was an abolitionists who worked on the Underground Railroad.
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Searl, a prominent and successful farmer, risked everything for a cause he fervently believed in – the freedom of all men.  He died on April 11th, 1860 without learning that the approaching Civil War would lead to the cause 
2 CONC he believed in.
2 CONT
2 CONT The final accolade to this brave man was that "he left a legacy richer by far – that of a blameless life and spotless reputation and the passerby may pause at his grave and truthfully say "Here lies all that can die of the noblest
2 CONC  work of God – an honest man."
2 CONT
2 CONT From: HISTORY OF CATTARAUGUS COUNTY NEW YORK, 1879 by L. H. Everts
2 CONT ▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬▬
2 CONT Served in the War of 1812 as a Sergeant in Capt Pliny Adams Regt, NY Militia
2 CONT
2 CONT
