1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Samuel Damon=
2 CONT * BIRTH 23 Jun 1656 Reading, Middlesex County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 12 Jan 1724 (aged 67) Reading, Middlesex County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Old Burying Ground, Wakefield, Middlesex County, Massachusetts, USA [5]
2 CONT * PLOT Sec. B. Row 11 MEMORIAL ID 193104800
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel was the son of Deacon John & Abigail (MNU) Damon. His father "came from Reading, England and settled first, perhaps, on Cowdrey's Hill, where was a very early seat of the Damons."   He and Mary are the parents of nine child
2 CONC ren.
2 CONT
2 CONT In December 1675 Samuel was a soldier in the Narragansett War. [In 1765 Timothy Damon settled the lot drawn in Westminster Mass. for his grandfather's military service.] [3]   "On the way to or from church he {Samuel} was thrown f
2 CONC rom his horse and killed; and his wife who was riding on the pillion behind him was so injured as to be unable to walk for the remainder of her life."  Samuel died intestate. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Mary Davis Damon 1657–1727
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Abigail Damon Nickols 1688–1732
2 CONT Benjamin Daman 1693–1771
2 CONT John Damon 1697–1755
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference
2 CONT [1] https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/193104800/samuel-damon
2 CONT
2 CONT [2] [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/31702988/person/19533000739 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 20 2017, 4:01:53 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT [3] Lilly Eaton, Genealogical History of the Town of Reading, Mass., including the present towns of Wakfield, Reading, and North Reading, with chronological and historical sketches, from 1639 to 1874, Mudge & Son, Boston, 1874, ht
2 CONC tp://archive.org/details/cu31924025963517.)
2 CONT
2 CONT [4] Historical Sketch of Ancient Redding, Massachusetts. . . Volume 1, Copy 2, 180.
2 CONT
2 CONT [5] William E. Eaton's "Old Burial Ground" now Wakefield, Massachusetts, 1688, 1935.
