1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Davis married 1) Matthew Grover; married 2) Samuel Damon. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (Davis) Grover's name is shown in the old Reading First Church records, established 1659:
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 June 1680:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Mary Davis, allias widdow Grover, after just satisfaction given, was owned of the Church, and her children baptized. Mary Davis having broken one of God's commandments before her marriage, had a true sense of her sinne and the di
2 CONC shonour that came to the gospel thereby, and did bewayle it before the church so as they did at length accept of her repentence, and it being published to the congregation, and she desired to own the covenant, after she stood for 
2 CONC a time propounded she was freely acknowledged the 6th of June 1680 to stand as an approved member of the Church, capable of the privileges to her belonging."
2 CONT
2 CONT "Mary Davis, allias widdow Grover, after just satisfaction given, was owned of the Church, and her children baptized."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Davis-9758
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Damon formerly Davis aka Grover
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 16 Feb 1658 in Reading, Middlesex, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Matthew Grover — married about 1673 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Thomas Grover, Matthew Grover Jr and Sarah (Grover) Gould
2 CONT
2 CONT Died [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 22 Aug 2019 | Created 27 Jan 2012
2 CONT
