1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Henry Woodward''' Was  b 1679/80 in Northhampton, Hampshire, Massachusetts, son of John Woodward and Ann Dewey. He died in Lebanon, New London County, Connecticut on about  8 Sep 1741.
2 CONT
2 CONT He  married at Lebanon on March 17, 1703 to Hannah Burrows.  She' was born to John Burrows and Hannah Culver on 15 December 1684 at New London, New London, Connecticut, and died on 05 March 1772.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Henry Woodward and Hannah Burrows, born at Lebanon, were:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Samuell, b. September 10, 1705
2 CONT # Israel, b. May 20, 1708
2 CONT # Hannah, b. July 9, 1710
2 CONT # Abigail, b. September 21, 1712
2 CONT # Sarah, b. October 25, 1715
2 CONT # Martha, b. November 14, 1717
2 CONT # Henry, b. December 22, 1720
2 CONT # Anne, b. December 13, 1721
2 CONT # David, b. May 20, 1725
2 CONT # John, b. December 6, 1727
2 CONT
2 CONT In "History of descendants of Henry Woodward of Dorchester, 1635" Henry Woodward is referred to as Lieutenant Henry Woodward. 11 children are named as children of he and Hannah Burrows corresponding by and large with the children 
2 CONC listed above with one unnamed child who died in infancy. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The daughter of Hannah Culver Burrows (Culver-124). All available evidence suggest that Culver-124 gave birth to only one daughter named Mary on 14 Dec 1672. The will of Culver-124, dated 1731 Groton CT, states (1) “I give unto my
2 CONC  loving daughter Mary Tuttle my best feather bed” and (2) “I give all the Remainder of my Estate, after my just debts and funeral charges are paid unto my three daughters Mary Tuttle, Margaret Duey, and '''Hannah Woodward''' . . .
2 CONC ” See Probate Court (New London District) records 1675-1916, v. C, pp. 651-652. Film 5112, DGS 7627378,
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Henry Woodward (1679-abt.1741)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Woodward-1445 : accessed 22 February 2024). cites 
2 CONT ## Town of Northampton: Births, Marriages, and Deaths; images, FamilySearch; DGS 004329300 ("Births, marriages, deaths 1654-1853."): Volume 1, Page 20.
2 CONT ##Genealogy and social history : the early settlement of Lebanon, CT
2 CONT ##Town of Lebanon. Births, Marriages, Deaths; imaged, FamilySearch; DGS 007730346 ("Records of births, marriages, and deaths, vols. 1-4, 1700-1915"): Volume 1 Page 325.
2 CONT ## Woodward, Samuel B. and Hubert Madison Woodward, compilers, ''History of Descendants of Henry Woodward of Dorchester, 1635'', p. 29-30.
2 CONT ##Connecticut, Town Marriage Records pre 1870 (Barbour Collection).
2 CONT ##Hale Collection reference to Lieut. Henry Woodward on memorial stone of Mercy, his 2nd wife
2 CONT ##FamilySearch Person: LCPZ-59K
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Hannah (Burrows) Woodward (1674-abt.1772)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Burrows-301 : accessed 22 February 2024). Cites
2 CONT ##U.S. and International Marriage Records, 1560-1900
2 CONT ## Family Search lists the death of Hannah (Burrows) Woodward (LZP3-RXN) as 5 Mar 1772 in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut. Her burial is listed as 1772 in Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut Colony of British America.
2 CONT ## Ancestry- Family Trees.
2 CONT ## Connecticut Church Record Abstracts, 1630-1920. American Genealogical-Biographical Index (AGBI). Millenium Files. US and International Marriage Records, 1560-1900. US Sons of the American Revolution-Membership Applications, 188
2 CONC 9-1970.
2 CONT ## Connecticut, Town Birth Records pre-1870 (Barbour Collection).
2 CONT ## "Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QLM7-KSSS : 22 July 2021), Burrows in entry for Israel, 1708.
2 CONT ## "Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QLM7-KSSS : 22 July 2021), Burrows in entry for Israel, 1708.
2 CONT ## "Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QLMQ-G422 : 22 July 2021), Burrows in entry for Sarah, 1715.
2 CONT ## "Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QLMQ-G4LY : 22 July 2021), Burrows in entry for Henry, 1720.
2 CONT ## "Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QLMQ-G4GV : 22 July 2021), Burrows in entry for Anne, 1721.
2 CONT ## "Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QLM7-V2T1 : 22 July 2021), Burrows in entry for David, 1725.
2 CONT ## "Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QLM7-V2YG : 22 July 2021), Burrows in entry for John, 1727.
2 CONT ## "Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906", database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QLMQ-G4LZ : 22 July 2021), Burrows in entry for Martha, 1717.
2 CONT ## Woodward, Samuel B. and Hubert Madison Woodward, compilers, History of Descendants of Henry Woodward of Dorchester, 1635, p. 29 - https://www.familysearch.org/library/books/records/item/320962-history-of-descendants-of-henry-wo
2 CONC odward-of-dorchester-1635?viewer=1&offset=441930#page=37&viewer=picture&o=search&n=0&q=Sweetland.
2 CONT ## Andrews, Henry Porter (b. 1822), Descendants of John Porter of Windsor, Connecticut 1635, Saratoga Springs, NY: G W Ball, 1893. Here the birthdate of Hannah, daughter of John Burrows and Hannah Mary (Culver) Burrows is said to 
2 CONC be 9 Oct 1684. This seems more likely since the birth of her last child was in 1727. Ancestry- Family Trees has five sources that agree.
