1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Birth: Notes
2 CONT # There is no primary source for Richard's place of birth. Circumstantial evidence points to Windsor. (Northampton wasn't settled until 1647.) 
2 CONT # One or more Family History books supply a specific date of birth without primary sourcing. If it were up to me, I'd prefer a date change to show "about 1647." – Ken Shelley, 5 Feb 2025.
2 CONT ## updated birth data from May 26, 1647 Windsor, Hartford, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Marriage
2 CONT * '''Digital-records with images are wrong in showing 1675 for marriage.''' The couple married on 26 May 1674 in Northampton, MA. There is one handwritten document that probably led to the digital error, but close scrutinizing of 
2 CONC that document reveals that the last digit is not a 5 compared to all other 5s on the page. I amended that FamilySearch record. (Elizabeth was pregnant with Benjamin when married.) Ken Shelley, 5 Feb 2025.
2 CONT ** "Massachusetts, State Vital Records, 1638-1927", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FHHY-39H FamilySearch]; Entry for Richard Lyman and Elizabeth Cowles, 26 May 1674.
2 CONT ** "Massachusetts, Town Clerk, Vital and Town Records, 1626-2001", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:Q29L-LLX1 FamilySearch]; Entry for Richard Lyman and Elisabeth Cole, 26 May 1674.
2 CONT ** "Massachusetts, Town Clerk, Vital and Town Records, 1626-2001", [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:Q29L-2RV2 FamilySearch]; Entry for Richard Lyman and Elizabeth Cowles, 26 May 1674.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Primary-Sourced Children b. in Northampton, MA
2 CONT * '''FamilySearch [https://www.familysearch.org/en/search/record/results?count=20&q.birthLikeDate.from=1674&q.birthLikeDate.to=1690&q.birthLikePlace=Northampton%2C%20Hampshire%2C%20Massachusetts%20Bay%20Colony%2C%20British%20Colon
2 CONC ial%20America&q.fatherGivenName=Richard&q.motherGivenName=Elizabeth&q.surname=Lyman&q.surname.1=Limon&q.surname.2=lemon query link].'''
2 CONT * '''Note:''' There is primary source birth/baptism record for Josiah. However, "Josiah" shows as Richard's "son" in Richard's Will.  At this FamilySearch [https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:S3HT-691S-465?view=index&perso
2 CONC nArk=%2Fark%3A%2F61903%2F1%3A1%3AQ29L-LG2Q&action=view&cc=2061550&lang=en&groupId= link with image], there is a Josiah (hard to read date), a son of Thomas and Johannah, who was baptized 1687 in Northampton. Either the record keep
2 CONC er erred in when writing the manuscript about a son "James" when it should've been "Josiah", or there is an unaccounted for son of Richard named James and we don't know when Josiah was born. On the document, it reads: "James son o
2 CONC f Richard Limon" (mother not identified) baptized "24 Jan" in 1690. The month is hard to decipher, but months on the page are in sequential order. The baptism date comes right after December.
2 CONT ** '''There was a Josiah Lyman with a burial inscription''' in Old Cemetery in what would become the town of Columbia, which was then within Lebanon, CT. (see [https://www.familysearch.org/en/search/record/results?count=20&q.birth
2 CONC LikeDate.from=1689&q.birthLikeDate.to=1692&q.birthLikePlace=Farmington%2C%20Hartford%2C%20Connecticut%20Colony%2C%20British%20Colonial%20America&q.fatherGivenName=Richard&q.givenName=Josiah&q.surname=Lyman&q.surname.1=Limon&q.surn
2 CONC ame.2=lemon Ancestry.com]). It reads by Hale leading off with a question mark preceding: "Joseph Lyman died Feb. 6, 1760 age 70".
2 CONT *** * At U.S., FindAGrave® [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/22050848/josiah-lyman Josiah Lyman], a picture of the legible that reads: "To the Memory of Mr. Josiah Lyman who died Feby 6th AD 1760 Ætat 70. He was endowed with go
2 CONC od natural Abilities, a Heady Temper, a sound Judgment & witnessed a good Profession."
2 CONT ** '''An untitled compilation of genealogy by compiler unknown''' appears at [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/62282/images/62282_b1086260-00313?ssrc=&treeid=174604283&personid=132612630609&queryId=6137415d-e03b-4a
2 CONC e1-a13d-fde779c142fb&usePUB=true&pId=4405977233 Ancestry.com]. Perhaps it is from this compilation that a birth date for Josiah was derived. There is no reference to sources given by the compiler for any aspect related to the fami
2 CONC ly of Richard and Elizabeth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ====When did Richard and Elizabeth remove to Lebanon, CT?
2 CONT * ''The Genealogy of the Cowles Families in America'' ([https://archive.org/details/genealogyofcowle00cowl/page/36/mode/1up Archive.org]) asserts that Richard removed to Lebanon in 1696, and he “lived in that part now Columbia.” T
2 CONC he author points to no source for this assertion.
2 CONT * Barring an historical sound source being found to prove the year, a precise year for https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Lyman-III/6000000002060381013 and https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Lyman-King/6000000001012997370?thro
2 CONC ugh=6000000002060381013 having to Lebanon is uncertain. However, it assuredly occurred before 1701. Here's why:—
2 CONT ** '''Two Richard Lyman's Jr.''' were admitted to the Lebanon church in 1701 and 1707. Probably the first year represent this profile's Richard and the second representing Richard's son Richard. — ''Connecticut, U.S., Church Recor
2 CONC d Abstracts, 1630-1920,'' Vol. 57, Lebanon. [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/3032/images/41107_620303988_0346-00133?pId=543752 Ancestry.com]. “Elisabeth Lyman” (possibly Josiah's mother?) was admitted to the Leban
2 CONC on Church in 1704. CT U.S., Church Record Extracts, Vol. 57 [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/3032/images/41107_620303988_0346-00131?pId=543752 Ancestry.com]. '''“Elisabeth Lyman”''' (possibly Richard's wife) was a
2 CONC dmitted to the Lebanon Church in 1704. CT U.S., Church Record Extracts, Vol. 57 [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/3032/images/41107_620303988_0346-00131?pId=543752 Ancestry.com].
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Death 4 Nov 1708
2 CONT * "Connecticut, Deaths and Burials, 1772-1934", [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QLM7-J2S8 FamilySearch]. (22 July 2021), Richard Lyman, 1708. — date and month not yet digitzed but appear on the handwritten page. The next 
2 CONC link is a duplicate image.
2 CONT ** "Connecticut, Deaths and Burials, 1772-1934", [https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QLM7-C9KC FamilySearch] (22 July 2021), Richard Lyman, 1708.
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Will & Probate [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/9049/images/007629909_00512?treeid=174604283&personid=132612630609&hintid=1038377560802&usePUB=true&_phsrc=Bec47860&_phstart=default&usePUBJs=true&currentPageIsS
2 CONC tart=&useCurrentPageInfo=&showinfopanel=true&pId=18876 Ancestry.com]
2 CONT * '''Note:''' Beautiful handwriting, prob. transcribed at a later date
2 CONT * '''Will:''' 2 Nov 1708 • Lebanon, New London, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America
2 CONT * '''Probate:''' 19 Dec 1709 • New London, New London, Connecticut Colony, British Colonial America
2 CONT * Richard's named his sons (probably by order of birth) with Josiah's name appearing last, which are then followed by the names of Richard's surviving daughters.
2 CONT '''<nowiki>—————————————————————————————————————————</nowiki>'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ====From what Website was the following information derived?
2 CONT * '''Note about the Following:''' Much of it is correct. On the other hand, there's no evidence that Elizabeth died in Farmington.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard LYMAN III38 was born on 26 May 1647 in Hartford, Hartford, Connecticut. He died on 4 Nov 1708 in Lebanon, New London, Connecticut.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard LYMAN III and Elizabeth COWLES were married on 26 May 1675 in Northampton, Hampshire, Massachusetts.39, 40 + 5. Elizabeth COWLES5 (daughter of John COWLES and Hannah HART) was born on 6 Feb 1645/46 in Farmington, Hartford,
2 CONC  Connecticut. She died in 1696 in Farmington, Hartford, Connecticut. 42 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes Richard LYMAN III and Elizabeth COWLES had the following children: 18
2 CONT  i. Anne LYMAN 43 was born about 1675 in Leabonon, Connecticut.   19
2 CONT  ii. Samuel LYMAN (born on 16 Apr 1676).   +20
2 CONT  iii. Richard LYMAN (born in Apr 1678).   21
2 CONT  iv John LYMAN (born on 6 Jul 1680)..   22
2 CONT  v. Isaac LYMAN (born on 20 Feb 1681/82)..   23
2 CONT  vi. Lt. Johnathan LYMAN (born on 1 Jan 1683/84)..   24
2 CONT  vii. Elizabeth LYMAN (born on 23 Mar 1685/86)..   25
2 CONT  viii. David LYMAN43,43,45, was born on 28 Nov 1688 in Northhampton, Hamps., Massachusetts..46   26
2 CONT  ix. Josiah LYMAN (born on 6 Feb 1689/90).
