1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ====Notes
2 CONT # '''Please review''' her husband Richard's exhaustive [https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Lyman-III/6000000002060381013 master-profile Overview] updated 5 Feb 2026. It details her marriage to Richard Lyman and the children she h
2 CONC ad by him.
2 CONT # There's '''''no''''' primary source in the FS and AA repositories proving that this Elizabeth married a https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-King/6000000038346571201?through=6000000001012997370 . Indeed there's '''''no''''' reliab
2 CONC le secondary source showing this Elizabeth having married a Thomas King. 
2 CONT # '''Elizabeth's birth''' showing "8 February 1645" in Farmington needs a reliable source to prove the date. I find no such source. These tertiary sources purport birth in 1651:—
2 CONT ## U.S. and International Marriage Records estimated birth in 1651 in CT.
2 CONT ## ''Margaret Bready Genealogy Collection'' likewise gives birth in 1651 in Farmington
2 CONT ## ''Genealogy of the Cowles Families in America'' doesn’t give a date but asserts she was born in Farmington.
2 CONT # '''Elizabeth may've been born later than 1651.''' The ''Cowles Families in America'' book and [https://www.americanancestors.org/databases/connecticut-vital-records-the-barbour-collection-1630-1870/RecordDisplay?volumeId=13153&p
2 CONC ageName=109&rId=234498253 AmericanAncestor$.org], Barbour Collection shows "Ann, d. Richard & Elizabeth, b. Aug. 30, 1698" in Lebanon. To think that Elizabeth gave birth to Ann at about age 46 is risible. Hmm....there doesn't seem
2 CONC  to be another Richard Lyman and Elizabeth couple living in Lebanon, CT.
2 CONT # '''Further research''' for a primary or reliable secondary source might reveal her year of death. Either this Elizabeth or her daughter Elizabeth was living in 1704 and was admitted to the Lebanon church. (''See below.'')
2 CONT
2 CONT ====When did Richard and Elizabeth remove to Lebanon, CT?
2 CONT * ''The Genealogy of the Cowles Families in America'' ([https://archive.org/details/genealogyofcowle00cowl/page/36/mode/1up Archive.org]) asserts that Richard removed to Lebanon in 1696, and he “lived in that part now Columbia.” T
2 CONC he author points to no source for this assertion. '''Also of note,''' this book does not suggest a year for Elizabeth's death.
2 CONT * '''Without an historically sound source''', a precise year for https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Lyman-III/6000000002060381013 and https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Lyman-King/6000000001012997370?through=600000000206038101
2 CONC 3 having removed to Lebanon is uncertain. However, it assuredly occurred before 1701. Here's why:—
2 CONT ** '''Two Richard Lyman's Jr.''' were admitted to the Lebanon church in 1701 and 1707. Probably the first year represent this profile's Richard and the second representing Richard's son Richard. — ''Connecticut, U.S., Church Recor
2 CONC d Abstracts, 1630-1920,'' Vol. 57, Lebanon. [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/3032/images/41107_620303988_0346-00133?pId=543752 Ancestry.com]. “Elisabeth Lyman” (possibly Josiah's mother?) was admitted to the Leban
2 CONC on Church in 1704. CT U.S., Church Record Extracts, Vol. 57 [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/3032/images/41107_620303988_0346-00131?pId=543752 Ancestry.com]. '''“Elisabeth Lyman”''' (possibly Richard's wife) was a
2 CONC dmitted to the Lebanon Church in 1704. CT U.S., Church Record Extracts, Vol. 57 [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/3032/images/41107_620303988_0346-00131?pId=543752 Ancestry.com].
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Death
2 CONT * The Wikitree profile manager for [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cowles-10 Elizabeth (Cowles) Lyman (1645–aft. 1698)] asserts "'''Death''' 1698 Farmington, Hartford, Connecticut. Daughter Amy [sic] was born 30 August 1698[1]. Dea
2 CONC th would have to be after this date." (The data-source cited is at FamilySearch. It shows Ann Lyman, not Amy.) 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''<nowiki>————————————————————————————————————————</nowiki>'''
2 CONT
