1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Josiah's name appears in his father's Will. His name appears last in Richard's naming of his sons. There is no primary record of birth/baptism that proves when and where Josiah was born. This situation is now detai
2 CONC led in his father's Geni master profile Overview. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Lyman-III/6000000002060381013 and https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Lyman-King/6000000001012997370?through=6000000002060381013 removed to Lebanon isn't known for certain, but it probabl
2 CONC y occurred before 1701 (or certainly before 1707). Two Richard Lyman's Jr. were admitted to the Lebanon church in these years. — Connecticut, U.S., Church Record Abstracts, 1630-1920, Vol. 57, Lebanon. [https://www.ancestry.com/im
2 CONC ageviewer/collections/3032/images/41107_620303988_0346-00133?pId=543752 Ancestry.com]. “Elisabeth Lyman” (possibly Josiah's mother?) was admitted to the Lebanon Church in 1704. CT U.S., Church Record Extracts, Vol. 57 [https://www
2 CONC .ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/3032/images/41107_620303988_0346-00131?pId=543752 Ancestry.com].
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Burial Inscription(s)
2 CONT ** Josiah Lyman's with burial inscription by Hale was recorded in "Old Cemeter" in what would become the town of Columbia, which was then within Lebanon, CT. (see [https://www.familysearch.org/en/search/record/results?count=20&q.b
2 CONC irthLikeDate.from=1689&q.birthLikeDate.to=1692&q.birthLikePlace=Farmington%2C%20Hartford%2C%20Connecticut%20Colony%2C%20British%20Colonial%20America&q.fatherGivenName=Richard&q.givenName=Josiah&q.surname=Lyman&q.surname.1=Limon&q.
2 CONC surname.2=lemon Ancestry.com]). It reads by Hale leading off with a question mark preceding: "Joseph Lyman died Feb. 6, 1760 age 70".
2 CONT * At U.S., FindAGrave® [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/22050848/josiah-lyman Josiah Lyman], a picture of the legible that reads: "To the Memory of Mr. Josiah Lyman who died Feby 6th AD 1760 Ætat 70. He was endowed with good n
2 CONC atural Abilities, a Heady Temper, a sound Judgment & witnessed a good Profession."
