1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Eleazer Swetland=
2 CONT * BIRTH 22 Feb 1801 East Longmeadow, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * DEATH Feb 1867 (aged 65–66) Hop Bottom, Susquehanna County, Pennsylvania, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Portland Evergreen Cemetery, Portland, Chautauqua County, New York, USA
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 83239135 Photos by Ron Kinney
2 CONT
2 CONT Eleazer and Philinda lived in the old Swetland homestead in Massachusetts until about 1831 or 1832. They then moved to Middlefield, Otsego County, New York. About 1850 they moved again to Portland, Chautauqua County, New York they
2 CONC  were there for the 1850 Census.  He died Feb 1867 in Hop Bottom, PA, while visiting his dauther, Martha. His body was brought home to Portland, NY and buried next to his wife in Evergreen Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1850 Census lists Eleazer and family as living in Chautauqua, Chautauqua County, New York. Eleazer's occupation is shown as "Farmer". The household listed after theirs is that of Palta and Mariah Swetland.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1860 Census lists Eleazer and "Pilenda" as living in Portland, Chautauqua County, New York. Eleazer's occupation is shown as "Farmer". Another member of their household is "Eleazer Swetland" born about 1760 in New York. Father
2 CONC : Theophilus Swetland b: 17 JAN 1757 in Coventry, Tolland County, Connecticut  Mother: Ann Brown b: 2 MAR 1778 in Coventry, Tolland County, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Theophilus Swetland 
2 CONT Ann Swetland
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Philinda A. Crane Swetland 1802–1861 m. 9/22/1821 East Longmeadow, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children''' 9x b. in East Longmeadow, MA*, Middlefield, Otsego County NY
