1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Joseph Rood=  
2 CONT * BIRTH 7 May 1750
2 CONT * DEATH 31 Mar 1843 (aged 92)
2 CONT * BURIAL Pioneer Cemetery. Fredonia, Chautauqua County, New York, USA
2 CONT * GPS-Latitude: 42.4434254, Longitude: -79.326771
2 CONT * PLOT 1460
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 15797606 photos added by Diane LM & Ron Kinney
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inscription'''
2 CONT Pioneer Cemetery has 2 stones for Joseph -- a stone and a veteran's plaque. 
2 CONT Stone inscription: Joseph Rood Died Mar. 31, 1843. In the 91 year of his age. 
2 CONT Veteran's plaque: Joseph Rood Connecticut PVT Continental Line Revolutionary War May 7, 1750 March 31, 1843
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Gravesite Details'''
2 CONT The Geo C Rood monument is in the Forest Hill Cemetery of Fredonia, Plot O/1. Captain Rood's name appears on the monument as a cenotaph. Plot Map for O/1 does not show him buried there.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Jeremiah Rood 1728–1816
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Lois White Rood 1760–1847
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Cast. Joseph W Rood 1750–1843
2 CONT Hannah Rood Treadway 1756–1832
2 CONT Jeremiah Rood 1759–1820
2 CONT Jeremiah Rood 1759–1820
2 CONT Olive Rood Stiles 1767–1843
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Maj Asa Rood 1785–1859
2 CONT Harriet Rood 1799–1875
2 CONT George Coomer Rood 1802–1892
2 CONT
2 CONT ==References==
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/15797606/joseph-rood
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT =Capt. Joseph W Rood=
2 CONT * BIRTH 7 May 1754 Lebanon, New London County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 31 Mar 1843 (aged 92) Pomfret, Chautauqua County, New York, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Pioneer Cemetery, Fredonia, Chautauqua County, New York 
2 CONT * PLOT 1460  MEMORIAL ID 15797606
2 CONT * CENOTAPH Forest Hill Cemetery, Fredonia, Chautauqua County, New York, USA
2 CONT * PLOT 0/1  MEMORIAL ID 202964707
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth date discrepancies: His grave monument is engraved that he died 31 Mar 1843 in the 94th year of his age. This would make his birth date 1750. This appears to be a latter stone, perhaps erected for his son George. A Revolutio
2 CONC nary War plaque, which also appears to be newer, has a birth of 7 May 1750 and death 31 Mar 1843. An older stone reads Joseph Rood died 31 Mar 1843 in the 94 year of his age. This is a bit difficult to read, and could possibly be 
2 CONC 91 instead of 94. Joseph Rood, the son of Jeremiah Rood and Hanna Grover Briggs and brother of Jeremiah and Asa, was born 7 May 1754 in Lebanon, Connecticut.[1][2][3] He stated that he was age 88 in 1838 when he applied for a revo
2 CONC lutionary war pension. Lebanon Vital Records[4] state "Joseph Rude ye son was born 7th May A.D. 1754". This is likely correct if his parents were married 10 May 1753.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Lois White in Connecticut. She was born 18 Sep 1760 in Lebanon, Connecticut, the daughter of Nathaniel White and Lois Coomer, and died 26 Feb 1847 in Fredonia, New York.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Yesterdays column in the 9 Jun 1960 Fredonia Censor has a history of the Rood Family.[6] Jeremiah Rood born 1753 in Lebanon, Connecticut came to Pomfret in 1808. After the war of 1812, he returned to Connecticut and persuaded 
2 CONC his brother Joseph to emigrate. They traveled through snow with 2 ox teams and a horse team, arriving 17 Feb 1816. They traveled with Joseph's step mother who was over age 90. Joseph was born in Lebanon about 1750. Joseph's time a
2 CONC t home around 1775 caring for his aged father and sick brother, described in his pension application, is mentioned. Joseph's son George Rood was born in Windom County 4 Sept 1802.
2 CONT
2 CONT Early purchasers in the town of Pomfret, Chautauqua County, New York included 1809 Jeremiah Rood lot 31, 1817 Standish Rood lot 38, 1819 Asa Rood lot 37. Undated Joseph Rood on lot 22, owned by George C Rood in 1875[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was replaced as a trustee of the Fredonia Presbyterian Church in Dec 1819. Trinity Church at Fredonia was organized in Aug 1822. He was a warden, and later a vestryman.[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1820 he was living next door to Asa Rood in the town of Pomfret, Chautauqua, New York.[9] The household included 1 male age 16 to 25, 1 male over age 45, 1 female under age 10, 1 female age 16 to 25, and one female over age 45.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1830 he was living in the town of Pomfret, Chautauqua, New York.[10] The household included 1 male age 10 to 14, 1 male age 70 to 79, 1 female age 10 to 14, 1 female age 15 to 19, and 1 female age 60 to 69.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Rood, age 87, called at the office of the Fredonia Censor on 5 April 1836, and stated that he had voted at every election and town meeting since the age of 21.[11]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 27 Oct 1838, at age 88, he applied for a Revolutionary War pension in Chautauqua County, New York. [12] He cited service 19 April 1775 leaving from Lebanon, Windham County, Connecticut to the battle of Lexington near Boston und
2 CONC er the service of Capt Joseph Hill. He was then drafted to go to New York. His brother Jeremiah Rood enlisted about the same time to go to New York. About this same time another brother became sick and went crazy and Joseph had to
2 CONC  return home to care for his aged father and insane brother. In February 1776 his brother became rational and Joseph volunteered to go to Roxbury in Capt Greenville Mason's company. He was injured in his right ???? and disabled fr
2 CONC om duty. He later volunteered with the same company and was at Providence for some time before becoming sick and returning to his home in Lebanon. He remained in Lebanon until moving to the town of Pomfret in Chautauqua County 22 
2 CONC years ago (1838 - 22 = 1816). When he filed for the pension in 1838, both of his brothers were dead. His brother Jeremiah Rood died in Chautauqua County about 1820. He testified that he was born 7 May 1750 in Lebanon, Windham Coun
2 CONC ty, Connecticut and that there is no town record, he has a record of his birth in a family bible. George C Rood testified that he was acquainted with both Joseph and Jeremiah Rood, and that Jeremiah spoke of Joseph's service. On 1
2 CONC 9 February 1853, Asa Rood signed a power of attorney claims for the service of his father, Joseph Rood, deceased. The application was refused.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died 31 Mar 1843 in Pomfret, Chautauqua, New York.[13][14] and was buried at Pioneer Cemetery, Fredonia, Chautauqua County, New York.[15] His gravestone is engraved that he died at age 94. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Jeremiah Rood 1728–1816
2 CONT Hanna (Briggs) Rood 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Lois White Rood 1760–1847 m ca1784 in Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Joseph Rood 1750–1843
2 CONT Hannah Rood Treadway 1756–1832
2 CONT Jeremiah Rood 1759–1820
2 CONT Jeremiah Rood 
2 CONT Olive Rood Stiles 1767–1843
2 CONT Briggs Rood
2 CONT Bridget Rood
2 CONT Asa Rood 
2 CONT Tryphena Rood West
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children'''
2 CONT Asa Rood, 
2 CONT Rebecca Rood Tarbox 
2 CONT Harriet Rood 
2 CONT George Coomer Rood
2 CONT
