1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Pvt. Benjamin Day=  
2 CONT * BIRTH 13 Sep 1731 Colchester, New London County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 26 Jan 1811 (aged 79) South Royalton, Windsor County, Vermont, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL North Royalton Cemetery, North Royalton, Windsor County, Vermont, USA
2 CONT * PLOT section 1, row 3, #1
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 35317945 photos added by Joie Finley
2 CONT
2 CONT Pvt. Benjamin Day served in the Revolutionary War under Capt. Jos. Parkhurst's Company, 1780.  He settled in Royalton before 1780, left after the raid and returned in 1783.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inscription'''
2 CONT ''Go home my friends, dry up your tears
2 CONT We must lie here til Christ appears''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Capt Benjamin Day 1704–1777
2 CONT Margaret Foote Day 1711–1801
