2 CONT Name: *Nathaniel "Nathan" Hiscock Given Name: *Nathaniel "Nathan" Surname: Hiscock 1 Name: Nathaniel Hiscox Given Name: Nathaniel Surname: Hiscox Nickname: Nathan Sex: M Birth: 03 Apr 1749 in Sutton, Massachusetts 1 Death: 11 Jan 
2 CONC 1811 in Stafford, Tolland County, Connecticut [poss] Note:
2 CONT
2 CONT (Killed By Son Robert Who Was Insane)
2 CONT
2 CONT *Father: Nathan Hiscock b: Abt 1706 perhaps of Ipswich, Massachusetts
2 CONT *Mother: Hannah Gale b: Bef 09 Oct 1715 at Watertown 
2 CONT *Marriage 1 Rebecca (Keeney) Keene b: Bef 1765 Married: 09 Jan 1772 in Union, Connecticut 2
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT *Has No Children Hulda Hiscock b: Abt 1776 [This is more likely the daughter of David and Anstice Hiscox]
2 CONT *Has Children *Clarissa "Clara" Hiscock b: 1778 in Ashford, Windham County, Connecticut
2 CONT *Has No Children Lydia Hiscock b: Abt 1779
2 CONT *Has No Children Robert Hiscock
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Thankful Unknown 1775. She was born WFT Est. 1735-17 59, and died WFT Est. 1782-1848.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=sandman55&id=I3314]<br/>
2 CONT Notes for Nathan Hiscox: Nathan and his brother Stephen disagreed about their loyalty to their mother country about the time of the Revolutionary War. Nathan declared he was for the British, A Loyalist, while Stephen said he favor
2 CONC ed the Colonies, whereupon Stephen changed the spelling of his name to Hescock to avoid relationship to his brother Nathan Hiscox, for he wanted it known that he was a PATRIOT.<br/>
2 CONT     Marriage: 1775
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Nathan Hiscox and Thankful Unknown are:
2 CONT *    23i.Hulda4 Hiscox, born 1776; died WFT Est. 1777-1870.
2 CONT *    24ii.Clara Hiscox, born 1778; died WFT Est. 1795-1872. She married Sylvester Hiscox WFT Est. 1795-1827;born June 08, 1780; died WFT Est. 1809-1 871.
2 CONT
