1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Early Life and Family'''
2 CONT Birth and Ancestry: Born on June 11, 1668, in Milton, Norfolk County, Massachusetts. He was the son of Humphrey Tiffany (often referred to as "Squire" or "Honorable") and Elizabeth Baker.
2 CONT Siblings: He grew up in a large family with several brothers, including Ebenezer, James, Hezekiah, William, and Consider.
2 CONT Social Standing: His father's title of "Squire" suggests the family held a respected social status, likely possessing independent means or serving as a local official, such as a justice of the peace.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Marriage and Career'''
2 CONT Marriage: In 1689, Thomas married Hannah Mary Humphries in Swansea, Massachusetts.'''
2 CONT Residency: The couple initially lived in the Bristol/Swansea area of Massachusetts (now part of Rhode Island). During this time, they began raising their family, including their son Nathaniel.
2 CONT '''Pioneer in Ashford:''' Thomas was among the early settlers of Ashford, Connecticut. He moved his family inland as new lands were being incorporated and developed in the early 18th century.
