1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Biographical Highlights'''
2 CONT Marriage: She married Thomas Tiffany in 1689 in Swansea, Massachusetts.
2 CONT Migration: Along with her husband, she was an early settler of Ashford, Connecticut, moving there in the early 1700s as the town was being developed.
2 CONT Family: She was the mother of Nathaniel Tiffany (b. 1701), who married Keziah Ward. She is frequently cited in genealogical records as the matriarch of a significant branch of the Tiffany family in America.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Tiffany and Hannah Mary Humphries had several children, primarily born in Swansea, Massachusetts, before the family moved to Ashford, Connecticut. 
2 CONT
2 CONT According to records from RootsWeb and The Tiffanys of America, their children included:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Tiffany (Jr.): Born May 22, 1692, in Swansea, Massachusetts.
2 CONT Recompence Tiffany: Born March 11, 1694, in Swansea. He later lived in Barrington, Rhode Island.
2 CONT Isaiah Tiffany: Born February 22, 1697, in Swansea. He died in 1780.
2 CONT Edward Tiffany: Born circa 1700.
2 CONT Nathaniel Tiffany: Born January 20, 1706, in Bristol/Ashford (this is the Nathaniel who married Keziah Ward).
2 CONT Eliezer Tiffany: Born circa 1708. 
2 CONT Most of these children migrated with their parents to Ashford, Connecticut, which became a central hub for this branch of the Tiffany family.
