1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''The Tiffanys of America : History and genealogy''.  by Tiffany, Nelson Otis, 1842-; Tiffany, Charles Lewis, 1812-1902. Person # 1820.  Page 124 < [https://archive.org/details/tiffanysofameric00tiff/page/n209/mode/1up Archive.Org
2 CONC ] >
2 CONT
2 CONT 1820. ISAIAH (2 Thomas, 1 Humphrey). Married, first, about 1726, Elizabeth Smith of Swansea ; m., second, Jemima Griswold of Bolton.
2 CONT
2 CONT He removed to Woodstock, where he was a selectman, was town clerk 1730-40, and representative of the town to the General Court, 1742-43. He finally removed to Lebanon, Conn., where his first wife died and he married again.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN BY FIRST MARRIAGE. (No issue by second marriage.)
2 CONT * 1833. i. Isaiah, b. Woodstock, Conn., about 1726.
2 CONT * 1834. ii. John, baptized in Woodstock, Conn., November 11, 1727 ; d. 1766.
2 CONT * 1835. iii. Recompense, b. June 19, baptized June 27, 1731 ; was living in 1800.
2 CONT * 1836. iv. ELIZABETH, b. June 18, 1736; d. March 26, 1790; m., in Lebanon, Conn.,
2 CONT * November 25, 1756, Ebenezer Bushnell. Children : 1912 Ebenezer, b. September 13, 1757; d. August 3, 1800; m., August 14, 1780, Triphena Clark ; had Ilezekiah, b. September 27, 1782 ; d. December 4, 1851 ; 1913 Isaiah, b. Februar
2 CONC y 16, 1759 ; an officer in the Connecticut Lines during the revolution ; 1914 Mary, b. March 27, 17C1 ; 1915 Lucinda, b. January 17, 1764 ; 1916 Alpame, b. May 24, 1705 ; 1917 Jerusha, b. June 16, 1768 ; d. January 16, 1833; m., A
2 CONC pril 15, 1804, Deacon Daniel Strong (b. April 23, 1752; d. July 6, 1826); had Persis Elizabeth, b. May 19, 1807; m. Leonard Hebard.
2 CONT * 1837. v. Asa, b. October 19 ; baptized October 22, 1738 ; d. 1762.
2 CONT * 1838. vl. Persis, b. October 19 ; baptized October 22, 1738 ; d. 1779.
