3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Lieut-Nathan-Tiffany/6000000013030863969?through=378569895220003377 who married 1) https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Tiffany/6000000009618159130?through=6000000013030
2 CONC 863969 2) https://www.geni.com/people/Sarah-Tiffany/6000000095649954852?through=6000000013030863969
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: He and Keziah had several children, including a son also named Nathaniel Tiffany (born May 1, 1731, in Ashford), which sometimes causes confusion in genealogical records.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Marriage''': Keziah married Nathaniel Tiffany on September 6, 1726, in Ashford, Connecticut.
2 CONT '''Siblings''': Keziah was one of several children, with siblings including Jemima, Gamaliel, Jacob, Judith, and Dinah.
2 CONT '''Residency and Family Life'''
2 CONT Following their marriage in 1726, Keziah and Nathaniel lived in Ashford, Windham County, where their first few children were born. They eventually moved to Somers, where they established their permanent home and where Nathaniel hi
2 CONC mself passed away in 1785.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Clarifying the Conflation'''
2 CONT The discrepancies in dates are primarily due to different regional records being applied to the same individual:
2 CONT '''Birth''' (c. 1701): Many family trees list his birth as approximately 1701 in Ashford, Connecticut, or Rhode Island. This date is often used because it aligns better with a 1726 marriage and his recorded age at death (84 years 
2 CONC old in 1785).
2 CONT '''Christening/Birth''' (January 20, 1706): Vital records from Bristol, Rhode Island (then part of Massachusetts), explicitly record the birth of a Nathaniel Tiffany, son of Thomas and Hannah, on this date. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The "Cousin" Nathaniel
2 CONT There is a high likelihood of conflation with Nathaniel Tiffany (b. 1709), who was the son of James Tiffany and Bethiah Fuller. James was Thomas Tiffany's brother, making these two Nathaniels first cousins. This cousin Nathaniel l
2 CONC ived in Attleboro, Massachusetts, and died there in 1788, whereas your ancestor Nathaniel moved to Ashford and later Somers/Enfield, Connecticut.
