1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John, son of John "the Carpenter" Read and his first wife Bashua.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===John Reed Jr.
2 CONT * Born 5 Jun 1674 in Weymouth, Norfolk, Massachusetts
2 CONT * Died 6 Jun 1739 at age 65 in Barrington, Bristol, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT * Son of John Reed and Bethiah (Frye) Reed
2 CONT * Husband of Bethia (Cobb) Reed — married 15 Jun 1697 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography  
2 CONT
2 CONT John (23) married Bethia Cobb (19) (born on April 5, 1678 in Taunton, Bristol; daughter of Augustine Cobb) on June 15, 1697.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT The Chaffee Genealogy 1635-1909 by William H. Chaffe of New York City The Grafton Press p.567 < [https://books.google.com/books?id=cFc5AAAAMAAJ&vq=Bethia%20Cobb&pg=PA567#v=snippet&q=Bethia%20Cobb&f=false GoogleBooks] >
2 CONT
2 CONT John Read, born in Weymouth, Jun 5, 1674 5, 1674, and died in Barrington, Mass., 1739. He married Bethia Cobb. His will dated Jun 6, 1739, mentions all the children given below and directs that his land in Willington, Conn., shall
2 CONC  be divided between his sons, William and John. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT * i. Mary Read, married ____ Tiffany.
2 CONT * ii. John Read, born August, 1701; married Lydia or Elizabeth Caswell.
2 CONT * iii. George Read, born May, 1704, married Abigail _____.
2 CONT * iv. William Read, born in Swansea, Mass., February 18, 1712-13; married Elizabeth Wood of Rehoboth, Mass.
2 CONT * v. Bethia Read a twin, born in Swansea, Februay 28, 171-13; married Nathan Watson
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Reed-6395
2 CONT
2 CONT === Probate
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of John Read of Barrington, yeoman, was dated 6 June 1739 and proved on 19 February 1739/40 in Bristol. He mentioned his widow, his children, John Read, William Read (executor) (bequeathed the continued enslavement of his
2 CONC  black man), Mercy Tiffany, Bethiah Watson, his grandson, George Read, and his daughter-in-law, Abigail Read (mother of George).[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT His inventory was taken on 28 February 1739 in Barrington.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
