2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethiah was born in 1713 at Swansea, Massachusetts, the daughter of John and Bethiah Reed.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethiah married Matthew Watson at Christ's Church in Barrington on 13 March 1733.[2][3] Children:[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail b. 13 January 1733-4
2 CONT Mary b. 5 March 1734-5
2 CONT Rachel b. 14 June 1736
2 CONT Mercy b. 30 March 1738
2 CONT Bethiah b. 12 October 1739
2 CONT Matthew b. 4 April 1741
2 CONT Lydia b. 17 December 1742
2 CONT William b. 25 June 1744
2 CONT John b. 3 October 1746
2 CONT Samuel b. 1748
2 CONT According to Murray, Matthew and Bethiah were said to have had as many as five additional children.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethiah died in 1778.[6][7]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Reed-6412
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethiah (Reed) Watson (1713 - 1778)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Bethiah Watson formerly Reed===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 28 Feb 1713 in Swansea, Bristol County, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of John Reed Jr. and Bethia (Cobb) Reed
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of John Reed III, George Reed and William Read
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Matthew Watson — married 13 Mar 1733 in Barrington, Bristol County, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Rachel (Watson) Marcy, Matthew Watson, William Watson and John Watson
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 9 Feb 1778 at age 64 in Barrington, Bristol County, Rhode Island, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 15 Dec 2022 | Created 12 Aug 2014
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
