1 NAME Calvin /Tiffany/
2 GIVN Calvin
2 _MARNM Tiffany
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 CITY Waukegan
3 STAE Illinois
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 5 NOV 1772
2 ADDR
3 CITY Ashford
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 NOV 1863
2 ADDR
3 CITY Waukegan
3 STAE Illinois
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Date of death December 20, 1863 per IL soldiers index, but November 20, 1863 according to a descendant's SAR application. November 20, 1863, is consistent with obituary age of 91 years, 15 days. The IL soldiers ind
2 CONC ex is probably a transcription error.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is Calvin Tiffany who, with his first wife Abigail Walker (August 8, 1771--July 20, 1823 per SAR application of a descendant), and infant son Rufus, moved from CT to Mexico, NY on February 21, 1799 (date provided in a letter 
2 CONC to the editor in Mexico Independent, February 22, 1866, by Silas Davis, son of Phineas Davis who relocated from CT with the Tiffanys). After the loss of Rufus's family in 1820s and early 1830 (wife and 3 children, all of whom are 
2 CONC buried in Colosse Cemetery), Rufus moved from Mexico, NY, (but he was still in Mexico through November 7, 1833, (per Oswego Palladium, November 27, 1833) when he appeared at an Oswego County Temperance Convention as a representati
2 CONC ve from Mexico). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Calvin's wife Abigail died on July 20, 1823 (age 50 yrs, 10 mos, 26 days, according to her headstone, which would retroactively generate a birthdate of August 24, 1772). Calvin Tiffany married Polly Tiffany and they lived with son
2 CONC  John Tiffany (his wife Mary and son Willard) in 1850 US census in Mexico NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks to Jeffrey Jerrett (#48128221) for posting a copy of the obituary (Mexico Independent, May 5, 1864, p.3.) of Calvin Tiffany and for clarifying that most of the early family of Calvin Tiffany (his wives Abigail and Polly) ar
2 CONC e buried in Mexico Primitive cemetery, Mexico, NY, and not in Colosse. As noted in the prior paragraphs, the early family of his son Rufus (wife and children) are the family members buried in Colosse Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: US census data. Mexico Independent, August 8, 1900, p. 6.  Rancier, Esther. Biography of Calvin Tiffany, Town of Mexico, NY. 2003. Also see Landmarks of Oswego County New York, edited by John C. Churchill, L.L.D., assiste
2 CONC d by H. Perry Smith & W. Stanley Child, Syracuse, N.Y., D. Mason & Company Publishers, 1895. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rancier's bio did not locate Rufus or Calvin after they left Mexico, NY. Rufus Tiffany appears in 1850 U.S. census, Waukegan IL, with wife Louisa. Calvin Tiffany appears in household with Rufus and Louisa in 1860 US census, Waukeg
2 CONC an, IL. (although Calvin's age is shown as 98 he was only 88 in 1860). Calvin was 91 and 15 days old when he died 3 years later.
