1 NAME Richardene /unknown/
2 GIVN Richardene
2 SURN unknown
2 _MARNM Chambers
2 NICK Richardene (__?__) (Curtis) Chambers
1 NAME Richardene (unknown) [Curtis] Chambers
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1589
2 ADDR
3 CITY Probably Ash
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 18 NOV 1672 AND 29 OCT 1673
2 ADDR
3 CITY Scituate
3 STAE Plymouth Colony
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT CURTIS, Thomas, bp. 2 Nov. 1619, s. of Thos. of Ash, Kent, bur. 11 Dec. 1631, and '''Richardene,''' born about 1597, m. 2nd Thos. Chambers. Her maiden name and place of birth and their place of marriage are unknown!
2 CONT
2 CONT Children include
2 CONT # Thomas Curtis b abt 1619 Ash Juxte Sandwich, Kent, England, d 1692, York, Maine.  Married 1) Elizabeth 2) Abigail 
2 CONT # Richard Curtis b abt 1620 Ash Juxte Sandwich, Kent, England d. 1693, Scituate, Plymouth County, Massachusetts.  Married 1) Ann Hallet.  Perhaps a 2nd marriage to Lydia.
2 CONT # Elizabeth Curtis b abt 1624  Ash Juxte Sandwich, Kent, England, d bef 1667, York, Maine.  Married Richard Banks
2 CONT # William Cutis ch 1626 (died young)
2 CONT # William Curtis,   b. Abt 1627, Ash Juxte Sandwich, Kent, England ,   d. Aft 1680, Scituate, Plymouth County, MA.  Wife unnamed. 
2 CONT # Stephen Curtis (died young)
2 CONT # John Curtis b abt 1632, Ash Juxte Sandwich, Kent, England.  died bef Jun 1680 in Scituate, MA.  No descendants. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT Richardene's maiden name, birth or marriage date to Thomas Curtis of Ash, Kent, England, or her home town are unknown.  She was the  second spouse of Thomas Curtis. His first spouse was Bennett Lott, who died in 1615 following the
2 CONC  birth of her second son John, who died at 2 months of age.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Curtis died and was buried 11 Dec. 1631 in Ash (juxta or 'next to' Sandwich), Kent, England.  
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife Richardene or Richardine married second on  May 1632, to  Thomas Chambers.  Richardene married Thomas Chambers six months after the death of her first husband.
2 CONT
2 CONT She and her children emigrated with Chambers to Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts in 1638.  Within a few years, son Thomas ch. 7 Nov 1619 settled in 1642 in York (originally Gorgeana, then Agamenticus, then York), Maine with his s
2 CONC ister Elizabeth, wife of Richard Banks, next door. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps in October 1638, but before December 4th of the same year, when the name of Thomas Chambers first appears in the Plymouth Colony records, Richardene, her new husband, and her children emigrated to New England and settled i
2 CONC n Scituate. The ship and port of entry are unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Chambers bought land in York, Maine, but his residence was in Scituate, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richardene's estate was settled 29 Oct 1673.  She left a bequest in her will to Abigail, wife of her son Thomas Curtice, and his daughter Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~barbpretz/ps03/ps03_414.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT “Thus perhaps in October 1638 but before December 4th on the same year when his name first appears in the Plymouth Colony records, Thomas Chambers, with Richardene his wife, and the five Curtis children, Elizabeth, Thomas, #1, Ric
2 CONC hard, #2, William, #3, and John, #4, emigrated to New England and settled in Scituate, Mass.”1527
2 CONT
2 CONT “From Richardene’s will it is known that she left a bequest to Abigail, her son Thomas’ wife and to Elizabeth, HIS daughter. That shows Elizabeth was the daughter of the first wife, Elizabeth. She was probably the first grandchild
2 CONC  and therefore special.”1529
2 CONT
2 CONT “The widow Richardene left a will [74] dated November 18, 1672 and witnessed by Elisha Besley and Abraham Suttliff. This together with the inventory and transcripts thereof are reproduced as Figures 5 and 6. She bequeathed by her 
2 CONC ‘late husband’s desire’ her house and land to her son John Curtis, whom she named executor, leaving her wearing apparel to Abigail, wife of her son Thomas, and 10 pounds to Elizabeth, daughter of Thomas. The inventory, taken Octob
2 CONC er 27, 1673 by Thomas King, Richard Curtis and Abraham Suttliff, included only the goods and chattels and totalled 91 pounds and 14 shillings.”1527
2 CONT
2 CONT “Richardene and Thomas Chambers were married 25 May 1632, just 12 days after John was christened. It was certainly necessary for a woman to find another husband as quickly as possible when she had a houseful of children”.1529
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional information provided by Nancy R. Purchase (June 28, 2015):
2 CONT
2 CONT RIchardene/Richardine ___(surname unknown) married 1. Thomas Curtis of "Ash-juxta (next to)-Sandwich, Kent, England had 7 children with Thomas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When Thomas died (Buried 11 Dec 1631 in Ash, Richardene remarried 25 Jun 1632 to Thomas Chambers (no issue from this marriage). However, Thomas Chambers took Richardine and her 5 children* (2 had died) to New England by 1639. 
2 CONT
2 CONT SOURCE: Source Bibliography: FARMER, JOHN. A Genealogical Register of the First Settlers of New-England;  Containing an Alphabetical List of the Governours, Deputy-Governours, Assistants or Counsellors, and Ministers of the Gospel
2 CONC  in the Several Colonies, from 1620 to 1692; Graduates of Harvard College to 1662; Members of the Ancient and Honourable Artillery Company to 1662; Freemen Admitted to the Massachusetts Colony from 1630 to 1662; With Many Other of
2 CONC  the Early Inhabitants of New-England and Long-I Page: 55, Thomas Chambers Year 1639. Publication Code: 1936. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Richardine and Thomas Curtis;
2 CONT # Thomas Curtis of Scituate & York ch. 7 Nov 1619; 
2 CONT #Richard Curtis of Scituate ch abt. 1621; 
2 CONT #Elizabeth Curtis of York (m. Richard Banks/Bankes); 
2 CONT #William Cutis ch 1626 (died young); 
2 CONT #William Curtis of Scituate ch 29 Apr 1627; 
2 CONT #Stephen or Steven Curtis ch 5 Dec. 1629 (bur.  16 Sep 1630); and 
2 CONT #John Curtis ch 13 May 1632. 
2 CONT
2 CONT References for Baptism of Thomas Curtis: 
2 CONT 1. BAPTISM: Kent, England, Tyler Index to parish Records, 1538-1874 Image 22 of 124, p.21: "Worth 1619 Baptisms: 1 Nov " (1619) Thomas, s of Thomas Curtes." 
2 CONT NOTE: Worth used to be called Worde in Old English,
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. BAPTISM: Bishop's Transcripts, Worth, Kent, England DCB/BT1/267 Item 2 Roll 63. [I viewed the record in person at the Canterbury Cathedral Arichives, and checked each with their "handwriting expert" to be sure I was reading the
2 CONC  Old English writing correctly. She varified each record I found for the Curtis family. Nancy] BAPTISM: B.T., Worth, Kent, England (from film at Canterbury Cathedral) 1619 Nov 7 Thomas Curtis sonne of Thomas Curtis. Copy from film
2 CONC . [NOTE: 2nd or 7th hard to read - unsure]
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT The Will of Mistris Richarden Chambers Widdow of Scittuate was proved at Plymouth, 29 October, 1673.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Legacies in the will included:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT *     To Abigal Curtice, wife of my son Thomas Curtice, all my wearing clothes  
2 CONT *     To Elizabeth Curtice, daughter of my son Thomas Curtice aforesaid, 10 [English pounds] in money, goods or cattle  
2 CONT *     and whereas my husband Thomas Chambers Deceased; a Day or Two before hee Died; did manifest and declare before Leister Torrey and Sarah the wife of Abraham Suttliffe; and in my hearing, that it was his will that his son-in-l
2 CONC aw John Curtice should have his house and land both upland and marshland lying and being in Scittuate and Marshfield, Immediately after my Death...  
2 CONT *     all the Rest of my estate; my Debts and legacyes and Charges of funerall being Deducted, I Give unto John Curtis my son aforesaid whom I appoint to be the sole Executor.  
2 CONT * Witnesses to the will were Thomas Kinge, Elisha Besbey and Abraham Suttliffe. The inventory, taken 27 October, 1673, by Thomas Kinge, Richard Curtice, and Abraham Suttliffe, was exhibited in court, and sworn to 29 October, 1673,
2 CONC  by John Curtis. The total was 91 pounds, 14 shillings. Ne real estate was mentioned.[1]  
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
