1 OCCU Farmer - Overland Farm (leasee) in Ash
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Thomas Curtis''' of Ash-juxta-Sandwich (juxta means 'next to' as there are other Ash villages in Kent and other counties), Kent. Thomas was buried 11 Dec. 1631 in St. Nicholas, Ash Parish church, Kent, England.''
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married:
2 CONT #1  Bennett Lott - License 22 Dec 1612 St. Peter and St. Paul, Temple Ewell, Kent, England.
2 CONT #2  Richardene about 1617/1618 England. (Her maiden name and residence is unknown - marriage not found. Richardine married secondly Thomas Chambers in the Parish Church of St. Nicholas, in Ash, Kent, England
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Chambers was a dissenter from the Church of England so they fled, with her children by Thomas Curtis, to  Scituate (south Scituate later split off as Norwell), Massachusetts in 1638.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 children with spouse #1 Bennett include:
2 CONT # Nicholas Curtis (c.1613, probably in Worth, Kent, England)
2 CONT # John Curtis (bap. 2 Sept. 1615 Worth, Kent, England, buried 12 Nov. 1616)
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 children with spouse #2 Richardene include:
2 CONT #Thomas Curtis (ca 1619 Worth, Kent, d. 25 Jan 1691/92 New Calendar, probably in Maine, USA)
2 CONT #Richard Curtis (ca 1620-15 Oct 1693)
2 CONT #Elizabeth Curtis (bap. 1 Aug 1624 Worth, married Richard Banks/Bankes)
2 CONT # William Curtis (ca 1626 - died young)
2 CONT #William Curtis (bap. 29 Apr 1627 Ash, d. c.1700 Scituate, Massachusetts)
2 CONT #Stephen/Steven Curtis (bap. 5 Dec. 1629 Ash, bur. 16 Sep 1630 Ash, Kent, England)
2 CONT #John Curtis (bap. 13 May 1632 Ash, Kent, England-bef Jun 1680 Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts, USA)
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Curtis b. c 1587-1591 is the beginning of his line, as registered with the Curtis-Curtiss Family Society.  See  www.curtis-curtiss.org   His parents are unknown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: Thomas Curtis (above) of Ash, Kent is the progenitor of the Kent line to Scituate, Massachusetts and York, Maine.  It is a completely different line than that from Nazeing/Nazing, Essex, England. Both of these lines are in t
2 CONC he Curtis-Curtiss Family Society database.
2 CONT
2 CONT Findmypast.co.uk, viewed 2018, had two possible Baptisms for Thomas Curtis around the time we have for   his birth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. 1582 Kent, Canterbury Archdeaconry Baptisms  Location: Hythe, St. Leonard, Kent, England. "Curtis  Thomas ye sonne (son) of Thomas Curtis was baptized ye 6 April 1582."  Transcript. Archive reference: CCA/U3/282/1/A/1  https:/
2 CONC /www.findmypast.com/transcript?id=GBPRS%2FCANT3%2FBAP%2F000600
2 CONT *   2. 1596 Kent Baptisms, Tenterden, Kent England, St. Mildred [He would have been only 16 when he married -   not likely but... ]  Tenterden St Mildred baptisms 1544-1860. Parish baptisms. Connect?  Not knowing his parents or si
2 CONC blings makes it impossible to know if we have correct Thomas Curtis.
2 CONT *   BURIAL: Findmypast  lists "Thomas Curtis 1630 Record set: Canterbury Archdeaconry Burials,    Ash, St. Nicholas, England. A second entry for Thomas Curtis died (Event:) 1631 England Deaths &  Burials 1538-1991  Ash, Parish Ken
2 CONC t, England. "Thomas Curtis 1574-1631 LT55-P7M."  It says: "No   similar records were found."   NOTE: St. Nicholas Parish Church of Ash website 2021: www.s8nicholas.org.uk/index.html [Yes,that's s8 not st.] I have photos of the chu
2 CONC rch. Click on History to read more, including "Family History Enquiries" which states  "Parish registers, with baptisms, marriages and burials, have been transferrred to Canterbury Cathedral Archives."   Added Nov 17, 2023 by Nanc
2 CONC y Purchase.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Death of Thomas Curtis of Ash-next-Sandwich, Kent, England sources: 
2 CONT *BURIAL: "England Deaths and Burials, 1538-1991," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:JD4R-9YX : 10 February 2018), Thomas Curtis, Householder Burial Date: 11 Dec 1631;  citing Ash Parish, Kent, England
2 CONC , index based upon data collected by the Genealogical Society of Utah, Salt Lake City; FHL microfilm 1,736,522. Index online 2018 at familysearch.org (no actual images). 
2 CONT *BURIAL, Canterbury Burials Transcription from findmypast.co.uk obtained Dec. 2015: "Thomas Curtis Death year: 1630 Burial date 11 Dec. 1631 Burial Place: Ash, St. Nicholas, Kent, England. Canterbury Cathedral Archives 1561-1640 R
2 CONC ecord set: Kent, Canterbury Archdeaconry burials 1538-1988. Copy Actual image shows Burials 1630: " September William Curtis fonne (son) Thomas Curtis 16." Copy 
2 CONT *Also: "Thomas Cirrtis buried 11 Dec. 1631 Subc [Subdeanery? NRP] at Canterbury." 
2 CONT *Also: "Robert Curtis Male Burial date 20 Oct 1684 Burial placer: Ash Parish, Kent, England. Connect?  "England Deaths and Burials, 1538-1991," database, FamilySearc (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1: JD4R-72J : 10 February
2 CONC  2018), Robert Curtis, burial 20 Oct 1684; citing Ash Parish, Kent, England, index based upon data collected by the Genealogical Society of Utah, Salt Lake City; FHL microfilm 1,736,522. 
2 CONT *Also: "England Deaths and Burials, 1538-1991," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:JZ21-JYR : 10 February 2018), Richard Curtis, burial 03 Sep 1619; citing , index based upon  data collected by the Gen
2 CONC ealogical Society of Utah, Salt Lake City; FHL microfilm 1,736,929. Connect? 
2 CONT *BURIAL, Kent, Canterbury Archdeaconry Burials 1538-1988 on Findmypast.co.uk Again viewed May 2016.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disambiguation 
2 CONT
2 CONT Not the same as:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) "The Great Migration Begins, Immigrants to New England 1620-1633," by Robert Charles Anderson (Great Migration Study Project, NEHGS, Boston, 1995) 3:2090.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage to Mary CAMP: (1) Change Date: 22 Mar 2007 at 01:00:00
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Mary Camp 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT #  William Curtis c: 12 Nov 1592 in Nazeing, Essex, England
2 CONT #  Thomas Curtis (Curtice) b: in , England
2 CONT #  Katharine Curtis
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Richardene  first married Thomas Curtis, secondly to  '''Thomas Chambers'''. Thomas Chambers emigrated to Scituate with his wife Richardene, widow of Thomas Curtis, and his step children (children of Thomas and Richardene Curtis).
2 CONC  Thomas Chambers bought land in York, Maine, but his residence was in Scituate, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richardene's estate was settled 29 Oct 1673.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From Genealogical Dictionary of Maine and New Hampshire page 135:
2 CONT
2 CONT >CHAMBERS, Thomas, brought the Curtis family from Kent to Scituate, having m. 25 May 1632 in Ash-juxta-Sandwich, their mo., Richardene, her will at Plymouth 18 Nov. 1672?29 Oct. 1673. He is almost continually ment. in Scituate rec
2 CONC ords Dec. 1638?July 1666, but in 1642 had come to York to buy the land on which Thomas Curtis and Richard Banks lived.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~barbpretz/ps03/ps03_415.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT “Thomas Chambers left his house and property to John Curtis. He was just a small baby when his parents married and Thomas Chambers brought him up and was fond of him as the will shows. Richardene and Thomas Chambers had no childre
2 CONC n.”1529
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
