2 NOTE GRATITUDE TO WILLIAM L. GRANT WHO DEEDED THIS PROPERTY
3 CONT TO THE ASSOCIATION FOR THE PRESERVATION OF HISTORIC LANDMARKS
3 CONT IN YORK. THIS ASSOCIATION WILL PROTECT THE MONUMENT IN MEMORY
3 CONT OF THE WORST INDIAN ATTACK IN AMERICAN HISTORY.
2 NOTE Photo of monument taken by Barbara Fleming in August, 1997 in York, Maine (on file):
3 CONT “Near this spot
3 CONT are interred the remains of the victims
3 CONT of one of the worst massacres of colonial days,
3 CONT on Candlemas Day 1691-2,
3 CONT In the dawn of a January monring, Abenaki Indians
3 CONT attacked the settlement of York,
3 CONT burning the houses and killing or capturing
3 CONT 300 of its inhabitants.
3 CONT About 40 were killed, the rest marched
3 CONT to Canada, many dying on the way.
3 CONT Erected to the memory of these hardy pioneers
3 CONT by the Society
3 CONT for the Preservation of Historic Landmarks.” 
3 CONT
