1 NAME Elizabeth /Curtis/
2 GIVN Elizabeth
2 SURN Curtis
2 _MARNM Banks
2 NICK Bankes
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE AUG 1624
2 ADDR
3 CITY Ash-Juxta-Sandwich
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 1667
2 ADDR
3 STAE Massachusetts Bay Colony
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Elizabeth Curtis==
2 CONT * Born: 1624, York, York, Maine, British American Colonies 657
2 CONT * Died: ?
2 CONT * Parents: Thomas Curtis (d 1631) & Richardene
2 CONT
2 CONT Ca 1644 in England, Elizabeth married Richard Banks, his 2nd wife.  Born ca 1607, Richard died on 15 Jan 1690/1 in York, York Co., ME, in the Raid on York.  Richard, of Alkham, Kent married Joan Harrison 1st & Elizabeth Alcock 2nd
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include:
2 CONT # Elizabeth Bankes (ca 1645-aft 1709).  Married 1) Richard Blackmore 2) Jacob Bumpas
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT HIST: Richard Banks (3), "of Scituate Row," York , (see Preble), presumably brother of Samuel (4); he and Thomas Curtis sharing the lot of Thomas Chambers; he had taken the freeman's oath at Scituate, Mass., in same list as Preble
2 CONC . York witness Mar.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1642-3. Godfrey's Council 1651-2. Prominent in town, Church and probate business, often selectman, 1653-1680, Commissioner t.e.s.c. under Mass. 1669, 72, 79, repeatedly grand juror, overseer of county prison 1673. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Apparently victim of York massacre, administration 28 Nov. 1693, granted to son Joseph. Lists 24, 25, 33, 273-7.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married first about 1644 Elizabeth Curtis, bapt. Aug. 1624 in Ash, Kent, daughter of Thomas and Richardine, and step-daughter of Thomas Chambers (2); he married 2d, Elizabeth Alcock (1), '''living in 1698'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://cybergata.com/roots/7942.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth (Curtis) Banks, in Scituate, Mass. Elizabeth was the daughter of ______ Curtis & Richarden ______, and the sister of William, Richard, Thomas and John Curtis. She was born about 1640 and died after 1687. She was a widow 
2 CONC before 1666, after her first husband, named Banks who was perhaps a brother of Richard Banks. She married as her second husband, 17 Jul 1666, William Blackmore. '''(SIC: this was her daughter, Elizabeth Banks)'''  Her third ('''SI
2 CONC C: second''')  husband was Jacob Bumpus, son of Edward and Hannah Bumpas, on 24 Jan 1677. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ~Three Blackmore Genealogies, p. 3
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/m/o/r/Steven-Morrow-Ma/GENE3-0001.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Although dates listed came from two files, it remains questionable as to the accuracy.  It is possible that Elizabeth Curtis ( Richards 2nd wife) died in 1667 NOT Elizabeth Alcock.  Richard may have married Elizabeth Alcock AFTER 
2 CONC 1667 not before. Records indicate that following Richards death, that his WIFE and TWO sons settled his estate. This, of course, would not have been posssible if she died in 1667. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * Curtis, Harold Everdell, ''Descendants of Thomas (1), Richard (1) and William (1) Curtis of Scituate, Mass. - 163''8 -- Part 1: Introduction, References, Indexes -- Part 2: Descendants of Thomas & Richard Curtis Through Eight Ge
2 CONC nerations --Part 3: Descendants of William Curtis Through the First Six Generations -- Part 4: Descendants of William Curtis - The Seventh & Eighth Generations, v 2, Henry #16, p. 1. (Curtis Society Source)
