1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Willam-Curtis-of-Salem/6000000190696583822 
2 CONT Not the husband of https://www.geni.com/people/Alice-Curtis/6000000017286957798
2 CONT Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/William-Curtis-died-young/6000000003938473838?through=6000000036859851101
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===William Curtis
2 CONT * Born about 1631 Ash, Kent, England or 
2 CONT ** ALT:  Christening, 29 April 1627 in Ash-juxta-Sandwich, Kent, England
2 CONT * Died about 1702 in Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts, New England
2 CONT * Son of Thomas Curtis and Richardene (Unknown) Chambers
2 CONT * Brother of John Curtis, Thomas Curtis, Richard Curtis, Elizabeth (Curtis) Banks and Stephen Curtis
2 CONT * Husband of Unknown (Unknown) Curtis — married [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT * Father of Joseph Curtis, Benjamin Curtis Sr, William Curtis, John Curtis, Miriam Curtis, Mehitable Curtis, Stephen Curtis, Sarah Curtis and Samuel Curtis
2 CONT * Occupation: Farmer.
2 CONT * Residence: Scituate, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT The father of the children attached is William Curtis, son of Thomas Curtis (c 1587-1631) and Richardene, according to the Curtis/s Family Society database,[1] not William Curtis, son of William Curtis (1592-1672) and Sarah Elliot
2 CONC , who died in 1634.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Curtis-1110
2 CONT ''Profile Last modified 2 Mar 2024 • Created 8 Jul 2011''
2 CONT
2 CONT William Curtis was born in Ash-next-Sandwich, Kent, England,  son of Thomas Curtis and Richardene.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT >it is unclear if he was the second William of the same name, or if there was an error in vital records.  “William Curtis bapt. 29 April 1627, Ash-next-Sandwich[6], named in a burial record in Ash, 16 September 1630,[10] but this 
2 CONC was likely a clerical mistake and it was Stephen who was buried then.” <BR>
2 CONT
2 CONT >”An interesting correction - Stephen previously had the burial date in 1630. It's actually for William, which makes it unlikely that the William who immigrated was baptized on 29 April 1627, which appears to be the current assump
2 CONC tion.”
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT William is on the 1643 "Able to Bear Arms" list next to Richard Curtis, both of Scituate.[3] His farm was on North river, next south of the Wanton farm.”[4] William was also on the list of “allowed and approved inhabitants” who re
2 CONC ceived common lands by the joint committee of the Court and Town in 1673.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Land Records
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1724, his land was divided among his children, Joseph Curtis (eldest son), Benjamin Curtis, William Curtis, John Curtis, Stephen Curtis, Samuel Curtis, Miriam Curtis, Mehitabel Curtis, and Sarah Curtis all of Scituate.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT The births of William's children are listed in the Scituate vital records, no mention of his wife is made. It is sometimes mentioned that a Sarah Moore, might be his wife, but proof is lacking. His first child, Deborah, is only re
2 CONC corded in the Scituate Second Church baptisms.
2 CONT
2 CONT # Deborah Curtis, bap. 18 May 1662.[7]
2 CONT # Joseph Curtis, s. William, b. May 1664,[8], bap. 26 June 1664, Scituate,[7] m. Rebecca ______
2 CONT # Benjamin Curtis, s. William, b. January 1666/7,[8], bap. 14 April 1667,[9], m. Mary Silvester (b. 24 Dec 1666 Scituate)
2 CONT # William Curtis, s. William b. January 1668/9,[8], bap. 20 June 1669,[9] d. 25 Mar. 1738 Scituate, bur. South Parish Cem., Norwell
2 CONT # John Curtis, s. William, b. February 1670/1[8], m. 4 Mar. 1707/8 Scituate, Experience Palmer (b. 31 Mar. 1679 Scituate)
2 CONT # Miriam, d. William, b. April 1673[8]
2 CONT # Mehetable Curtis d. William b. December 1675,[8] Mehittabell Curtice, d. William, bap. 23 March 1677.[10]
2 CONT # Stephen Curtis, s. William b. September 1677,[8] bap. 1 December 1678,[11] d. 29 Mar. 1758 Scituate, bur. South Parish Cem., Norwell
2 CONT # Sarah Curtis, d. William, b. August 1679,[8] Sara Curtice, d. William, bap. 5 September 1680,[12] m. 30 Aug. 1705 Scituate, William Cook (Researcher's Note: According to Scituate probate records, in 1744, Sarah Curtis, sister to
2 CONC  Samuel, and Miriam, is non-comp mentis.) Her last name is not Cook or Cock.[13]
2 CONT # Samuell Curtis, s. William b. June 1681,[8] Samuell Curtice, s. William, bap. 29 November 1685,[14] m. 11 September 1707 Scituate, Anna Barstow (b. 26 June 1681 Scituate, d. 20 Dec. 1746 Scituate), d. 16 December 1747 Scituate, 
2 CONC bur. South Parish Cem., Norwell
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT The last record of William alive was when he and '''Sarah''', relinquishing her dower rights, sold two separate pieces of land in Scituate on 12 March 1702/3.[15]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.geni.com/people/Nancy-Purchase/6000000016793029569
2 CONT
2 CONT I have that William 1627-1703 married Sarah (_?_) and they had 9 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT The History of Scituate (LDS Film #0369741), Samuel Deane, pub. J. Loring, Boston, 1831, p118-121 and family sketches p251-254, 13,18, 22, & 152-6: "William (brother of Richard), bore arms in Scituate 1643. His farm on North River
2 CONC , next south of the Wanton farm. His children were Joseph born 1664, Benjamin 1666, William 1668, John 1670, Miriam 1673, Mehitabel 1675, Stephen 1677, Sarah 1769, Samuel 1681."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''William Curtis & ?Deborah? married  by 1664, ca 1660; Scituate'''
2 CONT '''William Curtis & _?_, b. 1696; Scituate 
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id=6000000218341147828&size=large}}
2 CONT
