1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==brief biography and family==
2 CONT John Hallet was the head of one of the founding families of Scituate, Plymouth Colony, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born c. 1606 in England.  He married his wife, Anne Tucker, on May 6, 1629 in Allington, Dorset, England.  Their only child, Lydia Hallet Curtis, was born in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family arrived in Scituate in 1638.  Lydia married Richard Curtis there in 1649. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John died on December 12, 1673 in Scituate.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==sources==
2 CONT * "Anne Tucker & John Hallet."  ''England Marriages, 1538–1973'',  Indexing Project (Batch) Number: M39139-8, System Origin: England-VR, GS Film number: 599466, Reference ID: 2:3W25F03.  Hosted by MyHeritage.  Accessed September 1
2 CONC 5, 2016.
2 CONT * "[http://www.scituatehistoricalsociety.org/families/HalletJohn.htm John Hallet]."  Scituate Historical Society.  Accessed September 8, 2011.
2 CONT
