1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nathaniel/3p Brooks was born in Aug 1693 at Scituate, Massachusetts.1 In 1717 he purchased lands of Michael Wanton, the Quaker teacher, and built upon them a house still standing on Main Street, Norwell, in 1936. D
2 CONC eane described the location, in 1831, as "a half mile west of Hoop-pole hill, where the fifth Nathaniel Brooks now resides."
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1723 Nathaniel bought another property in South Scituate (now Norwell), about which descendant Steve Ivas writes in Dec 1999, "My son, who is 11½, goes to school on a property (White Oak Plain) that Nathaniel Brooks the 2nd (of
2 CONC  seven) purchased in 1723. It stayed in the family until the 1930s, when it was transferred to the Town by William Penn Brooks, president of the University of Massachusetts."3,4,5 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel married, 27 Nov 1717 at Scituate, Mary Taylor of S., daughter of William Taylor, with whom he had 9 children.6 William Taylor willed his York County, ME farm, 1748, to his three daughters. The same year, Mary Brooks (w. 
2 CONC of Nathl.), Wm. Brooks and Mercy Wright, spinster, all of Scituate, were deeded as heirs of our father William Taylor, who formerly lived in Arundel, Maine.7        Nathaniel Brooks died 14 Jan 1764 (g.s.) at age 70.8,9 Buried in 
2 CONC First (South) Parish Cemetery, Norwell (formerly South Scituate).8,9 Mary's death is unrecorded.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Nathaniel and Mary (Taylor) Brooks, born in Scituate: Taylor 1718, Noah 1720, Nathaniel bp 1722, Nathaniel 1723, Lydia 1726, Mary 1727, Michael 1729, Mercy 1731, Simeon 1733, Stephen 1737.72
2 CONT
