1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Clark-26805
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LHL5-D58
2 CONT >>This Thomas Clark was previously attached as a child of early New England immigrants Thomas Clarke of Westhorpe, Suffolk, England and later Portsmouth, RI and Susanna Ring. However, there is no proof that the couple had a child 
2 CONC Thomas and in the primary sources found for the couple and in the genealogical works about them, no son Thomas appears. This profile has been detached from those parents. Nor was he known to be a son of another early immigrant Tho
2 CONC mas Clarke of Newport, RI (c. 1605-1684) who apparently never married and had no children and in his will bequeathed only to his brothers and their children.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Not a known child of https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Clark-of-the-Plymouth-Colony/6000000003593247117?through=6000000042844819881
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://trees.wmgs.org/getperson.php?personID=I229&tree=Schirado
2 CONT
2 CONT From Deane’s History of Scituate:
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Thomas Clark was in Scituate 1674. He came hither from Plymouth, and was probably the son or grandson of Thomas Clark, the mate of the May-flower in 1620. His farm is Scituate was on the west of Walnut tree hill, (a half mile we
2 CONC st of late Judge William Cushing's mansion), and adjoining that of Cornet Buck.”
2 CONT
2 CONT It’s not clear to whom Deane referred by “Thomas Clark, mate of the May-flower.” Few of the Mayflower crew members’ names are known, and none of those were named Thomas Clark.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sometime after the birth of his children, Thomas moved to Rochester, Massachusetts, then to Coventry, Connecticut. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of birth have also been (erroneously?) reported to be circa 1651 (including specifically 1650) at Scituate, Plymouth County, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Citations 
2 CONT *"Massachusetts, Town Clerk, Vital and Town Records, 1626-2001," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FHHB-2RM : 5 November 2017), Thomas Clarke and Martha Curtis, 02 Jan 1676; citing Marriag
2 CONC e, Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts, United States, , town clerk offices, Massachusetts; FHL microfilm 423,512.
2 CONT * https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Thomas_Clark_%2820%29  Whittemore, H. Genealogical guide to the early settlers of America: with a brief history of those of the first generation and references to the various local histories,
2 CONC  and other sources of informatio, pg. 90. “THOMAS CLARK, of Plymouth, came in the "Ann" 1623, married Susanna, daughter of widow Mary Ring, and had Andrew, James, Susanna, William, John and Nathaniel. He was a representative 1651-
2 CONC 5. He married second wife 1664, widow Alice Nichols, daughter of Richard Hallett, lived in 1670, at Harwich, where he had a third wife, Elizabeth Crow, and died March 24, 1697, aged 92.”
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT <references />* <span id='Dimock'></span>Dimock, Susan Whitney. ''[[Space:Records ofthe Town and Churches in Coventry, Connecticut, 1711-1844|Records of the Town and Churches in Coventry, Connecticut, 1711-1844]]'' (Baker &Taylor 
2 CONC Co., New York, 1897) [https://archive.org/details/birthsmarriagesb00dimo/page/177 Page 177]
2 CONT * The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, "Pedigree Resource File," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/2:2:34QN-5WX : accessed 2016-07-10), entry for Thomas /Clark/ *.
2 CONT *"Massachusetts, Town Clerk, Vital and Town Records, 1626-2001," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FHHB-2RM : 13 July 2016), Thomas Clarke and Martha Curtis, 02 Jan 1676; citing Marriage, 
2 CONC Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts, United States, , town clerk offices, Massachusetts; FHL microfilm 423,512.
2 CONT
2 CONT *Marriage: Thomas Clark & Martha Curtis - m. 11 or 2 Jan 1676 ::http://dunhamwilcox.net/ma/scituate_marr.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://www.ancestry.com/genealogy/records/thomas-clark_22426579
