1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the daughter of https://www.geni.com/people/Robert-Cook/6000000012582721963?through=6000000012583294643
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cocke-1217
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was born in 1676. She was the daughter of William Cocke and Mary Jenkins.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Thomas Curtis on 6 March 1695 in Scituate.[1] Son of Richard Curtis and Ann Hallet.  
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children[3]:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Deborah Curtis, b. 17 February 1697
2 CONT # Ruth Curtis, b. 19 April 1699 d.y.
2 CONT # Mary Curtis, b. 6 March 1701/02
2 CONT # Thomas Curtis, b. 5 March 1703/04
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1712, her daughters, Deborah and Mary are mentioned in her father's will.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 1 May 1712, her husband Thomas Curtice of Scituate is appointed guardian of the estate that her father had passed down to her, to her son Thomas, who is nine years old.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married his second wife, Mary Gilford on 19 September 1711 in Scituate.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT # Many trees online have her last name as Cooke. The transcription of her last name on her marriage record is Cooke, however, when you look at the original document, it is not a clear name. The second "o" in the last name is uncle
2 CONC ar. More documents are needed to argue the last name.
2 CONT # William Cocke did have a daughter named Mary who married Thomas Curtis. She was deceased at the time of his death. Her daughters, Deborah and Mary Curtiss are mentioned in his will
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT # https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cocke-1217 Cites 
2 CONT ##"Massachusetts, Town Clerk, Vital and Town Records, 1626-2001," database with images, FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FHH1-WH7 : 20 May 2022), Mary Cook in entry for Thomas Curtis, 6 Mar 1695; citing Ma
2 CONC rriage, Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America, Massachusetts Secretary of the Commonwealth, Boston; FHL microfilm 007009271.
2 CONT ## "Massachusetts, Plymouth County, Probate Records, 1633-1967," images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-L97D-ZF7G : 20 May 2014), Probate records 1708-1717 and 1817-1861 vol 3-3P > image 84 of 710; Stat
2 CONC e Archives, Boston.
2 CONT ##"Massachusetts, Plymouth County, Probate Records, 1633-1967," images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QS7-997D-ZF3Q : 20 May 2014), Probate records 1708-1717 and 1817-1861 vol 3-3P > image 87-88 of 710; St
2 CONC ate Archives, Boston.
