2 CONT ==concerns==
2 CONT '''not a husband of https://www.geni.com/people/Jane-Hand/6000000003747476954 or https://www.geni.com/people/Rebecca-Bushnell/6000000000181160708
2 CONT
2 CONT ==comments==
2 CONT Given name has also been reported to be '''Stephan'''.
2 CONT
2 CONT Date and place of birth have also been (erroneously?) reported to be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * between 1634 and 1635 at Tonbridge, Kent, England (possibly reported at FamilySearch, conflicts with his Find A Grave memorial)
2 CONT * October 15, 1637 at Sevenoaks, Kent, England (unattested, conflicts with his Find A Grave memorial)
2 CONT * 1648 at Tonbridge, Kent, England (unattested, conflicts with his Find A Grave memorial)
2 CONT * circa 1658 at East Hampton, Suffolk County, New York (possibly reported at FamilySearch, conflicts with his Find A Grave memorial)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT * FamilySearch AFN HRBS-GT
2 CONT * FamilySearch AFN 1LB5-0T5
2 CONT
2 CONT ==content to clean up==
2 CONT It must have been Stephen Hand for whom Stephen Hand's Path was named.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Nov. 3, 1668, he granted the Town of East Hampton leave to put a highway through his woodland, 12 feet wide, "only to drive carts and oxen in yoake & to ride & lead a horse through; not to drive cattle through out of yoake".
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen  was Constable 1674 and 1680 and in 1683 was chosen one of a committee to join Southampton in selecting a representative for the First Colonial Assembly under Governor Dongan.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT A HAND FAMILY - by Harriet Woodbury Hodge, C.G. Library of Congress Catalog Card Number: 81-82589 Stephen Hand's will, written 17 May 1688 and probated 2 May 1693, mentions his wife (unnamed), sons Stephen (eldest), Joseph (living
2 CONC , but apparently not at East Hampton in 1688), and Samuel (youngest) to have the homestead after wife's decease or remarriage: and five unnamed daus, all under age eighteen.  Widow Rebecca Hand, administratrix in 1693, [VV-pp. 76-
2 CONC 78 
2 CONT
2 CONT * Children by first wife Sarah- 1) STEPHEN, b. abt. 1661; 2) JOSPEH, b. a bt. 1664; 
2 CONT
2 CONT * By second wife Rebecca - 3) SAMUEL, b. abt. 1667; 4)probably ALICE, m. 26 Nov. 1690 at Saybrook, CT, M, WILLIAM SHIPMAN; 5) REBECC A, m. 20 July 1694 at Guilford, CT M, JOHN MEIGS; 6) ABIGAIL, of Guilford, CT, "daughter of Steph
2 CONC en" m. JACOB GRISWOLD, "last" Nov. 1696, [VI; and two other daughters, born after 1670.
2 CONT
