2 CONT * Source: [http://www.ourdeadrelatives.com/wc01_077.html Our Dead Relatives]
2 CONT
2 CONT Photo ref.: "Hands Creek Beach, East Hampton #1, oil painting by Joseph Palazzolo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial Place, ref.: Find A Grave Memorial# 77834317 < http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=77834317 >
2 CONT
2 CONT Constable of East Hampton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Steven Hand, Senr., died testate with a will dated May 17, 1688, which was proved at Brookhaven on May 2, 1693, mentioning his property at Wainscott, Acabonnack, Napeaque, and Montauk. He was the father of three sons, Stephen, Jos
2 CONC eph, and Samuel, and five daughters, and his widow Rebecca served as executor of the estate. His name is perpetuated to this day at East Hampton in Hand's Creek and Stephen Hand's Path.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Constable of East Hampton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Steven Hand, Senr., died testate with a will dated May 17, 1688, which was proved at Brookhaven on May 2, 1693, mentioning his property at Wainscott, Acabonnack, Napeaque, and Montauk.  He was the father of three sons, Stephen, Jo
2 CONC seph, and Samuel, and five daughters, and his widow Rebecca served as executor of the estate.  His name is perpetuated to this day at East Hampton in Hand's Creek and Stephen Hand's Path.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John Hand (1609-1660) of East Hampton, Long Island in Suffolk County, New York, by his wife Alice Gransden Hand (1613-alive in 1670), who were married at Tonbridge, Kent, on Apr. 24, 1634.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandson of [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=135272301 Stephen Hand] of Sundridge in Kent, England, and his wife [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=135272325 Anne], widow Buckland, and als
2 CONC o of [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=135272265 Henry Gransden], gentleman, of Tonbridge in Kent, England, and his wife [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=135272154 Alice Harris Gransden].
2 CONT
2 CONT Steven Hand's first wife [Sarah?] died before the 1684 will of her father [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=136840022 John Stretton], and sometime between 1684 and 1686 he married his sister-in-law, Rebecca St
2 CONC retton Bushnell.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [[http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=77834130 Elizabeth Osborne] (d. 1711) is said by some to have been his daughter.]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=77834317 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 31 2017, 5:50:57 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Constable of East Hampton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Steven Hand, Senr., died testate with a will dated May 17, 1688, which was proved at Brookhaven on May 2, 1693, mentioning his property at Wainscott, Acabonnack, Napeaque, and Montauk.  He was the father of three sons, Stephen, Jo
2 CONC seph, and Samuel, and five daughters, and his widow Rebecca served as executor of the estate.  His name is perpetuated to this day at East Hampton in Hand's Creek and Stephen Hand's Path.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John Hand (1609-1660) of East Hampton, Long Island in Suffolk County, New York, by his wife Alice Gransden Hand (1613-alive in 1670), who were married at Tonbridge, Kent, on Apr. 24, 1634.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandson of Stephen Hand of Sundridge in Kent, England, and his wife Anne, widow Buckland, and also of Henry Gransden, gentleman, of Tonbridge in Kent, England, and his wife Alice Harris Gransden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Steven Hand's first wife [Sarah?] died before the 1684 will of her father John Stretton, and sometime between 1684 and 1686 he married his sister-in-law, Rebecca Stretton Bushnell.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Elizabeth Osborne (d. 1711) is said by some to have been his daughter.]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
