1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Elizabeth Hand Osborn=
2 CONT * BIRTH 27 Jan 1672
2 CONT * DEATH 16 Nov 1711 (aged 39) East Hampton, Suffolk County, New York, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL South End Cemetery, East Hampton, Suffolk County, New York, USA
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 77834130 Photos by THand
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Hand was born 27 Jan 1672 Easthampton, Suffolk, New York (some say she was born as early as 1668) and died 16 Nov 1711. She married ABT 1689 Daniel Osborne who was born 1665 c at East Hampton, Suffolk, New York . He was 
2 CONC the son of Thomas Osborn and Mary Bond, b. ca 1665, d. Jan. 6, 1712/3, aged 48 yrs., buried in the South end bur. Grd., East Hampton, the inscription reading ‘Daniel Osbond” and the year “1712,”
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Daniel Osbord prob. ca. 1689 and was, prob. daughter of Benjamin Hand & Elizabeth Whittier, b. Jan. 27, 1672, d. Nov. 16, 1711; 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Stephen Hand 1635–1693
2 CONT Sarah Bancroft Stratton Hand 1647–1684
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Daniel Osbond unknown–1713
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Stephen Hand 1661–1740
2 CONT Samuel Hand 1672–1735
2 CONT Rebecca Hand Meigs 1674–1719
2 CONT Abigail Hand Griswold 1676–1747
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children''' 
2 CONT Mary Osborn 1691–1706
2 CONT Daniel Osborn 1692–1757
2 CONT Abigail Osborn Baker 1694–1748
2 CONT Elizabeth Osborn 1696–1711
2 CONT Thomas Osborn 1700–1753
2 CONT Rebecca Osborn 1703–1720
2 CONT Mary Osborne Ogden 1706–1758
2 CONT Daniel Osborn 1713–1779
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Decendant Details==
2 CONT Children (by 1st wife):
2 CONT 1.Mary, b. ca. 1690, d. May 7, 1706, aged abt. 15 yrs.
2 CONT 2.Daniel, b. ca. 1692, d. May 17, 1757, in 65th yr., m. June 10, 1713, at East Hampton Elizabeth Austin.
2 CONT 3.Abigail, b. ca. 1694, d. Oct. 1768, m. at East Hampton Sept. 7, 1714, Daniel Baker, b. Aug. 1, 1694, d. Mar. 16, 1740. His will dated Mar. 15, 1740, proved aug. 26, 1740, names wife Abigail and brother Thomas Osborn, etc. 
2 CONT 4.Elizabeth, b. ca. 1696, d. Sept. 20, 1711, aged abt. 15 yrs.
2 CONT 5.A child b. prob. ca. 1698, d. Feb 7, 1699/1700.
2 CONT 6.Thomas, b. Nov. 24, 1700, bp. At east Hampton Dec. 1, 1700, d. Nov. 18, 1753, m. Hester Schellinger.
2 CONT 7.Rebecca, bp. Jan. 15, 1702/3, at east Hampton, d. Nov. 1, 1720, aged abt. 18 yrs.
2 CONT 8.Mary, b. May 22, 1706, bp. May 26, 1706, at East Hampton, d. Apr. 15, 1758, in 53rd yr., m. at East Hampton Oct. 8, 1722, John Ogden of Elizabeth Town, b. Nov. 22, 1700, d. Nov. 15, 1780, in LXXXth yr. both are buried in the Fir
2 CONC st Presbyterian Church Yard, Elizabeth, NJ.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT Said by some to be a daughter of Stephen Hand (1637-1693) of East Hampton, Long Island in Suffolk County, New York. Enough evidence to make this certain is lacking.
2 CONT
2 CONT ALT birth:	Elizabethtown, Union, New Jersey,  daughter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Benjamin-Hand/6000000001781014636?through=6000000000329676287 Benjamin Hand]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==References==
2 CONT [1] http://genforum.com/hand/messages/541.html
2 CONT
2 CONT [2] https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/77834130/elizabeth-osborn
2 CONT
2 CONT [3] Genealogies of New Jersey Families - From the Genealogical Magazine of New Jersey The Thomas Osborn Family - by Richard W. Cook
2 CONT
2 CONT [4] https://archive.org/details/mahlonjohnsonfam00unse Mahlon Johnson family genealogy book with chart as found online at archive.org --- shows this Elizabeth as Hedges ( of Isaac of William) and not as daughter of Stephen Hand..
