1 NAME Jacob /Root/
2 GIVN Jacob
2 SURN Root
2 _MARNM Root
2 NICK Jacob Root
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 2 FEB 1661
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hartford
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 BURI
2 DATE AUG 1731
2 PLAC Hebron, Tolland, Connecticut
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 9 AUG 1731
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hebron
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Moved in 1654 to Northampton, Mass. with his parents and brothers and sisters.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was among the first settlers of Hebron, Conn. where he moved in 1705. He had a farm which remained in the possession of his family for 125 years. Daughter, Ruth, stayed on the farm and died there.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT He was probably the youngest son of Thomas.  He is mentioned in the list of Northampton freeman, Feb 8, 1678. He was among the first settlers of Hebron Conn. Where he removed in 1705 and was one of those chosen to run the (bounds)
2 CONC  between Colchester and Hebron in 1710 as the latter was not incorporated when he moved there.  He had a farm which remained in possession of the family for 125 years.  He died Aug- 9, 1731, ae. a. 70.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Root Genealogical Records 1600-1870; Comprising the General History of the Root and Roots Families in America'', by James Pierce Root, page 106.  < [https://archive.org/details/rootgenealogical00root/page/106/mode/2up Archive.Or
2 CONC g] >
2 CONT
2 CONT He m. Feb. 2, 1680, Mary, dau. of Sampson and Mary (Daniel) Frary of Deerfield, Mass. She was b. July 24, 1662 She d. Feb. 8, 1744.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: (All born in Northampton, Mass.)
2 CONT * 382. I. Joanna, b. Nov. 5, 1681 ; m. Dec. 7, 1703, Samuel Pomeroy of Northampton ; had 3 children, and d. 1725. 
2 CONT * 383. II. Daniel, b. Oft. 2, 1684, f.
2 CONT * 384. III. Jacob, b. June 15, 1687, f. ; d. 1766, ae. 79.
2 CONT * 385. IV. Mary, b. Nov. 24, 1689, f. ; d. Oft. 15, 1735, ae, 45.
2 CONT * 386. V. Margaret, b. Oft. 1691 ; m. (1) June 25, 1727, John Warner, (2) Trumbull ; d. June, 1793, ae. loi, at Marlborough, Ct.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # ''Root Genealogical Records 1600-1870; Comprising the General History of the Root and Roots Families in America'', by James Pierce Root, page 106.  < [https://archive.org/details/rootgenealogical00root/page/106/mode/2up Archive.
2 CONC Org] >
