1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''''''New England families, genealogical and memorial: a record of the ..., Volume 2 edited by William Richard Cutter
2 CONT *http://books.google.com/books?id=1M8UAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA882&lpg=PA882&dq=Thankful+Phelps+Pomeroy+1710&source=bl&ots=QxvCbVFMys&sig=nYlIol-Xoqk8TnQfejl_2FmB28A&hl=en&ei=p32KTdelDYimsQO4_dmcDA&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=3&ved=
2 CONC 0CCIQ6AEwAg#v=onepage&q=Thankful%20Phelps%20Pomeroy%201710&f=false
2 CONT *Pg. 882
2 CONT *  (XX) Samuel Pomeroy, son of Caleb Pomeroy, was born at Northampton, Massachusetts, May 29, 1669. He married (first) 1690, Elizabeth French, of Rehoboth, Massachusetts, daughter of Joseph and Mary (Kingsley) French. He married (
2 CONC second) December 7, 1703. Johanna Root, who was born November 5, 1681, died January 20, 1713, daughter of Jacob and Mary (Frary) Root. He married (third) 1715, Elizabeth Strickland, born January 2, 1685, daughter of Joseph and Eli
2 CONC zabeth (Chapman) Strickland. His third wife survived him. His will was dated in 1746 and proved in December, 1748. 	. . . .  Children by first wife: Samuel French, born 1691; Caleb, May 14, 1693, died young; Elizabeth, September 3
2 CONC 0 1694; Caleb, December 1, 1696, died young; Ebenezer, My 31, 1700. Children by second wife: Joanna, 1704; Hepsibah, 1706; Caleb, mentioned below. Children by the third wife: Mary, July 1, 1716; Joshua, September 9, 1717; Noah, Oc
2 CONC tober 13, 1718; Richard, November 21, 1721, moved to Maine; Elizabeth, February 25, 1723, Simeon, June 5, 1725.
2 CONT **  (XXI) Caleb Pomeroy, son of Samuel Pomeroy, was born at Northampton, Massachusetts, October 2, 1707. He married, November 15, 1733, Thankful Phelps, born 1710, at Northampton, daughter of William  and Thankful (Edwards) Phelps
2 CONC . He was a farmer at Easthampton, but died in Sourthampton. Children: Abner, born September 7, 1734; Elijah, mentioned below; Eleanor, April 11, 1738; Caleb, July 10, 1740; Chloe, November 29, 1741; Joel, 1743, went south; Enos, 1
2 CONC 746; Thankful, 1747; Gershom, 1749, soldier in the revolution; Solomon, baptized January 26, 1752; ''''''Phebe, 1754''''''; Silas.
