3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 DEAT
2 DATE 29 DEC 1755
2 ADDR
3 CITY Sharon
3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Gifford, daughter of Stephen and Hannah Gifford.[1],  was born 14 Jan 1670 in Norwichtown, New London, Connecticut.[1]. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Gifford married on 16 November 1691 in Norwich, New London, Connecticut.[2] to  Samuel Calkins.  He was born in October 1663 in Norwichtown, Connecticut Colony to John Calkins and Sarah Royce.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel and Hannah had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Calkins b 30 March 1693 Norwich, Connecticut; m 1) Katherine Foster, daughter of Daniel Foster 2) 20 June 1743 Elizabeth Curtice[4]
2 CONT # Hannah Calkins b 4 July 1694 Hebron, Connecticut; m 29 July 1714 Hebron Timoty Phelps[4]
2 CONT # Ruth Calkins b 29 September 1695 Hebron, Connecticut; m Hebron, Nathan Stiles[4]
2 CONT # Samuel Calkins b 17 October 1699 Lebanon, Connecticut; m Hebron Damaris Strong[4]
2 CONT # Nathaniel Calkins b August 1701 Lebanon, Connecticut;, died young[4]
2 CONT # Nathaniel Calkins b 17 August 1703 Lebanon, Connecticut;[4]
2 CONT # Stephan Calkins b 4 April 1706 Lebanon, Connecticut;; m 1) Woodbury, Connecticut 15 June 1733 Mary Curtis 2) Elizabeth Heath[4]
2 CONT # Jemina Calkins baptized April 1708 Lebanon, Connecticut;; m Hebron, Connecticut 26 May 1726 Caleb Curtis [4]
2 CONT # Aquila Calkins b 4 June 1711 Lebanon, Connecticut;; m 27 May 1741 Desire Ackley[4]
2 CONT Samuel Caulkins did not die in November 1720 [This is his current death date listed on his Find a Grave Memorial], as sometimes stated, for a Lebanon deed completed in 1739 proves he was living at this point. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT While it is possible that he was the Samuel that died in Sharon, Connecticut on 29 December 1755, this is probably his son, Samuel Calkins, Jr. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Caulkins was a mariner. He first resided in Norwich, where his first three children were born. He moved to Lebanon about 1697, where he later died.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel is buried at the Old Norwichtown Cemetery, Norwich, New London County, Connecticut, USA[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT I can find no definiative proof that Samuel Caulkins/Calkins, Sr. died in Sharon, Connecticut. If he was a mariner as, the Hodge Genealogy asserts, he would live close to the coast in cities such as Norwich or Lebanon, not inland 
2 CONC in Sharon.
2 CONT
2 CONT I believe the death location of Sharon, CT comes from the confusion with his son's death record. I have switched his death location to Lebanon, to match the death location given in the Hodge Genealogy source.
2 CONT
2 CONT Carrie 14 September 2021
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # http://www.angelfire.com/ny/chickened/giffordfamily.html
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Hannah (Gifford) Calkins (1670-1755)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Gifford-163 : accessed 13 November 2025). cites
