2 CONT [[Category:Burial Details Unknown]]
2 CONT [[Category:Old Norwichtown Cemetery, Norwich, Connecticut]]
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biography == Samuel Calkins was born in  October 1663 in Norwichtown, Connecticut Colony to [[Calkins-9|John Calkins]] and  [[Royce-36|Sarah Royce]].≤ref>Family Search. '''Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906'''  [htt
2 CONC ps://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:V2SW-73  Samuell Calkins], 1663.≤/ref>
2 CONT Samuel married  [[Gifford-163|Hannah Gifford]] on 16 November 1691 in Norwich, New London, Connecticut.≤ref>Ancestry. '''U.S., Sons of the American Revolution Membership Applications, 1889-1970'''' [https://www.ancestry.com/discov
2 CONC eryui-content/view/573273:2204 Application for Hugh Hurst Shepard. SAR Membership	46906]. ≤/ref> She was the daughter ofStephen Gifford and Hannah Gore.≤ref> {{Blue|This source makes no reference to death information for Samuel Ca
2 CONC lkins.}}  Kenneth W., '''Calkins Family In America'''], Family Search Books. Calkins Family Association, September 2000, [https://www.familysearch.org/library/books/records/item/566674-calkins-family-in-america?viewer=1&offset=0#p
2 CONC age=15&viewer=picture&o=&n=0&q= page 12],≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel and Hannah had the following children: #[[Calkins-362|John Calkins]] b 30 March 1693 Norwich, Connecticut; m 1) [[Foster-4925|Katherine Foster]], daughter of [[Foster-1031|DanielFoster]] 2) 20 June 1743 [[Curtis-2678|Elizab
2 CONC eth Curtice]]≤ref name=CaulkinsFamily> Sharps, Turney, Mrs.. '''Caulkins Family of Connecticut, Vermont, New  York, Ect.''' Undated. Family Search Books. [https://www.familysearch.org/library/books/records/item/351848-caulkins-fam
2 CONC ily-of-connecticut-vermont-new-york-etc?viewer=1&offset=3#page=5&viewer=picture&o=&n=0&q= page 5 of 41]≤/ref>#[[Calkins-4157|Hannah Calkins]] b 4 July 1694 Hebron, Connecticut; m 29 July 1714 Hebron [[Phelps-243|Timoty Phelps]]≤re
2 CONC f name=CaulkinsFamily />#[[Calkins-377|Ruth Calkins]] b 29 September 1695 Hebron, Connecticut;m Hebron, [[Stiles-1500|Nathan Stiles]]≤ref name=CaulkinsFamily />#[[Calkins-56|Samuel Calkins]] b 17 October 1699 Lebanon, Connecticut;
2 CONC m Hebron [[Strong-344|Damaris Strong]]≤ref name=CaulkinsFamily />#[[Calkins-1536|Nathaniel Calkins]] b August 1701 Lebanon, Connecticut;, died young≤ref name=CaulkinsFamily />#[[Calkins-1537|Nathaniel Calkins]] b 17 August 1703 Le
2 CONC banon, Connecticut;≤ref name=CaulkinsFamily />#[[Calkins-1538|Stephan Calkins]] b 4 April 1706 Lebanon, Connecticut;; m 1) Woodbury, Connecticut 15 June 1733 [[Curtis-4286|Mary Curtis]] 2) [[Heath-2612|Elizabeth Heath]]≤ref name=C
2 CONC aulkinsFamily />#[[Calkins-2502|Jemina Calkins]] baptized April 1708 Lebanon, Connecticut;; m Hebron, Connecticut 26 May 1726 [[Curtice-83|Caleb Curtis]] ≤ref name=CaulkinsFamily />#[[Calkins-2503|Aquila Calkins]] b 4 June 1711 Le
2 CONC banon, Connecticut;; m 27 May 1741 [[Ackley-76|Desire Ackley]]≤ref name=CaulkinsFamily />
2 CONT Samuel Caulkins did not die in November 1720 [This is his current death date listed  on his Find a Grave Memorial], as sometimes stated, fora Lebanon deed completed in 1739 proves he was living at this point. ≤ref name=CaulkinsFam
2 CONC ily />
2 CONT While it is possible that he was the Samuel that died in Sharon, Connecticut on 29 December 1755, this is probably his son, Samuel Calkins, Jr. ≤ref name=CaulkinsFamily />
2 CONT Mr. Caulkins was a mariner.  He first resided in Norwich, where his first three children were born.  He moved to Lebanon about 1697, where he later died.≤ref>Hodge, Orlando John, '''Hodge genealogy from the first of the name in th
2 CONC is country to the present time : with a number of allied families and many historical facts''' (1900 Boston : Rockwell and Churchill Press) [https://archive.org/details/hodgegenealogyfr00hodg/page/803/mode/2up page 391]≤/ref>
2 CONT Samuel is buried at the Old Norwichtown Cemetery, Norwich, New London County, Connecticut, USA≤ref>h Find a Grave,  ''Memorial Page for Samuel Calkins'' (16 Oct 1663–1720), (accessed May 28, 2024),  {{FindAGrave|47838393|sameas=no
2 CONC }}, citing Old Norwichtown Cemetery, Norwich, New London County, Connecticut, USA; Maintained by James Ross Wagner Sr.(contributor 47223993).  Dubious source - This is no headstone photo.No sources  are cited.≤/ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes===I can find no definiative proof that Samuel Caulkins/Calkins, Sr. diedin Sharon, Connecticut.  If he was a mariner as, the Hodge Genealogy asserts, he would live close to the coast in cities such as Norwich orL
2 CONC ebanon, not inland in Sharon.
2 CONT I believe the death location of Sharon, CT comes from the confusion with his son's death record. I have switched his death location to Lebanon, to match the death location given in the Hodge Genealogy source. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Carrie 14 September 2021
2 CONT
