2 CONT https://mathcs.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr23/rr23_220.html#P3855
2 CONT
2 CONT * 48144. Timothy Phelps. Born on 29 Dec 1749 in Hebron, CT.316 Timothy died in Pompey, Onondaga County, New York, on 3 Jul 1830; he was 80. Buried in Pompey Hill Cemetery.
2 CONT * 
2 CONT * Timothy first settled in Hebron. He served in the Revolutionary War, enlisting in Sullivan’s Division with his brother Samuel. He later removed to Pompey, NY.260
2 CONT * 
2 CONT * 1790 Federal Census. Cambridge, Albany County, New York
2 CONT * Roll 6, page 309
2 CONT * Family of Timothy Phelps
2 CONT *     3 males under 16 [3 of William, Azor, Levi, and Timothy]
2 CONT *     1 male 16 and over [Timothy]
2 CONT *     7 females [Persis, Anna, Hannah, Rachel, ?, ?, & ?]
2 CONT * 
2 CONT * 1800 Federal Census. Charlton, Saratoga County, New York
2 CONT * Roll 27, page 1073
2 CONT * Family of Timothy Phelps Jr.
2 CONT *     2 males under 10 [? & ?]
2 CONT *     1 male 10-15 [Timothy Jr, 13]
2 CONT *     1 male 16-25 [Levi, 15]
2 CONT *     1 male 45 and over [Timothy, 50]
2 CONT *     1 female under 10 [?]
2 CONT *     1 female 10-15 [?]
2 CONT *     1 female 16-25 [?]
2 CONT *     1 female 45 and over [Persis, 46]
2 CONT * Timothy is listed in the census right under his father’s name.
2 CONT * 
2 CONT * 1810 Federal Census, Pompey, Onondaga County, New York
2 CONT * Roll 34, page 31
2 CONT * Family of Timothy Phelps
2 CONT *     3 males 16-25
2 CONT *     1 male 45 and over [Timothy, 60]
2 CONT *     1 female 10-15
2 CONT *     1 female 16-25
2 CONT *     1 female 45 and over [Persis, 56]
2 CONT * 
2 CONT * Pompey Hill Cemetery, Pompey, Onondaga County, New York
2 CONT *     Timothy Phelps, d. 3 Jul 1830, æ. 83 years 5 months 29 days
2 CONT *     Persis Phelps, d. 27 Mar 1811, æ. 56 years 9 months 8 days
2 CONT *     Temperance, wife of Timothy Phelps, d. 13 Jun 1880
2 CONT * Ca 1772 Timothy first married Persis Baxter (54851) , daughter of William Baxter (45475) (15 Aug 1725-) & Triphena Taylor. Born on 19 Jun 1754 in Hebron, CT. Persis died in Pompey, Onondaga County, New York, on 27 Mar 1811; she 
2 CONC was 56. Buried in Pompey Hill Cemetery.
2 CONT * Their children include:
2 CONT * 56646i.
2 CONT * Anna Phelps (1773-)
2 CONT * 56647ii.
2 CONT * Hannah Phelps (Died young) (1776-)
2 CONT * 56648iii.
2 CONT * William Phelps (1779-)
2 CONT * 56649iv.
2 CONT * Azor Phelps (30 Jul 1780-20 Jan 1853)
2 CONT * 56650v.
2 CONT * Hannah Christiana Phelps (ca May 1781-1 Jan 1869)
2 CONT * 56651vi.
2 CONT * Rebecca Phelps (11 Oct 1783-26 Nov 1869)
2 CONT * 56652vii.
2 CONT * Timothy Phelps (1787-)
2 CONT * 56653viii.
2 CONT * Levi Phelps (ca Nov 1791-19 Mar 1867)
2 CONT * Aft Mar 1811 Timothy second married Temperance Crocker, daughter of Thomas Crocker (8 Jun 1735-5 Jul 1796) & Mercy Hamblin (15 Nov 1737-1829). Born ca 1757. Temperance died on 8 Jun 1830 in Pompey, Onondaga County, New York. Bur
2 CONC ied in Pompey Hill Cemetery.
2 CONT * 
2 CONT * Temperance first married Levi Chase, second Timothy Phelps as his second wife
2 CONT --------------------
