2 CONT 48146. Samuel Phelps. Born on 22 Apr 1759 in Hebron, CT.316 Samuel died in Fenner, Madison County, New York, on 15 Oct 1826; he was 67.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel and Lydia removed to Fenner, Madison Co, NY. Samuel and his brother Timothy enlisted in the Revolutionary War in Sullivan’s Division and was with Washington when he evacuated New York City. He was quite sick at that time wi
2 CONC th a fever, but not wishing to remain he was helped by Thomas to ride on a horse and so leave with the troop rather than take his chances of remaining behind.260
2 CONT
2 CONT 1790 Federal Census. Hebron, Tolland County, Connecticut Roll 1, page 163 Family of Sam’l Phelps
2 CONT     1 male under 16 [Samuel jr]
2 CONT     1 male 16 and over [Samuel]
2 CONT     2 females [Lydia & Lydia jr]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1810 Federal Census. Smithfield, Madison County, New York Roll 28, page 875 Family of S. Phelps
2 CONT     1 male under 10
2 CONT     1 male 45 and over
2 CONT     2 females 10-15
2 CONT     1 female 16-35
2 CONT     1 female 45 and over On 18 Dec 1785 when Samuel was 26, he married Lydia Porter (38670) , daughter of Dea. Increase Porter (20769) (18 Feb 1722-) & Mary Niles (26 Jun 1726-4 Jun 1764), in Hebron, CT.316 Born on 8 Apr 1761 in H
2 CONC ebron, CT.316 Lydia died in Fenner, Madison County, New York.260
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel and Lydia were second cousins once removed; their common ancestors were Timothy and Mary (Griswold) Phelps. Their children include: 51947i. Samuel Phelps (17 Sep 1786-1886) 51948ii. Lydia Phelps (3 May 1788-) 51949iii. Poll
2 CONC y Phelps (27 Jul 1791-) 51950iv. Asa Phelps (Jun 1793-) 51951v. Myra Phelps (Aug 1796-) 51952vi. Harriet Phelps (Jul 1799-ca 1829) 51953vii. Porter Phelps (Died soon) (Sep 1802-bef 1804) 51954viii. Porter Phelps (4 Apr 1804-20 Sep
2 CONC  1885)
2 CONT --------------------
