2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Ancestor #: A056759
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife 1 Mehitable Andrews
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife 2 Naomi Tredwell
2 CONT
2 CONT Military Service • 
2 CONT 16 October 1780
2 CONT Ballston Spa, Saratoga, New York, United States
2 CONT captured by British Troops, Loyalist Rangers & Mohawks under Maj. Carleton, and taken to Quebec. Released 17 Oct 1782.
2 CONT
2 CONT Extensive history concerning his capture & imprisonment during the Revolutionary War is available in The Hollister Family, pp. 122-125.
2 CONT
2 CONT From "The History of Cattaraugus County, NY", published 1879 by Everts, edited by Franklin Ellis
2 CONT Chapter: Town of Mansfield, pages 455-461:
2 CONT Josiah K. Hollister, a veteran of the Revolutionary war, accompanied by his sons, Samuel L. and Josiah R., Jr., emigrated from Cairo, Green co., NY, to Ovid, Seneca County, settling first at '''Franklinville''', where they remaine
2 CONC d until 1816, when the removed to Great Valley, and in March, 1821, to Mansfield, locating in the eastern part, on log 14. They came to this town with a sled drawn by an ox-team. One mile west of Ellicottville they left the road a
2 CONC nd cut a passage through the woods to the place of settlement, a distance of three miles. A temporary house was built by rolling up logs and covering the same with hemlock-bark. In the autumn a good substantial log house was erect
2 CONC ed, and covered for a few years with the mime material. Help to raise it was procured at Ellicottville, where their nearest neighbors resided for the first two years.
2 CONT
2 CONT During the winter of 1821-22 two men came in and cut five acres of timber on the site of Union Corners. The following spring the Hollister's cleared this up, receiving in payment the ashes obtained by burning the timber and what c
2 CONC rops could be raised upon it the first season. They planted one-half of it to corn, and upon the remainder was sowed oats. The bears, which were very numerous at that time, destroyed most of the corn.
2 CONT
2 CONT The elder Holister, who, during the war of the Revolution, had been a prisoner in Canada for two years, died soon after his settlement in Mansfield. Josiah R., Jr., was a soldier during the war of 1812 and died at the age of eight
2 CONC y-one years. Samuel L. Holister, the elder son, died in 1849, aged sixty-one years. His widow, aged eighty-seven years, still survives, and resided with her son, Mr. Alson Hollister, of Mansfield
