1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Hutchinson--was born in Northampton about 1658 and received a grant
2 CONT
2 CONT in the Ten Allotments (in Lebanon) in December 1697. His first six
2 CONT
2 CONT children were born in Northampton from 1683 thru March 1696, and his
2 CONT
2 CONT seventh child was born in Lebanon in February 1699/1700. He was one of
2 CONT
2 CONT the nine founding members of the Lebanon church on 27 November 1700. he
2 CONT
2 CONT arrival in Lebanon was in 1697, 1698 or 1699. His wife was Hannah Root.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: (LD 1:7; LVR 1:145; LChR 4:4, 22; TAG 23: 122-23; Dunn 233;
2 CONT
2 CONT NhVr1:28)
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Early Settlers of Lebanon, Connecticut" by Robert Charles
2 CONT
2 CONT Anderson, (University of Massachusetts (a thesis) 1983.
