2 CONT (Family of) Timothy Closson - http://www.modistics.com/Family/Details.aspx?tree=93&indid=70258
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy was born either in 1680 or 1681, either at Marshfield or Tiverton, both in Plymouth Colony (see Research Notes). He was the son of Josiah and Mary Closson.[1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Martha Wilbor (1684-abt.1746) on 16 Jun 1702.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was probably less than 30 years old when he passed away after 1704 since his second son Timothy Closson (1705-aft.1774) was born 1705, and before 1708 when his wife had her son Joseph Burgess (1708-1768) with her second husband
2 CONC  Thomas Burgess III (1668-1743).
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Conflicted Birth Dates and Places: Timothy's parents were married in Marshfield, Plymouth Colony, and he may have been born in Marshfield before moving to Tiverton where Timothy's siblings were born: [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT "thy the Son of Josiah Clawson" (possibly named Timothy) "Borne the 5th of January 1680", at Marshfield.
2 CONT Plymouth Colony and Bristol County: In 1685, when the division was made of Plymouth Colony, Bristol County had the towns of Taunton, Rehoboth, Dartmouth, Swansea, Bristol, Tiverton, Little Compton, Freetown and the plantations of 
2 CONC Cumberland Gore and Attleboro. Little Compton’s name and land area were unchanged.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1691, Little Compton as part of the original settlement of Plymouth Colony merges with Massachusetts Bay Colony, et al. to form the Province of Massachusetts Bay. [Plymouth Colony existed without a formal charter since it’s fou
2 CONC nding, as the Pilgrim’s were originally chartered for a destination in the Hudson River (New York) area.]
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1747, Little Compton along with Tiverton secured their own royal decree, were incorporated, and annexed to Newport County as a part of Rhode Island along with Bristol. Because Little Compton was once part of the Plymouth Colony
2 CONC , all probate and land records prior to 1746 can be found in Taunton and New Bedford.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Closson-203
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy Closson (abt. 1681 - aft. 1705)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Timothy Closson aka Clawson===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 5 Jan 1681 in Tiverton, Plymouth Colony [uncertain]
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Josiah Closson and Mary (Williamson) Closson
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Unknown Closson, Nehemiah Closson, Mary (Closson) Bull, Caleb Closson, Hannah (Closson) Pettice, Nathan Closson and Josiah Closson
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Martha (Wilbor) Burgess — married 16 Jun 1702 in Tiverton, Newport, Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations, British Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Josiah Closson and Timothy Closson
2 CONT
2 CONT Died after 7 Jul 1705 after about age 24 in Little Compton, Newport, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 15 Apr 2022 | Created 30 Mar 2017
2 CONT
