1 NOTE {geni:about_me} NOTE
2 CONT
2 CONT Brief Life History of Moses
2 CONT When Moses Banks was born in 1690, in York Village, York, York, Maine, United States, his father, John Banks, was 33 and his mother, Elizabeth Turbat, was 24. He married Ruth Weare in 1712. They were the parents of at least 8 sons
2 CONC  and 3 daughters. In 1713, his occupation is listed as yeoman and mariner in York, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America. He died on 23 November 1750, in York Township, Upper Canada, British North America, at the age 
2 CONC of 60.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Moses
2 CONT English: variant of Bank 5, with excrescent -s. The final -s may occasionally represent a plural form, but it is most commonly an arbitrary addition made after the main period of surname formation, perhaps under the influence of p
2 CONC atronymic forms with a possessive -s.
2 CONT MORE
2 CONT Irish: Anglicized form of Gaelic Ó Bruacháin ‘descendant of Bruachán’, a byname for a large-bellied person. The English form was chosen because of a mistaken association of the Gaelic name with bruach ‘bank’. 
2 CONT -------------------------------------------
