1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=Annis&GSfn=John&GSmn=Closson&GSbyrel=all&GSdyrel=all&GSob=n&GRid=67734214&df=all& Find a Grave]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	May 8, 1785 Thetford Orange County Vermont, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Jun. 12, 1849 Nauvoo Hancock County Illinois, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN CLOSSON ANNIS was born May 8, 1785 at Thetford, Vermont; married June 16, 1806, Hannah Crawford at Thetford, Vermont. John was named for his maternal grandfather who died during the Revolution on an ill fated expedition again
2 CONC st the British in Canada. He was married about the same time that his parents and younger brother migrated to western New York state, and did not accompany them at that time. He later traveled west, spending time at Batavia, New Y
2 CONC ork, and than later worked as a boat builder at Cincinnati, Ohio. At some time before he became a Mormon preacher and was at Nauvoo, Illinois during the settling of the religious community there during the 1840's. John C. Annis wa
2 CONC s on this list: "Far-West, Mo. Saturday, July 7th 1838. The Conference convened agreeable to adjournment. Opened by Prayer by President Sidney Rigdon. When the following brethern, who came up in the Camp in 1834 received their ble
2 CONC ssing, also ordained as Seventies
2 CONT
2 CONT His sons, Hamlet and James stayed in the Cincinnati, Ohio area. There is some conflict in the Latter Day Saints records as to the year of his death, and they have it recorded as June 16, 1849.
2 CONT
