1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT Mary (Lewis) Mower Towne, Married Towne as widow Mower 
2 CONT *Wife of Thomas Mower — married 13 Nov 1711 (to 1730) in Essex, Massachusetts 
2 CONT *Wife of Joseph Towne — married 21 Feb 1730 in Lynn, Essex, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lewis-2665
2 CONT
2 CONT 4 Aug 1691 Mary Lewis, daughter of Thomas and Mary Lewis, was born in Lynn, Essex, Massachusetts.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 20 Oct 1711 intentions published for Mary Lewis to marry (1) Thomas Mower of Lynn[1][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT 21 Feb 1730/31 intentions published for Mary (Lewis) Mower to marry (2) Joseph Towne in Lynn, Essex, Massachusetts[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 Oct 1739 Mary (Lewis) (Mower) Towne died in Topsfield. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Adm. on the estate of Thomas Mower, late of Lynn, deceased, was granted on his widow, Mary Mower, on 8 March, 1730/31. Youngest child was then 2 years old.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT # Children of Thomas and Mary (Lewis) Mower:[5]
2 CONT # Mary, b. 7 June 1720, m. 4 May 1738 Mark Davis of Boston
2 CONT # Abigail, b. 30 July, 1723 d. 9 Dec. 1736
2 CONT # Thomas, b. 27 Aug. 1726, d. 9 Oct. 1788
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Joseph and Mary (Mower) Towne:[1]
2 CONT # Eunice, b. 22 Aug. 1733, d. 19 Dec. 1736
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT * ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 1.4 The Towne Family, William Towne and Joanna Blessing, Salem Massachusetts, 1635, Five Generations of Descendants, by Lois Payne Hoover, (2010, 3rd printing 2015), page 330
2 CONT * ↑ "Massachusetts, Town Clerk, Vital and Town Records, 1626-2001," database with images, FamilySearch (20 May 2014), Essex > County wide > County court births, marriages, deaths 1654-1795 > image 422 of 610; town clerk offices, M
2 CONC assachusetts.
2 CONT * ↑ Essex Institute Historical Collections. Essex, MA: Essex Institute, 1879. Page 77.
2 CONT * ↑ Edmund Lewis of Lynn, Massachusetts and some of his ancestors, George Harlan Lewis, Essex Institute, Salem Massachusetts, 1908,
2 CONT * ↑ Mower, Walter Lindley. Mower Family History. Southworth Press, 1923. Page 9.
