2 CONT ~ Dimmis "Ransom" Day (12/29/1749- ?)
2 CONT ~ Charles (5/12/1755-10/25/1776, Kent, CT)
2 CONT
2 CONT "He was one of the charter members of the Town of Kent and as long as he lived he had a large part in the control and management of its municipal affairs. He received a number of commissions from the General Assembly in the milita
2 CONC ry service of the province and served one enlistment as a lieutenant in the Continental army, Connecticut Line, during the Revolutionary war."
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "Historical Outline of the Ransom Family of America, Volume 2", by Wyllys Cadwell Ransom, 1903, page 74
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources: "Historical outline of the Ransom family of America", Vol. 1, by Wyllys Ransom, 1903, pages 73-74)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Inscription''
2 CONT
2 CONT "His faith was strong, his love was pure, His heart was patient to endure Affliction's keenest rod. The holy law was his delight, And 'twas his study day and night, To serve and please his God" (source: "Historical Outline of the 
2 CONC Ransom Family of America", Vol. 1, by Wyllys C. Ransom, 1903)
2 CONT ----
