2 TITL The Planters of the Commonwealth in Massachusetts, 1620-1640
1 NOTE REFNr 13  0
1 NOTE REFNr 13  0
1 NOTE  Came to America on the "Hercules" in March 1634.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Tilden was baptized at St. Mildred's Church, Tenterden, England 28 July 1583. He came to New England in the Hercules in March 1634/5 with his wife and seven children, and seven servants. He settled at Scituate, Plymouth,
2 CONC  Massachusetts and died in Scituate between May and 31 July 1641.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married in England, Lydia Huckstep. Lydia was the mother of all of Nathaniel Tilden's children. This is proved by the bequest in the will of Joseph Tilden, "to my sister Lydia Tilden, late wife of my brother Nathaniel Tilden...
2 CONC .and to her two daughters who are married in New England." (Water's Gleanings Vol. 1, p 71). These daughters were born in 1610 and 1613.
2 CONT (English Origins of New England Families, Series 1, Vol. 1, Hinckley, Sealis, Tilden, Gen. Pub. Co. CD #181.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Tenterden, a limb of the Cinque Port of Rye was a prosperous and important place in our ancestors day, as now, and the principal town in the weald of Kent.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Tilden , called "Mr." in both the Old and New England records, and "Gentleman" in his brother Hopestill's will was a man of importance: Mayor in 1622, and Jurat in 1624, 1625, 1627, 1629. In New England he was a town off
2 CONC icer and ruling elder.
2 CONT
2 CONT (From the Origins of New England Families Vol. 1, Gen. Pub. Co., 1984, Roberts, p 152.)
2 CONT
2 CONT /////////////////
2 CONT
2 CONT Some authors have thought his wife was Lydia Bourne however this is disproved in:
2 CONT (Origins of New England Families, Vol. 1, (from the New England Historical and Genealogical Register), by Roberts 1984, Gen. Pub. Co., p152.)
2 CONT
2 CONT ////////////////////////////////////////
2 CONT
2 CONT //////////////////////////////////////
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT From: Susan P. Canney
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Appreciation is expressed.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Nathaniel TILDEN
2 CONT Sex: M
2 CONT Baptism: 28 JUL 1583 Tenterden, co. Kent, England
2 CONT Death: 31 JUL 1641 BEF in Scituate, Plymouth Co., MA
2 CONT Burial: 1641 Scituate, Plymouth Co., MA
2 CONT
2 CONT Will: 25 MAY 1641 Plymouth, Plymouth Co., MA
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT Nathaniel Tilden emigrated to New England with his wife Lydia Huckstep and
2 CONT their children. They settled in Sciuate.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was of local prominence in Tenterden, serving the town as its mayor in 1622
2 CONT and being a jurat, or justice, in the years 1624, 1625, 1627 and 1629 and very
2 CONT probably in the intervening years.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Tildens, holding certificates from Mr. John Gee, vicar of Tenterden, Jno.
2 CONT Austin, the town's mayor and Fregift Stace, jurat, sailed for America in the
2 CONT "Hercules" of Sandwich, county, Kent, 200 tons, John Witherley, master, with a
2 CONT group of friends and neighbors. Mr. Gee's certificate was dated February 26,
2 CONT 1634 and that of the mayor and jurat March 4, 1634. With their father and
2 CONT mother, the children are listed - Joseph, Thomas, Stephen, Marie, Sara,
2 CONT Judeth, Lidia - and seven servants, Thomas Lapham, George Suttn, Edward Ford,
2 CONT Edward Jeakins, Sara Couchman, Mary Perien and James Bennett.
2 CONT
2 CONT After arriving in New England, Tilden went immediately to Scituate, to a great
2 CONT extent a Kentish community, and settled on the "two mile tract," now known as
2 CONT North Marshfield, his farm being on both sides of North river and on the sea.
2 CONT He was soon elected elder of the church presided over by Rev. John Lothrop,
2 CONT and, as his library indicates a strong interest in Puritan theology, he also
2 CONT enjoyed the controversy which engaged the attention of the Scituate men.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel bought land in Scituate on 10 April 1628, a deed of Henry Merritt,
2 CONT planter, conveying to him "all the land which I had of Goodman Byrd lying with
2 CONT the fence at the Northe end of the third cliff." It seems that 1628 was a
2 CONT mis-reading of 1638 however. He bought five acres in the third cliff from John
2 CONT Emerson in 1636, nine acres of marsh at New Harbor from the same grantor in
2 CONT 1639 and two acres of marsh from William Crocker in 1638.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1638 Nathaniel and Timothy Hatherly were appointed the Plymouth Colony's
2 CONT commissioners to treat with two representatives of Massachusetts Bay to
2 CONT determine the boundary between the two colonies. They were unable to come to
2 CONT any agreement.
2 CONT In the court records he appears only twice - two actions on the case - one
2 CONT against Comfort Starr in the sum of ú100 and the other against Henry Ewell.
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Nathaniel Tilden of Scituate, gentleman, is as follows:
2 CONT Will of Nathaniel Tilden
2 CONT "In the Name of God Amen the five and twentyeth Day of May Anno Dni 1641, I
2 CONT Nathaniel Tilden of Scittuate of New England within American gen being sick
2 CONT and weake of body but of good and prfect remembrance (thanks be given to God
2 CONT therefore) Do make ordaine and appoynt this my last will and testament in
2 CONT manner and forme as followeth. And first I will and bequeath my soul into the
2 CONT hands of Almighty God my creator and maker, and to Jesus Christ my redeemer by
2 CONT whose death and merits onely I hope to obtain everlastin salvation, and my
2 CONT body to be conveyed unto the earth from whence it was taken, at the place
2 CONT where it shall please God to put an end unto my Dayes. And as concerneing my
2 CONT worldly goods and estate wherewith it hath please God to blesse me I will give
2 CONT and bequeath in manner and forme as followeth. And first I will give &
2 CONT bequeath unto Lidea my welbeloved wyfe all her weareing apparell both linnen
2 CONT and wollen, also one bed furnished wch shee shall please to take also the
2 CONT greate trunck, also I give unto my said wyfe three paire of sheetes and two
2 CONT paire of pillowcoates which she shall please to take, one long table cloth one
2 CONT square table cloth one dosen of middle napkins and half a dosen of other
2 CONT napkins two long towells twelve peeces of pewter wch shee shall please to
2 CONT choose, and of wodden vessells so many as shee shall thinke to be convenient
2 CONT for her use also three silver spoones & two of my best cusheons, also I ive
2 CONT unto my said wyfe one peece of white fusteon wch shee shall please to take,
2 CONT also my two cloakes, also tenn bushells of Corne, five of England and five of
2 CONT Indian, also my will is that shee shall have the whole prfitt of my whitefaced
2 CONT cow and the calves and prfitt wch shall come of her During the tyme of her
2 CONT naturall life, to be mayntained and kept for her by mine Execuor hereafter
2 CONT menconed. Also my will is that my said wyfe shall have and enjoy the prfitts
2 CONT of one house and lands thereunto belonging wherein one Richard Lambert now
2 CONT Dwelleth being in the prish of Tenterden in Kent in old England During the
2 CONT terme of her naturall life, after the Decease of the said Richard Lambert Item
2 CONT my mynd and will is that my two yeongest children Lidea * Steeven shallbe
2 CONT manytayned both for meate drink apparell & lodging by myne Executor hereafter
2 CONT mentioned yet so as my aforesaid wyfe shall have the education and Disposeing
2 CONT of them All the residue of my goods my will and mynd is shalbe Disposed of in
2 CONT manner and forme as followeth. And first I will and bequeath unto my sonn
2 CONT Joseph A Double Portion (vizt) asmuch more as my otheer sonnes, that is asmuch
2 CONT as both my other sonnes Thomas and Steeven equally to be devided out of my
2 CONT lands and goods Itm my will is that my yeongest daughte(r) Lidea Lydea shall
2 CONT have half asmuch as one of my yeonger sonnes Thomas and Steeven Item I will
2 CONT unto my Daughter Judet one cow Item I will and bequeath unto Mary my Daughter
2 CONT the wyfe of Thomas Lapham tenn shillings of lawfull money of England also to
2 CONT Sara my daughter the wyfe of Georg Sutton tenn shillings of lawfull money of
2 CONT England to be payd to either of them within one yeare next after my Decease by
2 CONT mine Esecutor Item I will & appoynt that my two servants Edward Ginkins and
2 CONT Edward Tarte shall serve up the remaynder of their tyme of service wch by
2 CONT covenant id Due unto me with my sonne Joseph Itm my mynd and will is that my
2 CONT sonn Joseph shall prvide for his two brothers Thomas and Steeven for either of
2 CONT them half so much stock as his owne and for his yeongest sister Lidea one
2 CONT quarter asmuch as his owne, and that this their stock shallbe kept upon the
2 CONT lands given unto them as is before specyfyed untill such tyme as the said
2 CONT lands shalbe sould or hyred out. Item I will and appoynt my welbeloved sonn
2 CONT Joseph to be sole and whole Executor unto this my last will and testament. In
2 CONT witnes whereof I thabove names Nathaniell Tilden have hereunto set my hand and
2 CONT seale Dated the Day and yeare first above written.
2 CONT Sealed and Delivred as the last Will & Nathaniell Tilden
2 CONT testament of me Nathaniell Tilden
2 CONT in the prsence of
2 CONT Symon Sutton his mark
2 CONT Thomas Hatch
2 CONT
2 CONT My mynd and will is that my welbeloved sonne Joseph Tilden shall have full
2 CONT power and authorytie to sell my house with all the buildings thereunto
2 CONT belonging and also all my lands scituate and being in Scittuate & Tenterden
2 CONT all wch lands I give him power to sell or to dispose of at his pleasure, whom
2 CONT I make my whole and sole Executor of this my last will and testament. In
2 CONT witnes whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seale Dated the five and
2 CONT twentieth Day of May 1641.
2 CONT Sealed and Delivred as the last will & Nathaniell Tilden
2 CONT testament of me Nathaniell Tilden
2 CONT In the prsence of Symon Sutton his marke
2 CONT Thomas Hatch"
2 CONT The inventory of his estate contains several interesting items in addition to
2 CONT the usual fittings of house and farm. There are a musket, a sword and a
2 CONT "birding-peece," a great quantity of linen, thirteen silver spoons. The books
2 CONT number about forty-give, a very large number, including a great Bible, the
2 CONT Book of Martyrs, Calvin and many commentaries. Ten hives of bees were valued
2 CONT at ú1 apiece.
