2 CONT ////////////////////////////
2 CONT
2 CONT TILDEN, Nathaniel (the Elder): He came from Tenterden, Co Kent, England;
2 CONT was baptized there 28 Jul 1583; was one of the Jurats of Tenterden and
2 CONT Mayor in 1622; married about 1607 to Lydia HUCKSTEP; they were both
2 CONT passengers on the ship Hercules that brought the first HATCH to America;
2 CONT they had 12 children, all baptized at Tenterden, Co Kent, England; 5 of
2 CONT these children are buried at Tenterden, and 7 accompanied their parents to
2 CONT New England on the Hercules with William HATCH, a relative, in 1634.
2 CONT The servants that traveled with TildenÆs family were: Thomas Lapham,
2 CONT George Sutton, Edward Fford [or Ford], Edward Jeakins, Sara Couchman,
2 CONT Marie Perien & James Bennet.
2 CONT Nathaniel was chosen Ruling Elder of the First Church in Scituate, Ma.,
2 CONT 1634; his home lot was on Kent Street, the 3rd south of Greenfield Lane.
2 CONT He also had lands at Long marsh and lands in 1640 on the east side of the
2 CONT North River, below Gravelly beach. Elder Nathaniel died in 1641.
2 CONT His will gives "to wife Lydia, the income of my Stone house, with the
2 CONT lands, in Tenterden in Kent, Eng. in which Richard Lambeth now dwells, &c.
2 CONT &c. To son Joseph, a double portion, that is, as much as both Thomas and
2 CONT Stephen, (in lands, houses, &c. in Scituate and Marshfield [Ma.]). To
2 CONT Lydia and Stephen, my two youngest children, a maintenance till 21. To
2 CONT Judith, a cow. To Mary, wife of Thomas Lapham, 10s. To Sarah, wife of
2 CONT George Sutton, 10s." The inventory of his estate, in the Colony Records,
2 CONT shows that he belonged to the wealthiest class of early settlers. It
2 CONT included "Ten stocks or swarms of bees, appraised at ú10," and it is the
2 CONT earliest notice known respecting the keeping of bees in the Colony.
2 CONT Their children included:
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Joseph TILDEN - born in England; he belonged to the Second Church, of
2 CONT which he was chosen Deacon in 1655; he belonged to the liberal or moderate
2 CONT class of puritans; he married in 1648 to Elizabeth TWISDEN (daughter of
2 CONT John TWISDEN); he died 3 Jun 1670; his will gives "to wife Elizabeth ú100.
2 CONT To sons Nathaniel, John, Stephen, Samuel, Benjamin, lands already deeded
2 CONT to them. To daughter Elizabeth ú10. To sister Lydia Garrett ú5. To
2 CONT daughters Rebecca and Lydia, all my other goods in equal shares; also I
2 CONT acquit my brother Stephen of all dues."; they had 9 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Thomas TILDEN - was on the roll of those able to bear arms in Scituate,
2 CONT Plymouth Co., Ma. in 1643; there is no trace of a family history as yet.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. Stephen TILDEN - baptized 11 Oct 1629 at Tenterden, Kent Co., Eng.;
2 CONT possibly died at Scituate, Ma. in 1712; married 25 Jan 1661 at Scituate
2 CONT (or Marshfield), Ma. to Hannah LITTLE (daughter of Thomas & Ann (WARREN)
2 CONT LITTLE; resided principally in Marshfield, Ma.; they had 12 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. Mary (Marie) TILDEN - married 13 Mar 1636/7 to servant Thomas LAPHAM
2 CONT (was in Scituate, Ma. in 1640); they had 6 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 10. Sarah (Sara) TILDEN - married 13 Mar 1636/7 (1641) at Scituate, Ma. to
2 CONT servant George SUTTON (born 12 Apr 1613 at Sandwich, Kent Co., England;
2 CONT died 12 Apr 1669 in Perquiman Co., N.C.); they had at least 8 and probably
2 CONT nine children. George Sutton arrived in Boston, Mass., in 1634 on the ship
2 CONT Hercules. He came as a servant to Nathaniel Tilden of Tenterden, Co. Kent,
2 CONT England. He may have worked as servant to earn his passage to America.
2 CONT George was considered a devote member of the Society of Friends or
2 CONT "Quakers" in Mass. In 1668 the persecution of Quakers drove George and
2 CONT Sarah, along with some of their children, from Scituate to Perquimans,
2 CONT North Carolina. The area had just been opened for settlement for Quakers.
2 CONT One of the earliest Quaker Meeting Houses was built toward the end of the
2 CONT 17th century on "SuttonÆs Creek," so named because it bordered the lands
2 CONT of George Sutton and his sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. Judeth TILDEN
2 CONT
2 CONT 12. Lidia (or Lydia) TILDEN
