2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT She was baptised in St. Mildred's church in Tenterden, Kent, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah died at age 64 in the area that is now known as Perquimans county in NC.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.dragonbbs.com/members/ww8566/SuttonRobertAmbroseGenealogy.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the Quaker persecution in Mass., George Sutton and his wife, Sarah, moved to Perquimans County in the Colony of Carolina. He died there April 12, 1669, leaving two sons, Nathaniel and Joseph. They left many descendants w
2 CONC ho have spread out over North Carolina and Virginia. (The Suttons of Caroline County, VA by T. Dix Sutton)
