2 CONT The following information was found in 'Bancroft's History of The UnitedStates' Volume 1, Page 468: George Sutton, of Scituate, arrived in 1634,from Sandwich in Kent. He had a brother Simaon, of Scituate, of whomnothing further is
2 CONC  known. The rest of this article was found in thesame book but was hand written in by Edward F. H. Sutton in 1936:George Sutton, died in Perquimans County, North Carolina 4-12-1669.Sailed from Sandwich, Kent, 1634, settled at Scit
2 CONC uate, Mass., marriedthere March 13, 1636, Sarah Tilden, dau. of Nathaniel Tilden who camefrom Tenterden in Kent and was of ancient Kentish Family. She wasbaptized at Tenterden June 13, 1613, and died in Perquimans County, NorthCar
2 CONC olina, March 20, 1677, whither she and her husband had removed about1668. Children of George and Sarah Sutton (all born in HinghamlandScituate, Massachusetts) 1. Nathaniel, b. abt. 1637, d. North Carolina1682, m. Deborah Astine. 2
2 CONC . Joseph b. abt. 1639, d. North Carolina1695, m. Deliverance Nicholson. 3. William b. abt. 1641, d. Piscataway,New Jersey 1718, m. Demaris Bishop. 4. Daniel b. abt. 1643, d.Burington, New Jersey 174-, m. Mary Cole. 5. Lydia Baptis
2 CONC ed 9-13-1646.6. Sarah Baptised 12-3-1648, died an infant. 7. Sarah Baptised9-15-1650, m. John Barrow in North Carolina. 8. Elizabeth Baptised8-28-1623, d. North Carolina 1700, m. North Carolina Ralph Fletcher.END OF ARTICLE.
2 CONT
