1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Baptized January 19,1618/19 at St. Mildreds, Tenterden, Kent.  Thomas Tilden died at Marshfield, MA, on 1 Feb 1704/5.  He was the 2nd son called Thomas of Lydia Huckstep and  Nathaniel Tilden.  Thomas was on the ro
2 CONC ll of those that bore arms in Scituate in 1643.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Tilden married first, about 1653, to  Elizabeth Bourne, daughter of Thomas Bourne and Elizabeth. She was Robert Waterman’s widow.  She died in 1663.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Tilden married second, on January 24, 1664 at Marshfield, Massachusetts, to Mary Holmes.  Mary was the daughter of William Holmes.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT https://mathcs.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr02/rr02_094.html#P5951
2 CONT
2 CONT On 1 Jun 1653 Thomas first married Elizabeth Bourne (1824) , daughter of Thomas Bourne (713) (ca 1581-May 1664) & Elizabeth (ca 1585/1590-Jul 1660), in Marshfield, MA. Born ca 1618. Elizabeth died in Marshfield, MA in Dec 1663. Bu
2 CONC ried on 12 Dec 1663 in Marshfield, MA.60
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include:
2 CONT
2 CONT # (infant son) Tilden (Died soon) (25 Jun 1654-29 Jun 1654)
2 CONT #(infant son) Tilden (Died soon) (4 Oct 1655 [6?]-5 Oct 1656)
2 CONT #Lydia Tilden (26 Apr 1658-17 Sep 1740)
2 CONT
2 CONT On 24 Jan 1664 Thomas second married Mary Holmes, daughter of William Holmes (3 Jan 1591/2-9 Nov 1678) & Elizabeth, in Marshfield, MA.60 “Thomas Tilden and Mary Holmes were maryed y^e 14 of January 1664”. Born ca 1644 in Scituate,
2 CONC  MA. Mary was baptized in the Second Church of Scituate, in Apr 1661.52 Mary died aft 21 May 1705.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children include:
2 CONT #Elizabeth Tilden (ca 1665-18 Feb 1711/2)
2 CONT #Mary Tilden (14 Feb 1666-bef 13 Jan 1731)
2 CONT #Hannah Tilden (ca 1668-)
2 CONT #Thomas Tilden (ca 1668-11 Apr 1718)
2 CONT #Margery Tilden (ca 1673-)
2 CONT #Experience Tilden (ca 1675-)
2 CONT #Susannah Tilden (Died young) (ca 1678-9 Sep 1684)
2 CONT #John Tilden (Died young) (ca 1680-20 Apr 1685)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT >"Nathaniel Tilden arrived in New England in 1634 in the ship Hercules, of Dover, with his wife and children (Joseph, Mary, Sarah, Judith, Lydia, Stephen, and '''Thomas'''), and the following, who came under the designation of ‘se
2 CONC rvants:’ Thomas Lapham, George Sutton, Edward Ford, Edward Jenkins, James Bennett, Sarah Couchman, and Mary Perien. The Rev. William Witherell came on this same boat.39"
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1664 will of Thomas Bourne had been misinterpreted, and gave genealogists the impression there had been a (fictional) daughter Lydia Bourne who married either the Elder Nathaniel Bourne or his (fictional) son Nathaniel Tilden 
2 CONC ll.  
2 CONT
2 CONT >The expression "my Daughter Tildin: Daughter Lydia Tildin" means, and perhaps should be read, "my daughter Tildin's daughter Lydia Tildin," in other words, his granddaughter Lydia, child of his daughter Elizabeth (Bourne) (Waterm
2 CONC an) Tilden; and it will be noted that Elizabeth's four Waterman boys were given legacies in the same paragraph immediately following Lydia's legacy. The ambiguity of the Tilden clause has caused many genealogists to conclude that 
2 CONC Thomas Bourne had a daughter Lydia, but care-, ful study of the records fails to substantiate the existence of such a daughter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Therefore -
2 CONT
2 CONT *Lydia Bourne did not exist (she was her sister Elizabeth)
2 CONT *Nathaniel Tilden Jr did not exist (he was his brother Thomas, who married Elizabeth (Bourne), widow Waterman)
2 CONT
2 CONT ------
2 CONT
2 CONT * http://aleph0.clarku.edu/~djoyce/gen/report/rr02/rr02_064.html#P5951
