1 NOTE      Thomas Tilden came to Scituate, Plymouth Colony, Massachusettswith his parents soon after 4 March 1634/5.  Thomas Tilden removed toMarshfield before his first marriage, certainly as early as the year1645 .
2 CONT "Thomas Tilden and Mary Holmes were married 24 Jan 1664" Marshfield VR
2 CONT Will of Thomas Tilden, dated Marshfield February 1, 1704 (Plym.II:59)21 May 1705
2 CONT "I, Thomas Tilden of Marshfield in the County of Plimouth being inhealth and of sound mind and memory tho very aged, praysed e God,considering the time of my disolution draweth near do make this mylast will and testament in Manner
2 CONC  and form foloowing first I committmy soul to God and my body to decent burial when it shall Please Godto Call me hence and in hope of a Joyfull Resurecsion to Life andGlory thourgh the precious Merritts of my Lord and Saviour Jes
2 CONC urChrist and for the disposall of my outward estate which God hathGraciously given me my mind and will is that it shall be bestowed asin this my will is set down imp My will is that my beloved wife, MARYshall have the one half of 
2 CONC all my houseing and lands of what kind orNature fovever for and during the Term of her natural life.  Item Igive and bequeath unto my son THOMAS TILDEN all my other half of myhouseing and lands and also the aforesd half of my hous
2 CONC ing and landsbequeathed to my wife I give to my son THOMAS TILDEN to be injoyed byhim after his mother's decease to have and to hold to him and hisheirs for ever he therefore paying to my son in law Anthony Spraguethe sum of seven
2 CONC  pounds remaining due of my daughter MARY his wivesportion for which he has my bill.  Moreover I give to my daughter MarySprague five shillings item. I give and bequeath to my daughter LidiaRider twenty shillings over and above th
2 CONC e portion I have formerlygiven her.  Item. I give and bequeath to my daughter MARGERY the sumof ten pounds.  Item I give and bequeath to my well beloved wife mybest bed and furniture and one thrid part of all my goods andchattells
2 CONC  my debts and legacys aforesd being first paid and allremainder of my goods and chatels I give and bequeath to my fourdaughters Hannah, ELIZABETH, Margery and Experience to be equallydivided amongst them only first I give my daugh
2 CONC ter ELIZABETH TWENTYSHILLINGS.  Lastly I nominate and appoint my well beloved wife MaryTilden and my son Thomas Tilden to be executors of this my last willand testament.  THOMAS TILDEN 21 DAY OF May 1705: in presence ofTobias Oakm
2 CONC an and Elizabeth Oakman & Nathaniel Thomas.
