1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT
2 CONT "Samuel Tilden, the youngest son of the elder Nathaniel Tilden, was baptized at Tenterden, O ct. 11, 1629, and came to Scituate with his father and mother and six brothers and sisters i n 1634.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, Jan. 15, 1662, Hannah Little, daughter of Thomas Little, of Plymouth. Her brothe r Thomas was killed by the Indians in the Rehobeth massacre in 1676. Her father Thomas Little , married, April 16, 1633, Ann, daughter of
2 CONC  Richard Warren. Thomas Little removed from Plymou th to Marshfield in 1650. He was buried there the 12th of March 1671. Savage states that twel ve of this name had in 1829 been graduated at Harvard, eight at Dartmouth, and nine a
2 CONC t othe r colleges of New England.  Deane's "History of Scituate" mentions several members of this fa mily who became distinguished. His wife's father, Richard Warren, came in the "Mayflower" i n 1620, leaving his wife and five dau
2 CONC ghters to come in the third ship in 1623. He died in 162 8, having no children but those born in England. He had two sons, Nathaniel and Joseph.  Th e latter was the great-great-Grandfather of Major-General Warren who was killed a
2 CONC t Bunker Hil l."
2 CONT
2 CONT from: Tilden 1191 - 1894, by Samuel J. Tilden, 1894.
