2 CONT Benoni Studley Born about 1671 in Sandwich, Kent, Englandmap Son of [father unknown] and [mother unknown] [sibling(s) unknown] Husband of Abigail (Stetson) Studley — married 22 Dec 1701 in Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusettsmap DESC
2 CONC ENDANTS descendants Father of Abigail Studley, John Studley, Sarah Studley, Joshua Studley, Gideon Studley and Benoni Studley Died 14 Nov 1746 in Hanover, Plymouth, Massachusettsmap Profile manager: Raymond Zeller private message 
2 CONC [send private message] Profile last modified 20 Aug 2021 | Created 8 May 2016 | Last significant change: 19 Aug 2021 22:36: Dave May edited the Primary Photo for Benoni Studley (abt.1671-1746). [Thank Dave for this] This page has 
2 CONC been accessed 172 times. Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Flag of Kent, England Benoni Studley migrated from Kent, England to Massachusetts Bay Colony. Flag of Massachusetts Bay Colony Benoni Studly, of Sandwich, Mass., was in that part of Scituate, now Hanover, and his house, which was 
2 CONC built in 1702, is the oldest now [1853] standing in the town, on Hanover Street. He left only a verbal will, drawn up, at his request, by Rev. Mr. Bass, and the same is now in the hands of some of his descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT Deane, in his History of Scituate,53 did not identify Benoni’s parents: “There was also a Benoni Studley in Scituate, of another family, whose children, John, Abigail, Joshua, Gideon, Sarah, and Benoni, were born from 1802 to 1723
2 CONC ; of this family is Lewis Studley, and several also of Hingham.”
2 CONT
2 CONT The marriage record for Benoni and Abigall doesn’t mention her surname.52 Their children include: 42699i. Abigail Studley (13 Aug 1702-28 Oct 1760) 42700ii. John Studley (25 Feb 1704/5-23 Sep 1787) 42701iii. Joshua Studley (Aug 17
2 CONC 07-15 Jul 1759) 42702iv. Gideon Studley (15 May 1710-) 42703v. Sarah Studley (Died soon) (31 Mar 1716-) 42704vi. Sarah Studley (18 Jan 1718-) 42705vii. Benoni Studley (25 Jul 1723-)
2 CONT
2 CONT Benoni died at age 75 on 14 November 1746, in Hanover, Massachusetts. There is a monument of the Studley family in the Hanover Center Cemetery.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
