1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biography Joseph, son of Thomas and Mary Lapham, was born at Scituate, MA in September of 1670.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Lapham (Thomas, Thomas) was born in 1670, the son of Thomas and Mary Brooks Lapham. He married 1) Abigail Sherman; 2) Patience ---------;3) Hannah Eames, His children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph born 26 Apr 1709; married . Abigail Joyce 26 Sep 1729. Ichabod born 11 Oct 1711 died 11 Dec 1711. Ch. by 2nd wife. Joseph was a farmer on the 2 mile square, Scituate." [1] ABIGAIL SHERMAN (John, William), was born in Marshf
2 CONC ield MA, 15 Mar. 1679-80, and died in Scituate MA, 18 May 1709. She married about 1703, Joseph Lapham, born in Scituate, in Sept. 1670, who died after 1712 He was the son of Thomas and Mary Lapham. He married secondly in 1710 or 1
2 CONC 711, Patience-, who died in Scituate, 27 Oct. 1711. He married thirdly, in Marshfield 5 Feb. 1711-12, Hannah Eames.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph's children,born in Scituate, Mass.:
2 CONT
2 CONT By first wife, Abigail Sherman, Joseph Lapham, 26 Apr 1709 By second wife, Patience-: Ichabod, b. 11 Oct. 1711, d. 11 Dec. 1711.[2] "Joseph LAPHAM & Hannah EAMES, m. 25 Feb 1712-13"[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes Laphams in America has the date 'Feb. 5, 1711-12' following Hannah's name above for her wedding date with Joseph Sr. Joseph Jr's entry indicates his mother was Abigail, Ichabod appears to have been Patience's son.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources ↑ "Laphams in America" compiled and written by Bertha Bortle Beal Aldridge Victor NY 1932-1953; pg 408 ↑ Descendants of William Sherman of Marshfield by Mary Lovering Holman, pg 36, found at https://archive.org/details/des
2 CONC cendantsofwil00holm_0 ↑ Marriages from the Early Records of Marshfield, Mass. Miss M.A. Thomas, New England Historical & Genealogical Register, Vol 6, October 1852, p. 347 found at http://dunhamwilcox.net/ma/marshfield_ma_marriage
2 CONC s.htm Vital Records of Scituate Massachusetts to the year 1850, two volumes, (Boston: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1909), 1:214 (birth)
