2 CONT Samuel Lapham (1676 - abt. 1757)
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Lapham
2 CONT Born 12 Apr 1676 in Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusettsmap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Son of Thomas Lapham Jr and Mary (Brooks) Lapham
2 CONT Brother of Joseph Lapham Sr. and Lydia Lapham
2 CONT Husband of Hannah (Rogers) Lapham — married 19 Nov 1701 in Marshfield, Plymouth, Massachusettsmap
2 CONT Husband of Sarah (Low) Lapham — married after 9 May 1741 in Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts Bay Colonymap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Father of Hannah (Lapham) Stetson, Mary Lapham, David Lapham, Elizabeth (Lapham) Sherman, Joshua Lapham, Mercy (Lapham) Ewell, Thankful (Lapham) King, Amos Lapham and Lydia Lapham
2 CONT Died about Mar 1757 at about age 80 in Marshfield, Plymouth, Massachusettsmap
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile manager: Alyson Dossett private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 28 Jun 2023 | Created 5 Jul 2011
2 CONT This page has been accessed 755 times.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [hide]
2 CONT 1 Biography
2 CONT 1.1 Marriage
2 CONT 1.2 Death
2 CONT 1.3 Probate
2 CONT 2 Sources
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel, son of Thomas and Mary (Brooks) Lapham, was born at Scituate, MA on April 12, 1676[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Married First: Hannah Rogers at Marshfield, MA on November 19, 1701.
2 CONT They had 9 Children, all born in Marshfield [2] (Merrick has them all born in Scituate [3]):
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Hannah (Lapham) Stetson,[4] [5], born 1 April 1703, baptized 22 October 1704.
2 CONT ii. Mary Lapham, born 13 September 1704, baptized 22 October 1704, unmarried in 1748.
2 CONT iii. David Lapham, born 3 April 1706, baptized 12 May 1706.
2 CONT iv. Elizabeth (Lapham) Sherman, born 13 April 1708, baptized 4 July 1708
2 CONT v. Joshua Lapham, born 22 December 1710, baptized 25 March 1710/11.
2 CONT vi. Mercy (Lapham) Elwell, born 10 May 1713, baptized 12 July 1713.
2 CONT vii. Thankful (Lapham) King, born __ May 1715, baptized 24 July 1715.
2 CONT viii. Amos Lapham, born 1 December 1717 [6], baptized 28 September 1718*, died 25 March 1731, aged 14 years, buried in Marshfield Hills Cemetery [7] .
2 CONT ix. Lydia Lapham, born 17 November 1724, baptized 9 May 1725, died 6 November 1800, aged 77 years, buried Marshfield Hills Cemetery.
2 CONT On 20 July 1735, Nathaniel Holm[e]s, son of John Holm[e]s of Pembroke, & adopted son of Samuel Lapham, was baptized at the Second Church of Scituate[8].
2 CONT
2 CONT Married second, Sarah Low[9] probably in Scituate, MA (intentions published there 9 May1741*). Sarah died, date and place undocumented, probably in Scituate, after 10 February 1748, when her husband made his will, which referred t
2 CONC o a marriage settlement with his present wife[10].
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT He died at Marshfield in March of 1757 and is buried at Marshfield Hills Cemetery [11].
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Samuel Lapham of Scituate, dated 10 February 1747/8 and proved 24 March 1757, mentioned children: David (who received the land Samuel "had of my father Timothy Roggers"), Joshua, Hannah Stetson, Elizabeth Sherman, Merc
2 CONC y Ewell, Thankful King, Mary Lapham, and Lydia Lapham. The will also referred to a settlement with his “present wife, Sarah (Low) Lapham, made before marriage, bearing date, 19 May 1741.”[12][13]
2 CONT
2 CONT His inventory was taken on 3 April 1757 in Scituate.[14]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
