1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Josiah-Washburn/6000000010875432078
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT [http://books.google.com/books?pg=PA340&id=KIc-AAAAYAAJ&output=text History of the Early Settlement of Bridgewater in Plymouth County] ... By Nahum Mitchell.  Page 340.  WASHBURN.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 11. Josiah (s. of John 4) and his w. Mercy had 
2 CONT *Joanna 1703, 
2 CONT *Joseph 1705, 
2 CONT *Lydia 1707,
2 CONT * Jemima 1710, 
2 CONT *Rebeckah 1712, 
2 CONT *Josiah 1716,
2 CONT * Mercy 1718. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He had a 2d w. and a 
2 CONT *s. Nathan
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT *Joanna m. Ebenezer Leach 1734.—
2 CONT *Jemima m. Josiah Leonard, Jr., 1740, 
2 CONT * m. Samuel Alden 1752.—Mercy m. Pelatiah Phinney 1738.—
2 CONT *Lydia m. Samuel West 1737.
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://home.earthlink.net/~washburnmaltby/washburn_plymouth_3.html Families of the Children of John3 Washburn and Rebecca Lapham]
2 CONT
2 CONT The grandchildren of John Washburn and Rebecca Lapham have been pretty well established through vital records, deeds, and wills. The second wife of son '''Josiah Washburn''' remains a mystery, however.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mercy (Tilson) Washburn died in ca. 1719 or 1720, and Josiah Washburn remarried to 2.) (_____) in ca. 1724.[6] Josiah deeded his homestead land in Bridgewater to his son, Joseph Washburn, on 25 Nov. 1731, which Joseph acknowledged
2 CONC  as his share of his father’s estate on 3 Dec. 1731.[7] Josiah deeded land to his son Josiah Washburn, Jr., in 1746,[8] son Joseph Washburn in 1746,[9] and he deeded a 39-acre parcel of land in Bridgewater to his son Nathan Washbu
2 CONC rn on 12 Mar. 1746.[10] He deeded two more parcels of land to his sons Joseph Washburn and Nathan Washburn on 13 Dec. 1750.[11]
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah Washburn died intestate on 27 Feb. 1751 in Bridgewater,[12] and his sons Josiah (Jr.) and Nathan Washburn were granted administration of his estate on 1 Apr. 1751. His inventory was appraised by Josiah Edson Jr., Solomon Le
2 CONC onard, and Benjamin Willis Jr., on 5 Apr. 1751, and presented in probate court on 29 Apr. 1751.[13] Josiah Washburn’s second wife’s name is not mentioned in his probate records, and she may have died before 1751.
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah Washburn had 8 children by Mercy Tilson, and probably 1 more son by his unknown second wife:[14]
2 CONT
2 CONT (see referenced site for footnotes)
