2 CONT ----
2 CONT Rebekah was the daughter of Joseph Washburn and Hannah (Latham) Washburn. Rebekah was probably born in Bridgewater, Plymouth county, Province of Massachusetts Bay.
2 CONT
2 CONT From [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=64480164&ref=wvr Find A Grave Memorial# 64480164]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebekah married David Johnson on 7 January 1719/20 in Bridgewater, Plymouth county, Province of Massachusetts Bay. She preceded him in death. They had children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Isaac - 9 August 1721
2 CONT # David - 8 August 1724
2 CONT # Mary - 29 August 1729
2 CONT # Sarah - 19 July 1732
2 CONT # Rebecca - 22 June 1734
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebekah died in Bridgewater, Plymouth county, Province of Massachusetts Bay.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: Rebekah is often identified in various online family trees as "Bethia". The source of this misinformation is Williams Latham's book "Epitaphs in Old Bridgewater, Massachusetts". The book states "Bethia", her epitaph, and her
2 CONC  plot location. Both her headstone (despite the etching) and footstone demonstrate that her name is Rebekah.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=:2239140&id=I881hildren
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac JOHNSON b: 9 Aug 1721 in , , Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT David JOHNSON b: 8 Aug 1724 in Bridgewater, Plymouth, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Mary JOHNSON b: 29 Aug 1729 in , , Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah JOHNSON b: 19 Jul 1732 in , , Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca JOHNSON b: 22 Jun 1734 in , , Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT
