1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===Dorothy Burgess
2 CONT * Birth:	Nov 12 1670 - Sandwich, Barnstable, Massachusetts
2 CONT * Death:	Apr 10 1725 - Rochester, Plymouth, Massachusetts
2 CONT * Parents:  Joseph (Burgess) Burge and Patience Freeman
2 CONT * Husband:	Savory Clifton - married before 1690 in Rochester, Plymouth Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Burgess-989
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy Burgess (alternately spelled Burg, Burge, Burgis), daughter of Joseph and Patience (Freeman) Burge, was born 12 November 1670, at Sandwich in the Plymouth Colony.[1] Dorothy's father Joseph was instrumental in founding the
2 CONC  town of Sippican, now Rochester, in 1679.[2] It was probably there that Dorothy married Savory Clifton prior to 1690.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1695 will of Joseph Burgess named his daughter "Dorrity" Clifton leaving her 20 shillings. She also benefited from land transactions as a result of his estate. 17 March 1714/5 the children of Joseph Burge of Rochester, late de
2 CONC ceased relinquished and discharged to their brother Benjamin Burge, all their right in land which had belonged to their father. This deed was signed by Savorill [sic] Clifton, Dorothy Cliftion (mark), Edward Rose (mark), Rebecca R
2 CONC ose (mark) and Ichabod Burge. [4] 10 April 1725 Patience Burge of Rochester (Dorothy's mother), widow of Joseph acquitted and discharged to Benjamin Burge (er son) and her daughter Dorothy, the wife of Clifton Savory, her "right i
2 CONC n a share of land in Middleboro, which was formerly in the right of Governor Prence ... I am heir to a part of the same." [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy and Savory remained in Rochester and raised a family of at least eleven children there. [4] The Cliftons were closely allied with the Wing family and together they were founders of the Quaker movement in Rochester.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorothy Clifton died probably in Rochester, after April 10, 1725 (deed) and before June 1, 1727 (deed)[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT # Benjamin b. 1 Aug 1690
2 CONT # Patience b. 2 Mar 1693, prob. died young
2 CONT # Margaret/Margirit, b. 3 Nov 1695
2 CONT # Jane b. 15 Feb 1697
2 CONT # Dorothy b. 25 Mar 1699
2 CONT # Sarah b. Thursday 15 Oct 1702
2 CONT # Lydia/Lidia b. Tuesday 29 May 1705
2 CONT # Bathsheba/Barsheba, b. Sunday 9 May 1708
2 CONT # Mary b. Tuesday 10 Apr 1711
2 CONT # Savory/Savery b. Wednesday 15 July 1713, may have died young
2 CONT # Hannah b. Friday 21 Jun 1717
2 CONT
