2 CONT 1895  Page 26 - 27
2 CONT Peregrine son of  Wm. and Susanna (Fuller) White, b. in the cabin of the Mayflower, as it lay in Cape Cod Harbor, November 20, 1620; and derived his name from their perigrinations - the  name "Peregrine" signifying " A Pilgrim in 
2 CONC a strange land." He was the first native-born New Englander.
1 NOTE See Historical Document.
2 CONT 	 TYPE Book
