2 CONT 	 This book contains the history and genealogy of the William White family of Virginia.
2 CONT 	 DATE 1895
2 CONT 	 TYPE Book
2 CONT 	 AUTH Thomas and Samuel White
2 CONT 	 PERI Genealogy of the White Family, from 1607-8 TO 1895.
2 CONT 	 PUBL Republican Press Association. Concord.
2 CONT 	 CALN CS71.W585
2 CONT 	 This book contains the history and genealogy of the William White family of Virginia.
2 CONT 	 DATE 1895
2 CONT 	 Born in the cabin of the Mayflower, as she lay in Cape Cod
2 CONT 	 Harbor, November 20, 1620; and derived his name from their
2 CONT 	 perigrinations--the name "Peregrine" signifying "A Pilgrim in a
2 CONT 	 strange land." He was the first native-born New Englander. He
2 CONT 	 came to Green Harbor with the family of his step-father, Gov.
2 CONT 	 Edward Winslow, after 1632. He married about 1647, Sarah,
2 CONT 	 daughter of William and Elizabeth Bassett (passengers in the
2 CONT 	 Fortune, November 10, 1621.) He settled on an estate given him
2 CONT 	 by his father-in-law, lying between North and South rivers, not
2 CONT 	 far from their united outlet to the ocean. This tract was early
2 CONT 	 granted to Mr. Bassett by the freemen of the Colony. Mr. Bassett
2 CONT 	 was one of the land committee of the Colony and was a large land
2 CONT 	 holder. He resided in Duxbury, Mass; removed to Bridgewater,
2 CONT 	 probably about 1645 or '48, as at that time Bridgewater was
2 CONT 	 settled by freemen from Duxbury, Mass. All Duxbury, Mass freemen
2 CONT 	 were given lots to remove there, but only few moved. But many of
2 CONT 	 their sons settled there afterwards. Mr. Bassett died in
2 CONT 	 Bridgewater, 1667. He left a large and valuable library for that
2 CONT 	 period to his son-in-law, Peregrine White.
2 CONT 	 TYPE Book
2 CONT 	 AUTH Thomas and Samuel White
2 CONT 	 PERI Genealogy of the White Family, from 1607-8 TO 1895.
2 CONT 	 PUBL Republican Press Association. Concord.
2 CONT 	 CALN CS71.W585
2 CONT 	 This book contains the history and genealogy of the William White family of Virginia.
2 CONT 	 DATE 1895
2 CONT 	 The offices he held in town (Marshfield, Mass) affairs are as
2 CONT 	 follows: Nov. 1651 "Voted at Town-meeting that Mr. White look to
2 CONT 	 all such persons as live disorderly in the Township, and give
2 CONT 	 them warning, and in case they do not redress their course of
2 CONT 	 life, that he shall use such means to redress such abuses as he
2 CONT 	 finds in such persons." He was chosen one of the raters, (now
2 CONT 	 selectmen) 1651-1655, representative to General Court, 1659;
2 CONT 	 grand juryman, 1660; selectman 1661 to 1665. As early as 1637 he
2 CONT 	 was one of thirty volunteers "to assist them of Massachusetts
2 CONT 	 Bay and Connecticut in their wars against the Pequin Indians."
2 CONT 	 One of the jury to lay out highways, 1667; selectman, 1672;
2 CONT 	 deputy to General Court, 1673; foreman of a jury to lay out
2 CONT 	 roads in Marshfield, Mass, 1675. Chosen one of Council of War,
2 CONT 	 of which he was an active member "in tongue and gun," 1673.
2 CONT 	 After which he is styled Capt. White. On Marshfield, Mass's town
2 CONT 	 record bearing date 1644, there are thirty-three Freemen of
2 CONT 	 which Peregrine White's name is the twelfth.
2 CONT 	 Receipt. "Nov. 11, 1677-8, Received by mee, John Williams, for
2 CONT 	 use of Abraham Blush, of Perrigrine White the sume of thirty
2 CONT 	 shillings for rent, I say received by mee, John Williams, which
2 CONT 	 is the one halfe.
2 CONT 	 John Williams."
2 CONT 	 "5 June 1651. Surveyors for the Hiewaies Marshfield, Mass
2 CONT 	 Anthony Snow, Peregrin White."
2 CONT 	 "4 May 1651. Leiuetenant Perigren White Ppounded to take up his
2 CONT 	 Freedom."
2 CONT 	 "6 Feb 1665-6. Leift" Perigrine White, Ensigne Marke Eames,
2 CONT 	 Anthony Snow, John Bourne and Willam Foard, Senr are appointed
2 CONT 	 by the Court to bee the selectmen of the town of Marshfield,
2 CONT 	 Mass."
2 CONT 	 "3d June 1668. The Celectmen of Marshfield, Mass Leiftenant
2 CONT 	 Peregrine White, Ensigne Marke Eames, Anthony Snow."
2 CONT 	 "Deputy to serve att Court 3 June 1662. Leift Perrigrine White."
2 CONT 	 "In reference unto the request of the Kinges commissioners in
2 CONT 	 the behalfe of Leiftenant Peregrine White desireing that the
2 CONT 	 Court would accommodate him with a portion of land in respect
2 CONT 	 that hee was the first of the English that was borne in these
2 CONT 	 ptes and in answare unto his owne petition prefered to this
2 CONT 	 Court respecting the p'mises The Court have granted unto him two
2 CONT 	 hundred acrees of land lying and being att the path that goes
2 CONT 	 from Bridgewater to the Bay adjoyning to the Bay line" 2 October
2 CONT 	 1665. (This land went into his stepfather's possession.) 27
2 CONT 	 Sept., 1642 Mr. Edward Winslow acknowledged in Court that he had
2 CONT 	 given to his son Peregrine "those his lands lying at Eele
2 CONT 	 River."
2 CONT 	 "6 March 1673-4 According to a graunt of the Court bearing date
2 CONT 	 June 1662 and by a Court order bearing date 1671 Leiftenant
2 CONT 	 Peregrine White and John Nelson layed out 1000 acrees of land
2 CONT 	 lying and being neare the Old Indian way att Teticutt Rivier,
2 CONT 	 about a mile westerly where Narnaseakett Rivier runs into
2 CONT 	 Teticutt and soe runs easterly marked and numbered by the river
2 CONT 	 syde ten lotts of one hundred acrees in a lott running half a
2 CONT 	 mile in length southerly and one hundred lotts in breadth as may
2 CONT 	 appear by a draught thereof. vizS:--3 lott To Leiftenant
2 CONT 	 Peregrine White.
2 CONT 	 4 March 1673-4 Winslow Govr"
2 CONT 	 1672-5 June "Leift Peregrine White and Willam Nelson Senr were
2 CONT 	 appointed by the Court to lay out or divide certain meddows
2 CONT 	 belonging to Pachague Necke and the inlargement of Upland on
2 CONT 	 Bridgwater syde of the rivier and the petitioners of Pachauge
2 CONT 	 Neck aforesaid to defray the charge thereof 1672 June 5 Celect
2 CONT 	 men of Marshfield, Mass Leift White, John Bourne, Ensigne
2 CONT 	 Eames."
2 CONT 	 "Deputie to serve at Court 15 Sept. 1673 Leiftn White."
2 CONT 	 27 September, 1642.
2 CONT 	 "It is also agreed & concluded that Captaine Miles Standish
2 CONT 	 shall goe captaine to lead those forces that shallbe sent forth
2 CONT 	 and that Mr Thomas Prince shall go wth him to be his counsell
2 CONT 	 and advise in the warrs &c and that Willm Palmer shallbe
2 CONT 	 leiftennant and Perregrine White be the auncient bearrer."
2 CONT 	 7 July 1637
2 CONT 	 Among "the names of the souldiers that willingly offer
2 CONT 	 themselves to go upon the sd Service, with Mr Prince & the
2 CONT 	 Leiftent was Perregrine Whites."
2 CONT 	 10 June 1662
2 CONT 	 "A deputie of every towne in the goument was appointed to take
2 CONT 	 account of the Treasurer vizS of those that were att the Court
2 CONT 	 Marshfield, Mass Leiftenant Peregrine White" June 10 1662.
2 CONT 	 3 June 1652
2 CONT 	 "The Constables of Marshfield, Mass Anthony Snow, Leiftenant
2 CONT 	 Perigren White."
2 CONT 	 6 Oct. 1659
2 CONT 	 "Peregrine White one of the deputies impowered to acte in the
2 CONT 	 ordering and settling of the trad att Kennebecke which was
2 CONT 	 interupted by reason of some troubles amongst the Indians."
2 CONT 	 6 June 1660
2 CONT 	 "The Grand Enquest Leiftn Peregrine White."
2 CONT 	 5 March 1660-1
2 CONT 	 "impanelled on a jury to enquire how Jeremiah Burroughs came by
2 CONT 	 his death" Peregrine White.
2 CONT 	 2 Oct. 1658
2 CONT 	 "Appointed one of the "Councill of Warr" Leift Peregrine White."
2 CONT 	 3 June 1652
2 CONT 	 "Leiftenant Peregrine White admitted a Freeman and sworne."
2 CONT 	 8 June 1655
2 CONT 	 "The Milletary officers settled according to the request of the
2 CONT 	 seuerall townes are as followeth For Marshfield, Mass Mr Josias
2 CONT 	 Winslow Junr. for Captaine; for leiftenant Mr Peregrine White;
2 CONT 	 for Ensigne Marke Eames."
2 CONT 	 Taken from the Old Colony reports.
2 CONT 	 On the Marshfield, Mass church records appears the following in
2 CONT 	 Rev. Edward Thompson's hand-writing (record previous having been
2 CONT 	 lost or destroyed): "Capt. Peregrine White, the first born child
2 CONT 	 of New England was admitted into the church in the 78th year of
2 CONT 	 his age." On the occasion of which Rev. Mr. Thompson preached
2 CONT 	 from Matt. 20: 6-7. "And about the eleventh hour he went out,
2 CONT 	 and found others standing idle, and saith unto them, Why stand
2 CONT 	 ye here all the day idle? They say unto him, Because no man hath
2 CONT 	 hired us. He said unto them, Go ye also into the vineyard; and
2 CONT 	 whatsoever is right, that shall ye receive."
2 CONT 	 It is stated that he was a son always filial and loving,
2 CONT 	 visiting his mother daily, riding on a large black horse, his
2 CONT 	 coat buttoned with buttons the size of a silver dollar. In the
2 CONT 	 Boston Weekly News Letter of July 31, 1704, the fifteenth number
2 CONT 	 of the first newspaper printed in New England, appeared the
2 CONT 	 notice of his death. "Marshfield, Mass, July 20, Capt. Peregrine
2 CONT 	 White of this town died here the 20th inst., aged 83 years and 8
2 CONT 	 months. He was vigorous and of a comely aspect to the last."
2 CONT 	 The exact spot of his interment is unknown, but probably in the
2 CONT 	 Winslow burying-ground where his mother was buried. An old book,
2 CONT 	 "The Life of John Eliot," written by Cotton Mather about 1695,
2 CONT 	 once owned by Peregrine, is now in the possession of E. L. B.
2 CONT 	 Howard, Cambridge, Mass. It bears the autograph of Peregrine
2 CONT 	 White, 1702, two years previous to his death.
2 CONT 	 The following is taken from a tomb-stone in the Winslow cemetery
2 CONT 	 at Marshfield, Mass, in memory of the pastor that preached the
2 CONT 	 sermon at the time of Peregine's being admitted into the church:
2 CONT 	 Here Lyes Ye Ashes
2 CONT 	 Of Ye Reverend Learned
2 CONT 	 & Pious Mr Edward Tompson
2 CONT 	 Pastor of Ye Church Of Marshfield, Mass
2 CONT 	 Who Suddenly
2 CONT 	 Departed This Lyfe March
2 CONT 	 Ye 16th 1705.
2 CONT 	 Anno Aetatis Suee 40
2 CONT 	 Here In a Tyrants Hand Does Captive
2 CONT 	 Lye A Rare Synopsis Of Divinity,
2 CONT 	 Old Patriarchs Prophets Gospel Bishops Meet
2 CONT 	 Under Deep Silence In
2 CONT 	 Their Winding Sheet,
2 CONT 	 Here rest Awhile In Hopes
2 CONT 	 And full Intent
2 CONT 	 When Their King Calls
2 CONT 	 To meet in Parliament."
2 CONT 	 He was the grandson of Rev. Wm. Tompson of Braintree, was the
2 CONT 	 fourth pastor of the Marshfield, Mass church, 14 October, 1696.
2 CONT 	 He preached the sermon for his own ordination from Isaiah IX,
2 CONT 	 10, and had before 1690 been a teacher. He deceased suddenly,
2 CONT 	 March 16, 1704 or 5, aged 40.
2 CONT 	 TYPE Book
2 CONT 	 AUTH Thomas and Samuel White
2 CONT 	 PERI Genealogy of the White Family, from 1607-8 TO 1895.
2 CONT 	 PUBL Republican Press Association. Concord.
2 CONT 	 CALN CS71.W585
2 CONT 	 This book contains the history and genealogy of the William White family of Virginia.
2 CONT 	 DATE 1895
2 CONT 	 MAYFLOWER PILGRIMS
2 CONT 	 There were 104 passengers including men, women, and children, of
2 CONT 	 whom 24 were heads of families. Two of these left only a
2 CONT 	 daughter each, who married into one of the other families.
2 CONT 	 PLYMOUTH MUSEUM
2 CONT 	 Things on exhibit which belonged to our ancestors:
2 CONT 	 Cradle of Peregrine WHITE, first child born in the Colony
2 CONT 	 Bible owned by John ALDEN
2 CONT 	 Bible owned by Gov. BRADFORD
2 CONT 	 Slipper worn by Susannah WHITE
2 CONT 	 Brass candlestick which belonged to William WHITE
2 CONT 	 Silver cup used by Peregrine WHITE--height 2 15/16 inches
2 CONT 	 Signature of Peregrine WHITE on a deed to his sons Jonathon and
2 CONT 	 Peregrine WHITE 1649
2 CONT 	 Halberd found in cellar of John ALDEN'S house
2 CONT 	 Brick from Gov. BRADFORD'S home
2 CONT 	 Christening blanket from BRADFORD'S home
2 CONT 	 Baby cap and bib worn by Peregrine WHITE
2 CONT 	 Painted cabinet used by WHITE family
2 CONT 	 Basement window from ALLYN home (17th century)
2 CONT 	 (Probably many other things)
2 CONT 	 Susannah (Fuller) WHITE Winslow was by her first marriage the
2 CONT 	 mother of the first child born in the Colony; by her second
2 CONT 	 marriage its first bride; the wife of one governor and the
2 CONT 	 mother of another.
2 CONT 	 TYPE Book
2 CONT 	 PERI Samuel Richardson and Josiah Ellsworth
2 CONT 	 AUTH Ruth Ellsworth Richardson
2 CONT 	 PUBL Privately Published
2 CONT 	 CALN CS71.R52
2 CONT 	 This book contains the history and genealogy of the Richardson and Ellsworth families of Massacusetts.
2 CONT 	 DATE 1974
2 CONT 	 Peregrine, son of William White, was born in the cabin of the
2 CONT 	 "Mayflower" as she lay in the Cape Cod harbor, November 20,
2 CONT 	 1620, and received his name from the fact that he was born
2 CONT 	 during the journey or pregrination. The event is of historical
2 CONT 	 interest, as he was the first child of English parents born in a
2 CONT 	 New England colony, the first native of English parents. He was
2 CONT 	 brought up in the family of Governor Edward Winslow in Plymouth
2 CONT 	 colony. He came to Green Harbor with the Winslow family in 1632.
2 CONT 	 He married, about 1647, Sarah Bassett, daughter of William and
2 CONT 	 Elizabeth Bassett, who came from Leyden with other Pilgrims in
2 CONT 	 the ship "Fortune," in 1621. Peregrine White settled on an
2 CONT 	 estate given to him by Mr. Bassett, lying between North and
2 CONT 	 South rivers and not far from the ocean. This tract was granted
2 CONT 	 early to Bassett who was one of the land committee of the
2 CONT 	 Plymouth colony and who became a large landowner. Mr. Bassett
2 CONT 	 resided in Duxbury, Mass, Sandwich and Bridgewater. White
2 CONT 	 settled in Marshfield, Mass. He was admitted a freeman in 1644.
2 CONT 	 In 1637 he was one of the thirty volunteers from Plymouth colony
2 CONT 	 to assist the Massachusetts Bay colonists in the Pequot war. He
2 CONT 	 held various offices of trust and honor. He was rater (assessor)
2 CONT 	 from 1651 to 1655. In November, 1651, it was voted at the town
2 CONT 	 meeting that Mr. White look to "all such persons as live
2 CONT 	 disorderly in the township and give them warning in case they do
2 CONT 	 not redress their course of life that he shall use such means to
2 CONT 	 redress such abuses as he finds in such persons." He was deputy
2 CONT 	 to the general court in 1659 and 1673, grand juror in 1660,
2 CONT 	 selectman in 1661, 1665, 1672. He was on a committee to lay out
2 CONT 	 highways in 1667 and was one of the council of war in 1673,
2 CONT 	 after which he had the title of captain. He died July 20, 1704,
2 CONT 	 and his wife Sarah, January 20, 1711. His will was dated July
2 CONT 	 14, 1704, and is published in the "Mayflower Descendants."
2 CONT 	 TYPE Book
2 CONT 	 PERI New England Families Genealogical and Memorial: Third Series, Volume IV
2 CONT 	 AUTH William Richard Cutter
2 CONT 	 PUBL New England Families Genealogical and Memorial
2 CONT 	 EDTR Bibliographic Information: Cutter, William Richard
2 CONT 	 VOL Volume III
2 CONT 	 EDTN Third Series
2 CONT 	 DATE 1915
2 CONT 	 DATE 15 DEC 2000
1 NOTE Peregrine was b. 7 or 10 Dec 1620 at Cape Cod Harbor, son of William White (C d 100 said "Mayflower C".  His mother was Susanna. Peregrine d. 20 /22 Jul 1620).
