2 CONT 2.1 Mayflower Project Checklist Completed
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan White was born on 04 Jun 1658 in Marshfield, Plymouth Colony, and his parents were Sarah (Bassett) and Peregrine White, Sr. [1] [2] Jonathan's birth was recorded in Yarmouth: "Jonathan White the son of Perigen and Sarah W
2 CONC hite of Marchfeeld (w)as born at Marchfeeld upon the 4th day of June in the year 1658 brought to record by said Jonathan Whit this 18th of May 1700 and recorded by me John Miller, Clerk."[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan was in Yarmouth by 21 Oct 1677 when he testified.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan White married (1) on 02 Feb 1682/83 in Yarmouth, Barnstable, Plymouth Colony to Hester "Esther" Nickerson.[1][2] [4] Hester, daughter of Nicholas and Mary (___) Nickerson was born the last week of Oct 1656, in Yarmouth di
2 CONC ed there 08 Feb 1702/3. 14 May 1706 an agreement was made between the children of Mary Nickerson, late of Yarmouth, widow, deceased, and Jonathan White who had married one of Mary's daughters.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married (2) Elizabeth ______. She died Yarmouth 12 April 1718. "wife of Jonathan White"[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Disputed Information He did not marry Margaret Elizabeth Alexander. The Mayflower Society does not recognize the commonly asserted marriage of Jonathan White to Margaret Elizabeth Alexander[1] Her existence is unsupported by any p
2 CONC rimary sources, and she is most likely fictional. Please do not add her as a spouse to this profile, or her supposed children: Alexander and Margaret. Her origins are traced to a 1939 genealogy by Roscoe White,[5] whose Mayflower 
2 CONC application cited an 1870 family bible.[1] For a more detailed explanation see Parents of Alexander White..
2 CONT Jonathan died between 14 July 1736 (will) and 22 Feb 1737 (probate) in Yarmouth, Barnstable, Massachusetts Bay.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan White of Yarmouth, yeoman, made his will on 14 July 1736, presented 22 February 1737, in which he named his eldest son Jonathan, third son Joseph, son Ebenezer, daughter Elizabeth White (land for her use in "single state 
2 CONC which upon her marriage or death shall be to my son Joseph..."), daughter Esther Drake, daughter Sarah White, daughter Mary Russell, grandson Jonathan Dell, a minor. Son Joseph White to be sole executor. Witnesses were John Jones,
2 CONC  John Eldreg and Thomas Smith. A release was dated 14 November 1741 by John Arnold, administrator on the estate of Esther Drake deceased and guardian to Frances Drake, her heir. On 24 February 1741, another release was signed by E
2 CONC benezer White for his share of the moveable estate of his father.[6][7][1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Children probably born in Yarmouth, this is the order given by the Mayflower Society.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth White, living unmarried 14 July 1736 (father's will)
2 CONT Esther White, b: c 1685; d: 23 Jul 1738 age 53, Warwick, RI
2 CONT Sarah White,
2 CONT Jonathan White, oldest son in father's will
2 CONT Ebenezer White, b: 09 Aug 1698 Yarmouth, Massachusetts
2 CONT Joseph White, b: c 1702;
2 CONT Mary White, probably born before 1703
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 1.3 1.4 1.5 1.6 1.7 1.8 1.9 Wakefield, Robert S. (editor). Sherman, Ruth Wilder and Sherman, Robert Moody (original compilers). Mayflower Families Through Five Generations. Volume Thirteen Family of William White. Th
2 CONC ird Edition. (Plymouth, Mass.: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 2006) p. 10, 16
2 CONT ↑ 2.0 2.1 Massachusetts Vital Records to 1850: Yarmouth compiled by New England Historic Genealogical Society] (NEHGS) NewEnglandAncestors.org v1 p125-126
2 CONT ↑ Yarmouth. Massachusetts: Vital Records, 1620-1850 (Online Database: AmericanAncestors.org, New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2001-2016). Link at AmericanAncestors ($) p. 126
2 CONT ↑ Massachusetts Marriages 1633-1850 at Family History Library, Salt Lake City, UT; FHL#0945512.
2 CONT ↑ White, Roscoe R. "White Family Records: Descendants of Peregrine White, Son of William and Susanna (Fuller) White 1620 to 1939" ([Clarksburg, W. Va. : s.n.], c1939.)pp 22-25
2 CONT ↑ Barnstable County Probate records, Vol. 5:304 (will), 6:59-60 (releases).
2 CONT ↑ Bowman, George Ernest, "Will of Jonathan3 White," Mayflower Descendant, Vol. 9(1907):122-3.
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT
2 CONT White Family of Yarmouth, Yarmouth County, MA" by William P. Davis in 1912 #88 of Library of Cape Cod History and Genealogy. This is cited by Roscoe R. White in "White Family Records: Descendants of Peregrine White, Son of William
2 CONC  and Susanna (Fuller) White 1620 to 1939" as source for Margaret Alexander White. It does not mention her as second wife, only Elizabeth ____
2 CONT His wife Hester died on 08 Feb 1703.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married (2) Elizabeth ______. She died Yarmouth 12 April 1718. "wife of Jonathan White"[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He did not have a son https://www.geni.com/people/Alexander-White/6000000004382899821?through=6000000004547260895 or a daughter Margaret.  He was not married to https://www.geni.com/people/Margaret-White-Fictional/6000000004547260
2 CONC 895?through=6000000004382899821
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 22 Feb 1736/37 in Yarmouth, Barnstable, Massachusetts Bay. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan's will was dated 14 July 1736 and proved 22 Feb 1737. He names his eldest son Jonathan, 3rd son Joseph, son Ebenezer, dau. Elizabeth White, single, daughters Esther Drake, Sarah White, and Mary Russell and grandson Jonath
2 CONC an Dell (under age)[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT The Mayflower Society does not recognize the commonly asserted marriage of Jonathan White to Margaret Elizabeth Alexander. Her existence is unsupported by any primary sources, and she is most likely fictional. Please do not add he
2 CONC r as a spouse to this profile, or her supposed children: Alexander and Margaret. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Most likely she is a mixture of Jonathan's second wife Elizabeth Unknown, and the correct mother of supposed son Alexander White. Her origins are traced to a 1939 genealogy by Roscoe White [5] which in turn cites an 1870 family bi
2 CONC ble. Genealogists do not routinely accept family genealogies written in Bibles. What is acceptable from the 17th century are land, probate or town records. It has been found that town clerks in the Northeast USA especially have be
2 CONC en quite good at keeping records from early America which they will gladly share with researchers. For a more detailed explanation see here.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Contested Information
2 CONT
2 CONT The information below is not currently recognized by the "Mayflower Society" who are the leading authority on Mayflower Genealogy, [1] It is widely believed to be false and is unsupported by primary sources. However as it is also 
2 CONC widely repeated, so it has been included here for reference ...
2 CONT
2 CONT -Jonathan White was born on 04 Jun 1658 in Massachusetts.
2 CONT - Jonathan White married secondly on on 08 Aug 1708 to (Mary Margaret) Elizabeth Alexander. [6] [5] - Jonathan married Margaret Elizabeth Alexander and had at least two children Alexander and Margaret. Also sometimes included are 
2 CONC an older child named Elizabeth (not Jonathan's confirmed oldest daughter) and a youngest child named John. There are also numerous other children that occasionally appear. - He passed away on 22 Feb 1737 in Yarmouth, Barnstable Co
2 CONC unty, Massachusetts. [7]
2 CONT --------------------
