2 CONT AUTH Thomas and Samuel White
2 CONT PERI Genealogy of the White Family, from 1607-8 TO 1895.
2 CONT PUBL Republican Press Association. Concord.
2 CONT CALN CS71.W585
2 CONT This book contains the history and genealogy of the William White family of Virginia.
2 CONT DATE 1895
2 CONT It is stated that he probably married a second time. The date of
2 CONT his birth he carried to the Yarmouth Register office, May 18,
2 CONT 1700.
2 CONT Jonathan settled on Indian land in South Yarmouth at which place
2 CONT tombstones are to be seen of four generations, the third,
2 CONT fourth, fifth, and seventh from Peregrine. The spot where the
2 CONT old house used to stand is still known. He also lived in
2 CONT Middleboro, Mass. Jonathan's grandson, Joseph Jr., had a son
2 CONT Peregrine, who had six children, (I.) Peregrine, now about 84
2 CONT years. (II.) William, 82. He has a cane which was brought over
2 CONT in the Mayflower by William White and handed down from
2 CONT generation to generation. (III.) Alfred, aged about 79. (IV.)
2 CONT Abner, aged 75. (V.) Rufus, aged 71. (VI.) Henry Kirk, who died
2 CONT in Brookline and was buried in Dartmouth, Mass. They live in
2 CONT South Yarmouth and are engaged in the coasting trade.
2 CONT TYPE Book
2 CONT AUTH Thomas and Samuel White
2 CONT PERI Genealogy of the White Family, from 1607-8 TO 1895.
2 CONT PUBL Republican Press Association. Concord.
2 CONT CALN CS71.W585
2 CONT This book contains the history and genealogy of the William White family of Virginia.
2 CONT DATE 1895
2 CONT DATE 26 JUN 2001
