2 CONT TYPE Book
2 CONT PERI New England Families Genealogical and Memorial: Third Series, Volume IV
2 CONT AUTH William Richard Cutter
2 CONT PUBL New England Families Genealogical and Memorial
2 CONT EDTR Bibliographic Information: Cutter, William Richard
2 CONT VOL Volume III
2 CONT EDTN Third Series
2 CONT DATE 1915
2 CONT After living a short time in Weymouth, Peregrine, Jr., removed
2 CONT to Middleboro, Mass. From there he went to Boston, where he
2 CONT worked at his trade as a blacksmith. In 1710 he bought a farm in
2 CONT Concord, Mass., of Obadiah Wheeler, who mar. Elizabeth, dau. of
2 CONT Resolved White, where he lived three years, when he sold it,
2 CONT with one-half pew in the church of that place, and returned to
2 CONT Boston. Here he was baptised, in 1724, at the age of 64, and
2 CONT died in 1727, leaving the following will:
2 CONT "In the name of God, Amen.
2 CONT "I, Peregrine White of Boston, county of Suffolk, and Province
2 CONT of Massachusetts Bay in New England, Blacksmith, being sick and
2 CONT weak in body but of sound disposing mind and memory and calling
2 CONT to mind the uncertainty of this life Do make and ordain this my
2 CONT last will and testament in manner and form following; hereby
2 CONT revoking and making null and void all former and other wills by
2 CONT me at any time heretofore made.
2 CONT First and Principally, I commit my Precious & Immortal Soul into
2 CONT the hands of God, my Creator, Relying solely on his mercy,
2 CONT through the merits of satisfaction of my Lord and Saviour Jesus
2 CONT Christ, for the pardon of my sins and gracious acceptance with
2 CONT him; My Body I commit to the Earth to be decently buried at the
2 CONT direction of my Executrix hereinafter named, and for My Temporal
2 CONT Goods & Estate I will that the same be imployed and bestowed in
2 CONT manner as is hereafter Expressed:
2 CONT That is to say,--I will that my just Debts & Funeral Expenses be
2 CONT well and truly paid and ordained to be paid by my Executrix with
2 CONT all convenient speed next after my Interment.
2 CONT Item,--All the Remainder of My Estate both Real and Personal
2 CONT whatsoever and wheresoever the same is or may be found or of
2 CONT what nature soever, I, Give, Donate, and bequeath the same unto
2 CONT My Dear and Beloved wife Mary to be holden by her, her heirs and
2 CONT assigns forever.
2 CONT Item,--I do hereby nominate, constitute and appoint My said
2 CONT beloved wife Mary to be the sole Executrix of this my last Will
2 CONT & Testament.
2 CONT Signed,
2 CONT Oct. 7, 1727.
2 CONT In witness & ect."
2 CONT TYPE Book
2 CONT AUTH Thomas and Samuel White
2 CONT PERI Genealogy of the White Family, from 1607-8 TO 1895.
2 CONT PUBL Republican Press Association. Concord.
2 CONT CALN CS71.W585
2 CONT This book contains the history and genealogy of the William White family of Virginia.
2 CONT DATE 1895
2 CONT DATE 15 DEC 2000
