2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah White was born in Marshfield, then part of Plymouth Colony, Oct 1663, daughter of Peregrine and Sarah (Bassett) White.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah married at Scituate, Jan 1688/9, Thomas Young.[3][1] Thomas was born in Scituate, 5 Nov 1663, son of George and Hannah (Pinson) Young. He died 25 Dec 1732 in Scituate.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Administration of Thomas' estate was granted to his sons, George and Thomas Young, both of Scituate on 19 Mar 1732. Joseph Young and Joshua Young signed for their share of their father's estate 23 Jan 1737.[1] This number of sons 
2 CONC agrees with Sarah's obituary published in the Boston Newsletter.
2 CONT
2 CONT The death of Sarah (White) Young was reported in "The Boston Weekly News-Letter" of Friday, August 29, 1755:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Saturday August 9th died at Scituate, in the 92d Year of her Age, Mrs. Sarah Young, the virtuous Widow of Mr. Thomas Young, and eldest Daughter of That Mr. Peregine White of Marshfield, who was the First Born English Child in New
2 CONC -England: Being Son of William and Susannah White, born on board the Ship in Cape-Cod Harbour, in the latter Part of Nov. 1620, in which Governor Carver and the Rest of our Plimouth Planters came to New-England, before the Ship le
2 CONC ft said Harbour and set sail for said Plimouth. Said Peregrine White liv'd in great Health and Vigour to the 84th Year of his Age, when a Fever carried Him off on July 22. 1704 as our News-Letter soon after inform'd the Publick: A
2 CONC nd this his Eldest Daughter was Born at Marshfield in Oct 1663, enjoy'd her Senses and Health in good measure, till towards her End, and left four Sons surviving. Two observable Instances of the Long Lives of the very first and se
2 CONC cond Race of Children born in this happy Country."[4][2]
2 CONT Children of Thomas and Sarah (White) Young, all born in Scituate.[1][5][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT George Young b. 30 Nov 1689 Joseph Young b. 3 Oct 1692; d. Scituate Aug 1699 Sarah Young b. 12 Sep 1695; d. Scituate Aug 1699 Thomas Young b. 29 Sep 1698; d. Scituate Aug 1699 Thomas Young b. 18 May 1700 Joseph Young b. 10 Oct 170
2 CONC 1 Ebenezer Young b. 1 April 1703; d. before 23 Jan 1737 (division of father's estate) Joshua Young b. 27 Sept 1704 Isaac Young b. 20 Sept 1706; d. before 23 Jan 1737. Sources
2 CONT
