2 DATE 10 JUN 1707
2 PLAC Yarmouth, Barnstable, Massachusetts Bay Colony, British Colonial America
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorcas (Joyce) Bassett was born on 19 Sep 1640, in Yarmouth, Barnstable County, Massachusetts Bay Colony. She was the daughter of John Joyce and Dorothy (Cotchet) Joyce. Dorcas passed away on 10 Jun 1707, in Yarmouth, Barnstable C
2 CONC ounty, Massachusetts Bay Colony.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Dorcas married Nathaniel Bassett about 1661, in Yarmouth, Barnstable, Massachusetts Bay Colony.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue-
2 CONT
2 CONT # I.Mary- m. 28 Oct. 1690 Thomas Mulford of Truro
2 CONT # II. Nathaniel- m. 16 Dec. 1695 Joannah Borden. Nathaniel moved to Windon, CT
2 CONT # III. Joseph- m.1. 27 Feb. 1706/7 Susanna Hawes (d. 27 Feb. 1718/9), 2. 3 Dec. 1718 Thankful Hallett, d. 6 Jan. 1749/0 Yarmouth
2 CONT # IV. Ruth- d.s.p.
2 CONT # V. Samuel- b. 18 Jan. 1663/4
2 CONT # VI. Hannah- m. Joseph Covell
2 CONT # 4VII. SARAH- b. Yarmouth, MA, m.1. before 1709 JOHN NICKERSON (d. before 1722 in Harwich, MA), 2. 18 Apr. 1728 John Rogers (d. 10 Jan. 1738/9), living in 1744
2 CONT # VIII. Nathan- 26 Sept. 1677 Yarmouth, m. 7 Mar. 1708/9 Yarmouth, Mary Crowell (b. 2 Dec. 1688 # Yarmouth, d. 1742 Chatham), d. 1728 Chatham, MA
2 CONT # IX. Dorcus- b. 1676, d. 9 June 1707 Yarmouth
2 CONT # X. William- m.1. 10 Feb. 1710 Martha Godfrey, 2. Sarah Jenkins
