2 CONT The twentiseventh Day of July in the Twenty fifth year of his Majesty's Reign - George - the Second by the Grace of God of Great Britain France and Ireland King Defender of the Faith Anno Domini - One Thousand Seven Hundred and fi
2 CONC fty one, I Samuel Bassit of East Greenwhich in the County of Kent in the Colony of Rhode Island, yeoman, being now in good health and of a perfect and sound displaying mind and memory Thanks be to almighty God; and Therefore, call
2 CONC ing to mind the mortality of my body and knowing its appointed for all man, ones to Die, Do make and ordain this to be my Last Will and Testament. Imprimis, I Bequeath my Soul to God that Gave it to be Disposed of according to his
2 CONC  Blessed Will and as for my Body I commit, it to the earth to be buried in a Christian Like and decent Marns? at the discretion of my Executor hereinafter named. And as for Such Worldy Estate as it hath Pleased God to Bless me wit
2 CONC h in this world I Give devise and dispose of it as follows... Viz: it is my Will and I do order that in the first place all my Just Debts and funeral expences be fully Satisfied and paid, Item, I Give and Bequeath to my Son, Samue
2 CONC l Bassit, all my Tools of any kind whatsoever, and Twenty Shilling, Ten Bills of Credit. Item, I give and Bequeath to my four daughters Namely--- Elizabeth Vaughan, Hannah Biddlecome, Sarah Bassit and Dorkis Bassit, each of them T
2 CONC en Shillings in Bills of Credit to be paid by my executor. Item, I bequeath to my said daughter Dorkis my worstead combs together with all my hand held goods to be..... by my executor. Item it is my Will and I do order that my Exe
2 CONC cutor Shall Sell my Dwelling house and my Lall? of Land whereon my Said house stands in East Greenwhich aforesaid, and out of the mony arrising thereon and the remaining part of the mony arrising by the sale of my house and Land; 
2 CONC aforesaid, I give and bequeath it all to my ???? Daughter Mary Bassit; to be paid to her by my Executor... and I do Make ordain and appoint my son Samuel Bassit my Executor to Execute this my Last Will and Testament. In Witness wh
2 CONC ere of I have hereunto Set my Hand and Seal This Dan and year first above written. Signed, Sealed Published. Samuel (his X mark) Bassett By the Testator to be his mark Last Will and Testament In Presence of Wm Greene Wm Greene Jun
2 CONC . February 23, 1760 Marhan Greene
