1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph Covell, son of Nathaniel and Sarah (Niokerson) Covell, born at Monomoit about 1675, married first Lydia Stewart, daughter of Ensign Hugh of Monomoit, about 1700. She died not long after and he married second
2 CONC  Hannah Bassett, daughter of Nathaniel of Yarmouth and sister of Nathan of Monomoit, March 1, 1703-4.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Joseph Covell: 
2 CONT
2 CONT By wife Lydia: 
2 CONT * 1. Lydia, b. July 12, 1701 (Chat. Rec.), m. Thomas Nickerson, Jr., May 16, 1716(Chat. Rec.).
2 CONT
2 CONT By wife Hannah: (order uncertain): 
2 CONT * 2. Sarah, b....; m. Willam Nickerson ("Red Stockings"), son of William, about 1723 (Osborn Nickerson papers). 
2 CONT * 3. James, b...; m.1st Mehitable Nickerson, dau. of Samuel of Harwich, Aug. 4, 1727 (Har. Re.). She died Nov. 26, 1761(Chat. Rec) and he m. 2nd Ruth(Crowell) Kelley, widow of Amos Kelley of Yarmouth, Sept 16, 1762 (Yar. Rec.) . 
2 CONT *4. Nathaniel, b...; m. Mary Chase, dau. of Isaac of Yarmouth(Int. July 20, 1740, Yar. Rec.). 
2 CONT * 5. Joseph, b...;m. Hannah Bassett, dau. of Nathan, and died not too long after marriage, leaving widow and daughter Hannah. 
2 CONT * 6. Possibly a dau. Constant, who m. Ebenezer Nickerson, son of Thomas. 
2 CONT * 7. Possibly a dau. Dorcas, who m. James Nickerson, son of William."
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah4 Bassett, (Nathaniel3, William2, William1, b. ?; m. Joseph2 Covell (Nathaniel1).[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah's death date has been listed as 10 Jan 1709 but there are no sources. This date is 11 years before the birth of her son Nathaniel Covell) Holladay was born. FamilySearch has her death date as 1729 but there is no source att
2 CONC ached.[4] Her "death before birth of son" throws an error in the database and in order to fix this I have changed the death date to 1729. So neither the original of 1709 or 1729 are sourced.
