1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of Mayflower passenger Samuel Fuller
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Samuel Fuller'''  was born about 1628/1629 at Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts, and died on  17 AUG 1695 (gravestone) or 24 Aug 1695 (Church record). The Church record reads "Mr. Samuel Fuller, the Teacher of the chh at Midleb
2 CONC ury a sincere Godly man whom wee had the last yeare dismissed to that service, dyed August 24 being about 66 yeares old a great losse to that place."
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Samuel Fuller, born before 20 January 1580 and died between 9 August 1633 and 26 September 1633 in Plymouth, Massachusetts; his mother was Bridget Lee, who died after 1633. His parents were married 27 May 1617 in
2 CONC  Leiden, Netherlands.
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Before 1655 he had a liaison with Ruth Bassett; she married John Sprague in 1655. Their son was John Sprague,
2 CONT
2 CONT Before 1658 he married an unknown woman.  She was the mother of Samuel and possibly of Elizabeth.  Wikipedia gives her name as Susanna.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Between 11 April 1663 and 2 May 1667 he married Elizabeth (Nichols) Bowen, daughter of John Nichols and widow of Thomas Bowen. They had 5 children: John, Experience, Hannah, Mercy, and Isaac.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biological Child of Samuel Fuller and Ruth Bassett
2 CONT
2 CONT *Lt. John Sprague, b. Abt 1656, Duxbury, Plymouth Co., MA, d. 6 Mar 1727/28, Lebanon, New London Co., CT (Age ~ 72 years) [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel Fuller and his wives
2 CONT
2 CONT # Samuel b. c. 1658, Plymouth, d. 6 Sept 1728, 70th year in Plympton; m. 7 Jan 1685/6 Plymouth, Mercy Eaton. (See MBD 1:461 and MD 3:14 for 11 children. Samuel Fuller, b. 1659, d. 6 Sep 1728, Plympton, Plymouth Co., MA (Age 69 yea
2 CONC rs) [8]
2 CONT # Elizabeth Fuller b. 1663-1666, Plymouth; d. before June 1724; m. 24 May 1694, Middleboro Samuel Eaton [15] Elizabeth Fuller, b. 1666, Middleboro, Plymouth Co., MA,, d. Yes, date unknown [8]
2 CONT # John Fuller b. c. 1667 Plymouth; d. c. 1710 ae 42; m. c 1688 Mercy Nelson. John Fuller, b. 1663, Middleboro, Plymouth Co., MA,, d. Abt 1710, Middleboro, Plymouth Co., MA, USA (Age 47 years) [8]
2 CONT # Experience Fuller, b. c 1669 Plymout; d. between 16April 1725 (deed) and 21 Dec 1728 (husbands estate admin) m. James Wood [15] Experience Fuller, b. Abt 1661, Middleboro, Plymouth Co., MA,, d. Yes, date unknown [8]
2 CONT # Hannah Fuller b. c. 1671 Plymouth d. between 11 june 1707 (deed) and 1709 (husband's 2nd marriage); m. Eleazer Lewis after 27 July 1696 [15] Hannah Fuller, b. 1668, Middleboro, Plymouth Co., MA,, d. Yes, date unknown [8]
2 CONT # Mercy Fuller b. c. 1672/3 Plymouth; d. 25 Sept 1735 buried in Eastham; m. Daniel Cole [15] Mercy Fuller, b. Abt 1656, Middleboro, Plymouth Co., MA d. Yes, date unknown [8]
2 CONT # Isaac Fuller b. c. 1674/5 Plymouth; d. pr 16 Nov 1727 Middleboro (adm.); m. Mary Pratt, perhaps widow of Joshua; [15] Isaac Fuller, b. Abt 1675, Middleboro, Plymouth Co., MA, , d. 1727, Brockton, Plymouth Co., MA, USA (Age ~ 52 
2 CONC years) [8]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 siblings (no source cited)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From American Ancestors - New England Historic Genealogical Society - Founded 1845
2 CONT
2 CONT Pilgrim Village Families Sketch: Samuel Fuller (Samuel's father), by Robert Charles Anderson
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.americanancestors.org/pilgrim-families-samuel-fuller/
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Samuel and Agnes Fuller:
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. A child was buried on June 29, 1615 in Leiden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel and Bridget Fuller:
2 CONT
2 CONT *1. A child born in Leiden, who came to Plymouth after May 1627. Bradford’s list of passengers stated “His wife was behind, and a child which came afterwards.” If so, this child was not mentioned in Samuel’s will. Some have specul
2 CONC ated that the Bridget Fuller who married Henry Sirkman in Plymouth on September 30, 1641 might be this child.
2 CONT *2. Mercy was born after May 22, 1627. She was still living as of Bradford’s list of passengers made in 1651, but there is no further record.
2 CONT *3. '''Samuel''' was born about 1629. He married (1) a woman whose name is unknown and had one son. He married (2) Elizabeth (Nichols) Bowen between April 11, 1663, and May 2, 1667, and had six children. He died in Middleboro on A
2 CONC ugust 17, 1695.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From his Find A Grave page:
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Dr. Samuel Fuller, who arrived on the ship, "Mayflower."
2 CONT
2 CONT And Son of Bridget Lee, b. ? d. c 1667.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reverend Samuel Fuller was the son of Dr Samuel & Bridget Lee Fuller and one of five children.  On 11 April 1658, he married the widowed Elizabeth Nichols. They were the parents of 7 children-Samuel, Elizabeth (Eaton), John, Exper
2 CONC ience (Wood), Hannah (Lewis), Mercy (Cole)and Isaac. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT *  Samuel Fuller (1580 - 1633)
2 CONT *  Bridget Lee Fuller (1600 - 1667)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT *  Elizabeth Nichols Fuller (1637 - 1713)*
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT *  Samuel Fuller (1659 - 1728)*
2 CONT *  Mercy Fuller Cole (1672 - 1735)*
2 CONT *  Isaac Fuller (1674 - 1727)*
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Buried at the highest summit of this graveyard (courtesy of Mary Ellen DiCarlo)
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Nemasket Hill Cemetery, Middleboro, Plymouth County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * Putnam, Israel Warburton. First Church of Middleborough, Mass (C.C.P. Moody, Boston, 1854) Page 26-7: "But his ministry, after his ordination, was very brief, lasting for only seven months and twenty-one days. He died in the sev
2 CONC enty-first year of his age,and was interred in the first burying-place, commonly called the Hill."
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-40001-288287319/rev-samuel-fuller-in-familysearch-family-tree FamilySearch Family Tree] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 3 2018, 3:22:35 UT
2 CONC C''
2 CONT * However there is new information, published in Volume 67, Number 2, page 177 of the Mayflower Descendant: An Illustrated Quarterly Magazine of Pilgrim Genealogy, History and Biography (Massachusetts Society of Mayflower Descenda
2 CONC nts, Summer 2019), which is not yet available in the NHEGS database. This article, entitled Lt. John Sprague (ca. 1655–1727/8) of Duxbury, Mass., and Lebanon, Conn., an illegitimate son of Samuel2 Fuller (Samuel1)? by Christopher 
2 CONC Challender Child, an NEHGS staff member currently referenced on the NEHGS website. According to Wikitree member A (Fasg), in a comment on this profile, the article states that John may not have been the biological son of John Spra
2 CONC gue, and provides a case for his biological father to have been Samuel Fuller Jr, as follows: “At the General Court at Plymouth on 6 Jun 1655, John2 Sprague, son of Francis, and Ruth Bassett, daughter of William, of Duxbury were "
2 CONC present[ed] for fornication before they were married..." indicating that the infant John was born less than 9 months after the wedding. [4] This alone would be genealogically unremarkable, but comparison of the Y-DNA of descendant
2 CONC s of eldest son John3 to younger sons Samuel and William and other Sprague children show John3 was not John2 Sprague's biological child. These descendants match the Y-DNA haplogroup of the Fullers of Plymouth. Only Samuel2 Fuller 
2 CONC (Samuel1), born 1625, Plymouth Colony, died 17 August 1695, Middleboro, Plymouth County, was living near Duxbury. [4]
