1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===(Lieut.) John Sprague===
2 CONT * Birth:	Circa 1657 - Duxbury, Plymouth, Massachusetts
2 CONT * Death:	Mar 6 1727 - Lebanon, New London, Connecticut
2 CONT * Parents:	Samuel Fuller, Ruth Bassett.....DNA say's Dr. Samuel Fuller was Lt. John Sprague's father by Ruth Bassett...NOT John Sprague Sr.
2 CONT * Married: 1) Lydia 2) Lois Standish
2 CONT * Children:	Benjamin Sprague, Irene (Sprague) Fish, Lydia (Sprague) Way, Ruth Sprague, Capt. Ephraim Sprague, Captain John Sprague, Samuel Sprague
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT John Sprague: The Father Who Raised Him
2 CONT
2 CONT John was raised as the son of John2 (Francis1) Sprague and his wife Ruth Bassett of Duxbury, Massachusetts[1] [2] [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Fuller: His Biological Father
2 CONT
2 CONT However there is new information, published in Volume 67, Number 2, page 177 of the Mayflower Descendant: An Illustrated Quarterly Magazine of Pilgrim Genealogy, History and Biography (Massachusetts Society of Mayflower Descendant
2 CONC s, Summer 2019), which is not yet available in the NHEGS database. This article, entitled Lt. John Sprague (ca. 1655–1727/8) of Duxbury, Mass., and Lebanon, Conn., an illegitimate son of Samuel2 Fuller (Samuel1)? by Christopher Ch
2 CONC allender Child, an NEHGS staff member currently referenced on the NEHGS website. According to Wikitree member A (Fasg), in a comment on this profile, the article states that John may not have been the biological son of John Spragu
2 CONC e, and provides a case for his biological father to have been Samuel Fuller Jr, as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT >At the General Court at Plymouth on 6 Jun 1655, John2 Sprague, son of Francis, and Ruth Bassett, daughter of William, of Duxbury were "present[ed] for fornication before they were married..." indicating that the infant John was b
2 CONC orn less than 9 months after the wedding. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT This alone would be genealogically unremarkable, but comparison of the Y-DNA of descendants of eldest son John3 to younger sons Samuel and William and other Sprague children show John3 was not John2 Sprague's biological child. The
2 CONC se descendants match the Y-DNA haplogroup of the Fullers of Plymouth. Only Samuel2 Fuller (Samuel1), born 1625, Plymouth Colony, died 17 August 1695, Middleboro, Plymouth County, was living near Duxbury. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Documents will likely never answer whether John2 Sprague knew that he was not the biological father of his wife's first child.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Sprague-391
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage to Lydia Unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Circa 1684, John Sprague married Lydia Unknown in Duxbury (who is not to be confused with Lydia Goffe of Charlestown and Malden, see note above). He was a constable in Duxbury, and prominent in the church, and his wife's first nam
2 CONC e was provided in land deeds in Duxbury and Bristol[1] [3], and in various vital records shown in this profile[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia (Unknown) Sprague, wife of Lt. John Sprague died July 18, 1725 in Lebanon[7] [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Move to Lebanon, Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT Circa 1702 they moved to Lebanon, CT, and became prominent citizens there. He was a selectman, served in the General Court, and in the militia as Ensign and then Lieutenant[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage to Lois Standish
2 CONT
2 CONT Lt John Sprague remarried Lois Standish March 21, 1726[8] [1] [9]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lt John Sprague died March 26, 1727/8[10] [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT His will mentions his widow Lois (Stanidish) Sprague, grandaughter Mary Way and his son Ephraim [1] Land records show he distributed considerable property to other children before he died [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Sprague & Lydia:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Ephraim, born March 15, 1684-5[11], who married Deborah Woodworth first[12], and second married Mary Unknown[1]
2 CONT # Benjamin, b. July 15, 1686[11], who married Mary Woodworth, Prudence Miner, and Abigail Hodge[13] [1]
2 CONT # Samuel, who married Mary Burt[1]
2 CONT # John, who married Mary Babcock[14] and Hannah Burt[1]
2 CONT # Lydia, who married July 19, 1713, George Way of Lebanon, CT[1]
2 CONT # Irene, who married July 9, 1723, Aaron Fish[15], son of Samuel and Sarah Fish[1]
2 CONT # Ruth born Sept. 5, 1704[16]; who married Nov. 12, 1724, Clodus Dillis[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Sprague Families in America", by Dr. Warren Vincent Sprague, page 12.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Sprague was Constable of Duxbury in 1692, and held other public trusts there at various times from 1684 to 1701. He was one of the conspicuous members of the Church in Duxbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1702-3, January 8. John Sprague, "Mariner," and Lydia his wife, of Duxbury, deeded 40 acres of upland with dwelling house and barn standing thereon in duxbury for 125 pounds to Israel Sylvester of Scituate. His last deed in Duxbur
2 CONC y was given January 28, 1702-3. 1703. He removed to Lebanon, CT, probably in the spring of this year and became the owner of much land there.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1705, 1710, 1714. Selectman, Lebanon.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1706, May and Oct.; 1708, May and Oct.; 1709, May and Oct.; 1711, 1713, in May; 1714, 1716, 1718, in Oct.; 1719, May and Oct.; 1720, May. Rep. from Lebanon to General Court.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1706. He bore the title of Ensign; and of Lieut. in 1710-20.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1712-3, Jan. 8. He deeded to son Benjamin Sprague, land in Lebanon.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1713-4, Jan. 19. He deeded to son John Sprague, 120 acres of land.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1714, Sept. 21. He deeded to George Way, Jr., of Lyme, 100 acres of land.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1715-6, Jan. 18. He deeded to son Samuel sprague 120 acres of land.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1718, July 14. John Sprague, Sr., and John Sprague, Jr., agree to liberate Jack, an Indian slave bought by them when he has served faithfully 12 years, and give him a colt which they agree to keep free of charge until Jack sees fi
2 CONC t to dispose of him. They also give him a ewe sheep, which they agree to keep and her increase for two years.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1726, July 6. Will mentions beloved wife, Mrs. Lois Sprague, granddaughter, Mary Way, and son Ephraim Sprague.
2 CONT
2 CONT From George Sawyer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lt. John Sprague was a weaver and legislator.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT * [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=116176792 Find A Grave Memorial# 116176792]
2 CONT * Person ID 	I115897  	Sprague Project
2 CONT * http://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:John_Sprague_%285%29_
2 CONT **↑ "Lebanon Vital Records", in Connecticut, United States. The Barbour Collection of Connecticut Town Vital Records, Vol. 22, p. 190. SPRAGUE, John, Lieut., d. Mar. 6, 1727/8.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Married #1 Lydia _______
2 CONT
2 CONT Married #2 Lois Abel
2 CONT
2 CONT His son Ephraim is mentioned in his will.
2 CONT --------------------
