2 CONT He was married to Lydia Unknown about 1684 in Duxbury, Plymouth Co., MA. (47) Lydia Unknown w as born about 18 Jul 1658 in Duxbury, Plymouth Co., MA. She died on 18 Jul 1725 in Lebanon, N ew London Co., CT.(48) I have found no ref
2 CONC erences to support the name of Goff. However, this name has been reporte d to me by Warren H. Hasty as the result of "submitted by a person researching the Goff famil y". In follow-up correspondence between Warren H. Hasty and Dr.
2 CONC  David W. Lamberts, Mr. Hasty repo rts the following: My information was not from my research but through a Name Matching program sponsored by th e Silicon Valley PAF Users Group. I received two matches for John Sprague and Lydia 
2 CONC Goff and one match for a John Sprague and L ois Standish with approximate birth dates, etc. for John Sprague and spouses as follows: Kay Lewis Baker John Sprague and Lydia Goff 166 East 3620 North RIN Number for Lydia - 566 Provo,
2 CONC  UT 86404
2 CONT
2 CONT United Ancestries Inc. John Sprague and Lydia Goff 2530 West South Sute No RIN Number shown Taylor's Landing Taylorville, UT 84118
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Margaret Hansen John Sprague and Lois Standish 26600 S.E. 15th Street RIN Number for Lois - 3667 Issaquah, WA 98027-8240
2 CONT
2 CONT In writing to above persons, you should include their RIN number where shown above so they ca n quickly find this data on their computer. Several months ago, I called the Baker family reg arding their source of data on this marria
2 CONC ge of John Sprague and Lydia Goff and as I recall t hey stated it was from the Mormon Ancestral File. Unfortunately I did not follow through on a ny further research on this matter.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: December 11, 1996 by Richard E. Weber, The Composite Sprague Data Base. An extensive follow-up study was conducted by Dr. David Winton Lamberts to assist me in my pr oject efforts. The results are that no conclusive evidence
2 CONC  has been isolated to support Lydi a Goff(e) as the name of the wife of John Sprague. It would appear that the name Goffe come s from confusion between this John and John Sprague, son of Ralph Sprague, the 1628 immigrant . Only sc
2 CONC attered Family Group Sheets in the Ancestral File support the name Goffe and no othe r published reference was indicated by any correspondent. Lacking further evidence, I feel st rongly that this Lydia should be considered to have
2 CONC  an unknown maiden name.
