2 CONT
2 CONT "Sprague Families in America", by Dr. Warren Vincent Sprague, page 11.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Sprague and Ruth Bassett Sprague resided for a time in Marshfield, as the birth of their daughter Ruth is recorded there. This John, more likely than John of William, was a Counsellor of Sir Edmund Andros. He was slain in Pie
2 CONC rce's fierce fight at Pawtucket in Philip's war, March 26, 1676. His estate was appraised in 1676 and was sworn to by the widow Ruth Sprague. She afterwards married ______ Thomas. 
2 CONT
