1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "Sprague Families in America", by Dr. Warren Vincent Sprague, page 12. William Sprague was chosen "Surveyor of Highways" March 17, 1708. He was drowned, November 25, 1712, by the upsetting of a whale boat. 1716, Ap
2 CONC ril 2. Grace Sprague, widow of William Sprague, late of Duxbury, deceased, appointed guardian of Jethro, Terah, Ruth and Zerviah Sprague, minor children of said Grace Sprague. Her will dated 1748, January 13, proved April 3, 1758,
2 CONC  mentioned sons Jethro Sprague and Terah Sprague; daughter Zerviah Chandler; "my Six Grand Children the Children of my Daughter Ruth late deced viz/ William Keen, Levi Keen, Abel Keen, Samuel Keen, Josiah Keen and Grace Cole"; gra
2 CONC nddaughters Silvine Sprague and Grace Sprague; grandson William Sprague.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.sprague-database.org/genealogy/getperson.php?personID=I15216&tree=SpragueProject
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT William drowned when the Whaleboat he was in upset.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT m: Aft. April 23, 1700 in Duxbury, Plymouth, MA 
2 CONT
2 CONT d: November 25, 1712 Drowned - upsetting of a whale boat
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Surveyor of Highways in 1708. He ws drowned by the upsetting of  a whale boat.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is also a "sprague house" listed in historical listings that is in Danvers. unknown if it is from these spragues.
2 CONT --------------------
