2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Sprague-51
2 CONT Samuel Sprague (abt. 1670 - 1740)
2 CONT
2 CONT Lieut. Samuel Sprague
2 CONT Born about 1670 in Duxbury, Plymouth, British Colonial Americamap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Son of John Sprague Sr. and Ruth (Bassett) Thomas
2 CONT Brother of John Sprague [half], Elizabeth (Sprague) Sampson, Ruth (Sprague) Smith, William Sprague, Desire (Sprague) Gifford and Dorcas (Sprague) Hatch
2 CONT Husband of Ruth (Alden) Sprague — married 29 Nov 1694 in Duxbury, Plymouth, Province of Massachusetts Baymap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Father of Noah Sprague, Elizabeth (Sprague) Chapman, Nathaniel Sprague, Samuel Sprague, Mary Sprague, Priscilla (Sprague) West, Micah Sprague and Ruth Sprague
2 CONT Died 25 Jul 1740 at about age 70 in Rochester, Plymouth, Massachusetts Bay Colonymap
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile managers: Vic Watt private message [send private message], Tom Gerber private message [send private message], and Ann Borgers private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 14 Feb 2023 | Created 11 Sep 2010
2 CONT This page has been accessed 3,305 times.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Sprague was chosen constable of Duxbury, March 6, 1700, and town clerk, March 16, 1709, which latter post he held but one year. He was probably a carpenter by occupation, as the Town Records for 1708 show his receipt for th
2 CONC e sum of one hundred and eighty pounds in full for erecting the meeting house in Duxbury. He moved to Rochester, Mass., about 1710; and died there July 25, 1740, in the 71st year of his age. The widow, Ruth Sprague and Noah Spragu
2 CONC e were appointed administrators of his estate. The descendants of this Samuel became very numerous for a time and were prominent and useful citizens in the communities in which they lived. For some reason the name became almost ex
2 CONC tinct.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Sprague was born about 1670 to John Sprague and Mary Bassett.
2 CONT
2 CONT On November 29, 1694 he married Ruth Alden at Duxbury, Plymouth, Massachusetts.[2] The couple had seven children: Noah, Elizabeth, Nathaniel, Samuel, Mary, Priscilla, Micah, and Ruth. He was a "housewright" (carpenter) by professi
2 CONC on. He held the military title of Lieutenant. He was a town clerk at Duxbury, served as an attorney. [3].
2 CONT
2 CONT Lt. "Samul" Sprague died on 25 July 1740 at Rochester, Plymouth, Massachusetts Bay Colony.[4] Samuel is buried at the Center Cemetery in Rochester. The inscription on his weathered gravestone says:[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Here lyes ye
2 CONT body of Liutt Samll
2 CONT Sprague Who Decd
2 CONT July Ye 25th
2 CONT 1740 In
2 CONT Ye 71st year"
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel and Ruth (Alden) Sprague had the following (7) children:[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Noah, b. 18 Jan. 1696; m. Sarah Hammond
2 CONT Elizabeth, b. 4 July 1699; m. Isaac Chapman
2 CONT Nathaniel, b. 10 Jan. 1701/2; m. Keziah Baker
2 CONT Samuel, b. 23 June 1704; m. Ann/Anna Barlow
2 CONT Mary, b. 20 Dec. 1706; died 19 April 1708
2 CONT Priscilla, b. 18 March 1708/9; m. Benjamin Hammond, m. Rev. Thomas West
2 CONT Micah, b. before 1714; m. Elizabeth Turner
2 CONT Ruth b. 30 Aug 1714; d. 9 Apr 1730. The 2002 Mayflower Families Alden book not list Ruth, but she is clearly their daughter.
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Warren Vincent Sprague, M.D. comp. and pub., Sprague families in America, The Tuttle company, printers in Rutland, Vt, 1913. (Online at Archive.org) Page 14
2 CONT ↑ Vital Records of Duxbury, Massachusetts Boston, Massachusetts : New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1911. Page 316. Accessed on 15 Dec2020 at HathiTrust.org. Page 316
2 CONT ↑ Woodworth-Barnes p 164
2 CONT ↑ Vital records of Rochester, Massachusetts Boston, Mass, Pub. by the New England historic genealogial society, at the charge of the Eddy town-record fund, 1914. Vol. 2, Marriages and Deaths, Page 437. Accessed on 15 Dec 2020 at H
2 CONC athiTrust.org. Page 427
2 CONT ↑ Find a Grave, database and images (https://www.findagrave.com: accessed 15 December 2020), memorial page for Lieut. Samuel Sprague (1670–25 Jul 1740), Find A Grave: Memorial #107936660, citing Center Cemetery, Rochester, Plymout
2 CONC h County, Massachusetts, USA; Maintained by Caryn (contributor 47509429).
2 CONT ↑ Esther Littleford Woodsworth-Barnes, Mayflower Families through Five Generations, Vol 16, Part 1, The Descendants of John Alden, General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 2002. "The Silver Book" Page 164
2 CONT Source: Woodworth-Barnes, Esther Littleford and Williams, Alicia Crane, Mayflower Families through Five Generations, Vol 16 Part 1 of 3, John Alden, Boston, Mass.: General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 2002. p163-164.
2 CONT Source: Warren Vincent Sprague, M.D. comp. and pub., Sprague families in America, The Tuttle company, printers in Rutland, Vt, 1913. (Online at Archive.org)
2 CONT Source: The Sprague Project The Sprague Project web site
