1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Basset-599
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethia Bassett was named executor of her father's estate in his will dated 12 Jan 1735/6, at Bridgewater.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Bethia married William Coddington of Norton between 12 Jan 1735/6 and 19 Sep 1738. He had previously been married to Elizabeth Jones and apparently by her had a daughter Abigail. William bought land in Norton in 1721.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 19 Sep 1738, William and wife Bethia sold the homestead of their father Joseph Bassett of Bridgewater, deceased.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 Sept 1657, William Coddington of Norton, housewright, and Bethia his wife, and Samuel Phillips of Norton and Lydia his wife, sold two thirds of a lot that had beloged to their father Joseph Basset to Joseph Alger.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Coddington and wife Bethia, of Norton, acknowledged a deed of sale, dated 13 Dec 1763, of swampland on 21 May 1764. This is the last known record for Bethia.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple had no known children.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 5th Generation descendant of John Billington and 4th generation descandant of Francis Eaton.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
