2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Leonard3 of the Solomon Leonard line was married to Hannah Jennings.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT Memorial: Genealogical, Historical, and Biographical, of Solomon Leonard, 1637, Duxbury and Bridgewater, Massachusetts, and some of His Descendants. By Manning Leonard, Southbridge, Mass. Press of Knapp, Peck & Thomson, Auburn N.Y
2 CONC . 1896, page 61. < [https://archive.org/details/memorialgenealog00leon/page/60/mode/1up?view=theater Archive.Org] >
2 CONT
2 CONT 18.  Joseph Leonard3 (John2, Solomon1) brother of preceding, b. — : m. Nov. 19, 1712 Hannah, daughter of Richard Jennings of Bridgewater, (who was one of fourteen soldiers from that town in the ''Narragansett Fight'', Dec 19, 1675
2 CONC , and with the exception of Daniel Hudson, the only one living to draw his share of land uranted bv the State Oct. 17. 1788.)
2 CONT
2 CONT The births of all his children are recorded in Bridgewater, excepting the youngest who was born in Pomfret, Conn., where he seems to have removed about 1780. The family, probably did not remain long, and I have found it impossible
2 CONC  to trace them.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Hannah Jennings and Joseph Leonard were:
2 CONT * 69.  Joseph 4 b March 17, 1713
2 CONT * 70. Hannah.* twin to Joseph 
2 CONT * 71. Moses,M^ March 22, 1714.
2 CONT * 72. Seth,* b. Oct. 6, 1715.
2 CONT * 78. Timothy  Jnlv 6, 171-S.
2 CONT * 74. Rebecca,^ b. Sept. — . 1721.
2 CONT * 75. Mehitable,  Sei)t. 5, 1724.
2 CONT * 76. Thankful,^ b. ^[av — , 1726.
2 CONT * 77. Ebenezer,^ b. May 2<>. 1728.
2 CONT * 78. Betsey,^ b. Sejjt. .15, 1780
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Jennings (from Sandwich perhaps) m. Mary Bassett, and settled in S. B., and had .Joseph, Samuel 1703 ; Ephraim, Elizabeth, Anne, Mary and Hannah were also his children probably. He d. 1751, his w. 1734. Joseph d. 1756. - E
2 CONC lizabeth ni. Wm. Ames 1721.— Anne m. John Cavener (or Carver) 1718. - Mary m. John Tobey 1710.— Hannah m. .Joseph Leonard 1712. Ephraim m. Deliverance Washburn 1719. and had JIary 1720, Ephraim 1722. Sarah 172S.'- [Hist, of Bridge
2 CONC water. p. 203.]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
