1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph, his wife Elizabeth, and son Edmund were all baptized at the same time 5 July 1719 Church of Rumney Marsh, Chelsea.  There is just the one child born and it presumed that Elizabeth died in 1721.  It is not k
2 CONC nown really when Joseph died, but he is not mentioned in the will of his father who died in 1743. There is some information in Documentary History of Chelsea, volume II, available on Google books.  Information also in 1952-1954 is
2 CONC sues of NEHGR. The parentage of his wife Elizabeth Chamberlain has not been determined.  A few possibilities have been proposed.  My favorite is that she was born 29 May 1699 (along with twin Mary), the daughter of Samuel Chamberl
2 CONC ain and Elizabeth Emerson of Chelmsford.  Another proposed set of parents is John and Hannah Chamberlain as it has been suggested that they had a daughter Elizabeth born in 1692, but that would make Elizabeth 26 at the time of her
2 CONC  marriage to Joseph which seems too old.  The suggestion of John and Hannah as parents comes from the NEHGR and notes these "probably" as her parents, but that might be because their daughter Mary seems to have married Daniel Whit
2 CONC temore.  An old Whittemore genealogy book gave her father as Richard Chamberlain, but stated her birth date as 29 May 1699 and also said she was a twin.  But that Elizabeth is the daughter of Samuel.  But she would be the right ag
2 CONC e for marrying in 1718.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Whittemore's older brother Daniel (born 1689/90) married Mary Chamberlain and there seems to be evidence that Mary Chamberlain was a daughter of John and Hannah.  
2 CONT
2 CONT This Whittemore line were in Chelmsford at some point so Elizabeth coming from Chelmsford would make sense.  So far, I have not located any helpful will information for any of the proposed parents.
