1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "He was a soldier in the French wars. In 1760 he was in Captain Cheever's company at Ft. Cumberland and in 1762 served in Captain William Jones company. He served 7 years in the Revolutionary War. In 1777 he was ta
2 CONC ken prisoner by the British and taken to England where he was confined in the old mill prison in Plymouth. He was exchanged after the war was over. Upon his return he settled in Jay, Maine."
2 CONT  - Above quote taken from book published in 1907 - Historic Homes and Institutions and Genealogical and Personal Memoirs of Worcester County, Massachusetts - With a History of Worcester Society of Antiquity, Volume 2 - by Ellery B
2 CONC icknell Crane - pg. 400.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children were Timothy, born 7 Sep 1763 Needham.
2 CONT   - was a soldier in the Revolution 6 months in 1780. Sarah, born Needham 12 Apr 1768.
2 CONT   - married Thomas Dascomb, resided in Maine. Ebenezer, born 16 Dec 1772. Arnold, born Needham 22 Feb 1775.
