1 NAME Ichabod /Clark/
2 GIVN Ichabod
2 SURN Clark
2 _MARNM Clark
2 NICK Clarke
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 APR 1716
2 ADDR
3 CITY Middleborough
3 STAE Massachusetts
1 DEAT
2 DATE 20 SEP 1805
2 ADDR
3 CITY Sharon
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From information on the family of Joseph Clark of Braintree, by Frank O. Clark, Ph.D.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://sciway3.net/clark/clark/ichabodclark1716.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Ichabod Clark
2 CONT *1716, April 23: born in Middleborough, Plymouth County, Province of Massachusetts, to Nathan Clark and Jemima (who died two days after the birth). Moved with his elder brother Nathan to Stoughton.
2 CONT *1740, Dec. 20: Filed his intention to marry Sarah Wittamore (c1714-1792, daughter of Daniel Whittemore b. 1663 and Lydia Bassett of Bridgewater, d. 1756, the last of 10 children) of Malden (The Record of Births, Marriages and Dea
2 CONC ths and Intentions of Marriage in the Town of Stoughton 1727-1800 and in the Town of Canton 1797-1845 preceded by the records of the south precinct of Dorchester from 1715 to 1727 p29) 
2 CONT *1741, Mar. 30: Married in Malden by Rev. Joseph Simpson (p. 267).  Settled in Stoughtonham (present Sharon) shortly after.
2 CONT *1742, Feb. 23: first son Nehemiah born in Stoughtonham. (VR Stoughton: Stoughton 1727-1800, Canton 1797-1845 preceded by the records of the South Precinct of Dorchester 1715-1727)
2 CONT *1742, April: Nehemiah baptized.
2 CONT *1743, Aug. 7: second son Silvanus born ("Record of births, marriages and deaths and intentions of marriage in the town of Stoughton 1727-1800 and in the town of Canton 1797-1845 preceded by the records of the south precinct of Do
2 CONC rchester from 1715 to 1727", p. 49)
2 CONT *1745, Oct. 4: third son Asa born (VR Sharon, p. 17)
2 CONT *1747, Aug. 23: fourth son William or Billy baptized. He was a twin of Sarah or Salle, who was baptized on the same day, and who vanished from records shortly after, probably dying young (VR Sharon p. 18)
2 CONT *1748, Nov. 6: Eldest daughter surviving childhood Sarah Clarke baptized.
2 CONT *1750, Nov. 11: fifth son Samuell baptized. He later marries Ursula F. Church of Hardwick, Worcester County (b. Oct. 14, 1751, daughter of Samuel Church and Damaris Billings, VR Hardwick, p. 27, and d. Mar. 17, 1845) Ursula and su
2 CONC pposedly Samuel are buried in the West Street Cemetery of Granby, Hampshire County, Massachusetts. (She died Mar. 7, 1845, at age 93 years 5 months, was not listed as a Revolutionary War pensioner in the 1840 census.)
2 CONT *1764, Aug. 9: First son Nehemiah married Judith (or Judy) Payson (b. c1739) in Sharon (VR Sharon p. 83)
2 CONT *1766, May 1: Second son Silvanus married Rachel Sterns of Stoughtonham by Nath Sumner, Esq., justice of the peace for Suffolk County (p. 265)
2 CONT *1769, Nov. 25: Third son Asa declared his intentions to marry Prudence Savell of Dedham (VR Sharon p. 83, VR Dedham, p. 122)
2 CONT *1770, June 25: Third son Asa married Prudence Savell (VRD p. 109)
2 CONT *1770, Sept. 27, Fourth son William married Hannah Lealand in Holliston (VR Holliston, p. 189)
2 CONT *1775, July 12: first son, Nehemiah, dies (VR Sharon, p. 158). His widow (same source) dies Aug. 21, 1786 in her 47th year.
2 CONT *1776, May 19: The elder Sarah Clark is admitted into the Church in Stoughtonham (future Sharon).
2 CONT *1782, Nov. 18: Eldest daughter Sarah married John Christian Reupeke at Foxborough (VR Foxborough, p. 127), settling in Sharon over the next four years. According to Rev. Curtis' notebook, he was a Hessian Mercenary who surrendere
2 CONC d with Burgoyne at Saratoga in 1777. The British refused to transport him back to Hesse after the war. John's will is dated 1834 (N-15450) while sally's will is dated 1864 (N-15451)
2 CONT *1783: Third son Asa has his last child. He eventually dies on Dec. 20, 1808, in his 63rd year. (VR Sharon, p. 158)
2 CONT *1792, Apr. 7: Sharon, his wife, dies in her 78th year (VR Sharon, p. 158)
2 CONT *1792, Apr. 9, recorded as having been buried in Rev. Curtis' notebook, presumably at a burial location in Sharon.
2 CONT *1805, Sept. 20: died in his 89th year (VR Sharon, p. 158). Naed as "Ichebud".
2 CONT *1805, Sept. 23: recorded as having been buried in the West Cemetery of Granby, according to the Vital Records of Granby (p. 568, transcribed by Carlton O. Hommel, available at: durhamwilcox.net/ma/granby_m1.html). However, the ce
2 CONC metery does not have records of the burial or stone.  
