1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From information on the family of Joseph Clark of Braintree, by Frank O. Clark, Ph.D.
2 CONT
2 CONT sciway3.net/clark/clark/sylvanusclark.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Silvanus Clark:
2 CONT *1743, Aug. 7: Born in Stoughton, son of Ichabod Clark and Sarah ("Record of births, marriages and deaths and intentions of marriage in the town of Stoughton 1727-1800 and in the town of Canton 1797-1845 preceded by the records of
2 CONC  the south precinct of Dorchester from 1715 to 1727", p. 49). Probably not to be confused with the Silvanus  who was the son of Jeremiah Clark, baptized by Rev. Curtis in Stoughtonham August 1743, according to Sharon Vital Records
2 CONC  (although there is some conjecture that Ichabod's middle name might have been Jeremiah - please note qualifiers presented by Frank O. Clark on his page).
2 CONT *1766, Apr. 10: Filed intent to marry with Rachel Starns (Sharon Vital Records, supposedly born c1742, but no record has yet been identified verifying her birth place or date; she is listed on the Stearns Genealogy and Memoirs on 
2 CONC page 65 as the daughter of Jonathan Stearns b. Nov. 20 1701, who himself was the son of Isaac Stearns and Elizabeth Stone of Stoughton - Jonathan appears to have married Experience Linkhorn or Lincoln of Taunton, and died prior to
2 CONC  his Inventory dated Sept. 23, 1769, administered by son Nathaniel).
2 CONT *1766, May 1: Married by Nath Sumner, Esq. Justice of the peace for Suffolk County (p. 265).
2 CONT *1769, Apr. 3: Rachel Clark admitted into the Stoughtonham Church.
2 CONT *No records verified as yet as having served in the Revolution. May have been a Loyalist during the war.
2 CONT *1807, Apr. 22: Signed will in Sharon (Number 4005 - Probate Index Norfolk County Volume 1):
2 CONT ** In the Name of God amen.  I Silvanus Clark of the town of Sharon in the County of Norfolk of State of Massachusetts, Yeoman, being weak in body but sound & perfect mind & memory, blessed be almighty God for the same? do make & 
2 CONC publish this my last will & testament in manner & form following, that is to say
2 CONT **First I give & bequeath unto my beloved wife Rachel Clark all my estate both real & personal during her natural life.
2 CONT **I do also give & bequeath unto my youngest daughter Susannah Clark twenty dollars.
2 CONT **And I also give & bequeath unto all my children viz: Oliver Clark, Samuel Clark, Jacob Clark, Elijah Clark, Jesse Clark, Mille McIntosh, Rachel Fuller, Susanna Clark each of them an equal share in all my real & personal estate a
2 CONC t the decease of my wife.
2 CONT **I also will & ordain that my beloved wife Rachel Clark pay all my just debts.
2 CONT **And I also will & ordain that the above legacy of twenty dollars be paid to my daughter Susanna after the death of my wife & that she also have an equal share of all the residue of my real & personal estate as specified above.
2 CONT **I also hereby appoint my second son Samuel Clark sole executor of this my last will & testament.
2 CONT **In witness whereof I have here unto set my hand? and seal the twenty second day of April in the year of our Lord one thousand eight hundred & seven.
2 CONT **(s) Silvanus Clark
2 CONT **Signed, sealed, published, & delivered by the above named Silvanus Clark to be his last will and testament in the presence of us who at his request & in his presence have hereunto subscribed our names as witness to the same: Mat
2 CONC thew Harlow, John Randall, John Whitaker
2 CONT *1807, Apr. 27: Died in his 64th year. Buried with wife Rachel (d. Dec. 31, 1822, age age 79 years, intestate) on Lots 6 and 7, Lane Q, Section 1 at Chestnut Hill Cemetery in Sharon, on Canton Street between Apple Valley Drive and
2 CONC  Richards Avenue. 
2 CONT *1807, July 7 (Tuesday): Probate Court in Dedham addresses Silvanus' will: "The foregoing instrument, purporting to be the last will and testament of Silvanus Clark, late of Sharon, Yeoman, deceased, being presented for Probate, b
2 CONC y Samuel Clark, Executor named there in, Matthew F. Harlow and John Randall, Witnesses there to subscribed, appear and make Oath that they saw the said Silvanus Clark sign, seal, and heard him publish the said instrument to be his
2 CONC  last Will and Testament, and that he to the best of their discernment, of sound and disposing Mind, I do therefore by the power and authority given me, hereby approve and allow the said instrument as the last will and testament o
2 CONC f the before named deceased, etc. W. Health, Judge of Probate. ---  Ordered that Samuel Clark Executor of the last Will and Testament of Silvanus Clark, late of Sharon, deceased, advertise notifications of his being Executor as af
2 CONC oresaid, and posting the same up in some public places at Sharon and by Publishing it in the Independent Chronicle, printed in Boston within three months.  W. Heath, Judge of Probate.  I Samuel Clark, testify & declare that I have
2 CONC  caused notification of my being Executor of the last will and testament of Silvanus Clark, late of Sharon, deceased, to be posted at public places in Sharon aforesaid, and also give notice thereof causing same to be published in 
2 CONC the Independent Chronicle printed in Boston within three months, etc. signed Samuel Clark 6 Oct. 1807.  Notice is hereby given the the subscriber has been duly appointed Executor of the last will of Silvanus Clark, late of Sharon,
2 CONC  yeoman, deceased, and has taken upon himself that trust by giving bonds as the law directs.  And all persons having demands upon the estate of the said deceased are required to exhibit the same, and all person indebted to the sai
2 CONC d estate, are called upon to make payment.  Samuel Clark, Executor." (These are all on one page) "Samuel Clark of Providence, RI, Painter, Matthew M. Harlow, Husbandman, John Randall Husbandman, both of Sharon, are bonded to Judge
2 CONC  of Probate for $20,000 for Samuel Clark as Executor of will of Silvanus Clark.  Signed in the presence of: John Baxter, Oliver Clark, Samuel Clark, Matthew H. Harlow, John Randall. --- To Joseph Hewins, Oliver Everett, Joshua Whi
2 CONC ttemore, all of Sharon, in the County of Norfolk, greetings.  You are hearby appointed a Committee to appraise on oath all the estate of Silvanus Clark, late of Sharon, yeoman, deceased, and make Return of your Doings, together wi
2 CONC th this Warrant, into the Probate Office, etc. W. Heath, Judge of Probate.  --- Then the before named Oliver Everett and Josua Whittemore Personally appeared and were sworn to the faithful performance of the service assigned them 
2 CONC by the foregoing Warrant, before me, Joseph Hewins, JP ---- Then the within Named Joseph Hewins Personally appeared and was Sworn to the Faithful Performance of the Service assigned him by the within warrant before me.  Elijah Cra
2 CONC ne, Justice of the Peace.
2 CONT *1807, Oct. 6: Inventory of the Estate of the late Silvanus Clark of Sharon, Norfolk County, yeoman, is presented: "Deceased appraised upon oath by us the Subscribers duly appointed to that Service by the Hon. William Heath, Esqr.
2 CONC , Judge of Probate of Wills for the County of Norfolk Viz
2 CONT **The Homestead of Said Deceased Situate in Said Sharon Containing 32 acres with the building thereon at $24 an acre 	760=00=0
2 CONT **Personal Estate	
2 CONT ***1 cow at $20, one ditto at $19, one Swine at $10	49=00=0
2 CONT ***2 cythes 2 axes? & Sundry other farming tools	 4=37=0
2 CONT ***Best bed Bolster & Pillows	9=00=0
2 CONT ***Second Bed & Beding	 8=50=0
2 CONT ***Third old bed & beding at $4, 2 bed Quilt? at $3.50	7=50=0
2 CONT ***Sundry other articles of Household Furniture	16=31=0
2 CONT ***Deceased wearing apparel	 11=83=0
2 CONT ***Library	1=92=0
2 CONT **Total Personal estate 100=43=0
2 CONT *Sharon 5 August 1807 Joseph Hewins, Oliver Everett, Joshua Whittemore - appraisers	
2 CONT *1808, Apr. 6: Samuel Clark of Providence, RI, Painter, Asa Clark, Housewright?, Matthew Harlow, Yeoman, of Sharon, bound unto probate court for $500, for Samuel Clark, Executor of the last will and testament of Silvanus Clark lat
2 CONC e of Sharon, Yeoman, deceased, at the Supreme Judicial Court, Dedham, the first Tuesday of March last, licensed to sell a part of the real estate of the said deceased, in order to discharge just debts, of charges of sale in the am
2 CONC ount of $110, that Samuel will follow the laws of the Commonwealth.  Signed in the presence of: Hannah Monk, Lydia Hurlow, Asa Clarke, Prudence Clark, Samuel Clark, Asa Clark, Jr., Matthew H. Harlow.
2 CONT *1808, Jun. 7: Second account of Samuel Clark, Executor of the last will and testament of Silvanus Clark, late of Sharon, Norfolk County, yeoman, deceased. "The said account charges himself with the process of a part of the Real E
2 CONC state of said deceased, as sds? by order of Court  $116.00 And prays allowance of the following charges & payments. The balance of his first account being $89.56. Amount paid 
2 CONT **Hammon Mann $1.00.
2 CONT **Nathaniel Leonard bill? $1.36. 
2 CONT **taxes on the estate $7.18. 
2 CONT **Fisher? H. Fairbanks Bill $2.85
2 CONT **Thomas Kollock Bill $1.00
2 CONT **Elijah Heninis? Bill	$1.00
2 CONT **Jacob Masest? Bill	$0.25
2 CONT **Jeremiah Richards, Jr. Bill $1.00
2 CONT **Bill of Execution $48.00
2 CONT **Subtotal: $148.40
2 CONT **Probate fees for Deceased?	$1.80
2 CONT **Total: $150.20
2 CONT *1809, Mar. 7: Samuel Clark of Providence, RI, Painter, Thomas Kollock?, Gentleman, and John C. Reupeke, Tailor both of Sharon, paid $150 as bond to the Judge of Probate, for Samuel Clark as executor of the will of Silvanus Clark,
2 CONC  late of Sharon, to make sale of a part of the real estate, and discharge a debt of $60. In presence of Elijah Friswith?, Zucker? Richard, Jr., Samuel Clark, Thos. Kollock, John C. Reupeke. Samuel Clark, Executor of the will of Si
2 CONC lvanus Clark, Yeoman, deceased, late of Sharon, having been authorized by the Supreme Judicial Court held in Dedham, on the first Tuesday  of March 1809 to dispose of a part of the real estate of the said deceased, appeared before
2 CONC  me the Justice of the Peace for Norfolk Co. and solemnly swore that in disposing of the said estate he would? use his best skill and judgment in fixing the time and place of sales and that he wants spent his utmost endeavors to d
2 CONC ispose of the same in in such manner as would produce the greatest advantage to all persons interested therein and without any sinister views whatever.  Samuel Havon?, JP Norfolk Co.
2 CONT *1809, May 2, first Tuesday: Samuel Clark, executor of will of Silvanus Clark, late of Sharon, Yeoman, deceased and made the forgoing account of his administration at a court in Dedham: "The third account of Samuel Clark Executor 
2 CONC of the will of Silvanus Clark yeoman debts charges himself with apart of the Real Estate Sold by and under Govt? amounting to $60 and pray for an allowance of the same? it being? as follows,
2 CONT **To Balance Due on Seckams Accounts	$34.20
2 CONT **To Cash paid probate office	$2
2 CONT **To Cash paid Superememrfort? of Indt?	$3
2 CONT **To my Expenses from Providence to Dedham and time	$10.60
2 CONT **To ditto Seck? and time	$10.20
2 CONT **$60.00 Samuel Clark Executor	
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Silvanus Clark and Rachel Starns (Sterns), all born in Sharon, MA:
2 CONT *Oliver Clark born 28 May 1767 (VR Sharon p18) died 26 Dec. 1831, married 27 Jan. 1794 to Hannah Davis born 28 Dec. 1777.
2 CONT *Miletiah Clark born 27 Nov. 1769 in Sharon, MA,  int to marry 2 Sept. 1797 Andrew McIntosh in Sharon. No Macintosh births in Sharon, or Dedham. I can find no record of them anywhere after the marriage.  Andrew McIntosh and "Milly
2 CONC " are both buried in Chestnut Hill Cemetery, Sharon, not far from Silvanus and Rachel.  Andrew McIntosh died 6 Sept. 1840 in his 72d year.  "Milly" died 23 Sept. 1855 in her 86th year (from their grave markers).
2 CONT *Rachel Clark born 4 Aug. 1772  (Clerk) married 7 July 1796  Augustus Fuller of Wrenthham (int. not  recorded)
2 CONT *Experience Clark born 7 Jan. 1775.  I cannot locate even a hint of her.
2 CONT *Samuel Clark born 27 Aug. 1777. Perhaps Samuel Clark (int. states Jr.) of Franklin who married Hannah Clap, 7 Jan. 1808 (VR Walpole p108).  Samual Clark removed to Providence, Rhode Island, as stated in the probate records.
2 CONT *Child Clark born Feb. 1778 died Feb. 1778
2 CONT *Jacob Clark born 20 Apr. 1780.  Note there is a different Jacob Clark in Medfield 1774-1837 (age 63) who married Prudence Straw.  
2 CONT *Susannah Clark baptized 10 April 1783 Rev. Philip Curtis, p56, Sharon Hist. Soc. pdf p237
2 CONT *Elijah Clark baptized 9 July1786 int to marry 21 July 1809 Nancy Fuller born 29 March 1787.(VR Sharon p83) no births listed in Sharon or Wrentham, and only the intent was filed.  I cannot (yet) find a marriage record.
