1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth:  Sep. 20, 1728 Chelsea Suffolk County Massachusetts, USA  Death:  Apr. 30, 1812 Dunstable Middlesex County Massachusetts, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Whittemore, daughter of Joseph & Ruth (Eustis) Whittemore was born in Rumney Marsh (now Chelsea), Suffolk, Massachusetts 20 September 1728. Her father died in 1735, and her mother married (2nd) 4 June 1737, Abraham Kendall.
2 CONC  When Hannah was 10 years old, her uncle, William Eustis, was appointed her guardian on 13 June 1738.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Whittemore and John Kendall/Kendel were married in Pepperell, Middlesex, Massachusetts 16 April 1747.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Kendall, widow of John, died in Dunstable, Middlesex, Massachusetts 30 April 1812.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: New England Historical & Genealogical Register 1953 - CVII (107) Pages 97-99 Source: Vital Records of Pepperell, Massachusetts Marriages: Page 185 Source: Vital Records of Dunstable, Massachusetts Deaths: Page 220 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   Joseph Whittemore (1693 - 1742)
2 CONT   Ruth Eustis Kendall (1698 - 1765)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   John Kendall (1723 - 1809)*
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Zebedee Kendall (1755 - 1839)*
2 CONT
2 CONT  Siblings:
2 CONT   Hannah Whittemore Kendall (1728 - 1812)
2 CONT   Samuel Whittemore (1732 - 1812)*
2 CONT   Mary Whittemore Hartshorn (1734 - 1807)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription: In  Memory of HANNAH KENDALL Relict of  John Kendall who died April 30, 1812 in the 84th year of  her Age
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Nason, Elias "History of Dunstable, Massachusetts": A Mudge & Son, printers, Boston 1877
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Central Cemetery  Dunstable Middlesex County Massachusetts, USA 
2 CONT
