1 NOTE John Crossman - Admitted freeman at Taunton, June 5, 1684. He left a Will dated May 18, 1727, whereby he makes provision for his wife, and devises his real estate to his four sons, John, Jonathan, Benjamin, and Henry Crossman. He 
2 CONC makes bequests to his daughter Abigail White, to the children of his deceased daughter, Sarah Babbitt, to his daughter Jahanna Rogers; to his daughter Mercy Lincoln, and his daughter Deborah Crossman. Appoints his wife and his son
2 CONC  John, executors.
2 CONT The N.Y. Genealogical Record - Vol. 22, 1891
2 CONT
2 CONT ---Robert Owen Crossman, A genealogy of the Crossman Family (1977)
2 CONT ---The Babbitt Family History 1643-1900 (1912)
