1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel '''Robert Crossman''', son of Robert Crossman and Sarah Kingsbury, was born 3 Aug 1657 at Taunton, Plymouth Colony, and died at Taunton, now in Bristol County, Massachusetts,  between 20 August 1736 (date will written) and
2 CONC  18 April 1738  (date will proved).
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert married Hannah Brooks (1659-1700) on July 21, 1679 at Taunton.  She was the daughter of Gilbert Brooks and his wife Elizabeth.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Nathaniel Crossman 1680 -
2 CONT # Hannah Crossman 1681/82 - Bef 1735
2 CONT # Son Crossman 1683 - 1683
2 CONT # Elizabeth Crossman 1684/85 - 1733/34
2 CONT # Robert Crossman 1686 - 1687
2 CONT # Seth Crossman 1688 -
2 CONT # Mehitable Crossman 1694 - 1695/96
2 CONT # Son Crossman 1697 - 1697
2 CONT # Bethiah Crossman 1700 - 1704
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert built his first house about 1700 at  78 Cohannet Street, Taunton, MA and still standing:  It served as a Home, Tavern, Inn, and Revolutionary Soldiers Headquarters through the years.  A pen and ink sketch by F.W.Hull was pr
2 CONC inted in the August 10, 1937 edition of the Taunton Daily Gazette.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Crossman (2nd) - Purchased the Grist Mill. He was a large landowner a selectman, representative to the General Court. American Ancestry 1891, Vol. VI - page 197
2 CONT
2 CONT === Will
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of Robert Crossman is dated 20 August 1736 and was proved 18 April 1738. [1] It opens with the statement that he was aged seventy eight years. The will names:
2 CONT
2 CONT * son Nathaniel Crossman (named executor)
2 CONT * grandsons Stephen and Nathaniel Crossman
2 CONT * grandchildren Seth Crossman (under 21), Jeremiah, Robert, Sarah, Susannah, and Hannah Crossman, children of his son Seth Crossman
2 CONT * daughter-in-law Susannah Crossman and her children
2 CONT * daughter Hannah Packerd, late of Bridgwater, and her children Israel and Robert Packerd
2 CONT * daughter Elisabeth Liscomb, her husband Francis Liscomb
2 CONT * grandchildren Robert Liscomb and Richard Liscomb, their sister Elisabeth Codding, and the children of Mary Willmouth deceased
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Estate notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 May 1747: Petition noting that of the grandchildren Jeremiah, Robert, Sarah, Susannah and Hannah Crosman were given several pieces of undivided land, and "som of s'd children being ded" with heirs, specifically mentioning a two 
2 CONC year old minor child of Hannah, request guardians be appointed and division made. Signed by William Hoskins Jr guardian for Sarah['s] Child, Benj'a Hodges guardian for Robbard Crosmon. 16 Jun 1748: Division among Jeremiah Robert S
2 CONC arah Susannah and Hannah children of Seth Crosman late of s'd Taunton deceased: 1/30 part (appears to be 1/6 of Jeremiah's 1/5, he leaving no issue) to each of: Susannah Crosman mother to the deceased Jeremiah; to Seth Crossman br
2 CONC other to the deceased Jeremiah; to Robert Crossman; to the representatives of Sarah she being deceased; to Susannah; to Hannahs representatives (she being dead)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/173107902/robert-crossman Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 19 2021, 0:10:25 UTC''
2 CONT # Find a Grave, database and images (https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/173107902/robert-crossman: accessed April 7, 2025), memorial page for COL Robert Crossman (1657–1738), Find a Grave Memorial ID 173107902, citing Plain Cemet
2 CONC ery, Taunton, Bristol County, Massachusetts, USA; Maintained by June Faulkner Crossman-Battisti (contributor 46943035).
2 CONT # Find a Grave, database and images (https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/173107982/hanna-crossman: accessed April 7, 2025), memorial page for Hanna Brooks Crossman (2 Oct 1659–1700), Find a Grave Memorial ID 173107982, citing Plai
2 CONC n Cemetery, Taunton, Bristol County, Massachusetts, USA; Maintained by June Faulkner Crossman-Battisti (contributor 46943035).
2 CONT # WikiTree contributors, "Robert Crossman (1657-1738)," WikiTree: The Free Family Tree, (https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Crossman-29 : accessed 08 April 2025).
2 CONT # https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Robert_Crossman_%287%29 cites 
2 CONT ##Dean, John Ward. "Genealogy of the Kingsburys of Dedham, Mass.", in The New England Historical and Genealogical Register. (Boston: New England Historic Genealogical Society)Vol. 16, page 338. Children of Robert Crossman and Sara
2 CONC h Kingsbury: Robert, b. 3 Aug 1657, m. 21 Jul 1679 Hannah Brooks.
2 CONT ##Taunton, Bristol, Massachusetts, United States. Vital Records of Taunton, Massachusetts, to the Year 1850. (Boston, Massachusetts: New England Historic Genealogical Society, 1929, c1978) Vol. 1, p. 111. CROSSMAN, Robert [T.P.R. 
2 CONC Crosman], s. Robert, [born] Aug. 3, 1657. [Crosman, P.C.R.]
2 CONT ##Massachusetts. Probate Court (Bristol County). Probate records 1687-1916; index, 1687-1926. (Salt Lake City, Utah: Genealogical Society of Utah, 1968) Case 7129: Robert Crossman Taunton 1738.
