2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT David White was born on 27 Jun 1731 in Raynham, the son of John and Elizabeth (Crossman) White. He first married Bethiah Daggett of Attleboro, on 26 Oct 1749, who died in childbirth on 9 Dec 1750. Their child was still born. David
2 CONC  then married Abigail Austin on 26 Aug 1752, Abigul was the daughter of John Austin of Norton. He sold his house and moved away. David and Abigail had six children probably all born in Raynham:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Lot, b. 14 Jul 1754; died 1 Jun 1755.
2 CONT 2) Bethia, b. 13 Nov 1755; died 16 Jul 1787.
2 CONT 3) A son, b. 27 Aug 1757 ; died the same day.
2 CONT 4) Mark, b. 4 Aug 1758.
2 CONT 5) Solomon.
2 CONT 6) Isaiah.
2 CONT David married Abigail Austen on 26 August 1752 in Norton, Bristol, Massachusetts, United States.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT David died on 13 May 1831.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Lothrop, Thomas J.. The Nicholas White family : 1643-1900. C.A Hack & Son,Taunton, Mass., 1902. (See also: https://archive.org/stream/nicholaswhitefa00lothgoog#page/n4/mode/2up)
2 CONT ↑ Marriage: "Massachusetts, U.S., Compiled Birth, Marriage, and Death Records, 1700-1850"
2 CONT New England Historical Genealogical Society; Boston, Massachusetts; Massachusetts Vitals to 1850
2 CONT Ancestry Sharing Link - Ancestry Record 61401 #439254 (accessed 14 May 2024)
