1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Macomber-38
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Briggs formerly Macomber
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1643 in Marshfield, New Plymouth Colony, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of William Macomber and Ursula (Cooper) Macomber
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of John Lincoln Macomber [half], Edith (Macomber) Lincoln, William Macomber [half], Matthew Macomber [half], Edith Macomber [half], Thomas Macomber I [half], Hannah (Macomber) Randall [half], Ursilla (Macomber) White [half]
2 CONC  and	John Macomber [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of William Briggs — married 6 Nov 1666 in Tauton, Bristol County, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of William Briggs 2nd, Thomas Briggs I, Sarah (Briggs) Lane, Elizabeth Macomber (Briggs) Babbitt, Hannah (Briggs) Waldron, Mary (Briggs) Forest, Mathew Briggs and John Briggs
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 20 Mar 1680 in Taunton, New Plymouth Colony, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 16 Jan 2019 | Created 31 Mar 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Macomber was born about 1643, the daughter of William & Priscilla (Thomas) Macomber in Marshfield, New Plymouth Colony She married William Briggs 6 Nov 1666 in Taunton, Massachusetts.[1] They had 9 children. Sarah died the d
2 CONC ay after giving birth to her son John on 20 Mar 1680 in Taunton, Massachusetts. She was buried in Oakland Cemetery in Taunton, Massachusetts. Sarah was born in 1640. She passed away in 1680.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ : Title: Massachusetts Town Marriage Records. Vital Records of Granville Massachusetts to the Year, Taunton VR - marriage http://ma-vitalrecords.org/MA/Bristol/Taunton/Images/Taunton_M068.shtml Torry, Clarence A. New England Mar
2 CONC riages Prior to 1700. Baltimore, MD, USA: Genealogical Publishing Co., 2004. Page 99. ALTERNATE SOURCE: Ancestry.com. U.S., New England Marriages Prior to 1700 [database on-line]. Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 2012.
2 CONC  Image 114 of 1022. Find A Grave Index," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:QVVY-CFRR : 11 July 2016), Sarah Macomber Briggs, 1680; Burial, Taunton, Bristol, Massachusetts, United States of America, Oa
2 CONC kland Cemetery; Find A Grave: Memorial #29711887 American Genealogical-Biographical Index (AGBI). Volume 06, Page number 91. U. S. and International Marriage Records 1660-1800 Macumber Genealogy. http://hausegenealogy.com/macumber
2 CONC .html
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/29711887/sarah-briggs
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Sarah was born in Marshfield, Plymouth Colony. She was the daughter of William Macomber and Priscilla Thomas. Sarah was married to William Briggs on November 6, 1666 in Taunton, Plymouth Colony.  William and Sarah had the followin
2 CONC g children: William Briggs, Thomas Briggs, Elizabeth Babbitt, Hannah Briggs, Mary Forest, Matthew Briggs, Amos Briggs, and John Briggs. She died on March 20, 1679/80 in Taunton, Plymouth Colony.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Founded in 1637 by members of the Plymouth Colony, Taunton is one of the oldest towns in the United States. <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taunton,_Massachusetts>
2 CONT ----
2 CONT History of Marshfield: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_Marshfield,_Massachusetts
2 CONT ----
