1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Briggs-671
2 CONT
2 CONT William Briggs
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 2 Apr 1645 in Thornbury, Gloucestershire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John Briggs Sr. and Agnes (Thayer) Briggs
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Richard Briggs, John Briggs Jr., Katherine Briggs, Richard Briggs, Joanna (Briggs) Tallman and	Hugh Briggs
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Sarah (Macomber) Briggs — married 6 Nov 1666 in Tauton, Bristol County, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Abigail (Mason) Briggs — married 7 Apr 1680 in Dedham, Suffolk, Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of William Briggs 2nd, Thomas Briggs I, Sarah (Briggs) Lane, Elizabeth Macomber (Briggs) Babbitt, Hannah (Briggs) Waldron, Mary (Briggs) Forest, Mathew Briggs and John Briggs
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 3 Jan 1728 in Taunton, Bristol, Massachusetts, Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 6 Nov 2018 | Created 31 Mar 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT William, son of John Sr. & Agnes Tayer Briggs, born or baptized in Thornbury, Gloucestershire, England 2 Apr 1645.
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: This William is NOT the son of Clement & Elizabeth (Fields) Briggs
2 CONT
2 CONT William married Sarah Macumber of Marshfield on 6 Nov 1666 in Taunton, daughter of William Macumber and Ursula Mathew. She died in Taunton 20 Mar 1680 after the birth of her son John. He probably married secondly in Dedham 2 July 
2 CONC 1680 Abigail Mason. In June 1673, he and his wife were called to the court at Plymouth and fined 12 pounds for killing a horse of Thomas Linkoline. William died 3 Jan 1728 in his 83rd year and is buried at Oakland Cemetery.[1] Chi
2 CONC ldren
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Taunton, Massachusetts: William b 25 Jan 1667/8 Thomas, twin, b 9 Sep 1669 Sarah, twin, b 10 Sep 1669 Elizabeth b 14 Mar 1671 (often confused with Elizabeth3 (Jonathan2, Clement1) who m. Elkanah Bobet) Hannah b 4 Nov 1672;
2 CONC  perhaps m Samuel Waldron or Samuel Woodward Mary b 14 Aug 1674;; perhaps m 24 Jul 1712 John Forrest John b 19 Mar 1680 Gloucestershire flag William Briggs was born in Gloucestershire, England. Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Thornburg, South Gloucestershire, England - place not found probably Thornbury, Gloucestershire, England Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Edna Anne Hannibal, Claude W. Barlow, "Richard, William and Hugh, son of John Briggs of Taunton, Massachusetts," in NEHGR, 127(Apr 1971):82 Taunton Vital Record book marriage Taunton Vital Record book death : 3 Jan 1728 at age 8
2 CONC 3 NEHGS, Massachusetts Town Marriage Records; Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: Ancestry.com Operations Inc, 1999. NEHGS, Massachusetts Town Death Records; Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: The Generations Network, Inc., 199
2 CONC 9. Lois Crabtree Johnson, Descendants of John Crabtree, immigrant to Boston, Mass., filed in the Daly Library. [http:www.dalyclan.org/page4/sscrab/sscrab-o/p12.htm Excerpts] Acknowledgements
2 CONT
2 CONT This person was created through the import of Dickinson Family Tree.ged on 31 March 2011. This profile was adopted and edited. Ramsey-1224 18:55, 28 December 2014 (EST) Profile created from - U.S. and International Marriage Record
2 CONC s 1560-1900 Macomber Genealogy; http://hausegen
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/29695891#add-to-vc
2 CONT ----
2 CONT William was the first of nine children, and the first of five sons, of William Briggs and Sarah Macomber. William was married to Elizabeth Lincoln on October 13, 1693 in Taunton, Massachusetts. William and Elizabeth had one child:
2 CONC  Sarah Lane. After Elizabeth's death, William was married to Mehitable Blake on June 16, 1696 in Milton, Massachusetts. William and Mehitable had the following children: Agnes Briggs, Nathaniel Briggs, Mehitable Ware, Eliphalet Br
2 CONC iggs, Seth Briggs, and Agnes Boldary.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT The towns and settlements of Plymouth Colony did not become a part of Massachusetts Bay Colony (later known as The Commonwealth of Massachusetts) until 1691./Taunton, Plymouth Colony, New England
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Member https://www.geni.com/people/Charles-Howell/6000000066290332845 contributes, Dec 2017:
2 CONT
2 CONT > from NEHGS research database, Vol 125  page 88 Sons of John Briggs of Taunton. (William 2, john 1) Thomas Briggs3 b. 1669 d bef.1JUL 1746 m. oct 1689 in Taunton  Abigail [Harvey] Thayer (wdo.) ...Her grandfather William Harvey o
2 CONC f one of original settlers of Taunton. Sourced from: Ruth (Thayer) Ravenscroft's in published genealogy of Nathaniel Thayer in Society's Library.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT William Briggs
2 CONT
2 CONT Genealogical and Family History of the State of Connecticut: A Record of the Achievements of Her People in the Making of a Commonwealth and the Founding of a Nation.
2 CONT Volume I Briggs (II) William Briggs , of Taunton, Massachusetts , thought to be son of Clement Briggs , and mentioned by Savage as probably brother of Clement 's son Jonathan , settled with others of this family in Taunton . He ma
2 CONC rried, in November, 1666 , Sarah Macomber . Children, born in Taunton : William , January 25, 1667-68 , mentioned below; Thomas (twin), September 9, 1669 ; Sarah (twin), September 10, 1669 , a day later than her brother; Elizabeth
2 CONC  , March 14, 1671 ; Hannah , November 4, 1672 ; Mary , August 14, 1674 ; Matthew , February 5, 1675 ; John , March 19, 1680
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
