1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sarah Willis 
2 CONT * Gender:	Female 
2 CONT * Birth:	March 01, 1651, West Bridgewater, Plymouth Colony  
2 CONT * Death:	December 1711 (60), West Bridgewater, Plymouth County, Province of Massachusetts  
2 CONT * Place of Burial:	Bridgewater, Plymouth County, Massachusetts, United States:	 
2 CONT * Daughter of Deacon John Willis and Elizabeth (Hodgkins) Willis  
2 CONT * Wife of John Ames, of Bridgewater  
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT (V) John Ames (4), son of William, born March 24, 1647, married Sarah, daughter of John Willis. He settled in West Bridgewater, Mass., as early as 1672. He served in King Philip’s War. He died about 1726, when his estate was settl
2 CONC ed.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Children ==
2 CONT
2 CONT All of the children of John Ames (son of William, called Jr. in town records to distinguish from his uncle John) and Sarah (Willis) Ames were born in West Bridgewater, Plymouth Colony (later Plymouth County, Massachusetts).
2 CONT
2 CONT *'''John Ames''' (b. ''1672'' - d. ''1726'') m. '''Sarah Willis'''
2 CONT *'''William Ames III''' (b. ''1673'' - d. ''1743'') m. '''Elizabeth Jennings'''
2 CONT *'''Nathaniel Ames''' (b. ''1677'' - d. ''1736'') m. '''Susanna Howard'''
2 CONT *'''Elizabeth Ames''' (b. ''1680'' - d. ''1739'') m. '''Capt. John Field'''
2 CONT *'''Thomas Ames II''' (b. ''1682'' - d. ''1737'') m. '''Mary Hayward'''
2 CONT *'''Sarah Ames''' (b. ''1685'' - d. ''1758'') m. '''Daniel Field'''
2 CONT *'''David Ames''' (b. ''1688'' - d. ''1754'') m. '''Mary Reynolds'''
2 CONT *'''Hannah Ames''' (b. ''1692'' - d. ''1767'') m. '''David Packard'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ''(Note: If the targeted profile specifically represents the younger Sarah Ames born in 1685, she had no children under the surname Ames, as she married Daniel Field in 1706 and her children carry the Field surname.)''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT John Willis was born 1610 in England and died 1692 in Duxbury, Massachusetts. He married Elizabeth Hodgkins (aka Hoskins) in 1637 and to this union was born nine children. She was the daughter of Henry Gent Hoskins and Ann Winthro
2 CONC pe. Deacon John Willis was at Duxbury very early. He and his wife Elizabeth are recorded as being there 1637. He was the original proprietor, and one of the first settlers of Bridgewater and as the first deacon sustained many town
2 CONC  offices in both Duxbury and Bridgewater. He represented Bridgewater at the old Colony Council for 25 years and sold his estate in Duxbury to William Peabody 1657. He was appointed to solemnize marriages and administer oath to wit
2 CONC nesses. His wife Elizabeth was the widow of William Palmer Jr. Her maiden name was Hodgkins, will drawn in 1692 proved 1693. In 1645 was listed as one of the 54 original proprietors of Bridgewater. The Willis family of Sudbury con
2 CONC nects John Willis, above, to a brother Nathaniel Willis and states that there were three other brothers that came to New England. At the time the article was written it appeared that those three had no issue John Willis bought lan
2 CONC d in Duxbury from Abraham Blush on 26 Nov 1638 for 8 pounds 10 s sterling. Abraham Blush bought land which contained a dwelling house and 20 acres from Richard Moore 1 Nov 1637 called Eagle's Nest for 21 pounds. He sold the easter
2 CONC ly half to John Willis with no mention of a house. John Willis sold his estate in Duxbury 1657 to William Paybody.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Middle name - starts with a D?
2 CONT
2 CONT
