2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate
2 CONT
2 CONT On 14 December 1712, his brother Nathaniel Eames was granted the letter of administration for his estate.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT His brother was also appointed guardian of his children. He died intestate. His moveable inventory was taken on 15 June 1713 in Plymouth.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1725, the estate accounts showed the debts and charges of the estate.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1726, the estate distribution was set out to his children, William Ames, Mary Alger, wife of Joseph Alger of Bridgewater, Martha Conant, wife of Thomas Connat of Bridgewater, Bethiah Ames, Hannah Ames, and Sarah Ames.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT William Ames  (1673 - 1712)
