1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Ames-187
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Elizabeth Ames'' was born at Bridgewater, Massachusetts on September 6, 1680, son of John and Sarah (Willis) Ames . [1][2] [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth married John Field 3d at Bridgewater in November, 1697. John, son of John and Elizabeth (Everden) Field was born on February 20, 1671 at Bridgewater, Massachusetts. [1] [2] [3] [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT The family lived in Bridgewater and later at Providence, Rhode Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth died in 1739 and was buried in the West Burial Ground. Her grave was moved to the North Burial Ground in May, 1865. [5]Her inscription reads: Elizabeth Field wife of John Field 3D daughter of John Ames of Bridgewater, Ma
2 CONC ss. Born in 1681 Died in 1739[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her husband Captain John Field 3d, 1671-1758, was buried in the West Burial Ground. His grave was moved to the North Burial Ground in May, 1865. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain John Field of Providence wrote his will on June 26, 1754 and it was proved on April 5, 1757. [Providence docket Vol. i: No. 708] In it he names: [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT * grandson John Field, sole executor
2 CONT * grandson James Field
2 CONT * my three daughters Elizabeth Snow, Sarah Howard and Susannah Keith
2 CONT * children of my sister Elizabeth Briggs
2 CONT * children of my sister Lydia Mandly
2 CONT * nephews Anthony, Jonah, Jeremiah and Samuel Steers
2 CONT * niece Loranna Coman
2 CONT * Mary Snow, singlewoman of Providence
2 CONT * my negro man Jefferey [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT # Elizabeth born on August 4, 1698 [1]; married Joseph Snow in Providence. [4]
2 CONT # Sarah born on January 7, 1700; married Jonathan Haward on July 30, 1719. [1]
2 CONT # Susannah born on February 25, 1702; married Joseph Keith on October 3, 1721[1]; died at East Bridgewater on November 1, 1759. [7]
2 CONT # John born on February 27, 1704; married Mary Haward November 15, 1726 [1]; died in 1729, [5] was buried in the West Burial Ground, but was removed to Bridgewater, Massachusetts in May, 1865. [6] His widow married second Elisha P
2 CONC ierce. [4]
2 CONT # James born on September 12, 1705 [1]; died on August 11, 1729 [8] at sea, unmarried. His father Captain John was granted administration of his estate in October, 1729. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT
