2 CONT SAMUEL WASHBURN: No birth record has been found for Samuel but his parentage is shown by the will of his father, John Washburn, dated 10/30/1686 and naming son Samuel, with other children. In a deed, dated Jan 9, 1677, recorded Ap
2 CONC ril 26, 1720, John Washburn Sr. of Bridgewater, planter, with the consent of his wife Elizabeth, gave 35 acres of land in Bridgewater to his son Samuel. «i»Note:«/i» The will of Samuel Washburn of Bridgewater, yeoman, dated March 
2 CONC 13, 1720, probated April 4, 1720, names wife Deborah Washburn, sons Samuel, Nehehiah and Benjamin; heirs of son Noah Washburne, deceased; heirs of his son Israel Washburne deceased; daughter Hannah wife of John Keith; grandson Isr
2 CONC ael Washburn son of son Israel; and cousin Deliverance Jennings wife of Ephriam Jennings. 7 «i»Note:«/i» Source: Frances COOKE of the Mayflower and His Descendents for Four Generations, Compiled by Robert S. Wakefield, 4th Edition
2 CONC , General Society of Mayflower Descendants, 1996 Samuel, b. ca. 1652, Duxbury, MA; d. Bridgewater 24 March 1720 i n 69th year.  He m. ca 1677 Deborah Packard; d. aft 1 Jul 1725; dau. of Samuel and Elizabeth (_____) Packard.  The w
2 CONC ill of Samuel Packard senr dated 29 Oct 1684 names dau. Deborah Washburn the wife of Samuell Washburn.  The will of Samuel Washburn of Bridgewater, yeoman, dated 13 Mar 1720, probated 4 Apr 1720, names wife Deborah Wasburne; sons 
2 CONC Samuel Washburne; heirs of son Noah Washburn deceased; heirs of son Israel Washburn dec.; sons Nehemiah and Benjamin Washburne; dau. Hannah Deliverance Jennings, wife of Ephraim Jennings.  On 30 Jan 1722/3 Samuel Washburn, Nehemia
2 CONC h Washburn and Benjamin Wasburn brethren of Bridgewater sold to John Keith of Bridgewater land in Bridgewater.  On 14 Dec 1724, ack. same day, Samuel Washburn, Nehemiah Washburn, Benjamin Washburn Jr., John Keither and wife Hannah
2 CONC  Keith all of Bridgewater sold to Thomas Hayward third land in Bridgewater.
2 CONT
