1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Benjamin Washburn was related to a passenger on the Mayflower.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Washburn-362
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Washburn
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1657 in Duxbury, Plymouth Colony, New England
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John Washburn Jr. and Elizabeth (Mitchell) Washburn
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of John Washburn, Thomas Washburn Sr., Samuel Washburn Sr., Joseph Washburn Sr., Jonathan Washburn, Elizabeth (Washburn) Seely, Mary (Washburn) Kinsley, Jane (Washburn) Orcutt, James Washburn Sr. and	Sarah (Washburn) Ames
2 CONT
2 CONT [spouse(s) unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT [children unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 12 Dec 1690 in Bridgewater, Plymouth, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 20 Aug 2018 | Created 21 Oct 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Washburn was related to a passenger on the Mayflower.
2 CONT
2 CONT Discuss: MAYFLOWER
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin, son of John Washburn VI, eldest son of John Washburn V, both in the line of the Washbornes' of Bengeworth. John VI sailed to New England on the "Elizabeth & Ann", with his mother and brother in 1635.
2 CONT
2 CONT They settled first in Duxbury, Plymouth Colony and John VI married Elizabeth Mitchell, daughter of Experience and Jane (Cooke) Mitchell, of Duxbury. They had eleven children, including the first set of Seven Brothers in the Americ
2 CONC an Washburn line.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Washburn b. abt. 1646 Thomas Washburn b. abt. 1648 Samuel Washburn b. abt 1651 Joseph Washburn b. 7 July 1653 Jonathan Washburn b. abt. 1655 Benjamin Washburn b. abt. 1658 Mary (Washburn) Kinsley b. abt 1661 Elizabeth (Washbu
2 CONC rn) Seely b. abt. 1664 Jane Washburn b. abt. 1670 James Washburn b.15 May 1672 Sarah (Washburn) Ames b. abt. 1675
2 CONT
2 CONT Source
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: #S-1450862356 Page: Ancestry Family Trees Note: Data: Text: http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=890183&pid=-584814026
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT Source S-1450862356 Repository: #R-1958205582 Title: Public Member Trees Author: Ancestry.com Publication: Online publication - Provo, UT, USA: The Generations Network, Inc., 2006.Original data - Family trees submitted by Ancestry
2 CONC  members.Original data: Family trees submitted by Ancestry members. Note: This information comes from 1 or more individual Ancestry Family Tree files. This source citation points you to a current version of those files. Note: The 
2 CONC owners of these tree files may have removed or changed information since this source citation was created.
2 CONT
2 CONT Repository R-1958205582 Name: Ancestry.com Address: http://www.Ancestry.com Note: Acknowledgments
2 CONT
2 CONT master 11_12.ged on 21 October 2010. grant2.ged on 07 February 2011.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Benjamin was killed in Sir William Phipp's expedition against Port Royal in 1690, Cananda during King William's War (the first of four French and Indian Wars). He was unmarried.
