2 CONT Elizabeth (Washburn) Seely was related to a passenger on the Mayflower.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Elizabeth Washburn
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: Date: 1660 Place: Duxbury, Plymouth Colony Plymouth Colony and Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT From John Maltby: Elizabeth Washburn, second daughter of John and Elizabeth (Mitchell) Washburn, born probably in Bridgewater, Plymouth Colony, in ca. 1664,[1] married:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.) James Howard, son of John and Martha (Hayward) Howard/Haward, of Bridgewater,[2] in ca. 1685.[3] He was a grandson of Thomas Hayward, of Duxbury,[4] and he died in the Sir William Phipps Expedition to Canada in 1690.[5] His in
2 CONC ventory was dated 6 Feb. 1690/1.[6] She remarried to: 2.) Edward Selee/Seale/Sealley, of West Bridgewater, in ca. 1692.[7] Edward Sealley died testate in 1699 in Bridgewater. His will was dated 25 May 1698, and probated on 17 Apr.
2 CONC  1699. He mentioned his wife Elizabeth, and sons Benjamin and John both minors, and it was witnessed by Joseph Hayward and Jonathan Haward.[8] (See appendix [C][9] for a full transcription of his will.) Elizabeth (Washburn) (Howar
2 CONC d) Selee died on 27 Feb. 1741/2 in Norton, MA.[10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Washburn had 3 children by James Howard and 2 more sons by Edward Selee:[11] + 158 i Elizabeth3 Howard, born on 16 Jan. 1685/6 in Bridgewater,[227] married Thomas Buck (Jr.), probably son of Thomas and Mary (Turner) Buck
2 CONC , of Scituate, MA,[228] on 18 Dec. 1712 in Bridgewater,[229] and they lived in Bridgewater. (Continued in Plymouth Generation 4.)
2 CONT
2 CONT 159 ii Mercy Howard, born on 27 Feb. 1687/8 in Bridgewater,[230] died on 26 Jan. 1704/5 in Bridgewater.[231]
2 CONT
2 CONT + 160 iii Dr. James3 Howard (Jr.), born on 26 Jan. 1689/90 in Bridgewater,[232] married Elisabeth Wallis on 26 Jan. 1709/10 in Bridgewater,[233] and he moved Stoughton, MA, then to Cumberland, RI.[234] (Continued in Plymouth Gener
2 CONC ation 4.)
2 CONT
2 CONT + 161 iv Benjamin Selee, born on 5 Mar. 1693 in Bridgewater,[235] settled in Easton, MA, and married Sarah Lane, possibly widow of John Lane, of Norton, MA, on 11 Dec. 1718 in Norton.[236] (Continued in Plymouth Generation 4.)
2 CONT
2 CONT + 162 v John Selee, born on 10 Apr. 1697 in Bridgewater,[237] married Hannah Briggs, daughter of Clement and Elizabeth (Field) Briggs,[238] of Easton, on 12 Jan. 1723/4 in Norton, MA,[239] and also lived in Easton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband: James Howard Wife: Elizabeth Washburn Marriage: Date: ABT 1684 Place: , Plymouth, Massachusetts Husband: Edward Seely Wife: Elizabeth Washburn Marriage: Date: BEF 1693 Parents Marriage
2 CONT
