2 CONT ↑ Calculated from the date of her marriage, in ca. 1685. ↑ Mitchell, History of Bridgewater, pp. 191-192. ↑ Calculated from the birth of their first child on 16 Jan. 1686 in Bridgewater. ↑ Mitchell, History of Bridgewater, p. 176.
2 CONC  ↑ Mitchell, History of Bridgewater, p. 192. ↑ Plymouth Co. Probate Docket #9802. ↑ Calculated from the birth of their first child on 5 Mar. 1693 in Bridgewater. ↑ Plymouth Co. Probate Docket #17769, Vol. 1, p. 303. The inventory 
2 CONC was valued at £122 13s, and Elizabeth Sealley, relict and widdow of Edward Sealley, gave her oath to the inventory on 25 May 1699. ↑ See appendix [C] ↑ Norton VRs, p. 393, under “Silley.” ↑ Mitchell, History of Bridgewater, p. 192
2 CONC , says James Howard and Elizabeth Washburn had Elizabeth 1686, Mercy 1688, and James 1690; Mitchell, History of Bridgewater, p. 289, says Edward Sealy and Elizabeth Howard had Benjamin 1693, and John 1697. Maltby Genealogies - Eli
