2 CONT Profile last modified 25 Aug 2019 | Created 21 Oct 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane (Washburn) Orcutt was related to a passenger on the Mayflower.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband: William Orcutt Wife: Jane Washburn Marriage: Date: AFT 28 Jul 1690 V.R.Hingham, Plymouth, Massachusetts[1][2][3] Maltby
2 CONT
2 CONT Jane Washburn, the sister of Samuel Washburn, married William Orcutt (Jr.), of Scituate, MA, in ca. 1691. Her daughter Joanna Orcutt married Benjamin Edson on 14 July 1715 in Bridgewater, and their son Seth Edson settled in Staffo
2 CONC rd, CT, where he had a big family. Seth's son Levi Edson married Mary (Blodgett) Washburn, widow of Jacob Washburn, on 29 Oct. 1783 in Stafford, and Levi's son Daniel Edson married Sarah/Sally Howe, daughter of Israel and Hannah R
2 CONC obinson (Washburn) Howe, on 21 Sept. 1820 in Stafford. The other Orcutt families found in Stafford were probably not descendants of Jane (Washburn) Orcutt, but of William's second wife, Hannah Smith. William and Hannah's daughter 
2 CONC Deliverance Orcutt married Capt. Joseph Washburn, son of Josiah and Mercy (Tilson) Washburn, in ca. 1728, and Deliverance's sister Martha Orcutt was the one who married Solomon Washburn (Sr.) on 13 Jan. 1831/2 in Bridgewater.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ [1] Pedigree Chart for Lt. Solomon Washburn: has b abt 1670. ↑ Francis Cook of the Mayflower, compiled by Robert S. Wakefield, FASG and Ralph Van Wood, Jr., third edition; General society of Mayflower Descendants, 1994; p 55. ↑ 
2 CONC http://www.compuology.com/richard/richard/ped_028.html has Jane b 1666, :: Duxbury, Plymouth, Massachusetts. ↑ John A. Maltby - Plymouth Colony and Massachusetts
