2 CONT
2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT Packard 1 English: from Middle English pa(c)k ‘pack’, ‘bundle’ + the Anglo-Norman French pejorative suffix -ard, hence a derogatory occupational name for a peddler.2 English: pejorative derivative of the Middle English personal na
2 CONC me Pack .3 English: from a Norman personal name, Pachard, Baghard, composed of the Germanic elements pac, bag ‘fight’ + hard ‘hardy’, ‘brave’, ‘strong’. Dictionary of American Family Names © Patrick Hanks 2003, 2006. Possible Rela
2 CONC ted Names Pack Packer Packett
2 CONT
2 CONT 1680 1700 1720 1740 1760 1780 1800 1820 1840 1860
