2 PLAC Oak Ridge Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Springfield
3 STAE Illinois
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Originally buried in Hutchinson Cemetery and reinterred in 1881. Her grave is unmarked.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married in November of 1794 to Captain Peleg Canedy. He was born around 1774 in Middleboro, Massachusetts and is believed to be a son of Isaac Canedy and Deborah Benson. He was a well to do business man in Greenwich, Massa
2 CONC chusetts and after some legal trouble he located briefly to Scioto Co., Ohio. By 1810 he was living in Middlebury, Vermont where he enlisted into the regular army for the War of 1812. According to family legend he died around 1818
2 CONC  after falling off a raft in the Ohio River. After 1805 she relocated to Middlebury, Vermont. In 1820 she is listed as the head of household.
2 CONT
2 CONT She lived in Washington, DC and had a store on Pennsylvania Avenue. Her store and materials were auctioned off in 1840. After this time she relocated to Springfield, Illinois.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Springfield, Sangamon, Illinois, United States - 1850
