1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Littlefield-558
2 CONT Ruth (Littlefield) Paine (1710 - 1801)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth Paine formerly Littlefield aka Dyer, Payne
2 CONT Born 6 Mar 1710 in Braintree, Suffolk County, Province of Massachusetts Baymap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Daughter of Edmund Littlefield and Elizabeth (Mott) Littlefield
2 CONT Sister of Mary (Littlefield) Harden [half], Edmund Littlefield Jr [half], John Littlefield [half], Samuel Littlefield [half], Nathaniel Littlefield, Elizabeth (Littlefield) Linfield, Sarah (Littlefield) Cheney, Anna (Littlefield) 
2 CONC Dyer, Abigail (Littlefield) Smith, Lydia Littlefield, Levi Littlefield, Deborah Littlefield, Hepzibah Littlefield and Dorcas (Littlefield) Horton
2 CONT Wife of John Dyer — married 15 Aug 1727 in Dorchester, Suffolk, MAmap
2 CONT Wife of Samuel Paine Jr. — married 7 Jul 1741 [location unknown]
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Mother of Abijah Dyer, Sarah Dyer, John Dyer, Christopher Dyer, Rachael (Paine) Stetson and Rebecca (Payne) Hunt
2 CONT Died 23 Dec 1801 at age 91 in Bridgewater, Plymouth County, Massachusetts, United Statesmap
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile manager: DavaLynn Joy private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 7 Jun 2022 | Created 15 Feb 2014
2 CONT This page has been accessed 559 times.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth was the daughter of Edmund and Elizabeth (Mott) Littlefield. Her first marriage was to John Dyer 15 August 1727 Dorchester MA.[1][2] After his death, she married again on 7 July 1741, to Samuel Payne, Jr.. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Payne and his second wife, Ruth, had two daughters, both baptized in the Braintree South Parish on 14 March 1742:[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel, married John Stetson.
2 CONT Rebecca, married John Hunt, Jr.
2 CONT Samuel Payne made his will on 1 June 1759; it was filed for probate on 17 October 1763. The will contained an unusual insult directed toward Ruth: "To that woman that lives with me, called my wife, Ruth Payne, so much of my estate
2 CONC  as she can get by law, and no more, for she is a very imprudent and bad woman and hath hurt my estate many hundred of pounds by giving and selling out of my house things that did not belong to her. I know she doth not deserve any
2 CONC  of my estate and I hope she will not get much of it." The will also made provision for sons Peter, Ebenezer, and Jacob; daughters Hannah Payne, Rachel Payne, and Rebecca Hunt; grandson Stephen Payne; and granddaughter Silence All
2 CONC en. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried Scotland Cemetery, Bridgewater, Plymouth, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth died 23 Dec 1801 Bridgewater MA.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Waldo Chamberlaian Spraque, AB, Genealogy of the Families of Braintree Mass. 1640-1850, card 3055.
2 CONT ↑ Pricilla Eaton, The Littlefield Genealogy, Descendants of Edmund Littlefield of Wells ME Through Six Generations, 220, 28.
2 CONT ↑ Sprague, #3694R Page 1222 - 1223 ($subscription)
2 CONT ↑ Sprague, #3695R Page 1223 ($subscription)
2 CONT ↑ Sprague, #3694 and #3694R. Page 1222 - 1223 ($subscription)
2 CONT ↑ FindaGrave, https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/61950405/ruth-pain
2 CONT Sprague, Waldo Chamberlain, Genealogies of the Families of Braintree, MA. 1640-1850 (2001).
