1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Dyer-8697
2 CONT John Dyer (1706 - 1739)
2 CONT
2 CONT John Dyer
2 CONT Born 1706 in Braintree, Suffolk County, Province of Massachusetts Baymap
2 CONT ANCESTORS ancestors
2 CONT Son of John Dyer and Hannah (Unknown) Dyer
2 CONT Brother of William Dyer [half], William Dyer [half], Nathaniel Dyer, Christopher Dyer, Anna (Dyer) Pratt, Samuel Dyer, Jonathan Dyer, Sarah (Dyer) Sloan, William Dyer, Mary (Dyer) Price, Peter Dyer and Deborah (Dyer) Grice
2 CONT Husband of Ruth (Littlefield) Paine — married 15 Aug 1727 in Dorchester, Suffolk, MAmap
2 CONT DESCENDANTS descendants
2 CONT Father of Abijah Dyer, Sarah Dyer, John Dyer and Christopher Dyer
2 CONT Died 1739 at about age 33 in Braintree, Suffolk County, Province of Massachusetts Baymap
2 CONT PROBLEMS/QUESTIONSProfile manager: DavaLynn Joy private message [send private message]
2 CONT Profile last modified 7 Jun 2022 | Created 15 Feb 2014
2 CONT This page has been accessed 422 times.
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT John Dyer (John3, William1) was born about 1706 in Braintree, Massachusetts,[1] and died in 1739 in Braintree, about age 33.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Dyer lived some years in Dorchester; he, however, returned to his farm in Braintree, where he died, in 1739 [2]S.D.115-1, 1768: Christopher Dyer of Bridgewater, guardian of brother John Dyer who is deaf & dumb sells to Samuel
2 CONC  Wales, blacksmith, half of the 11th lot in 5th Division in Cochato in Braintree. (Sprague #1475)
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Ruth Littlefield on 15 Aug 1727 in Dorchester, Suffolk, MA., daughter of Edmund Littlefield and Elizabeth Mott. Ruth was born on 6 Mar 1709/10 in Braintree, Norfolk, MA, and died on 23 Dec 1801 in Bridgewater, Plymout
2 CONC h, MA at age 91, and was buried in 1801 in Scotland Cemetery, Bridgewater, Plymouth, MA. They were of Braintree on April 16, 1728 when they conveyed to brother Nathaniel Littlefield their interest in the estate of their father Edm
2 CONC und Littlefield. [Frank A. Bates]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children from this marriage were:
2 CONT
2 CONT + 92 M i. Abijah Dyer 41 120 121 was born about 1727 in Braintree, Norfolk, Ma and died on an unknown date.
2 CONT
2 CONT + 93 F ii. Sarah Dyer was born between 1727 and 1739 in Braintree, Norfolk, Ma and died on 26 Apr 1768 in Dorchester, Suffolk, Ma.
2 CONT
2 CONT + 94 M iii. John Dyer 118 122 was born in 1728 in Braintree, Norfolk, Ma, died on 27 Dec 1817 in Bridgewater, Plymouth, Ma12 67 at age 89, and was buried in 1817 in Scotland Cemetery, Bridgewater, Plymouth, Ma.
2 CONT
2 CONT + 95 M iv. Christopher Dyer 12 123 124 was born about 1730 in Braintree, Norfolk, Ma, died on 15 May 1800 in Bridgewater, Plymouth, Ma67 about age 70, and was buried in 1800 in Scotland Cemetery, Bridgewater, Plymouth, Ma.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Pricilla Eaton, The Littlefield Genealogy, Descendants of Edmund Littlefield of Wells ME Through Six Generations, 220, 28.
2 CONT ↑ NEHGR, vol.60:389]
2 CONT Sprague, Waldo Chamberlain. Genealogies of the Families of Braintree, MA. 1640-1850 (2001)
