2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Samuel Jr. and Abigail (Leonard) Washburn removed from Bridgewater to Stafford Tolland Co., Conn. about 1735
2 CONT In a "love and affection" deed dated and acknowledged 6 October 1718, Samuel Washburn of Bridgewater, yeoman, gave several piece of land in Bridgewater ot his son Samuel, also of Bridgewater. In another deed dated 8 December 1734 
2 CONC and acknowledged 8 April 1735, Samuel Washburn and wife Abigail of Bridgewater sold theri homstead in Bridgewater and a cedar swamp "...which my father Samuel Washburn died seized of..." together with all rights yet to come in the
2 CONC  will of Samuel's father. No Plymouth County probate has been found for Samuel or Abigail Washburn.
2 CONT
