1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Joseph-Shaw-of-Weymouth/6000000182818621917
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Shaw
2 CONT * Birth:	Jan 11 1691 - Weymouth, Massachusetts (Suffolk)
2 CONT * Death:	 7 Dec 1761 in Bridgewater, Plymouth, Province of Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT * Parents:	Joseph Shaw, Judith Whitmarsh
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph was born on January 11, 1691. He was the son of Joseph Shaw and Judith[1] Whitmarsh.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph removed from Weymouth to Bridgewater with his parents. He died their sometime before 7 December 1761 when his will was probated. Joseph did not marry or have children, as evidenced by his will which only names his siblings 
2 CONC Ebenezer John and Zachariah and sister Martha Allen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Last will and testament
2 CONT
2 CONT Dated 23 November 1759, Joseph Shaw of Bridgewater. Names brothers Ebenezer Shaw, John Shaw, sister Martha Allen, brother Zachariah (named executor). Administration of estate granted 7 Dec 1761. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disambiguation 
2 CONT
2 CONT oseph Shaw confusion explanation
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Shaw (b 11 Jan 1691 Weymouth d. abt 1761 Bridgewater) is very often confused with Joseph Shaw b 1682 poss Weymouth. (Including myself for years.) Joseph Shaw (b. 1691) was the son of Joseph Shaw (1664-1718) and Judith Whitm
2 CONC arsh (1669-1760). Joseph Shaw (b. 1682) was the son of (Deacon) John Shaw (1653-1717/8) and Hannah Whitmarsh (1661-1735) (Note: John Shaw (1653-1717/8) was the brother of Joseph Shaw (1664-1718) and they married sisters Judith and
2 CONC  Hannah Whitmarsh.) Joseph Shaw, b 15 Apr 1664, was the son of John Shaw & Alice Phillips, above, m. Judith Whitmarsh b 2 Sep 1669. Joseph & Judith (Whitmarsh) Shaw's son, Joseph Shaw, b 11 Jan 1691 Weymouth never married. Joseph 
2 CONC & Judith (Whitmarsh) Shaw later moved to Bridgewater. Joseph Shaw (b. 1682) possibly married sisters (1) Sarah (?Blanchard?) & (2) Mary Blanchard [Blancher in Weymouth vital records for both], contrary to most genealogies. The evi
2 CONC dence for this is as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. The Joseph Shaw who died in 1744 is listed in Weymouth VR as the son of John and Hannah (Shaw). 2. The first three children (including Joseph b. 1691) of Joseph Shaw (1664-1718) and Judith Whitmarsh (1669-1760) were born in Wey
2 CONC mouth, the rest of their children were born in Bridgewater. Thus the family moved to Bridgewater between1695 and 1698. Weymouth VR and Bridgewater VR 3. In the probate cases of John Shaw (1653-1717/8) Joseph Shaw (b. 1691) is list
2 CONC ed as being of Bridgewater. The Suffolk County probate lists Joseph and nine of his ten siblings, matching the names of the children of Joseph Shaw (1664-1718) and Judith Whitmarsh (1669-1760). Plymouth Co Probate case 17869 and S
2 CONC uffolk Co Probate case 4162 4. The will of Joseph Shaw (b. 1691) makes no mention of wife or children and names his siblings. Plymouth Co Probate case 17970 5. Nahum Mitchell states on p. 304 of his book History of the Early Settl
2 CONC ement of Bridgewater that Joseph & Judith (Whitmarsh) Shaw's children, Joseph Shaw and Judith Shaw never married. 6. There is no evidence that a Joseph Shaw died on 25 Mar 1742, a date given in many genealogies and Early Pleasant 
2 CONC River Families. That is the date for the will of Joseph Shaw.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Shaw-1425
2 CONT *The New England Historical and Genealogical Society, Vital Records of Weymouth, Massachusetts to the Year 1850 Volume I - Births (Boston, Mass. 1910)(Free e-book) p. 270
2 CONT *Plymouth County, MA: Probate File Papers, 1686-1881.Online database. AmericanAncestors.org. New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2015. (From records supplied by the Massachusetts Supreme Judicial Court Archives.) [ https://
2 CONC www.americanancestors.org/DB1558/i/20956/17970-co5/45531524 Case 17970: Will]
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-255068091-1-598600/joseph-shaw-in-myheritage-family-trees MyHeritage Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 29 2021, 16:52:32 UTC
2 CONC ''
