1 NOTE {geni:about_me} DAR Ancestor #: A102230 
2 CONT
2 CONT REVOLUTIONARY WAR VETERAN?
2 CONT
2 CONT Zachariah may have been in the Revolution, over sixty years old at the time.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Zacharias is probably the Zacharias Sr. mentioned in the Revolutionary Rolls. Zacharias Sr. is named in connection with 'Alarms' on which he marched. The family of Zacharias and Sarah are recorded in Bridgewater. The break betwee
2 CONC n Elizabeth, born 1744, and Judith born 1749 would serve to indicate that he served in King George's War which lasted from 1743 to 1748, and since he had had service, he very probably served in the French and Indian War, making a 
2 CONC total of three wars in which he had some part." --Kenneth Linwood Shaw
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Links''':
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=glencoe&id=I29069
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Shaw-4925
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-306397661-3-501807/zachariah-zechariah-shaw-in-myheritage-family-trees?indId=externalindividual-5c6eb4d0429a5c483ec21bd16aa297bd&mrid=7d0fc70599550e7a58ea96f87c949594 MyHe
2 CONC ritage Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Feb 22 2019, 17:34:38 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT *
2 CONT Zackarias was the youngest of 7 children of Joseph Shaw (1664-1718) & Judith Whitmarsh (1669-1760).
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married on 30 Aug 1733 at Bridgewater, Plymouth County, Massachusetts to Sarah Packard.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had 9 children:
2 CONT . Sarah Shaw (1734)
2 CONT + sp: Elijah Snow
2 CONT . Joseph Shaw (1736 - 1760)
2 CONT . Ruth Shaw (1738)
2 CONT + sp: Joseph Snow
2 CONT . Martha Shaw (1740 - 1825)
2 CONT . Daniel Shaw (1742 - 1830)
2 CONT + sp: Olive Lillie
2 CONT . Elizabeth Shaw (1744)
2 CONT + sp: Obadiah Reed
2 CONT . Judith Shaw (1749)
2 CONT + sp: John Edson
2 CONT . Zechariah Shaw (1751 - 1820)
2 CONT + sp: Hannah Bisbee
2 CONT . Nehemiah Shaw (1753)
2 CONT + sp: Molly Beal
2 CONT ∼Zacharia was married to Sarah Packard Shaw.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/47964873/zackarias-shaw Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 17 2025, 18:50:14 UTC'
