1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/130751731/mary-oliver
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Walker Oliver BIRTH	1706 DEATH	20 Aug 1788 (aged 81–82) Chester Center, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA BURIAL	 Chester Center Cemetery Chester Center, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA  MEMORIAL ID	130751731 · View Sourc
2 CONC e
2 CONT
2 CONT Member Photo ×
2 CONT Memorial updated successfully. ×
2 CONT Yeah, no more ads! Memorial has been sponsored successfully. ×
2 CONT Your suggestions have been submitted and will be reviewed by the memorial manager. ×
2 CONT Your edit did not contain any changes from the original. ×
2 CONT Thank you! Your suggested merge has been submitted for review. ×
2 CONT You are now the manager of this memorial. Thanks for helping with Find a Grave! ×
2 CONT The Photo Request has been fulfilled.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Mary <I>Walker</I> Oliver Photo added by Howard Knickerbocker
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Walker Oliver BIRTH	1706 DEATH	20 Aug 1788 (aged 81–82) Chester Center, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA BURIAL	 Chester Center Cemetery Chester Center, Hampden County, Massachusetts, USA  MEMORIAL ID	130751731 · View Sourc
2 CONC e
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 1 FLOWERS 2
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: The memorial for Mary (Walker) Oliver #100852932, buried in Ohio is perhaps a cenotaph.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary was the daughter of William Walker and his wife (_).
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Walker Oliver (1706-8/20/1788), born perhaps in Ireland, died in Hampden Co., MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1 WALKER sibling known: William Walker of Worcester, MA. William: 96771739.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary married Lancelot/Lanslet/Lanslot Oliver (1704-1781) who was born in Ireland in 1704. Lancelot: 99937824. Buried in Caldwell Cemetery, Barre, Worcester, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lancelot came to Boston, MA with a large group of Ulster Scots in about 1719.
2 CONT
2 CONT A second place of burial for Lanslot/Lancelot Oliver has been found in OH: #100853000, with a nearly unreadable headstone, and is, perhaps, a cenotaph.
2 CONT
2 CONT 9 OLIVER children:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. William Oliver B~1730.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Margaret Oliver B~1733 in Worchester Co., MA, D~1791; m. William Galloway.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Robert Richard Oliver (1738-8/7/1811); m. Mary "Mollie" Walker on 10/13/1863 in Worcester, MA. Robert was a Captain in the Revolutionary War (MA). He was one of the leading men in Washington Co., OH. He was a Representative of 
2 CONC Washington Co., OH in 1798, and one of the five councilors. Robert: 77850761. Born in Middlesex Co., MA, died in Marietta, Washington Co., OH. [See a study of R.R. Oliver and his family: 130982654.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Lanslet Oliver Jr. (1739-7/16/1750) born and died in Worcester Co., MA, buried in Caldwell Cemetery, Barre, Worchester, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. James Oliver (10/13/1741 (Mass.)- 1784 (New Brunswick, Canada); m. Isabel Walker (sister of Mary Walker who married Col Robert R. Oliver (sic: wife's name may be incorrect).
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Col. Alexander Oliver Sr. (1744-1827); m. Mary Warner. Alexander: 18218503. Buried in OH. Revolutionary War Soldier. ...12 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Katherine Oliver B~1744 or 1746; m. (_) Kimpland.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. David Oliver (~1747-3/3/1821 born and died in Worcester Co., MA; m. Elizabeth Boyd B-1746. Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. John Oliver (1755-1777) born and died in Worcester Co., MA. Buried in Caldwell Cemetery, Barre, Worchester, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Primary source: http://www.aleighasfamilytree.com/oliverlancelot.htm __________ Preliminary research: Kim B (#47765575), 2012. __________ Research: Mary E. Warner, 2014.
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Mary WALKER [mother of Alexander Oliver] Birth: 1706 in probably Ireland Death: 20 Aug 1788 in Chester, Hampden County, Massachusetts Birth: 1711 in Barre, Worchester County, Massachusetts, Colonial America (from 1492 to 7/4
2 CONC /1776) Burial: Aft 20 Aug 1788 Row 30, Old Section, Greenlawn Cemetery, Lowell, Washington County, Ohio. Event: Property 3 Jul 1781 See Notes Note: REFN: 59173 PROPERTY: Received through husband's will [Lanslot/Lancelot Oliver] ".
2 CONC ..all my indoor Moveables and household furniture and an Annuity of Twenty Spanish milled Dollars, or an equivalent thereunto in such money as Shall be the then circulating medium, the above sum to be paid to her. . . annually Dur
2 CONC ing her natural life." Source: "History of the Oliver & Bryan Families from 1700 to the Present, 9 Generations", online, Kathleen Celeste Bryan, web master, downloaded 16 June 2005.
2 CONT
2 CONT Greenlawn Cemetary, Lowell, Ohio, records show inscription to say " wife of Lanslot Oliver" - the rest is gone; perhaps a cenotaph.
2 CONT
2 CONT FROM: HISTORY OF MARRIETTA AND WASHINGTON COUNTY, OHIO, by Martin R. Andrews 1789--Belpre, Ohio 1793--Bought Lot 19, Belpre, Ohio Was first buried in Wesley Chapel Burying Grounds, Cincinnati, Ohio. August 19, 1865, his remains we
2 CONC re moved to Section 22, Lot 34, Spring Grove Cemetery, Cincinnati, Ohio. (sic: Lancelot was NOT buried in Ohio, but in Massachusetts.) ____________________
2 CONT
2 CONT ABOUT Lancelot Oliver, Mary Walker's husband
2 CONT
2 CONT Lancelot Oliver
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1703 or 1704 in Ulster, Ireland, - died after 1781 in Worcester Co., MA. Buried in Caldwell Cemetery, Barre, Worcester, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Email from W. Smith (author of a family history on this family):
2 CONT
2 CONT "In 1718, Lancelot arrived in Boston, Massachusetts, (Colonial America from 1492 to 7/4/1776) from northern Ireland (Province of Ulster) with parents and brother [William].
2 CONT
2 CONT "Lancelot Oliver's Last Will and Testament, Signed January 3, 1781 Recorded July 3, 1781:
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the name of God Amen. I, Lancelot Oliver of Barre in the County of Worcester and Commonwealth of Massachusetts, husbandman, being weak in Body but of perfect mind and memory, thanks be to God for it, calling to mind the mortal
2 CONC ity of my body and knowing that it is appointed to all men once to die. I do make and ordain this my last Will and Testament that is to say principally and first of all I give and recommend my soul into the Hands of the Almighty G
2 CONC od that gave it and my Body I recommend unto the Earth to be buried in decent Christian burial, in blessed hope that I shall receive it again at the general resurrection, to a blessed and glorious immortality, through him who is t
2 CONC he Resurrection and the Life. And as touching such worldly estate where with it has pleased God to bless me in this Life, I give, demise and dispose of the Same in the following Manner and Form:
2 CONT
2 CONT "First, I give and bequeath to my beloved Wife, Mary Oliver, all my indoor Moveables and household furniture and an Annuity of Twenty Spanish milled Dollars, or an equivalent thereunto in such money as Shall be the then circulatin
2 CONC g medium, the above sum to be paid to her the said Mary, annually During her natural life.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Item. I give to my son William Oliver five shillings, to be paid him within one year after my decease -- which together with what he has received is his full share of my estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Item. I give to my Daughter Margaret Galloway five shillings which together with what she has received is her full proportion of my Estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Item. I give to my son David Oliver five shillings which together with what I have given him by Deed is his full proportion of my Estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Item. I give and bequeath to my son Robert Oliver and to my son Alexander Oliver and to my daughter Katherine Kimpland the whole and every part of the remainder of the real and personal estate of which I shall die seized and poss
2 CONC essed to be divided equally among them.
2 CONT
2 CONT "The above named Robert Oliver and Alexander I also make and ordain the sole executors of this my Last Will and Testament. And I do hereby disallow, revoke and disannull all and every other former Testaments, Wills, Legacies, Bequ
2 CONC ests and Executors by me in any ways before named, willed, and testified, ratifying and confirming this and no other to be my Last Will and Testament. In witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seal, this third day of Janu
2 CONC ary in the year of our Lord one Thousand, Seven hundred and Eight one.
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed Lanslet Oliver "Signed, sealed, published, pronounced and declared by said Lanselot Oliver as his last Will and Testament in the presence of us who in his presence and in the presence of each other have hereunto subscribed 
2 CONC our names.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Thomas Rice, Peter Fessenden, Josiah Dana, Recorded July 3, 1781." __________ Primary source: http://www.aleighasfamilytree.com/oliverlancelot.htm
2 CONT
