2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT This Mary had two older sisters named Mary who died young. One was born on 19 November 1722. The other was born on 2 August 1727. This Mary was baptized 21 February 1730/1.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Kneeled, a direct descendent of John Alden, was born in Boston, and died in 1766. She married Thomas Walley, and had a daughter, Mary Walley, who became the wife of the Revolutionary War soldier, Capt. John Langdon. She was o
2 CONC ne of the progenitors of the Langdon, Lodge, Pratt, and Whitney families of Boston.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Kneeland. [2][3][4][5][6][7][8]
