2 CONT William Hilton and Mehitable (Nowell) had the following known children, born and baptized at Charlestown:[2]
2 CONT # Nowell, b May 4, 1653; d between October 6, 1687 and Sept 17, 1689
2 CONT # Edward, b March 3, 1666; not mentioned in mother's or siblings' wills
2 CONT # John, bp May 24 1668; d before January 14, 1741; m Sarah Parruck
2 CONT # Richard, b September 13, 1670; d Charlestown January 25, 1720/1; m Elizabeth Lord January 22, 1711/12 at Charlestown
2 CONT # Charles, b April 19, 1673; not mentioned in mother's or siblings' wills
2 CONT # Samuel, living December 8, 1709 when mother mentioned him in her will; not mentioned in brother Richard's will in 1721.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT From Cutler, Nahum Sawin. Cutler Memorial and Genealogical History: Containing the Names of a large proportion of the Cutlers in the United States and Canada, and a Record of many Individual Members of the Family, with an Account 
2 CONC also of other Families allied to the Cutlers by Marriage. (Greenfield, Mass.: Press of E.A. Hall & Co., 1889), 509.
2 CONT
2 CONT >John Cutler m. (2) 29 Oct 1684 Mehitable, d/o Increase Nowell, widow of William Hilton, who d. 29 Sep 1711, age 74. Will mentions her sister Mary Long, Mrs Simon Bradstreet, her maid Elizabeth Lord, and residue to two sons John a
2 CONC nd Richard Hilton.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
