2 CONT ==Notes==
2 CONT Often confused with: Thomas Graves, engineer, married Sarah Whiting  http://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Graves/6000000015830558790 and Thomas Graves of Hatfield, married Sarah Scott http://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Graves-of-Hatfi
2 CONC eld/6000000002315691094
2 CONT
2 CONT Rear Admiral Thomas Graves has sometimes been confused with the engineer of the same name.  Thomas Graves, the engineer was of Gravesend, County of Kent, England, signed a contract with the Massachusetts Bay Company in March 1629,
2 CONC  arrived in New England in July 1629, and laid out Charlestown.  Thomas Graves, the engineer, was clearly not the same as Rear Admiral Thomas Graves.  In 1629 the engineer already had an impressive reputation for engineering, had 
2 CONC traveled extensively, and had a wife and five children.  He was older than the 24 years of age that the Rear Admiral was at that time.  In addition, the signature of the Rear Admiral from his will, and that of the engineer from hi
2 CONC s contract, as shown below, are different (from History of Charlestown, page 140, by.Richard Frothingham). http://www.gravesfa.org/gen028.htm 
2 CONT
