1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Thomas Graves==
2 CONT * BIRTH 1638 Boston, Suffolk County, Massachusetts Bay Colony 
2 CONT *1656: Graduated Harvard College. [1]
2 CONT *1665: Sept. 17: Admitted to the First Church at Charlestown. [1]
2 CONT *1676: 77: 78: Served as Deputy to Massachusetts General Court. [1]
2 CONT * DEATH 30 May 1697 (aged 58–59) Boston, Suffolk County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Central Burying Ground, Boston, Suffolk County, Province of Massachusetts
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID 182267818 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT Thomas Graves was born at Charlestown about 1638, son of Thomas Sr. and Katherine Graves. [1] He was both a physician and a Judge to the County Court. [2]  Hemarried 1st on May 16, 1677, the widow Elizabeth (Hagbourne/Hackburn) Ch
2 CONC ickering, widow of Dr. John Chickering. Elizabeth died on July 2, 1679. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT After her death, Thomas married 2nd widow Sarah Alcock on May 15, 1682 at Charlestown. [5] [1] Sarah was the daughter of John Stedman, and the widow of first John Bracket, and second, Samuel Alcock. (p. 9379) [6] Hon. Thomas Grave
2 CONC s, who was distinguished as a physician and judge died on May 30, 1697.  After Thomas' death, his widow Sarah married Colonel John Philips. She died on March 1, 1731 aged eighty seven.  He and Sarah had one son, Thomas, born at Ch
2 CONC arlestown on Sept. 28, 1683; died June 19, 1747 [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Will of Thomas Graves== [1]
2 CONT written May 25, 16976, has bequests to:
2 CONT * beloved wife Sarah, executrix
2 CONT * son Thomas
2 CONT * children of his sister Rebecca Adams
2 CONT * children of his sister Susannah Symes 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Parents'''
2 CONT Rear Admiral Thomas Graves 1605–1653 
2 CONT Katherine Gray Graves 1605–1681
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Spouse'''
2 CONT Elizabeth Chickering (Hagborne)
2 CONT Sarah Stedman Alcock 1644–1729
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Siblings'''
2 CONT Elizabeth Graves (____ - 1676)
2 CONT Rebecca Graves Adams 1630–1664
2 CONT Capt. John Graves 1633–1664
2 CONT William Graves
2 CONT Thomas Graves 
2 CONT Nathaniel Graves 1639–1679
2 CONT Susannah Graves Symmes 1643–1681
2 CONT Joseph Graves 1645–1689
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Half Siblings'''
2 CONT Thomas Greaves 1683–1747
2 CONT John Brackett
2 CONT Sarah Brackett
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children''' with Elizabeth*, Sarah**
2 CONT **Thomas Greaves 9/28/1683 Boston, MA, d. 6/19/1747 Boston, MA m. Sybil Graves; Phoebe Vassall and Ann Watts Father of Margaret Graves and Katherine Russell 
2 CONT
