1 NAME Joseph /Graves/
2 GIVN Joseph
2 _MARNM Graves
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 13 APR 1645
2 ADDR
3 CITY Charlestown
3 STAE Massachusetts
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 1689
2 ADDR
3 CITY Sudbury
3 STAE Massachusets
3 CTRY British Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} •Birth: 13 APR 1645 in Charlestown, Suffolk Co., MA 2 3  •Death: AFT 1689 in prob. Sudbury, Middlesex Co., MA 4  •Note:  Graves Family Association http://www.gravesfa.org/gen028.htm Rear Adm. Thomas Graves of Charl
2 CONC estown, MA
2 CONT
2 CONT  Joseph Graves (8) was born 13 April 1645 (written 13th day, 2nd month, in old style calendar) in Charlestown, Middlesex Co., MA, and probably died in Sudbury, MA. He first married Elizabeth Maynard, daughter of John Maynard and M
2 CONC ary Axtell, on 15 Jan. 1665/6 (VR, p. 206) in Sudbury, Middlesex Co., MA. She was born 26 May 1649 and died 5 June 1676 in Sudbury, MA (VR, p. 307). They settled in Sudbury, MA, then a growing plantation (the name in the colony fo
2 CONC r a settlement or town) in the receding wilderness. After his first wife died in 1676, Joseph secondly married Mary Ross, daughter of James Ross and Mary Goodnow, in 1678. She was born 25 Dec. 1656 in Sudbury, Middlesex Co., MA. H
2 CONC e was a soldier in King Philip's War. They lived in Sudbury, where all his children were born (all listed on p. 58, VR). (R-8, R-201, R-202, R-203) Children - Graves, by Elizabeth Maynard +31. Samuel Graves, b. 14 Feb. 1666/7, m. 
2 CONC Anna <nowiki>------</nowiki>, d. 1757. +32. Richard Graves, b. 7 April 1672, m. Joanna <nowiki>------</nowiki>. +33. John Graves, b. 10 May 1674, m. Sarah Loker, 10 Oct. 1710. May not be a son, since he does not appear in the publ
2 CONC ished birth VR for Sudbury.
2 CONT  34. Deliverance Graves, b. 10 May 1674 (according to J. C. Graves, who said she and John were twins) (or 1676). Children - Graves, by Mary Ross
2 CONT  35. Mary Graves, b. 23 May 1680. +36. Ebenezer Graves, b. 28 Feb. 1681/2, m. Elizabeth Haynes, c. 1702, d. 6 Feb. 1755.
2 CONT  37. Hester Graves, b. 3 April 1689.
2 CONT
2 CONT NEHGS Register Vol. 8, p. 346, Early Records of Boston Charlestown Joseph son of Thomas & Katherine borne 13 (2) 1645 Graves
2 CONT
2 CONT Vol. 17, p. 171, Sudbury Records Births Elizabeth, dau. of John & Mary Maynard, ... born 26 May 1649 
2 CONT
2 CONT Vol. 17, p. 257, Sudbury Records Marriages Joseph Graves & Elizabeth Maynard .. 15 Jan 1665  Births Samuel, son of Joseph & Elizabeth Graves .. born 14 Feb 1667 Marriges Jacob Moore & Elizabeth Loker .. 29 May 1667
2 CONT
2 CONT Vol. 17, p. 259 Sudbury Records Births Richard, son of Joseph and Elizabeth Graves .. born 7 Apl. 1672
2 CONT
2 CONT Vol. 17, p. 260 Sudbury Records Births Deliverance, daughter of Joseph and Elizabeth Graves . born 10 May 1674 Note, I did not find a record for the birth of John Graves in the Sudbury births, but apparently he was a twin of Deliv
2 CONC erance, with the same birth date, per. records found by William Berry
2 CONT
2 CONT Vol. 17, p. 312, Sudbury Records Deaths Elizabeth, wife of Joseph Graves ... Dyed 5 June 1676
2 CONT
2 CONT Barry, William, A history of Framingham, Massachusetts, including the plantation, from 1640 to the present time : with an appendix containing a notice of Sudbury and its first proprietors, also a register of the inhabitants of Fra
2 CONC mingham before 1800, with genealogical sketches  Boston: J. Munroe and Co., 1847, 460 pgs.
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 266, Genealogical Register, GRAVES
2 CONT
