1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nathaniel Graves
2 CONT Birthdate: October 5, 1639 (39)
2 CONT Birthplace: Ratcliff, London, England
2 CONT Death: February 12, 1679 (39)
2 CONT Died and on Atlantic Ocean
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~*
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT Rear Admiral Thomas Graves
2 CONT Katherine (Gray/Grey) Graves
2 CONT Spouse:
2 CONT Elizabeth (Russell) Herbert / Graves (1639-1679)
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~*
2 CONT SIBLINGS:
2 CONT Brother of *Rebecca Graves Adams; Captain John Graves; William Graves; Thomas Graves; Susanna Symmes (Graves); and Joseph Graves
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~*
2 CONT ~ Katherine Gray/Grey Graves ~
2 CONT
2 CONT About Katherine Graves
2 CONT Katherine was the wife of Rear Admiral Thomas Graves. She was born before 1605. Thomas came to this Country, with Governor Winthrop in 1630, having command of the "Talbot" the vice-admiral of the fleet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Winthrop's fleet consisted of eleven vessels, having on board about seven hundred people, two hundred and forty cows, and sixty horses. They sailed from Cowes on April 8, 1630, and after a stormy voyage, four vessels, the Arabella
2 CONC  with Winthrop on board, the Talbot, the Ambrose, and the Jewel, reached Salem, on June 12. By July 8, all the vessels had arrived. Not liking the vicinity of Salem, they soon left for Boston and distributed themselves in Charlest
2 CONC own, Watertown, etc. Thomas Graves settled in Charlestown. He made seven voyages to England, afterward commanding the "Trial" the first large vessel built in Boston, in her long voyages to Bilbo and Malaga. He died on July 31, 165
2 CONC 2. Their daughter Rebecca married Samuel Adams. (Pg 38). The long line of ledges outside of Boston Harbor, called "The Graves" was named for him.
2 CONT
2 CONT •~••~════~••~════~••~════~••~•
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT Father~
2 CONT Thomas Gray/Grey, of Harwich (1572 - 1607)
2 CONT Mother~
