1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Habijah Savage''' was the son of Major Thomas Savage and Faith Hutchinson. Some of his records are under spelling as : Abijah, Habbiah. Source: Massachusetts, Town and Vital Records. He was baptized at First Church of Boston, g
2 CONC raduated Harvard College and served as Captain of Mass. Militia. In 1665, he became a member of The Ancient & Honorable Artillery of Boston, like his father and brothers. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Habijah married Hannah Tyng 1640-1688, on 8 May 1661. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children are:
2 CONT # Joseph Savage 1662-1663
2 CONT # Thomas Savage 1664-1749 (Linked) 
2 CONT # Hannah (Gookin) 1667-1702. (linked) twin, wife of Nathaniel Gookin 1656-1692.
2 CONT # Mary (Weld) 1667-1731 (linked) twin, wife of Rev Thomas Weld 1653-1702
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Habijah Savage "died while on a trip to Barbados in connection with his business as trader". (Pg9)
2 CONT Source: Lawrence Park, 1914, Major Thomas Savage of Boston and his descendants. Pgs. 8-9.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
