2 CONT Hannah Savage Gookin BIRTH	27 Aug 1667, Boston, Suffolk County, Massachusetts, USA DEATH	14 May 1702 (aged 34), Cambridge, Middlesex County, Massachusetts, USA BURIAL	Old Burying Ground, Cambridge, Middlesex County, Massachusetts,
2 CONC  USA, MEMORIAL ID 49546987
2 CONT
2 CONT Pictures added by Liz L.
2 CONT
2 CONT Boston births: Hannah of Abijah & Hannah Savage born Aug. 27. 1667.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Nathaniel Gookin, Hannah Savage, Cambridge, Aug. 3, 1685 ? (from an online family tree, not in VRs)
2 CONT
2 CONT Cambridge deaths: GOOKIN, Hannah, wid. Rev. Nathaniel, late Paster of Church of Christ in Cambridge, May 14, 1702, in her 35th y. GR1
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents: Habbiah Savage & Hannah Ting daughter of Mr. Edward Ting of Boston were married 8th May by John Endecott Governor, [in Boston 1661.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Savage at the time of the marriage [was] also the step-dau. of Nathaniel's father. The Major-General Daniel had married Mrs. Hannah Savage, mother of Hannah, about 1684. Hannah Savage's father was Habijah Savage, b. Aug. 1,
2 CONC  1638, grad. Harvard Oct. 28, 1659 - m. May 8, 1661 Hannah Tyng, b. May 7, 1640, d. Oct. 28, 1688, (she m. 2nd Major General Daniel Gookin.) Hannah Tyng's father was Edward Tyng, Boston merchant, b. 1610, d. Dec 28, 1681, m. about
2 CONC  1636, Mary Sears.
2 CONT
2 CONT Habijah's father was Thomas, son of William Savage, b. 1604, came from London in the "Planter", 1635, d. Feb. 14, 1682. His mother was Faith Hutchinson, dau. of William H. and Ann Marbury. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (from Gookins, Richard N. An historical and genealogical sketch of the Gookin family of England, Ireland, America, 1952, 209 pgs.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents Habijah Savage, 1638–1668	 Hannah Tyng Gookin, 1640–1688
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse	 Nathaniel Gookin, 1656–1692 (m. 1685)
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings	 Thomas Savage, 1664–1749	 Mary Savage Weld, 1667–1731
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	 Nathaniel Gookin, 1687–1734	 Hannah Gookin Kent, 1693–1758
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription
2 CONT
2 CONT HERE LYES THE BODY  OF MRS. HANNAH  GOOKIN, RELICT OF  THE Revd. NATHANIEL  GOOKIN, LATE PASTOUR  OF THE CHURCH OF CHRIST  IN CAMBRIDGE, SHE DIED  MAY 14th, 1702, IN  HER 35th YEAR OF HER AGE.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/49546987/hannah-gookin
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Hanah's mother was already married to her husband's father (as his second wife) when they got married in 1685.
