1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Burgess to the Virginia House of Burgesses fir Upper Norfolk, Virginia, January 1641-42.
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Sewall of Coventry" (on-line): Hon. Daniel Gookin was born in 1612 either in Ripple, Kent, or Ireland.3,4,5 He was the son of Daniel Gookin and Mary Byrd.2 He first arrived n the New World from Ireland on 22nd November 1621 
2 CONC with fifty men of his own and thirty passengers and settled in Newport News, Virginia. He had been deputy, speaker, assistant, and superintendent of Indian affairs, he visted England twice and on his last return had the regicides 
2 CONC Goffe and Whalley under his protection. He is the author of Historical Collections of the Indians of Massachusetts, published posthumously, 1792.6,7 Hon. Daniel Gookin married secondly Mary Dolling after 11 November 1639 which was
2 CONC  the date of the licence to marry at St. Sepulchre's, London. Daniel Gookin is described in the licence as a gentleman and a widower, there is no trace of his earlier marriage.8,9,10 Hon. Daniel Gookin and Mary Dolling set sail in
2 CONC  1641 for Virginia.9 Hon. Daniel Gookin married as his second or third wife Hannah Tyng, daughter of Hon. Edward Tyng and Mary Sears, before 10 April 1685 at Cambridge, Massachusetts.11 Hon. Daniel Gookin died on 19 March 1686/87 
2 CONC in Cambridge, Massachusetts, "Satterday, about 5. or 6. in the morn, Major Daniel Gookin dies, a right good Man."6,12 He was buried on 22 March 1686/87 in the burying ground of the First Church, opposite the gate to Harvard Colleg
2 CONC e.7,13,14
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birthbef 6 Dec 1612 Birth Memo(bapt) Death19 Mar [1686/]1687, Cambridge, Middlesex, MA FatherDaniel GOOKIN , 10824 (?-1633) MotherMary BYRD , 55225 (?-?) Research 116 Children :
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Samuel Gookin - born 1640 died 1644 2.Mary Gookin - born 1642 died 1702 3.Elizabeth Gookin - born 1645 died 1700 4.Hannah Gookin - baptised 1647, Massachusetts died 1647 5.Daniel Gookin - born 1649, Massachusetts died 1649 6.Dan
2 CONC iel Gookin - born 1650 died 1718 7.Samuel Gookin - born 1652, Massachusetts died 1730, Massachusetts 8.Solomon Gookin - born 1654, Massachusetts died 1654 9.Nathaniel Gookin - born 1656 died 1692
2 CONT
2 CONT (3485) GOOKIN, Daniel (1612-87), from Eng., to Va thence to Boston, Mass., 1644; resided at Roxbury and Cambridge; capt., 1648; ma;. gen. Mass. forces, 1681; dep. Gen. Ct., 1649-51; speaker, 1651; gov.'s asst., 1652-86; commr. to 
2 CONC the Indians, 1656. Misc. Notes Date: Mon, 18 Feb 2002 13:11:04 -0800 From: Bill & Chris Strickland <lechevrier@earthlink.net> Reply-To: lechevrier@earthlink.net Organization: Le Chevrier French Alpines X-Accept-Language: en To: Ed
2 CONC  Cooper <emerald_city@mac.com> Subject: Daniel Gookin
2 CONT
2 CONT Ed --
2 CONT
2 CONT Since you appear to be knowledgeable in the matters of the various Daniel Gookins, and since your notes are not included in your website (that I have been able to find), I have a question ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Can you identify the two Daniel Gookins (Sr & Jr) who signed Edward Shepard's will in Cambridge, MA on 1 Oct 1674? To wit:
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the name of God, Amen. Know Ye that I, Edward Shepheard of Cambridge, New England, Mariner, being through the favor of God arrived unto old age expecting daily my change, I account it my duty to set my house in order; and ther
2 CONC efore do heregy make and declare this instrument for my last will and testament, 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. I commit my immortal soul into the hands of the Lord God Almighty, the only living and true God: distinguished into three glorious persons, The Father, Son, and Holy Ghost; resting and relying on the merits, righteousness and s
2 CONC atisfaction of my dear Lord Jesus Christ for life and salvation. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. That concerning my body, my will is that it be decently interred resting in hope that by the virtue of Christ's Resurrection it shall in God's appointed time be raised up again and united to my soul and both soul and body in on
2 CONC e man be translated to eternal happiness and there to live with God and praise him forever. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Lastly, concerning my temporal estate my will is that that which shall be and remain after my death, my will is that my just debts and funeral expenses, being first paid, the remainder to be disposed of as followeth, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Imp- I geve and bequeath unto my dear wife Mary either the sum of twenty pounds to be paid her by my executors within three months after my decease in such household goods and other things as may be suitable for her at equal price
2 CONC s as two honest men shall judge or in case of difference to be determined by the County Court; or else the use of my dwelling house, barn and orchard that lie on the north side of the Street during her life, provided she keep the 
2 CONC same in tentable repair. All the rest of my estate my will and order is that it be divided into six equal parts-- two parts I give and bequeath unto my son, John Shipard, or in case of his death before me then equally divided amon
2 CONC g his children; unto my daughter Elizabeth one sixth part or in case of her death before, then equally divided among her children; unto my daughter Deborah one sixth part, and in the case of her death before me then equally divide
2 CONC d among her children; Unto the children of Daniel Pond which he had by my daughter Abigail, deceased, one sixth part equally divided; unto my daughter Sarah one sixth part, or in case of her death before me then equally divided am
2 CONC ong her children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I do hereby nominate and appoint by dear son, John Shipard my executor of this will and in case he should decease before me that I do appoint his eldest son my executor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In testimony of the truth hereof, I have hereunto set my hand and seal this first day of October, 1674. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed: Edward Shephard 
2 CONT
2 CONT In presence of us,  Daniel Gookin, Senior  Daniel Gookin, Junior." 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward's will is on file at the Middlesex Probate Office in East Cambridge, Mass.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Daniel Gookins are of interest to me as part of my Strickland genealogy. It is commonly accepted that it was Thwaite Strickland who built a dwelling for a Daniel Gookin in Westerly, RI, and that this Daniel Gookin is reportedl
2 CONC y the son of a Daniel Gookin who emigrated to Virginia from Ireland and is possibly a clue to any possible connections between the Stricklands of New England and those who descended from Matthew Strickland of Isle of Wight, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT The above Edward Shepard is Thwaite Strickland's father-in-law.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thank you for any help you can provide, including reference to other sources,
2 CONT
