1 NAME Sarah /Gibbons/
2 GIVN Sarah
2 SURN Gibbons
2 _MARNM Tyng
2 NICK Richards
2 NICK Davie
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 17 AUG 1645
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hartford
3 STAE Connecticut Colony
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 FEB 1714
2 ADDR
3 CITY Woburn
3 STAE Province of Massachusetts
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sarah Gibbons, daughter of Walter Gibbons of Hartford.  Married first to James Richards of Hartford; he died 1680.  She became the second wife of  Humphrey Davie of Boston.  She married Jonathan Tyng for her third 
2 CONC husband; his 2nd wife.  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT From The Memorial History of Boston: Including Suffolk County ..., Volume 1edited by Justin Winsor, Clarence F. Jewett.  Page 578 [https://books.google.com/books?id=fb14AAAAMAAJ&lpg=PA578&ots=E9dJBKtOby&dq=Humphrey%20Davie%2C%20of
2 CONC %20Boston&pg=PA578#v=onepage&q&f=true GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT James Richards, presumed to be brother of John, of Boston and Hartford, was very wealthy, and held high rank in Connecticut. His wife was Sarah, only child of William Gibbons of Hartford, who married secondly Humphrey Davie, and t
2 CONC hirdly Colonel Jonathan Tyng. James Richards had an only son, Thomas, and the following daughters: Sarah, wife of Captain Benjamin Davis; Mary, married to Benjamin Alford, both of Boston; Jerusha, wife of Rev. Gurdon Saltonstall; 
2 CONC and Elizabeth, married first to John Davie, and secondly to Jonathan Taylor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Humphrey Davy, or Davie, was son of Sir John Davie, Bart., of Creedy, co. Devon. He was a leading man here, though of the later immigration,— 1662.- His son by his first wife was John, — H. C. 1681,—-who went to Hartford and marri
2 CONC ed his step-sister, Elizabeth, daughter of James Richards. He succeeded to the estate and title of his grandfather, and returned to England. Humphrey, the father, married, here, Sarah, widow of James Richards, and had Humphrey and
2 CONC  William, the former of whom moved to Hartford.
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *"Connecticut Births and Christenings, 1649-1906," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F77V-HRM : 11 February 2018), Sarah Gibbons, 17 Aug 1645; citing ; FHL microfilm unknown.
2 CONT *"Massachusetts Births and Christenings, 1639-1915," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:FCWG-WH4 : 10 February 2018), Sarah in entry for William Davie, 27 Jun 1686; citing BOSTON,SUFFOLK,MASSACHUSETTS,
2 CONC  ; FHL microfilm 397,042.
2 CONT * Early Generations of the Founders of Old Dunstable: Thirty Families By Ezra S. Stearns.  Page 84. [https://books.google.com/books?id=UCduacZqPYcC&lpg=PA84&ots=NsCm3cpI1f&dq=Sarah%20(Gibbons)%20Richards&pg=PA84#v=onepage&q&f=true
2 CONC  GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * The New England Merchants In The Seventeenth Century By Bernard Bailyn.  Page [https://books.google.com/books?id=y-J8CgAAQBAJ&lpg=PT126&ots=QFz2DHOy2N&dq=Sarah%20(Gibbons)%20Tyng&pg=PT125#v=onepage&q=Sarah%20(Gibbons)%20Tyng&f=t
2 CONC rue GoogleBooks]
2 CONT *https://www.werelate.org/wiki/Person:Sarah_Gibbons_%289%29
2 CONT *Barbour, Lucius Barnes. Families of Early Hartford, Connecticut. (Baltimore: Genealogical Publishing Co., 1977), 208. Humphrey Davie of Boston m. (2) Sarah (Gibbons) Richards, widow of James Richards, d/o William & Ursula Gibbons
2 CONC , b. Hartford 17 Aug 1645.
2 CONT *Johnson, Edward F. Woburn Records of Births, Deaths, and Marriages . (Woburn, Massachusetts: Andrews, Cutler & Co., 1890-1919), 2:198. Yyng, Sarah, wife of Col. Jonathan, Esq., Feb. 8, 1714; 69 y.[p. 1:7 says years are given as m
2 CONC odern equivalents so this is 8 Feb 1713/14. Birth calculates to about 1645.]
2 CONT *Plantagenet Ancestry: A Study In Colonial And Medieval Families, 2nd Edition ... page 629. [https://books.google.com/books?id=kjme027UeagC&pg=PA751&lpg=PA751&dq=Sarah+(Gibbons)+Tyng&source=bl&ots=qwHpMv1hgm&sig=ACfU3U14g3wBRxuvOm
