1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daughter of Rev. John Reyner.  Widow of Jabez Fox.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://homepages.rootsweb.com/~marshall/esmd91.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Rev. Jabez Fox (Thomas1); m. Judith Rayner, daughter of Rev. John Rayner and Frances Clark; bur. at Woburn, MA; b. 1647 at Concord, MA; d. 26 Feb 1702 at Boston, MA. He resided at Woburn, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Judith Rayner married 2nd to Col. Jonathan Tyng, son of Col. Edward Tyng and Mary Sears, either 1722 or 1723. She died on 5 Jun 1736.
2 CONT
2 CONT Known children of Rev. Jabez Fox and Judith Rayner all b. atWoburn, MA, were as follows:
2 CONT *      3.          i. Rev. John Fox, b. 16 May 1678; m. Mary Tyng.
2 CONT *                 ii. Thomas Fox; b. 6 Nov 1680.
2 CONT *                iii. Thomas Fox; b. 13 Nov 1681.
2 CONT *                 iv. Jabez Fox; b. 2 Dec 1684; m. Hannah Burroughs,
2 CONT *                     daughter of Rev. George Burroughs, 8 Mar 1705.
2 CONT *                  v. Judith Fox; b. 19 Jun 1690; d. 1703 .
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * Early Generations of the Founders of Old Dunstable: Thirty Families By Ezra S. Stearns.  Page 84. [https://books.google.com/books?id=UCduacZqPYcC&lpg=PA84&ots=NsCm3cpI1f&dq=Sarah%20(Gibbons)%20Richards&pg=PA84#v=onepage&q&f=true
2 CONC  GoogleBooks]
2 CONT * The New England Merchants In The Seventeenth Century By Bernard Bailyn.  Page [https://books.google.com/books?id=y-J8CgAAQBAJ&lpg=PT126&ots=QFz2DHOy2N&dq=Sarah%20(Gibbons)%20Tyng&pg=PT125#v=onepage&q=Sarah%20(Gibbons)%20Tyng&f=t
2 CONC rue GoogleBooks]
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT *ref: [http://records.ancestry.com/Judith_Reyner_records.ashx?pid=7296488 public Ancestry record]
2 CONT
2 CONT Four children with Jabez Fox:
2 CONT *Jabez Fox
2 CONT *John Fox
2 CONT *Thomas Fox
2 CONT *Judith Fox
2 CONT
2 CONT Also married Jonathan Tyng (1634-1724)
