1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Known children of Col. Edward Tyng and Elizabeth Clarke were as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. '''Elizabeth Tyng'''; b. circa 1685; m. Samuel Franklin, son of Josiah Franklin and Ann Child, 16 May 1705 at Boston, MA.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~ffru/Docs/FFRU_back/vol21.pdf footnote 14:
2 CONT
2 CONT "children of Elizabeth Compton (daughter of Samuel Franklin) descended in the right line from Samuel Franklin; they lived at Providence, R.I., 1793."
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://homepages.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~marshall/esmd90.htm Tyng Family Genealogy]
2 CONT
2 CONT Eldest son of Josiah and Ann and married Elizabeth Tyng.  Samuel became a blacksmith, the traditional trade for the eldest Franklin son.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==notes==
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~ffru/Docs/FFRU_back/vol21.pdf footnote 14:
2 CONT
2 CONT "children of Elizabeth Compton (daughter of Samuel Franklin) descended in the right line from Samuel Franklin; they lived at Providence, R.I., 1793."
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From [https://books.google.com/books?id=TLJH5N1XmXQC&pg=PA18&lpg=PA18&dq=Samuel+Franklin+1681+Elizabeth+Tyng&source=bl&ots=l8e_OGgpRg&sig=ys618iBza3sy0Mj8bXwXIxdRZ-Q&hl=en&sa=X&ei=_2ItVd-bKcaXgwSimYFY&ved=0CCEQ6AEwAQ#v=onepage&q=S
2 CONC amuel%20Franklin%201681%20Elizabeth%20Tyng&f=false Franklin Family] page 18.  The New England Historical and Genealogical Register, Volume 11
2 CONT
2 CONT (g) 9. Josiah,|| son of Thomas, had: ...  2. Samuel, b. May 16, 1681; m. Elizabeth Tyng, in New England.fi
2 CONT
2 CONT >fi. They appear to havo had descendants. The following memorandum is attached to my record: "Children of Elizabeth Compton (Daughter of Samuel Franklin) and Grandchildren descended in a right line from Samuel Franklin; they lived
2 CONC  at Providence, R. I., 1793.
