1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Norton Quincy (1716–1801), public servant, recluse, married Martha Salisbury (1727–1748) 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Attorney. Born to Colonel John and Elizabeth (nee Norton). He inherited the family property on Mount Wollaston along Quincy Bay, south of Boston.  A tragic figure, he was said to be Abigail Smith Adam's favorite uncle.  At 29 he m
2 CONC arried Martha Salisbury on 12 February 1746.  She died within the first year of the marriage.  His deep mourning turned him into a recluse for the rest of his life. He is mention in the letters of Abigail and her husband, who were
2 CONC  visitors at Mount Wollaston.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/27971484/norton-quincy Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 30 2019, 3:55:23 UTC''
