1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A.B. of Harvard 1727; A.M. Harvard, 1785. He was a physician in Boston for many years, and accumulated a large estate; among other items on the inventory of his estate was "one-half of Roanoke Island, N.C." He was 
2 CONC chosen proprietor's clerk of Topsham, Me., in 1757.
2 CONT
2 CONT October 4, 1731 Belcher Noyes (Gentleman) deeds to Hugh Hall, Esq., land in the West side of Orange St.; E. on Orange St., S. on land of William Payne, W. by the sea, N. on land of Sarah Noyes (sister). (SD 46:77). W. side Washing
2 CONC ton St. S. of Boylston St. September 13, 1733 Belcher Noyes (Gentleman) & Sarah Noyes (spinster) deed to Hugh Hall Esq. land at the South End; W. on Orange St., N. by land belonging to Obadiah Gore; E. by the sea; S. on the sea; (
2 CONC SD 47:276-7). E. side Washington S. of Boylston St. July 21, 1743 Belcher Noyes (physician) buys the shop, middle room, with cellar, and upper rooms of a mansion house, of Henry Gibbs. (SD 159:196). Change Ave. [Corn Market]. The 
2 CONC Dock. September 15, 1764 Belcher Noyes, Esq. and wife Ann deed to Benjamin Phillips (wharfinger) land, fronting on Oliver St. S.W., S.E. heirs of Anna Byles, late wife of Mather Byles, N.E. Benjamin Hollowell, Esq., N.W. Andrew Ol
2 CONC iver. (SD 105:115). N.E. side of Oliver St. October 5, 1770 Belcher Noyes, Esq. and wife Ann mortgages to Ezekiel Goldthwait, Esq., land; W. Pierce's Alley, S. house and land belonging to estate of Charles Apthorp, W. land belongi
2 CONC ng to estate of Charles Apthorp, and land belonging to heirs of John Hancock. Cancelled October 5, 1770. (SD 117:254). E. side of Change Ave. November 20, 1775 Belcher Noyes: Mortgages to Archbald MacNiel (baker) mansion house and
2 CONC  land in Corn Market St., where sd Belcher now lives; this being more fully described and bounded in division of estate of his honoured father, Oliver Noyes, Esq., deceased. Cancelled November 8, 1780. (SD 127:28). The Dock. [Corn
2 CONC  Market.]. November 8, 1786 Belcher Noyes, Esq., the mortgaged, Nathaniel Noyes, Adm. to estate of sd Belcher Noyes, buys a quit claim of Adm. of estate of Archibald McNiell. (SD 159:58). 
