1 OCCU Banker, businessman, Council member, militia officer, and landholder
1 TITL Colonel
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Banker, businessman, Council member, militia officer, and landholder, Albany native Jacob Wendell achieved unparalled distinction in New England. He died on September 7, 1761. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Doctor/poet Oliver Wendell Holmes Sr. was his great-grandson.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.nysm.nysed.gov/albany/bios/w/jawendell2696.html]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: August 1691 Albany, NY  
2 CONT
2 CONT Came from Albany to Boston, as a young man, to work for the merchant John Mico.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage:  12 AUG 1714 
2 CONT
2 CONT Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death:  07 SEP 1761 
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Lost multiple buildings in Boston's Great Fire of 1760
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "Jacob Wendell (bapt. Aug. 11, 1691), Baptismal Record, the youngest child of Johannes Wendel and Elsie Staets. was the first of the name to remove to New England, and came to Boston when a youth, receiving his business education 
2 CONC in the counting-house of Mr. John Mico, a well know Boston merchant of the period. At the close of this connection he entered into business upon his own account, accumulated a handsome estate, and became one of the most prominent 
2 CONC citizens of his day. He was uncle of John Wendell, the son of his eldest brother Abraham, who came to Boston at a later period, and became associated with him in business. He was of his Majesty's Council from 1737 to 1760, command
2 CONC er of the Ancient and Honorable Artillery 1735 and 1745, and in 1733 director of the first banking institution of the province...
2 CONT
2 CONT The Hon. Col. Wendell lived at the corner of School and Common (the present Tremont) Sts. and married (Aug. 12, 1714) Sarah, daughter of Dr. James and Mercy (Bradstreet) Oliver, of Cambridge, by whom he had issue twelve children, 
2 CONC four sons and eight daughters."
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob b. September 4, 1715-6
2 CONT Mary b. January 20, 1719 d. August 6, 1717
2 CONT Elizabeth b. January 20, 1719
2 CONT Sarah b. March 3, 1720
2 CONT Mary b. April 10, 1722
2 CONT Catherine b. June 18, 1726
2 CONT John Micro b. May 30, 1728
2 CONT Ann b. December 7, 1730
2 CONT Oliver b. March 5, 1733
2 CONT Abraham b. November 2, 1735
2 CONT Susannah b. June 15, 1737, bp. 19 June 1737
2 CONT Margaret b. August 20, 1739 [2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT He died Sep. 16, 1761 in Boston, Massachusetts and was buried in Van Rensselaer Family Cemetery, East Greenbush, New York. [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Wendell-133
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacobus Wendell (bef. 1691 - 1761)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Jacobus (Jacob) Wendell===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born before 5 Aug 1691 in Albany, Albany County, Province of New York
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Johannes Wendel and Elizabeth (Staets) Schuyler
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Maritie (Wendel) Oothout [half], Elsie (Wendel) Staets [half], Abraham Wendell, Elizabeth (Wendel) Ten Broeck, Johannes Wendell Jr, Ephraim Wendel, Isaac Wendell, Sara Wendell, Isaac Wendell, Susanna (Wendel) Schuyler, 
2 CONC Catalynjte (Wendel) Schuyler, Philip Johannise Schuyler [half], Johannes Schuyler Jr [half] and Margarita Schuyler [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Sarah (Oliver) Wendell — married 12 Aug 1714 (to 7 Sep 1761) in Boston, Suffolk, Massachusetts [uncertain]
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Jacob Wendell, Elizabeth (Wendell) Wibird, Mary Wendell, Sarah (Wendell) Hunt, Mercy (Wendell) Oliver, Katherine (Wendell) Cooper, John Micro Wendell, Ann Wendell, Oliver Wendell, Abraham Wendell, Susannah Wendell and Ma
2 CONC rgaret Wendell
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 7 Sep 1761 after age 70 in Boston, Suffolk County, Massachusetts Bay
2 CONT
