3 CTRY Canada
1 TITL Captain
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elijah's parents were,  ELIJAH ESTABROOK and HANNAH DANIEL, from Massachusetts (From Estabrook Family of Aroostook County, Maine).
2 CONT
2 CONT Elijah served 1758-1760 in Col. Prebbles's Regiment of Provincials and fought at Ticonderoga. In 1776, Elijah took part in an expedition against the British at Fort Cumberland. He was a farmer and a member of the Congregational Ch
2 CONC urch. Elijah died in 1796 in Swan Creek, Queens Co., New Brunswick, Canada and was buried in the Garrison Graveyard, Jemseg, Queens Co., New Brunswick, Canada.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT http://silverhawkauthor.com/ticonderoga-soldier-elijah-estabrooks-17581760-a-massachusetts-provincial-soldier-in-the-french-and-indian-war_301.html<br/>
2 CONT ----
