1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Roots, son of Edmund Rootes and Emma Norrington, was baptized on December 11, 1607 at Eastwell, Kent. He married Margery (_____) unknown surname.
2 CONT
2 CONT >Richard Rootes. He lived in Lynn and Salem. In the latter place he was a member of the Congregational Church in 1636. He was made free March 9, 1637. He removed to Fairfield, Ct., taking with him his nephew John,* son of Josiah, 
2 CONC and it is altogether probable that he left no children of his own. He d. in Fairfield before 1653, when his widow married Michael Try.
