2 CONT Name Meaning
2 CONT
2 CONT Gale
2 CONT
2 CONT Azor
2 CONT English: nickname from Anglo-Norman French gal, gale, galle ‘cock, cockerel’.
2 CONT English: habitational name from a minor place called with either Middle English gale, gagel (Old English gagel) ‘bog myrtle’, or with Middle English gale ‘fishery paying dues to the lord’ (Old English gafol ‘tax’?) such as Gale in
2 CONC  Bickington (Devon) and The Gale, the name of a fishery in Ham and Stone (Gloucestershire).
2 CONT MORE
2 CONT English: topographic name from Middle English gale, gail (Old Norse geil) ‘ravine, narrow lane’, or a habitational name from a place so named such as Gale in Littleborough, Rochdale (Lancashire), or possibly High Gale in Tatham or
2 CONC  Tunstall (Lancashire). With the sense ‘narrow lane’ it is found in several street names in medieval York.
2 CONT MORE
2 CONT Dictionary of American Family Names © Patrick Hanks 2003, 2006.
