2 CONT World Events (2)
2 CONT 1692 · Salem Witch Trials
2 CONT Age 23
2 CONT In 1692, the Salem Witch Trials began when Betty Parris fell sick with an unknown illness. Her cousin Abigail William claimed that she was being made sick because of witchcraft. As other strange events began to happen more of the 
2 CONC young ladies in the town started accussing more people. These people mainly consisted of people the young ladies did not like. By the time the hysteria ended over 200 people were accussed of being witches. Nineteen men and women w
2 CONC ere found guilty and hung.
2 CONT 1727 · Crowninshield-Bentley House Built
2 CONT Age 58
2 CONT The Crowninshield-Bentley house was built in 1727 by ship captain John Caspar Crowninshield. His family occupied the house for generations until it was taken over by Revend Bentley.
