2 CONT DEED July 6, 1725 Azor Gale, Jr. (merchant) deeds to John Gibbons (shopkeeper) the notherly half part of a certain piece of land lying on both sides of the highway leading toward Roxbury upon the neck of land adjoining to the lot 
2 CONC of land belonging to William Payne Esq. on the northerly side thereof and the lot of William Clark on the southerly side E. on the flats next the sea. front on Orange St. (SD 47:174) both sides Washington St. S. of Boylston Decemb
2 CONC er 3, 1725 Azor Gale (merchant) and wife Anna, one of the daughters of Oliver Noyes, deed to Stephen Boutineau (merchant) W. 1/2 part of warehouse No. 5 upon Long Wharf or King St. Pier. (SD 39:73) Long Wharf, State St. December 2
2 CONC 5, 1725 Azor Gale, Jr. (merchant) and wife Anna, one of the daughters of Oliver Noyes, mortgages to Sarah Martyn (widow and shopkeeper) N. 1/2 part of brick warehouse and land in Corn Market; N. on warehouse and land of Thomas Pal
2 CONC mer, E. on warehouse and land of Alexander Sheerar, S. on other half of sd warehouse of Oliver Noyes and W. on passageway leading up to house and land of Nicholas Morecock. Cancelled September 29, 1729 (SD 39:95)
2 CONT
2 CONT WILL April 2, 1725
2 CONT
2 CONT PROBATE February 24, 1728 Azor Gale (merchant): Ex.: wife Anna. Legatee: wife Anna. Inventory: 147 pounds, 10 shillings. (SPR 27:77)
