0 @N6000000006345214953@ NOTE "Four brothers, Richard, William, John and Thomas Curtis, settled in Scituate. Thomas went to York Co., ME; John appears to have left no descendants, while those of Richard and William are numerous in Scituate, Hanover and vicinit
1 CONC y in Massachusetts
1 CONT
1 CONT "Richard Curtis, immigrant ancestor, was born in Kent, England. He settled in Scituate, Massachusetts, about 1643, and died there in 1693. Some writers have confused this Richard with Richard Curtis, of Dorchester and Milton; and 
1 CONC with Richard Curtis, of Salem and Marblehead. Richard, of Scituate, was on the list of Plymouth colony men able to bear arms in that 1643, and was a town officer in 1650. His brother William as also on this list, and together they
1 CONC  took the oath of fidelity. He was one of the 'allowed and approved inhabitants' to whom portions of the common lands were assigned by the joint committee of the general court in 1673. Richard Curtis and Thomas Hyland were witness
1 CONC es to the will of General James Cudworth in 1682. His home was between that of Gowen White and the harbor below Millbrook."5
1 CONT
1 CONT "Richard Curtis was one of four brothers who came early to New England, viz. Richard, Thomas, John and William. John left no family.
1 CONT
1 CONT "Richard had lands at Marblehead in 1648, and in the same year he purchased lands in Scituate, and built a house between Gowin White's and the Harbour.
1 CONT
1 CONT "His will, dated 1692, gives 'To oldest son John two thirds ofmy real estate, he providing for my wife Lydia during her life. To son Thomsas one third, &c. To daughters Hannah Curtis, Elizabeth Brooks, Mary Badcocke, and Martha Cl
1 CONC ark.'"21
0 @N6000000006348241060@ NOTE
1 CONT
1 CONT 10. ROBERT1 BADCOCK or BABCOCK and his brother George settled in Milton, Mass., in 1648, and were among the first fourteen owners of land. Robert had 107 acres; assessor of Dorchester, 1657; selectman of Milton, 1668, '70, '73 and
1 CONC  '77; appointed sergeant, 1676; a captain in the Indian Wars; is called Capt. Badcock on the Milton Church records.
1 CONT
1 CONT He married in 1649, Joanna (???) who was born in 1629, and died Dec. 4, 1700, in Milton. He died Nov. 12, 1694. His will of Nov. 11, 1694, mentions his wife Joanna.
1 CONT
1 CONT Children, first six born in Dorchester, last five in Milton:--
1 CONT
1 CONT      1.  Samuel, b. 1650, d. 1690, m. 1674, Hannah Emes.
1 CONT      2.  Jonathan, b. 1652, d. 1732, m. 1676, Mary Curtis (Richard1), (2)
1 CONT    Mary Hebard.
1 CONT      3.  James, b. Jan. 12, 1654.
1 CONT     +4.  Abigail, b. Feb. 1656, m. 1674, John Barber (George1).
1 CONT      5.  Nathaniel, b. Mar. 14, 1658, d. 1719, m. Hannah (???).
1 CONT      6.  Caleb, b. Aug. 14, 1660.
1 CONT      7.  Ebenezer, b. Oct. 2, 1662, d. 1717, m. Hannah (???).
1 CONT      8.  Hopestill, bapt. Nov. 8, 1663.
1 CONT      9.  Hannah, b. Feb. 8, 1665, d. 1711, m. 1683, Joseph Morse.
1 CONT     10.  Elizabeth, b. Dec. 24, 1666, d. 1732, m. Henry Vose.
1 CONT     11.  Thankful, b. Feb. 18, 1669, m. 1687, George Lyon (George1) d.
1 CONT    1694, (2) 1701, Richard Smith.
1 CONT
1 CONT SOURCE:  Bibliographic Information: Preston, Belle. Bassett-Preston Ancestors. New Haven, Conn.: The Tuttle, Morehouse, and Taylor Co., 1930.
0 @N6000000006345214833@ NOTE Capt. John Sprague with 22 sentinels marched from Sims-
1 CONT         bury, Conn. (Conn. Hist. Papers, iv, 12.)1739, Capt. Sprague removed from Lebanon to Sharon, Conn.
1 CONT         He drew the 37th home lot. He was a Selectman for sev-
1 CONT         eral years, and what is singular he could not write his
1 CONT        name. The words John X Sprague are appended to many
1 CONT                       mark
1 CONT         official documents on the Sharon records. He built the
1 CONT         first frame house in the town. In 1748, he exchanged-
1 CONT         farms with Cornelius Knickerbocker and removed to
1 CONT         Furnace Village (now Lakeville) in Salisbury, Conn.
1 CONT         He afterwards removed to Canaan, Conn., where he
1 CONT         died. (Hist. Sharon, Conn.)
1 CONT
1 CONT Source:  SPRAGUE FAMILIES
1 CONT IN
1 CONT AMERICA
1 CONT Compiled and Published by
1 CONT WARREN VINCENT, SPRAGUE, M, D.
1 CONT
1 CONT THE TUTTLE COMPANY, PRINTERS
1 CONT RUTLAND, VERMONT 1913
