0 @N6000000003299374804@ NOTE [HOHORST.GED]
1 CONT
1 CONT "Three Laphams seem to have come to America in the 1600s.  One settled in Rhode Island and two in Massachusetts.  John married a Hollis in Malden in 1671 and THOMAS LAPHAM, born in Kent, England came to Scituate previous to 1635 f
1 CONC rom County of Kent in Old England.  Thomas came to seek a place to enjoy more perfect religious freedom.  He joined Rev. John Lathrop's church March 24th, 1636.  He married Mary, eldest daughter of Elder Nathaniel and Lydia Tilden
1 CONC , and they lived near Scituate Harbor. Thomas' name rarely appears in town records, but his hame appears frequently in the church records."
1 CONT - From Beatrice Hohrost's Family History
0 @N6000000001657779219@ NOTE
1 CONT Although some researchers believe that the surname of John's spouse was Lapham, the matter is not settled. Rebecca (________) Washburn's tombstone still stands in the old cemetery in Bridgewater.
1 CONT Sources: Mayflower Families in Progress - Cooke and visit to Bridgewater.
