0 @N6000000004547869651@ NOTE New Haven Proprietors  (From Great Migration Study by NEHGS)
1 CONT Thus, at some point between 1640 and 1646, the proprietary share of Mr. Mansfield, an absentee landowner, was broken up into six pieces, John Nash, Joseph Nash and Henry Lindell each receiving a quarter of the land, and William Ba
1 CONC ssett, Edward Hitchcock and Thomas Munson subdividing the remaining quarter among the three of them. Whether any one of these six men retained the proprietary rights attaching to the houselot has not yet been determined.
