0 @N6000000003525444210@ NOTE
1 CONT He was first child of Dolor Davis born in America. Settled in Concord at age 20 when his father and family moved from Barnstable; was deputy 1689, 1690, 1692, and 1705 and held other responsible positions. Was commander of troops 
1 CONC after wounding of Capt. Wheeler at Brookfield, 1675; freeman Mass. colony 21 Mar 1689/90. Will made 24 Jun 1710, on file at East Cambridge, has his signature. Died June 14, 1713, age 77. Gravestone standing in Concord (as of 1881)
1 CONC . Will proved 3 Jul 1713 and on file Middlesex, County, MA. (Number 6086). Most lands divided among sons prior to death.  Autograph may be seen on Concord records 1689/90 attesting election of town clerk. Divided most of his real 
1 CONC estate among sons before his death. He had inherited Dor's farm in Concord
1 CONT
1 CONT --Invalid Dates
1 CONT Burial: Concord, MA
