0 @N6000000006165935422@ NOTE PHEBE DAMON RISLEY
1 CONT By Roy D. Gould
1 CONT
1 CONT For the descendants of Jonathan Risley (220 DRR) the identity of his wife Phebe had long been a question that had gone unanswered. In the Risley Family History, 1909 Edwin H. Risley Stated: Jonathan married "Phoebe Deming in 1773,
1 CONC  h. 1753; d. Oct 10, 1833. Phoebe Deming was a lineal descendant of John Deming who was one of the persons named in the Connecticut charter of Charles 11 of England." This statement has been proved to be incorrect. Phebe was a Dam
1 CONC on or Daman with no relationship to John Deming of Wethersfield, Connecticut.
1 CONT
1 CONT Phebe is buried in the West Hills Cemetery, between Sangerfield and North Brookfield, Madison County, NY, next to Jonathan. Her headstone says: "In Memory of Phebe, wife of Jonathan Risley, died Oct. 10, 1833, aged 80 years." It p
1 CONC rovided no clue to her identity other than the year she was born. The Genealogy of the Descendants of John Deming of Wethersfield, CT by. Judson K. Deming, 1904 revealed no Phebe in 1753 in any of the families covered. Nor could w
1 CONC e find a record of her birth in other vital record sources. The author did provide a clue however. Deming lamented that "a large number of persons and families bearing the name Deming, are descendants of ancestors of various names
1 CONC  that changed to Deming. Most frequent among them are the descendants of John Damon of Scituate, Mass, a contemporary of John Deming of Wethersfield, Conn."
1 CONT
1 CONT Then out of the blue, the marriage record for Jonathan and Phebe was discovered in the vital records of Somers, CT by cousin, Robert J. Irwin. It states: "Phebe Deman, m. Jonathan Risley, both of Hartford, April 25, 1774, by Thoma
1 CONC s Pitkin, of Bolton, Conn." We now knew for a fact she was from Hartford, that there had to be a Deman, Damon, or Daman family living there. Indeed there was, the vital records of Hartford record the marriage of Benjamin Dammon of
1 CONC  Hartford, married to Mercy Palmer of Windham November 5th 1740, and the birth of a son in 1744, but, no mention of a daughter. Additionally, the ear mark for the creatures of Benjamin Daman Jr were entered Dec 6, 1749.
1 CONT
1 CONT The will of Benjamin Daman Jr provides us with the answer. It was written August 28, 1787, he was then living at East Hartford, Conn., and admitted for probate shortly after his death on November 4, 1807. He made the following beq
1 CONC uest:"Item: I give to my beloved daughter, Pnebe Risley the sum of five shillings lawful money to be paid out of my estate." Thus the wife of Jonathan Risley was Phebe Daman or Damon. It should also be noted that Jonathan and Pheb
1 CONC e named their first child and eldest son, Benjamin, in deference to her father.
1 CONT
1 CONT There was another Phoebe Risley in the family, but she could not be confused for Jonathan's spouse. She was Phoebe (Bills) Risley born July 24, 1761, a daughter of John and Irene (Swetland) Bills, who married Jonathan's first cous
1 CONC in, Elijah Risley Sr [215 DRR] in 1779, they lived at Fredonia, NY.
1 CONT
1 CONT Phebe's ancestry is as follows: she was a daughter of Benjamin Damon Jr, born 6 Mar 1723, Reading, MA, died 4 Nov 1806, East Hartford, CT, he married 5 Nov 1740 at Hartford, CT Mercy Palmer who died 30 Dec 1781; granddaughter of B
1 CONC enjamin Damon, born 30 Apr 1693, at Reading, MA, died 21 Aug 1771, Reading, MA, he married Mercy Flint, a daughter of George 2 and Elizabeth (Putnam) Flint, born 7 oct 1692 and died 26 Apr 1740, at Reading, MA; great granddaughter
1 CONC  of Samuef Damon, who was born 23 June 1656, Reading, MA, died 12 Jan 1723/4 Reading, MA, he married in 1680, Mary (Davis) Grover, a daughter of George and Sarah (Clark) Davis, born 16 Jan 1657/8 and died 29 Nov 1727, Reading, MA;
1 CONC  2nd great granddaughter of John Damon, who is said to have come to America in 1635, settling first at Scituate, MA, removing to Reading, MA where he died on 8 Apr 1708, he married, Abigail Sherman, a daughter of Richard and Eliza
1 CONC beth ( ? ) Sherman, she died 25 Dec 1713, at Reading, MA. Her father resided at Dedham, MA.
1 CONT
1 CONT Jonathan and Phebe settled at Brookfield, Madison County, NY in 1792, where they were first settlers. She may not have known of her father's passing. The confusion about her origins is directly attributable to the several spelling
1 CONC s of the surname as it appears in various record sources. All is now clear.
