0 @N6000000000130300746@ NOTE http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~michaelcaldwell/Scans/tenterden/baptisms/nathanieltilden.jpg
0 @N6000000000491051006@ NOTE [Himes.Core.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [143983.GED]
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT In New England, Nathaniel Tilden, "Gentleman," an elder of the church, who held important offices of trust, was accorded the position due to his social status, education, and comparative wealth.
1 CONT
1 CONT Nathaniel Tilden was baptized in Tenterden, County Kent, 28 July 1583, the son of Thomas and Alice (Biggs) Tilden. He remained in Tenterden, became a Jurat, then Mayor in 1622, an emigrated with his family to America, in 1634-5.
1 CONT  Background on his family is given in NEHGR 65:322, 75:226, and 114:153.
1 CONT      Tilden came to New England in the HERCULES 1634-35
1 CONT accompanied by his wife Lydia (Huckstep), seven children, and seven servants. He settled in Scituate and he probably died there between may and July 1641. All the children of Nathaniel and Lydia Tilden were born in England, five d
1 CONC ying there prior to the family’s departure. The children were Thomas, who died young; Mary, who married Thomas Lapham; Joseph, who died young; Sarah who married George Sutton; Joseph, who married Alice or Elizabeth Twisden; Stephe
1 CONC n, who died young; Thomas, who married Elizabeth (Bourne) Waterman; Judith, who married Abraham Preble; Winifred, who died young; Lydia, who died young; Lydia who married Richard Garrett; and Stephen, who married Hannah Little. Ma
1 CONC ry and Sarah were married on the same day, 13 March 1636-37 (NEHGR 9:286), and their husbands were Tilden’s servants. After his death, his widow Lydia married Timothy Hatherly.
1 CONT       Elizabeth French shows in NEHGR 70:256 that Lydia (Huckstep) (Tilden) Hatherly was a cousin of Thomas Hatch, q.v., who also came to New England in the Hercules and settled at Scituate. Tilden was of the gentry and addressed 
1 CONC as Mr., and he was one of the wealthier Scituate residents. He dated his will 25 May 1641, inventory 31 July 1641, and he names his wife Lydia and his
1 CONT children Stephen; Lydia; Joseph; Thomas; Judith; Mary, the wife of Thomas Lapham; and Sarah, the wife of George Sutton; and he also mentioned two indentured servants, Edward Jenkins and Edward Tarte.
1 CONT  (MD 3:220) (Plymouth Colony Biographical
1 CONT Sketches)
1 CONT      TILDEN, NATHANIEL, of Tenterden, Co. Kent, and of Scituate in the Plymouth colony, passenger in the HERCULES.
1 CONT  For his family and ancestry ct. REGISTER, VOL 65 PP322-333.
1 CONT       His wife was Lydia Huckstep, baptised at Tenterden 11 Feb. 1587/8,
1 CONT daughter of Steven and Winifred [Hatch] [Wills] [cf. REGISTER, VOL 67, PP 47, 48]
