0 @N6000000003122782160@ NOTE Jurat, Tenterden, Kent, England, 1624, 25, 27, 29.  A wealthy lawyer.  Mayor of Tenterton, Kent, England, 1622.  Arrived in America on ship "Hercules" with 7 children and 7 servants, 1634.  Ruling elder, first church in Scituate, 
1 CONC Mass., 1634.  Settled Scituate, Mass., 1634.  First beekeeper in Mass.   First Tilden ancestor in America.
0 @N6000000003186715971@ NOTE Nathaniel and family emigrated from England 1634 in Ship Hercules, John Witherley, Master. Nathaniel was one of the founders of Scituate, Plymouth Colony. Will written 25 May 1641. Sons Thomas and Stephen named in Will. Nathaniel 
1 CONC buried Kent Cemetery, Scituate, Plymouth Colony now Plymouth, Massachusetts.
0 @N6000000003490631846@ NOTE
1 CONT Nathaniel Tilden came to New England on the Hercules in early 1634/1635, acompanied by his wife, seven children, and seven servants.  He settled in Scituate and probably died there.  All the children of Nathaniel and Lydia were bo
1 CONC rn in England, five dying there prior to the family's departure.Tilden was a gentleman and addressed as "Mr." and he was one of the wealthier Scituate residents.  [Plymouth Colony by Eugene Stratton]
0 @N6000000000491073084@ NOTE [Himes.Core.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [143983.GED]
1 CONT
1 CONT Arrived in New England in the HERCULES in 1634/35 accompanied by her husband and seven children and seven servants.
1 CONT       Elizabeth French shows in NEHGR 70:256 that Lydia (Huckstep) (Tilden) Hatherly was a cousin of Thomas Hatch, q.v., who also came to New England in the Hercules and settled at Scituate.
1 CONT      Nathaniel and Lydia [Huckstep] Tilden had twelve children baptized at Tenterden. Five of these children were buried at Tenterden, and seven accompanied their parents to New England. Their daughter Mary married 13 Mar. 1636/7 
1 CONC Thomas Lapham, and their daughter Sarah married on the same day GEORGE SUTTON, both of these men appeearing in the passenger list as servants of NATHANIEL TILDEN
1 CONT . (English Origins of New England Families Vol 3. pg 755)
