0 @N6000000003299356347@ NOTE [HOHORST.GED]
1 CONT
1 CONT "Nathaniel Tilden was of Tenterden, Kent, England.  He came to America in 1634 in the Hercules of Sandwich, bringing with him his seven children. His wife was a daughter of Thomas Bourne, formerly of Kent, but an early resident of
1 CONC  Marshfield.
1 CONT Nathaniel Tilden was a very prominent member of this family.  He was a ruling Elder in John Lathrop's Church in Scituate and one of the wealthiest of the early settlers.  He died in 1641.  He owned ten swams of bees.  This seems t
1 CONC o be the earliest notice of keeping of bees in the Colony.
1 CONT THOMAS LAPHAM married Mary, eldest daughter of Elder Nathaniel Tilden. After the death of her husband Mary married William Bassett."
1 CONT - From Beatrice Hohorst's Family History
0 @N6000000000130300683@ NOTE --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT ID: I20900  
1 CONT Name: **Sarah Tilden 1 
1 CONT Sex: F 
1 CONT Birth: BEF 13 JUN 1613 in Tenterden, Weald of Kent, England 2 
1 CONT Death: 20 MAR 1676/77 in Albemarle County, Perquimans Precinct, North Carolina 
1 CONT Note: 
1 CONT Sarah (Sara) TILDEN - married 13 Mar 1636/7 (1641) at Scituate, Ma. to
1 CONT servant George SUTTON (born 12 Apr 1613 at Sandwich, Kent Co., England;
1 CONT died 12 Apr 1669 in Perquiman Co., N.C.); they had at least 8 and probably
1 CONT nine children. George Sutton arrived in Boston, Mass., in 1634 on the ship
1 CONT Hercules. He came as a servant to Nathaniel Tilden of Tenterden, Co. Kent,
1 CONT England. He may have worked as servant to earn his passage to America.
1 CONT George was considered a devote member of the Society of Friends or
1 CONT "Quakers" in Mass. In 1668 the persecution of Quakers drove George and
1 CONT Sarah, along with some of their children, from Scituate to Perquimans,
1 CONT North Carolina. The area had just been opened for settlement for Quakers.
1 CONT One of the earliest Quaker Meeting Houses was built toward the end of the
1 CONT 17th century on "SuttonÆs Creek," so named because it bordered the lands
1 CONT of George Sutton and his sons.
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Father: ****Nathaniel Tilden b: BEF 28 JUL 1583 in Tenterden, Kent, England 
1 CONT Mother: *Lydia Huckstep b: BEF 11 FEB 1587/88 in Tenterden, Weald of Kent, England
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage 1 *George Sutton b: 12 APR 1613 in Sandwich, Kent County, England
1 CONT Married: 13 MAR 1636/37 in Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts 2
1 CONT Children
1 CONT  *Joseph Sutton , Sr. b: 1637 in Scituate, Plymouth County, Massachusetts
1 CONT  Daniel Sutton b: 20 NOV 1639
1 CONT  William Sutton b: 25 MAY 1641 in Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts
1 CONT  John Sutton b: 1642
1 CONT  *Nathaniel Sutton b: 1643 in Scituate, Plymouth, Massachusetts
1 CONT  Lydia Sutton b: 1646
1 CONT  Sarah Sutton b: BET 1648 AND 1650
1 CONT  Elizabeth Sutton b: 1653
1 CONT
1 CONT Sources:
1 CONT Title: Personal Communication from Audrey Hilton, Email: AHilton999@aol.com, 12/14/00 
1 CONT Title: English Origins of New England Families, Vol. 1, Roberts, Gen. Pub. Co. 1984, p152. 
1 CONT
