0 @N6000000001657778864@ NOTE
1 CONT John Washburn Jr. came to America with his mother and brother in 1635 on the Elizabeth. John Jr. participated in the campaign against the Narragansett Indians in August 1645. John Jr. and Elizabeth were among the original settlers
1 CONC  in Bridgewater, Plymouth Colony. Six of the seven sons of John Jr. and Elizabeth left children, and many Washburns in America are descended from one of these six sons.
1 CONT Sources: Bridgewater vital records, Mayflower Families in Progress - Cooke and Mayflower Families - Chilton.
