0 @N6000000003490724596@ NOTE In 1661 Elizabeth petitioned for and was granted a divorce after the court had sentenced her husband Thomas to two severe whippings for his "act of uncleanness" with Lydia Gaunt but suspended his having to wear "AD" dependent on h
1 CONC is future behavior.   In earlier convictions of adultery, the person had to wear an "AD" badge on the sleeve for as long as he or she lived in the colony.  The "AD" was an abbreviation for adultery.  If the person was ound withoug
1 CONC h the badge, she would be branded in the face.  (The Times of their Lives, Life, Love, and Death in Plymouth Colony, by James and Patricia Deetz)
